    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651836": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Pharmaceutical Sciences Neuroscience Addiction Lab Technician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Pharmaceutical Sciences Neuroscience Addiction Lab Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Pharmaceutical Sciences Neuroscience Addiction Lab Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Pharmaceutical Sciences Neuroscience Addiction Lab Technician Requisition Number DU15173 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 789 S Limestone Lexington, KY 40506 Salary Range $13.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education N/A Required Related Experience Previous work experience or equivalent. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Sitting and standing for long periods of time; lifting and/or carrying up to 15 lbs.; reaching and bending; using step ladder to reach objects on upper shelving. Shift Weekdays between 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Weekends and evenings depending on experiments. . Job Summary Dr. Anel Jaramillo in the Pharmaceutical Sciences Department in the College of Pharmacy is seeking a part-time research lab technician for the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters with the possibility of extension to other semesters. The primary responsibility will be to maintain research space, manage general inventory, conduct general mouse colony husbandry and assist with research projects. Projects examine the function of neural circuits regulating anxiety and alcohol-related behaviors. Projects include conducting animal drinking studies, brain sectioning, tissue and behavioral data analysis. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Ability to follow research protocols and detailed record-keeping. Works well with other lab members. Comfortable handling rodents. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Lab experience and/or animal handling. Biology, Neuroscience, Psychology, or equivalent field majors preferred. Deadline to Apply 01/31/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651835": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant/Ambulatory/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Medical Assistant/Ambulatory/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Medical Assistant/Ambulatory/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Medical Assistant/Ambulatory/UKHC Requisition Number RE53873 Working Title Medical Assistant/Ambulatory Department Name M2000: COMMUNITY - NORTON Work Location Louisville, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $18.54-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 0 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification One of the following: 1. State Registered Nurse Assistant ( SRNA ) 2. Certified Nursing Assistant ( CNA ) 3. Registered Nurse (RN) nursing student who has completed first fundamental course and a clinical 4. Emergency Medical Technician ( EMT ) / medic including military medic 5. Graduate from a medical assistant program. 5. Graduate from a licensed practical nursing program. 6. Clinical Services Technician ( CST ) III at UK in the last 12 months. Basic Life Support ( BLS ) at time of hire through American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider. Physical Requirements The ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis; as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift Monday-Friday 8:00am-5:00pm, may require some holidays. Job Summary The Medical Assistant (MA) will be responsible for direct patient care and provides clinical support to providers. Duties include but not limited to the following: obtain patient medical history information, expedite patient flow, room patients, stocking clinic with supplies, navigate electronic health record system, schedule and follow-up with appointments and assist with medication fill requests, prior authorizations and schedule tests, procedures and consults. The MA will communicate with pharmacies, insurance companies, patients and physicians in a respectful manner and follow UK Healthcare behavioral expectations for service excellence. The starting pay for this position was recently adjusted. The minimum hourly rate for this position will now be $18.20/hour. All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 1 year clinical experience Deadline to Apply 10/27/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have one of the following, or are you eligible to obtain this by date of hire? 1. Kentucky Registered SRNA, Certified Nursing Assistant (Aid) 2. RN nursing student who has completed first fundamental course and a clinical, 3. Paramedic 4. Graduate from an accredited medical assistant program 5. Graduate from a licensed practical nursing program 6. CST III at UK in the last 12 months Yes No * Do you have a current BLS (Basic Life Support) certification through the American Heart Association (AHA), or are you eligible to obtain this by date of hire? Yes No * Please indicate your paid employment experience in healthcare. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * If hired, can you provide proof that you are at least 18 years of age at start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
