    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651799": {
      "title": "STEPS Employee Records Clerk",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Employee Records Clerk Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Employee Records Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Employee Records Clerk Requisition Number TE09526 Department Name 3J541:Compensation Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education Required Related Experience Required License/Registration/Certification Physical Requirements Ability to lift, push, and pull objects up to 25lbs, sitting or standing for long periods of time, and repetitive motion. Shift Work Shift Monday – Friday; 8:00 am-5:00 pm Expected # of Hours Per Week 40 Job Summary The STEPS Employee Records Clerk will provide flexible support to the Employee Records team within the Human Resources department. The primary responsibility of this role is to upload documents into the employee records system. Additional duties may include, but are not limited to: Alphabetizing and filing documents Preparing and scanning materials for digital records Retrieving employee record information as needed Assisting with the No For Rehire process Supporting Verifications of Employment ( VOE ) The Records Clerk may also assist with general office tasks such as: Compiling informational packets Sending faxes Making copies Other administrative support duties as assigned This position offers an excellent opportunity to gain valuable experience at the University of Kentucky, especially for those interested in a career in Human Resources. It’s a great way to build competitive skills and get your foot in the door! Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated ability to: Handle confidential information Follow instructions accurately Work independently with minimal supervision. Prior experience in office support, data entry, or document management is preferred, but not required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have providing administrative support for a department or organization? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe your experience in a position that required constant attention to detail and accuracy. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
