    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651796": {
      "title": "Central Sterile Tech/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Central Sterile Tech/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Central Sterile Tech/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Central Sterile Tech/UKHC Requisition Number RE55700 Working Title CST Department Name H3320:Perioperative Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements This position requires regularly lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds; standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); and intermittently sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time. Also involves risk of injuries from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste; radiation; burns; cuts/punctures; blood-borne or airborne pathogens; and recombinant DNA or viral vectors. Shift The shifts for this position are M-TH 11a-930p. Job Summary UK Healthcare is seeking a Central Sterile Tech to operate as one of the most important team members in a hospital’s arsenal – assisting our front-line workers during complex cases as well as those with high levels of acuity. Our Central Sterile Techs are directly responsible for assembling and processing surgical instrument trays as well as decontaminating used instruments that assist in eliminating infections and maintaining supplies. The selected candidate will also be essential in answering unit phone calls, responding to OR requests, and maintaining cleanliness of the department/workstation. Qualified candidates will have a good working knowledge of regulatory standards for universal precautions, sterilization methodologies, and regulatory standards for biological monitoring. Applicants who possess the CRCST (Certified Registered Central Service Technician) certification are eligible to be hired into a Central Sterile Tech/Certified/ UKHC position, which is a grade 7 ($17.50/hour – $27.31/hour). Applicants who are not certified at time of hire are eligible to receive a pay increase and be moved into the Certified, grade 7 role once certification has been obtained and 90 days of successful employment have been completed. All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. Certification is required for all new hires within 12 months of hire date. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have basic knowledge of aseptic techniques following universal standard precautions; and knowledge of operating room instrumentation, processing technique, and equipment care. This person must adhere to UK Healthcare policies and must be able to read and follow manufacturer guidelines. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Central sterile experience preferred; current CRCST certification highly preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a Certified Registered Central Service Technician (CRCST)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651795": {
      "title": "Grants Accounting Manager Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Grants Accounting Manager Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Grants Accounting Manager Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Grants Accounting Manager Senior Requisition Number RE56106 Working Title Department Name 3A600:Research Financial Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 47 Salary Range $58,302-96,179/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting and/or standing for long periods of time; performing repetitive motion tasks; effectively communicating with individuals from diverse backgrounds and varied professional levels. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm. As a professional supervisor position, additional time as needed to accomplish work goals and meet deadlines. Job Summary The University of Kentucky’s Research Financial Services team is seeking an experienced supervisor to serve as one of two managers leading the Financial Administration team. Each manager directly supervises approximately five Financial Administrators and is responsible for employee development, performance management, workload coordination, training, and operational leadership. Working within a shared supervisory model, the two managers collaborate closely to provide consistent leadership, guidance, and oversight across the Financial Administration team. They also partner with peer leaders throughout Research Financial Services to address operational challenges, promote consistent practices, maintain appropriate boundaries among functional areas, and support the timely and accurate submission of grant-level invoices and financial reports. This position does not maintain an assigned portfolio of sponsored projects. Instead, the manager provides day-to-day leadership and technical oversight for staff responsible for grant-level invoicing and financial reporting. As a primary resource for direct reports, the manager answers questions, interprets departmental policies and procedures, troubleshoots complex issues, monitors work quality and data integrity, supports month-end draw activities, and escalates matters outside Research Financial Services’ area of responsibility when appropriate. This position is well suited for individuals who enjoy mastering complex business processes, continuously expanding their knowledge, and applying what they learn to develop others and solve challenging operational problems. Successful candidates will develop and maintain expertise in the policies, procedures, business processes, and financial requirements governing the work performed by their teams. They are expected to become trusted resources for staff by providing practical guidance, supporting problem resolution, and promoting the consistent application of departmental expectations. Success in this role requires initiative, intellectual curiosity, sound judgment, and a commitment to continuous professional growth. While prior grants management experience is beneficial, candidates with supervisory experience in accounting, finance, compliance, auditing, healthcare administration, higher education, government, banking, or other complex operational environments are encouraged to apply. Candidates without direct grants management experience must demonstrate the ability to apply transferable leadership, analytical, and problem-solving skills to a specialized financial environment. The manager develops employees through structured training, ongoing feedback, mentoring, coaching, and career-development discussions. Responsibilities include assessing performance, supporting professional growth, evaluating readiness for advancement opportunities, recognizing achievement, fostering accountability, and addressing performance concerns through coaching and, when necessary, corrective action. Strong supervisory, communication, organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills are essential. Work Location Expectations This position requires regular onsite presence in Lexington, Kentucky. New hires should expect to work primarily onsite during the first 90 days to support onboarding, training, relationship-building, and development of role-specific expertise. Following successful completion of the onboarding period and demonstrated proficiency in the role, the position becomes eligible for a hybrid work arrangement consistent with university and departmental guidelines. Candidates should reside within a reasonable commuting distance of Lexington or be willing to relocate. This position is not eligible for a fully remote work arrangement. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Grants Administration, Supervision, Leadership, Employee Development, Coaching and Mentoring, Organization, Communication, Critical Thinking, Analytical Thinking, Problem Solving, Technical Aptitude, Team Building, Excel, SAP , Tableau Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 11/08/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which of the following best describes your experience in reviewing, interpreting and applying terms and conditions or policies and procedures related to grants management and/or areas within higher education? None More than 0, up to 1 year More than 1, up to 3 years More than 3, up to 5 years More than 5 years * Describe your level of proficiency utilizing various software packages and reporting tools to complete data analysis, generate reports, and/ or investigate areas of concern. Beginner Intermediate Advanced Expert * Please indicate the number of years of paid work experience during which you were responsible for providing training, presentations and/or formal coaching to others. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate your number of years of full-time paid supervisory experience. None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe a time when you helped an employee develop new skills, assume additional responsibilities, or prepare for advancement. How did you approach their development, and what was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about a time you were responsible for overseeing work in an area where you were not initially the technical expert. How did you build your knowledge, apply what you learned, and use that knowledge to support others? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651794": {
      "title": "Patient Clerical Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Patient Clerical Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Patient Clerical Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Patient Clerical Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE56105 Working Title PCA - 7.200.ICU Department Name H7000:Trauma and Acute Care Surgery Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 05 Salary Range $15.00-22.60/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements This position requires regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); intermittently standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds, and lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds. Also involves some exposure to risk of injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials, and exposure to loud noises, temperature extremes, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, cuts/punctures, blood-borne or airborne pathogens, and combative/violent people. Shift Must be able to work three 12.5-hour shifts per week (7:00 a.m. – 7:30 p.m.) Will also be required to work some weekends and holidays. Job Summary The Patient Clerical Assistant’s primary responsibility is to support patient care delivery by processing physician orders, maintaining patient records, managing patient information, and providing customer service. This involves working independently, acting as a communications liaison for patients, visitors, and all service departments involved in the care of the patient, as well as processing all requests/orders for patient care by fax/phone/computer/intercom and imprinters. Also includes filing, chart assembly and maintenance, maintaining patient records, and extensive verbal communication. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Basic administrative skills such as receptionist abilities (including phone, keyboarding, filing, and fax machine skills); knowledge of medical terminology; and interpersonal skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience High school diploma and at least one year of clerical experience within a medical setting preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of customer service experience do you have working with patients, doctors, nurses, etc.? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years * Have you ever worked in a very demanding or high volume clerical setting? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of medical terminology? Yes No * Rate your level of computer experience. Basic Moderate Advanced No computer experience Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
