    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651756": {
      "title": "Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences - Martin County",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences - Martin County Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences - Martin County Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences - Martin County Requisition Number RE55905 Working Title Department Name 81E06: KCES Region East Area 06 Work Location Inez, KY Grade Level 00 Salary Range Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education No set minimum requirements. Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No set minimum requirements. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Job-related travel including overnight stays; visiting clientele at sites throughout the county (including farms); standing/walking for long periods; handling of average-weight objects up to 25 lbs. Shift Monday-Friday (8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m.) with evenings and weekends as needed. Most weeks will exceed 40 hours. Job Summary Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences – Martin County. Location: Inez, KY The Extension Agent for Family and Consumer Sciences will develop, implement, and evaluate a plan of work based on locally identified needs which will lead to improved quality of living for families & individuals. Will plan and implement educational programs which focus on: 1) making healthy choices; 2) nurturing families; 3) embracing life as you age; 4) securing financial stability; 5) promoting healthy homes and communities; 6) accessing nutritious food; and 7) empowering community leaders. Will develop expertise and serve as a resource in family and consumer sciences programming areas including: food and nutrition; family resource management; human development and family relations; health, safety and wellness; leadership development; clothing and textiles; housing and the environment; home based and micro business. Will implement educational programs which strengthen families and individuals. Will develop and implement leadership programs such as Kentucky Extension Homemakers resulting in the development of personal and organizational leadership skills. All agents in a county will support the dissemination of useful and practical information on subjects relating to Agriculture, Family Consumer Sciences, 4-H and Community and Rural Development as outlined in the KRS statues 164.605 to 164.675. State law requires a national and state criminal background check and a letter from the Cabinet for Health and Family Services stating the employee is clear to hire based on no findings of substantiated child abuse or neglect found through a background check of child abuse and neglect records as a condition of employment or involvement in this program. Resume, cover letter and transcripts are required at time of application. Visit the Extension Careers page: https://ces-personnel.ca.uky.edu/careers Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated ability to communicate orally and in writing with groups and individuals and through mass media. Ability to use the computer for program delivery and management. Ability to visit clientele at sites throughout the county. Ability to plan and teach educational programs. Demonstrated leadership and ability to serve as a positive role model. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s Degree or Master’s Degree in the field of Family & Consumer Sciences such as: Family & Consumer Sciences Education; Family Sciences; Family Studies; Child and Family Studies; Early Childhood Education; Child Development; Dietetics; Nutrition or Human Nutrition; Community Food Services; Food Science; Merchandising, Apparel and Textiles; Hospitality, Management and Tourism; Retailing and Tourism Management; Community & Leadership Development; Consumer Economics and Family Financial Counseling; Health Promotions; Health, Society & Populations; Health Communications; Leadership for Community Education & Human Learning; Social Work; Marriage & Family Therapy; Human Health Sciences; Public Health; Health & Human Performance / Health Studies; or Nursing. Driver’s License preferred Deadline to Apply 11/03/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or expect to graduate within 6 months? yes no * What is your undergraduate GPA? Note: If you will receive your degree within 6 months, indicate your current GPA. If you have already completed a Master’s Degree please indicate that instead of your undergraduate GPA. Completed Master's 3.0-4.0 2.75-2.99 0- 2.74 * How many years of experience (paid or unpaid) do you have working in an FCS-related field? None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you or a family member serve as a member on any county Extension District Board in Kentucky?  If yes, please state the family member’s name and the county for which either you or this individual serves as a member of the Extension District Board. (Open Ended Question) * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK jobs, UK's online employment system (ukjobs.uky.edu) Newspaper Handshake Received an email about the posting Social Media Friend or Family Journal of Extension Indeed.com Other online job board Other * Were you previously a UK Cooperative Extension summer intern? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver’s license and are you able to drive? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651754": {
      "title": "Medical Laboratory Scientist/Cert/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Medical Laboratory Scientist/Cert/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Medical Laboratory Scientist/Cert/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Medical Laboratory Scientist/Cert/UKHC Requisition Number RE56102 Working Title Medical Laboratory Scientist-Certified (Core) Department Name H3200:Laboratory Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $27.00-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification American Society for Clinical Pathology ( ASCP ) certification must be obtained within 6 months from date of hire Physical Requirements Sitting and walking for long periods of time; repetitive motion; lifting, pushing, or pulling object up to 50 lbs. Shift Night Shift 7p-7a; Rotating weekends, holidays, and on-call as needed Job Summary The Medical Laboratory Scientist/Certified will be responsible for performing clinical laboratory testing in a fast-paced academic medical center. The Laboratory provides services to all aspects of this Level I trauma center and throughout the healthcare enterprise, including solid organ and bone marrow transplant, KY Children’s Hospital, and Markey Cancer Center. This position will be instrumental in maintaining a quality of service based on accuracy and timely result reporting. This position will be located in the Blood Bank, and testing will include, but is not limited to, type and screen, cross-matching, antibody workup, elution, absorption, antibody titering, neonatal workup, and component preparation. This CAP and AABB -Accredited Laboratory at the University of Kentucky showcases the use of state-of-the-art instrumentation and technology. IMPORTANT : Resumes and CVs cannot be substituted for a completed application. Incomplete applications could disqualify you from being considered for this position. To be considered for this position you must fully complete the online application being sure to only put one (1) job title for each entry (multiple job titles for one employer must have separate entries), the # of hours worked per week and your ending salary. All job titles and dates must correspond with those appearing on your resume. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Clinical Laboratory background, ability to work under pressure, to work independently and to work well with others; must have organizational and computer skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s Degree in Medical Technology/Clinical Laboratory Science or equivalent. MT/ MLS or equivalent certification. Previous Blood Bank experience Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you obtained or are you in the process of obtaining a bachelor’s degree in medical laboratory sciences? Yes No * If you are in the process of obtaining a bachelor’s degree in medical laboratory sciences, what is your anticipated graduation date? (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate your current licensure status. Currently hold MLS certification (ASCP or AMT) I am eligible to obtain MLS certification within 6 months I do not hold MLS certification and am not eligible to obtain within 6 months * Please choose the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience in a clinical laboratory setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651751": {
      "title": "Student: Campus Recreation Building Assistant Fall 2026",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Campus Recreation Building Assistant Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Campus Recreation Building Assistant Fall 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Campus Recreation Building Assistant Fall 2026 Requisition Number DU14947 Department Name 1B310:Campus Recreation Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12 / Hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Must be a current student at the University of Kentucky. Required Related Experience none Required License/Registration/Certification none Physical Requirements The position may require lifting or pushing objects up to 50lbs, or extended amounts of time walking or standing. Shift 2-3 hour shifts, during operation hours (Mon – Fri 5:30am – 12am, Sat 8:30am-9pm, Sun 10:30 – 12am) Job Summary Building Assistants are responsible for providing UK Students and the UK Community with quality customer service while providing information, controlling access, checking out equipment, and monitoring the fitness areas. Staff maintain a safe environment by actively supervising activities and enforcing facility policies. Staff are trained to respond to emergencies according to the outlined Emergency Action Plans. Building Assistants help to maintain a clean facility by completing routine cleaning, performing laundry duties, and completing other chores as assigned. This position is also Federal Work-Study eligible, if you qualify. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Policy enforcement, customer service, attention to detail, time management, initiative Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Building Assistants will serve as a first responder. CPR / AED /First Aid certifications are required for Building Assistants. Free certification classes will be available to all new employees who are not currently certified. Student employees are expected to maintain a current certification throughout their employment. Deadline to Apply 05/31/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure Would you be available to work early morning shifts starting at 5:45 a.m.? Yes No No Response Would you be available to work closing shifts that finish around 12:30am? Yes No No Response Are you available to work weekends? Yes No No Response To help us understand your availability for the applicable semester, please provide the specific times when you are NOT available to work. Our hours of operation are: Monday - Friday 6:00 a.m. to 12:00 a.m., Saturday 10:00 a.m. to 9:00 p.m., and Sunday 11:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. (EXAMPLE: 'I cannot work M/W/F 11:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. because I have class.') (Open Ended Question) * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No What is your overall GPA (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
