    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651742": {
      "title": "Dean Assistant/Academic Affairs",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Dean Assistant/Academic Affairs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Dean Assistant/Academic Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Dean Assistant/Academic Affairs Requisition Number RE56095 Working Title Assistant Dean of Academic Affairs Department Name 7N650:HEALTH SCIENCES - STUDENT SERVICES Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 48 Salary Range $64,210-105,914/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 6 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements sitting for long periods of time Shift Monday-Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm Job Summary Reporting to the College of Health Sciences ( CHS ) Vice Dean, the Assistant Dean of Academic Affairs is a senior leadership position within the College of Health Sciences and a member of the Dean’s executive leadership team. This position provides leadership for strategic planning, academic affairs administration, academic standards and progression processes, and operational initiatives through data-informed decision-making that support the growth and success of the College’s academic programs. Responsibilities include supporting academic policy administration and the consistent application of academic standards across the college, emphasizing professional and graduate programs; coordinating and/or supporting processes related to student progression, degree completion, and academic review; and providing oversight of key academic affairs operations. The Assistant Dean collaborates with faculty, staff, program leaders, and University partners to develop and implement strategies that support institutional priorities, enhance organizational effectiveness, and advance the College’s strategic goals. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Minimum of 5-7 years of experience in student affairs, enrollment management, or higher education administration, with a focus on graduate or professional students. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe a situation when you had to leverage your process improvement and strategic planning experience to complete a complex project. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience in providing leadership and coordination for academic operations, including advising workflows, academic calendars, milestone tracking, degree progress coordination, and student-facing academic processes in a University setting. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
