    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651741": {
      "title": "Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE55536 Working Title Specialty Dental Assistant Department Name MD100:DENTAL GROUP CLINICAL PRACTICE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $19.00-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Basic Life Support ( BLS ) at time of hire through the American Heart Association ( AHA ); must obtain Coronal Polishing, Dental X-ray, and IV Sedation competencies within 6 months of hire Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting, standing, walking, with some pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. Shift Depends on operational needs of the assigned clinic, generally this is Monday – Friday, Day Shift Job Summary The Specialty Dental Assistant provides clinical support for surgical and general dental procedures performed by faculty, residents, and students. This includes four-handed chairside assisting during pediatric and adult treatments such as orthodontics, restorative, endodontics, periodontics, prosthodontics, oral surgery, and implant placement. This position may also be on a rotation to assist in the operating room setting. Responsibilities include obtaining patient consent, reviewing medical histories, initiating IVs, drawing blood for PRF preparation, and setting up or breaking down operatories. The assistant monitors and documents vital signs during oral and IV sedation, administers medications under supervision, and assists during medical emergencies. Additional duties include passing instruments during procedures, delivering post-operative instructions, escorting patients after surgery, and managing clinical inventory and supply orders. The role also involves diagnostic tasks such as taking radiographs, impressions, and intraoral scans. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail and accuracy, excellent communication and customer service skills, dependability, communication, initiative Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Expanded duties certificate, Coronal polishing certificate, Experience assisting with sedation, and working in the operating room environment. Experience in working with patients with special needs. Knowledge of implant procedures is desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a current BLS (Basic Life Support) certification through the American Heart Association (AHA), or are you eligible to obtain this by date of hire? Yes No * Do you have current Coronal Polishing, Dental X-ray, and IV Sedation certificates, or are you eligible to obtain these 6 months of hire into the Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC job title? Yes No * Please indicate your paid employment experience in dental assisting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651737": {
      "title": "Business Development Center Director",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Business Development Center Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Business Development Center Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Business Development Center Director Requisition Number RE56098 Working Title State Director Department Name 81045:Small Business Development Center (SBDC) Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 00 Salary Range Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education See position qualifications/posting details Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience See position qualifications/posting details Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time. Travel. Shift Monday-Friday; 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM: and some evenings/weekends occasionally. Job Summary The Kentucky Small Business Development Center ( SBDC ) State Director is a dynamic statewide leadership role focused on advancing entrepreneurship, strengthening small businesses, and driving economic opportunity across the Commonwealth. The State Director provides executive leadership for the Kentucky SBDC network and translates its mission, vision, and strategy into impactful programs, services, and annual priorities. This position oversees network operations, program performance, and financial affairs; ensures compliance with applicable laws, regulations, federal grant requirements, national accreditation standards, and cooperative agreement terms; and serves as the U.S. Small Business Administration’s principal point of contact for the network. The State Director sets a clear vision for excellence, leads and develops a talented statewide team, stewards personnel and financial resources, expands and strengthens strategic partnerships and funding opportunities, and continually enhances the delivery of high-quality services to Kentucky’s entrepreneurs and small businesses. The successful candidate will foster a culture of integrity, accountability, collaboration, transparency, and high performance while positioning the Kentucky SBDC as a trusted and innovative resource for businesses throughout the Commonwealth. About the Role Provides executive leadership, oversight, and operational direction for the statewide Small Business Development Center ( SBDC ) in accordance with federal SBDC requirements and the cooperative agreement. The State Director dedicates not less than 75 percent of their time to the supervision and control of SBDC operations and is vested with the authority necessary to direct personnel, budgets, and expenditures. Leads the strategic and operational administration of the SBDC , working collaboratively with the University of Kentucky Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment, Cooperative Extension, other University units, public and private-sector partners, and the statewide SBDC service network to strengthen small-business development, entrepreneurship, and economic opportunity throughout Kentucky. Why Join Us At the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment, you’ll find a community that values collaboration, growth, and recognition. Benefits of joining our team include: Exceptional benefits package. A formal mentoring program to support your professional development Access to a staff development fund for continued learning and skill building Dedicated staff recognition programs that celebrate your contributions A shared commitment to making the University of Kentucky the University of, for, and with Kentucky Join us in shaping the future of teaching and learning—where innovation meets impact. For additional information about the SBDC please click here . To find out more about Martin-Gatton CAFE and how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky, Click Here . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated experience managing complex programs, multiple work units or a statewide network, including personnel, budgets, performance, and compliance responsibilities. Demonstrated ability to develop partnerships, negotiate agreements, secure resources, communicate with varied stakeholders, and exercise executive-level independent judgment. Proficiency with common productivity, financial, reporting, and management information systems. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Knowledge of the SBDC program, SBA cooperative agreements, federal grant administration, 2 CFR part 200, and SBDC accreditation standards. Experience leading a statewide, multi-site, university-hosted, public-service, economic-development, or entrepreneurship-support organization. Demonstrated success in fundraising, grant writing, financial stewardship, organizational improvement, and measurable economic-impact performance. Experience collaborating with universities, Cooperative Extension, government agencies, chambers of commerce, regional economic-development organizations, and private-sector partners. Nine years of relevant management, administrative, operational, grant-funded program, economic-development, or small-business development experience Deadline to Apply 11/12/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651732": {
      "title": "Amb/Retail Pharmacist/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Amb/Retail Pharmacist/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Amb/Retail Pharmacist/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist/UKHC Requisition Number RE56017 Working Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist/UKHC Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 14 Salary Range $55.20-75.03/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Pharmacist Physical Requirements This position requires intermittently sitting at a computer workstation; performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds; and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds. Also involves some risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job; and exposure to blood-borne or airborne pathogens, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, cuts/punctures, burns, and combative/violent people. Shift Primarily day with some early evening shifts which will include some weekend and holiday rotations. Coverage of shifts will be discussed during interview. Position supports multiple local UK HealthCare Retail Pharmacy locations which may include coverage at an off campus location. Hours, location, and days of the week subject to change based on the needs of the department for scheduling coverage. This is a full-time 40hr/week position. Job Summary Compounds and dispenses medications and pharmaceutical supplies upon receiving written orders from physicians. Reviews and interprets prescriptions and drug profiles to ensure appropriate drug therapy has been prescribed and ensures that drug interactions are considered. Contacts and confers with physicians and other practitioners to optimize drug therapy. Maintains inventory and records on narcotics and other forms of drugs. Participates in the routine supervision and training of technical staff related to daily operations of drug distribution. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires attention to detail; the ability to provide excellent customer service; reliability; punctuality; teamwork; and exceptional communication and interpersonal skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience PharmD and ambulatory/retail pharmacy experience preferred Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you licensed or eligible to be licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have practicing as a licensed pharmacist? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Briefly describe your pharmacy experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience in working with physicians, nurses, and pharmacists to secure Prior Authorizations. (Open Ended Question) * Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651731": {
      "title": "STEPS Animal Care Associate",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Animal Care Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Animal Care Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Animal Care Associate Requisition Number TE09419 Department Name 40832:Laboratory Animal Resources Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $16.15/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education High school diploma or GED Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification Physical Requirements Must be able to stand for long periods, ability to walk to various locations on campus in a timely manner. Requires heavy lifting, pushing or pulling of objects over 50 pounds; Able to work in hot, wet areas and wear personal protective clothing; animal handling (including carcasses); exposure to temperature extremes. Shift Monday – Friday; 7:00 am – 3:30 pm (40 hours per week) Job Summary The Division of Laboratory Animal Research seeks motivated individuals for a STEPS Animal Care Associate . After 6 months of satisfactory performance and training you may also be eligible for a full-time University of Kentucky staff position or continue as a STEP’s employee. After 12 months you have the potential to become certified as an Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician through AALAS , a membership association of professionals employed around the world in academia, government, and private industry who are dedicated to the humane care and treatment of laboratory animals, as well as the quality research that leads to scientific gains that benefit people and animals. You will be trained in routine and specialized animal caretaking duties, including: 1. Safe handling of multiple species of animals including: mice, rats, pigeons, dogs and non-human primates. 2. Feeding and watering animals according to their prescribed diets. 3. Changing cages, cleaning pens or runs 4. Observing animals regularly during the day, noting and reporting any variances in eating, drinking or deviation from normal habits. 5. Observing and reporting changes in environmental parameters (i.e., temperature, humidity, lighting, etc.). 6. Assisting in maintaining records of animals such as: weight, health, food consumption. You will also learn facility maintenance and sanitation procedures including: 1. Cleaning and sterilizing cages, equipment 2. Sanitizing supplies, animal rooms and procedure space 3. Operation and maintenance of washers and sterilizers to maintain proper working condition. 4. Efficient operational organization and flow of supplies and equipment throughout the facilities. 5. Assists in organizing feed, bedding and dry supplies in storage facilities Occasional mandatory overtime will be required to meet staffing needs and provide care and feeding of animals. *If you are interested in full time position that could lead to a potential career in laboratory animal care. Interested in Health Benefits? If working over 30 hours per week, on average, you will be eligible for medical/dental/vision plans offered at UK. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Microsoft office, basic computer skills. Ability to work independently, as well as part of a team is essential. Strong attention to detail. Oral and written communication skills also required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous animal care experience Deadline to Apply 10/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Rate your level of expertise in using Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Windows, Excel, and PowerPoint). None Basic Average Proficient Expert * Describe what \"teamwork\" means to you and how you function in an environment that fosters teamwork. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your ability to work independently, handling a large, varied and complex workload, including how you address challenges related to balancing attention to detail with working efficiently. (Open Ended Question) * The essential functions of this position will require you to push, pull or lift objects over 50lbs.  Can you meet this requirement with or without reasonable accommodations? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
