    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651724": {
      "title": "Athletics Analytics Intern",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Athletics Analytics Intern Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Athletics Analytics Intern Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Athletics Analytics Intern Requisition Number DU14746 Department Name 12F00:UKAA - Support Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range 15.00 hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Attending UK Required Related Experience Be familiar with Software packages, Excel and using Power BI, Power Automate, and Qualtrics. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements To be able to lift 10 lbs. Shift Days Job Summary The Athletics Analytics Intern in the Student Athlete Experience division will play a vital role in maintaining and improving our data systems to enhance the support to our student-athletes. The ideal candidate will be familiar with Excel and possess a strong willingness to learn tools like Power BI, Power Automate, and Qualtrics. The Data Management Intern will be able to clean, analyze, and visualize data, helping us make informed decisions that positively impact the student-athlete journey. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Proficiency in Microsoft Excel for data manipulation and basic analysis. Strong attention to detail, analytical mindset, and desire for working with data. Excellent communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively within a team. ·Willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies, such as Power BI, Power Automate, and Qualtrics. Basic understanding of data visualization concepts is a plus, but not required Prior experience with data cleaning, entry, or analysis is a plus, but not required. Adaptable problem-solving skills and a proactive positive attitude towards challenges. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
