    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651706": {
      "title": "Administrative Support Associate I",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Support Associate I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Support Associate I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Support Associate I Requisition Number RE56096 Working Title Opera Theatre Program Coordinator Department Name 8X200:Fine Arts -  Music Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Occasional lifting/pushing/pulling objects up to 50 pounds; standing/walking on campus and occasionally with objects up to 25 pounds; and sitting at computer workstation for extended periods. Shift Monday – Friday during normal business hours; and occasional night/weekend for special events. Job Summary The School of Music in the College of Fine Arts is seeking an organized and collaborative Administrative Support Associate I to provide administrative and operational support for UK Opera Theatre and the UK Choral Programs. Responsibilities include coordinating facility operations and space scheduling; supporting academic programs, choral recruitment, tours, purchasing, travel, and financial recordkeeping; supervising student employees and coordinating graduate assistants assigned non-teaching duties; assisting with productions, concerts, collaborative performances, special events, patron services, marketing, and audience engagement; and serving as a liaison to patrons, schools, community organizations, and other external partners. The University of Kentucky College of Fine Arts thrives by engaging individuals and communities with unique creative perspectives. The College fosters a supportive environment through artistic programming and curricula that reflect a broad range of experiences and voices. We believe the arts are essential to both individual and community life, and we actively promote creative expression among our faculty, staff, and students. We are committed to attracting skilled and passionate faculty, staff, and students who contribute meaningfully to the arts and academic excellence. As a member of the state’s flagship institution, the College promotes thoughtful engagement, respect, and collaboration. Visit our website: https://finearts.uky.edu/ Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Computer literate in MS Windows, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Driver’s license preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of paid administrative work experience do you have (i.e., responsible for administrative tasks such as scheduling, planning events, or other activities requiring organization and communication)? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please describe your experience with marketing, community building and customer relations None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe your experience with purchasing, coordinating travel, and financial recordkeeping. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651700": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator III",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Clinical Research Coordinator III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Clinical Research Coordinator III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinical Research Coordinator III Requisition Number RE56094 Working Title Department Name 7N800:COLLEGE OF HEALTH SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 47 Salary Range $58,302-96,179/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Ability to stand for periods of time, travel across campus for meetings, and lift up to 25 pounds. Also ability to work in a sedentary position utilizing computer, mouse, keyboard, and telephone for portions of the day. Shift Monday – Friday; 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary The Clinical Research Coordinator III will independently coordinate complex clinical and translational research studies within the College of Health Sciences and provide advanced clinical research operations expertise to investigators and research teams. The position will manage multiple concurrent human-subjects research protocols, including participant recruitment, screening, informed consent, study visits, longitudinal follow-up, regulatory documentation, research data systems, and coordination of procedures involving the Center for Clinical and Translational Science ( CCTS ), imaging, biospecimen collection, and other University research resources. As a senior member of the Office of Research and Scholarship, the Clinical Research Coordinator III will also assist investigators with study start-up and implementation, IRB and regulatory processes, REDCap development, quality assurance, recruitment planning, research project management, and development of standardized research procedures. The position will serve as an advanced resource for faculty and research teams and will train and mentor research personnel in clinical research operations and best practices. This position will also lead and coordinate Responsible Conduct of Research education and training for College faculty, staff, students, and trainees. The position will contribute to evaluation and continuous improvement of CHS research operations, including monitoring study activity, identifying recurring barriers to research implementation, and developing tools and processes that improve the efficiency and quality of research conducted across the College. The Clinical Research Coordinator III reports to the College of Health Sciences Associate Dean for Research. The ideal candidate will exhibit excellent research management and study coordination experience, strong organizational skills, professionalism and empathy in working directly with research participants, the ability to independently problem-solve complex situations, and excellent interpersonal and communication skills. The successful candidate must be able to explain technical, regulatory, and research ethics information clearly to participants, faculty, staff, students, and internal and external constituencies. The University of Kentucky College of Health Sciences has a strong strategic focus on translational research that advances movement, function, communication, and health across the lifespan, leading to scientific impact and improved health for the people of Kentucky and beyond. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience • Experience working in an academic medical center or CTSA -supported clinical research environment. • Experience coordinating studies involving invasive procedures such as muscle biopsy or venipuncture, or involving MRI or other imaging. • Experience supporting federally funded research, including NIH , DoD, NSF , HRSA , or other federal sponsors. • Experience developing or delivering Responsible Conduct of Research, research ethics, or compliance education. • Professional clinical research certification such as CCRC , CCRP , or CCRA . • Experience mentoring, training, or supervising research staff and students. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience and knowledge with clinical research and protocols. (Open Ended Question) * Please choose the answer that best describes your amount of paid, full-time experience working with IRBs, protocol submissions, informed consent, and other requirements to ensure regulatory compliance. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe a complex data project that you completed which included data collection, integration, management and/or analysis. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the option that most accurately reflects your level of paid, full-time experience in utilizing REDCap or similar data capture software. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1, up through 3 years More than 3, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651698": {
      "title": "Nurse Clinical/PRN Progressive Care Pool/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Clinical/PRN Progressive Care Pool/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Clinical/PRN Progressive Care Pool/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Clinical/PRN Progressive Care Pool/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number NR15130 Working Title Nurse Clinical/Progressive Care Pool/On-Call/UKHC Department Name H3270:Nursing Practice and Support Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $23.25-39.10/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education ADN Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Active Kentucky Registered Nurse (RN) license, Temporary Work Permit ( TWP ), Provisional License or active compact state Registered Nurse (RN) license that is in good standing and American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid for at least 6 months after employment date Physical Requirements The essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis and 25-50 pounds frequently; as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases, hazards of radiation, and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift 7PM – 730AM, some weekends and holidays required. Level 2 or Level 4 Agreement only; Level 2 agreement requires 144 hours/6week schedule. Level 4 agreements require 216 hours/6week schedule. Job Summary Progressive Care Per Diem pool will care for Progressive/Universal patients within the UK Healthcare Enterprise at both Samaritan and Chandler locations . Per diem pay is based on the number of shifts agreed to work—with highest pay provided for night shift / weekend coverage. The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing total, comprehensive, continuous and patient centered care which includes: assessing, documenting, planning, implementing, teaching, developing, and evaluating a comprehensive nursing plan of care; delivering direct patient care; ensuring patient satisfaction; training and delegating duties for Nursing Care Technicians (Nursing Assistant); and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. Furthermore, this environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the team of physicians to increase communication and enhance expected patient outcomes. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have the following: knowledge of Maslow’s eight Basic Human Needs and the priority within Gordon’s Functional Health Patterns Frame Work as well as Swanson’s Caring model; superb direct patient care and critical thinking skills; basic computer navigation skills and working knowledge of the internet; ability to communicate in a professional and respectful manner with patients and their families, co-workers and physicians; and strong organizational, prioritization, and delegation skill. The candidate will be highly motivated, pro-active and confident in advocating for patients and their family members. Will also enjoy working in a strong team environment and provides open, honest communication with fellow staff and physicians. In addition, the ideal candidate will possess exceptional technical skills and a proven ability to work in a team as well as independently. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BSN + AT LEAST 18 MONTHS OF PROGRESSIVE CARE RN EXPERIENCE Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above * Please describe you nursing experience in detail. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the number of years paid RN work experience when you were responsible for direct patient care in a Progressive Care unit. None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3, through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651694": {
      "title": "Nurse Clinical/PRN ICU Pool/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Clinical/PRN ICU Pool/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Clinical/PRN ICU Pool/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Clinical/PRN ICU Pool/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number NR15129 Working Title Nurse Clinical/PRN ICU Pool/On-Call/UKHC Department Name H3270:Nursing Practice and Support Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $23.25-39.10/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education ADN Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Active Kentucky Registered Nurse (RN) license, Temporary Work Permit ( TWP ), Provisional License or active compact state Registered Nurse (RN) license that is in good standing and American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid for at least 6 months after employment date Physical Requirements The essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis and 25-50 pounds frequently; as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases, hazards of radiation, and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift 7PM – 730AM, some weekends and holidays required. Level 2 or Level 4 Agreement only; Level 2 agreement requires 144 hours/6week schedule. Level 4 agreements require 216 hours/6week schedule. Job Summary Critical Care Per Diem pool will care for ICU patients within the UK Healthcare Enterprise at both Samaritan and Chandler locations . Per diem pay is based on the number of shifts agreed to work—with highest pay provided for night shift / weekend coverage. Pool pay based on levels. The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing total, comprehensive, continuous and patient centered care which includes: assessing, documenting, planning, implementing, teaching, developing, and evaluating a comprehensive nursing plan of care; delivering direct patient care; ensuring patient satisfaction; training and delegating duties for Nursing Care Technicians (Nursing Assistant); and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. Furthermore, this environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the team of physicians to increase communication and enhance expected patient outcomes. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have the following: knowledge of Maslow’s eight Basic Human Needs and the priority within Gordon’s Functional Health Patterns Frame Work as well as Swanson’s Caring model; superb direct patient care and critical thinking skills; basic computer navigation skills and working knowledge of the internet; ability to communicate in a professional and respectful manner with patients and their families, co-workers and physicians; and strong organizational, prioritization, and delegation skill. The candidate will be highly motivated, pro-active and confident in advocating for patients and their family members. Will also enjoy working in a strong team environment and provides open, honest communication with fellow staff and physicians. In addition, the ideal candidate will possess exceptional technical skills and a proven ability to work in a team as well as independently. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BSN + AT LEAST 18 MONTHS OF CRITICAL CARE / ICU RN EXPERIENCE PREFERRED . Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above * Do you currently have at least 18 months of Nursing experience in a Critical Care setting? Yes No * Please describe you nursing experience in detail. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
