    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651693": {
      "title": "Smart Campus Digital Media Intern",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Smart Campus Digital Media Intern Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Smart Campus Digital Media Intern Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Smart Campus Digital Media Intern Requisition Number DU15170 Department Name 3DH00:Auxiliary Services Administration Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $14.00/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High School Diploma or GED Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Must be able to lift and carry 25 pounds, stand for long periods, ability to walk to various locations in a timely manner, possibly outdoors and upstairs. Shift Varies; 7:30AM – 12AM; Sunday through Saturday; Requires night and weekend availability. Must have in-person availability Job Summary The Smart Campus initiative is seeking student interns for the Esports Program to create engaging content to appeal to both the University of Kentucky Campus and surrounding communities through a variety of mediums. Interns will provide marketing and general media support for esports lounge programming, events, opportunities, and services. These interns will be expected to: - Ideate and create content that markets programming from the UK Esports Lounge and draws attention through trends and interactive means - Attend various Esports Lounge events; taking photos and videos for event recap - Design both still and motion graphics adhering to UK Branding guidelines - Film, edit, and produce short- and long-form video content, coordinate streams, and other video mediums Applicants should have experience and/or particular interest in multiple of the following: - Photography/Videography - Web Development/Design - Graphic Design - Social Media - Podcasts/Streaming The ideal intern(s) will have an interest in social media, streaming, content creation, and/or editing. Applicants should have an innovative, problem-solving, and curious mindset. Interns will be expected to take initiative and work independently while also having a positive attitude and a collaborative spirit. Students seeking for an internship opportunity will need to complete the 150-internship hours. Students will be expected to work an average 15-hour work week. Students will have flexibility in work location but will also be given the opportunity to work in the cornerstone building. Please note-hiring officials have included an optional Writing Assignment in the applicant documents section, please feel free to upload any video or graphical content created in the past. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The individual should have excellent communication, organization, and research skills with the ability to follow department procedures/policies, work independently, and collaborate among peers. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 11/08/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Writing Sample 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651690": {
      "title": "Administrative Research Assistant Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Research Assistant Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Research Assistant Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Research Assistant Senior Requisition Number RE56093 Working Title Department Name 7K700:PHARMACY PRACTICE & SCIENCE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 42 Salary Range $17.76-28.43/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for extended periods of time; extensive computer use; lifting up to 10lbs Shift Monday–Friday (20 hours per week) with occasional night and/or weekend Job Summary The laboratory of Dr. Olufunmilola Abraham is seeking a part time (20 hours per week) Administrative Research Assistant Sr. The Administrative Research Assistant Sr will conduct experiments or interviews, collect and analyze data, and document results according to established protocols. They will assist in composing and organizing research reports and manuscripts to provide updates on unit objectives. Additionally, they will schedule logistics and secure resources for research supplies, equipment, and facilities. They will track supply and equipment inventory levels and place replenishment orders. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
