    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651683": {
      "title": "Medical Lab Technician/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Medical Lab Technician/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Medical Lab Technician/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Medical Lab Technician/UKHC Requisition Number RE56090 Working Title Medical Lab Technician - Lab Outreach Department Name H3200:Laboratory Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $20.52-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Regularly standing or walking with objects up to 10 lbs., repetitive motion and utilizing a computer for long periods of time. Ability to traverse campus to work at multiple locations. Shift Monday – Friday, day shift with some early morning and early evening hours. Possibility of on-call and overtime. Job Summary The Medical Lab Technician/ UKHC will be responsible for assisting in the pre-analytical support for a fast-paced academic medical center. The Laboratory provides services to all aspects of the Level I trauma center and throughout the healthcare enterprise, including solid organ and bone marrow transplant, KY Children’s Hospital, and Markey Cancer Center. This position is in the Central Processing/Receiving department within the Clinical Laboratory and the Processing/ Receiving Department with the Emergency Department Laboratory. The MLT will provide general laboratory receipt, processing, and throughput of patient specimens while adhering to HIPAA requirements. The MLT will also provide support to all other clinical laboratories within the Enterprise, as well as customer service for all internal and external customers. This is a team-oriented environment and a successful candidate will be able to problem-solve, troubleshoot, and multi-task. This CAP Accredited Laboratory at the University of Kentucky showcases the use of state-of-the-art instrumentation and technology. IMPORTANT : Resumes and CVs cannot be substituted for a completed application. Incomplete applications could disqualify you from being considered for this position. To be considered for this position you must fully complete the online application being sure to only put one (1) job title for each entry (multiple job titles for one employer must have separate entries), the # of hours worked per week and your ending salary. All job titles and dates must correspond with those appearing on your resume. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Phlebotomy, general computing, customer service, and critical thinking. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Associate’s 2-year degree or equivalent college credits preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of paid work experience do you have in phlebotomy? None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Please choose the answer that best describes your educational training. Associates degree MLT/MT Phlebotomist plus some college classes Bachelor's degree or higher * Please choose the answer that best describes your experience accessioning/processing laboratory specimens. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate the response that best describes your paid employment experience in a medical related field. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate your paid employment experience performing lab testing. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651682": {
      "title": "Grants Financial Analyst Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Grants Financial Analyst Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Grants Financial Analyst Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Grants Financial Analyst Senior Requisition Number RE56089 Working Title Department Name 3A600:Research Financial Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 45 Salary Range $48,214-79,560/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time. Shift Monday-Friday; 8:00 am-5:00 pm. Job Summary The Grants Financial Analyst Senior is responsible for identifying, tracking and pursuing payment on past due sponsored project accounts receivable in a fast-paced, dynamic environment. Completes collection efforts while ensuring positive relationships with sponsors and campus partners are maintained. Conducts research and utilizes award information to track down appropriate contacts for invoices and payment among various entity types. Also serves as backup for the Accountant Financial Analyst, Associate in the daily posting of sponsor payments, aiding them in research and application of complex payments as necessary. Ability to understand and interpret data in the financial system and award documentation regarding invoicing requirements necessary to success in position. Requires a self-motivated, tenacious, flexible and organized individual with an eye for detail and proven technical abilities utilizing excel to analyze and track data. Upon successful completion of training, this position is eligible for consideration of a hybrid work arrangement. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Accounting, Grants, Financial Analysis, SAP /S4 HANA , Excel, Tableau, Word Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Higher education and grants management experience; Technical reporting and analysis; Review and interpretation of legal agreements Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which of the following best describes your experience in Accounts Receivable Accounting and Collections? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please choose your years of paid full time work experience with payment application and balancing. None More than 0 up to 1 year More than 1 year up to 2 years More than 2 years up to 3 years More than 3 years * Describe a recent situation where you had to research and review information for the purpose of making a decision or recommendation. (Open Ended Question) * Provide a recent example that illustrates your ability to communicate effectively. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your level of proficiency utilizing various software packages and reporting tools to complete data analysis, generate reports, and/ or investigate areas of concern. None Beginner Intermediate Advanced Expert * Which of the following best describes your experience with juggling competing priorities, monitoring progress and successfully meeting deadlines? I manage competing priorities in my daily tasks I manage daily tasks as well as the occasional special project I manage daily tasks, special projects and occasional long term projects I routinely manage daily tasks, special projects and various long term projects Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651676": {
      "title": "Nurse Navigator/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Navigator/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Navigator/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Navigator/UKHC Requisition Number RE55980 Working Title Nurse Clinical/Ambulatory/UKHC Department Name M3030:Cancer Clinic Services Work Location Lexington, KY. Grade Level 11 Salary Range $71,087-95,056/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BSN Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Registered Nurse (RN) + approved advanced national nursing certification required within 2 years of hire date Physical Requirements Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds, or standing/walking and sitting for long periods of time. Shift Monday- Friday days Job Summary The Nurse Navigator will work with the patient and members of the clinical care team to help navigate their way to timely and quality care and to assist in overcoming any barriers to care. This will include, but is not limited to, connecting them to resources and information to make informed decisions, providing education and emotional support, and coordinating team communications. The NN will assist the patient from initial diagnosis through diagnostic testing, treatment, and follow-up or end-of-life care. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will possess working knowledge of electronic health records for inpatient/outpatient. Strong knowledge and experience with Microsoft Office applications is encouraged. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BSN+1 year of experience Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently licensed by the state of Kentucky as a Registered Nurse (RN) or eligible to obtain license by date of hire? Yes No * Are you aware that you will be required to obtain the advanced national nursing certification in area of expertise within 2 years of hire date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
