    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651630": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Laboratory Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Laboratory Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Laboratory Technician Requisition Number RE54311 Working Title Lab Tech Department Name 7H750:PHYSIOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Moving and lifting object from floor to above shoulders up to 25 pounds. Standing and sitting at computer terminals and laboratory bench completing repetitive tasks for extensive periods of time. Continuous working with materials requiring personal protective equipment in accord with EH&S policy. Shift Primarily Days Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm (some evenings and weekends are possible due to experimentation) Job Summary The laboratory of Dr. Timothy McClintock is looking for a Laboratory Technician to contribute to research on the neurobiology of the sense of smell, especially effects of interactions between odor molecules on odor detection and odor perception in humans, and to a lesser extent in mice. Responsibilities include organizing and administering odor perception tests, processing data, and performing data visualization using computational tools. Duties also include ordering lab supplies, and maintaining a small mouse colony. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Familiarity with personal computers and Microsoft Office. Some knowledge of lab skills like pipetting, making solutions and dilutions of solutions. Some coding experience desired but not required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience B.S. degree in a field of science, engineering, or math. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience working in a research laboratory? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience coding in R or Python? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a working sense of smell? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651629": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Laboratory Technician Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Laboratory Technician Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Laboratory Technician Senior Requisition Number RE55023 Working Title Lab Tech Sr. Department Name 7H750:PHYSIOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Moving and lifting object from floor to above shoulders up to 25 pounds. Standing and sitting at computer terminals and laboratory bench completing repetitive tasks for extensive periods of time. Continuous working with materials requiring personal protective equipment in accord with EH&S policy. Shift Primarily Days Monday – Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm, some evenings and weekends are possible due to experimentation. Job Summary Lab Technician Senior position to participate in studies of the genomics and physiology of the sense of smell and its relationship to dementia. Responsibilities include mouse husbandry, ordering supplies, organizational tasks, assisting with mouse surgeries and dissections, administering odor perception tests to human subjects, and performing other experiments. The successful applicant is expected to be highly organized, proficient in English, work well with others, and to have strong verbal and written communication skills. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Proficient and IACUC compliant small animal care; basic lab skills (e.g., pipetting); basic computer skills (e.g., MS word, excel, PowerPoint); strong oral and written communication skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BA/BS degree in a related field plus two or more years of paid working experience in a research laboratory preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your years of paid work (or volunteer research) experience in a biomedical research lab. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you have paid employment experience with molecular biology techniques? Yes No * Do you have experience coding in R or Python? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
