    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651603": {
      "title": "Section Head/KGS",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Section Head/KGS Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Section Head/KGS Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Section Head/KGS Requisition Number RE56084 Working Title Hydrogeology Team Lead and Facility Manager Department Name 40520:KY Geological Survey Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 50 Salary Range $83,283-141,565/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 6 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting or standing for long periods of time. Research field work required. Lifting, pushing, pulling, carrying objects up to 50 lbs. Shift Monday – Friday 8-5pm Job Summary Lead Groundwater Resources and Strategic Hydrogeology Programs for Kentucky’s Future The University of Kentucky is seeking a Water Resources Team Lead and Facility Manager to join the Kentucky Geological Survey ( KGS ). This position provides scientific, operational, and strategic leadership for hydrogeology research and water resource initiatives that support the Commonwealth of Kentucky. The role oversees research programs, supervises scientific staff, manages projects and resources, develops funding opportunities, and advances collaborative partnerships while ensuring high-quality scientific outcomes and public service. What You’ll Do Lead and conduct research in hydrogeology, hydrology, groundwater flow, fracture and granular aquifers, low-temperature geochemistry, near-surface geophysics, and remote sensing. Collect, analyze, interpret, and publish scientific data and present research findings at professional meetings, seminars, workshops, and conferences. Manage hydrogeology and regional research projects, including project planning, budgets, funded agreements, proposals, equipment, and associated operational processes. Identify emerging research needs and develop long-term strategies to advance hydrogeology and water resources programs. Pursue external funding opportunities and prepare competitive proposals that support program growth and scientific advancement. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with KGS , University of Kentucky, state agencies, federal agencies, and external partners. Supervise scientific staff, direct research activities, conduct performance evaluations, and support employee development and mentoring. Ensure research quality, integrity, and productivity through effective leadership, planning, and performance management. Support stakeholder engagement by providing scientific expertise, responding to public inquiries, and representing KGS as a trusted source of information. Contribute to KGS strategic initiatives and collaborate on the development of outward-facing scientific and educational materials. What You’ll Bring Advanced scientific knowledge and experience in hydrogeology and water resources research. Strong leadership, management, and staff development capabilities. Experience managing research programs, budgets, grants, contracts, and scientific equipment. Effective proposal writing, strategic planning, and program development skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including scientific publications and presentations. Ability to build collaborative relationships across disciplines, agencies, and stakeholder groups. Strong organizational, project management, and computer skills. Knowledge of research administration and institutional policies and procedures. Minimum Requirements Doctoral degree 6 years of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to lead impactful groundwater and hydrogeology research that benefits communities across Kentucky. Ability to shape long-term scientific programs and contribute to statewide water resource initiatives. Opportunities for professional growth through leadership development programs, scientific conferences, workshops, seminars, and professional engagement. Hybrid work eligibility with approval. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Internal Employee Being Considered Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
