    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651577": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Project Manager Requisition Number RE56083 Working Title Community Intervention Program Manager Department Name 7P210:KY INJURY PREV & RESEARCH CTR Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 46 Salary Range $53,061-87,526/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time Shift Primarily days, Monday-Friday: between the hours of 8:00 am and 5:00 pm, additional hours as needed Job Summary Lead Community-Based Overdose Prevention Programs Across Kentucky The University of Kentucky is seeking a Community Intervention Program Manager to join the Kentucky Injury Prevention and Research Center ( KIPRC ) . This position manages community intervention activities supported by Kentucky’s Overdose Data to Action (OD2A) grant, working closely with local and district health departments, recovery community centers, and other partners. The role combines program management, evaluation, staff supervision, and compliance to strengthen overdose prevention efforts and meet CDC grant and reporting requirements. What You’ll Do Manage the development, implementation, and maintenance of community drug overdose prevention programs with local and district health departments and recovery community centers across Kentucky. Coordinate scopes of work, grant budget narratives, grant revisions, consultant agreements, invoices, program data, and other activities required to support OD2A-funded programs. Supervise and coach OD2A-funded navigator staff and provide guidance on systems and processes for accurate and timely program reporting. Develop and maintain IRB protocols and modifications and oversee adherence to ethical research practices and applicable grant requirements. Collaborate with community partners to develop evaluation plans and tools, including surveys, intake forms, and qualitative interviews, and analyze data to assess program activities. Disseminate evaluation findings to community and grant partners and collaborate with KIPRC faculty and staff and state and local public health partners to support CDC reporting and program sustainability efforts. Review community partner reports and outputs for alignment with CDC priorities, guidance, and reporting requirements. Collaborate with Principal Investigators, program managers, evaluators, and project staff to develop reports for the CDC , University of Kentucky leadership, and other stakeholders. Enforce applicable university policies, procedures, grant protocols, and CDC guidance across project activities. What You’ll Bring Strong leadership, problem-solving, multitasking, and time management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to build relationships and engage effectively with community, public health, and grant stakeholders. Knowledge of quantitative and qualitative evaluation methods and processes. Experience with data management, ethical research procedures, IRB protocols, and compliance requirements. Ability to manage community partnerships, reporting processes, and multiple program priorities. Minimum Requirements Master’s degree 4 years of related experience What’s In It for You The opportunity to help communities across Kentucky develop and strengthen programs focused on preventing drug overdose. Meaningful collaboration with local and district health departments, recovery community centers, public health partners, and KIPRC research teams. Hybrid work eligibility, with approval. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? Community-based overdose prevention programs depend on strong partnerships, reliable data, effective evaluation, and consistent grant oversight. This role helps connect those elements by supporting funded community partners from program development through evaluation and reporting. By managing OD2A-funded initiatives and strengthening coordination among community, public health, research, and grant partners, the Community Intervention Program Manager will help ensure prevention programs meet CDC requirements while generating information that can guide program improvement and sustainability. Internal Employee Being Considered Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Proficiency with Microsoft Office and evaluation software (i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Dedoose) is essential. Proficiency in SPSS , SAS or other statistical software is preferred. Knowledge of evaluation theories and principles is preferred in order to formulate hypotheses regarding health status and health outcomes and to conduct analyses and interpret data. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Master’s degree in education, public health, sociology, industrial psychology, public administrations, or another related field. At least 3 years of relevant work experience in program management in the field of research and/or evaluation is required. Driver’s License preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your program or project management experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your project evaluation experience including evaluation methods you have utilized for program evaluation. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience working with community partners. (Open Ended Question) * What is your preferred method to engage with stakeholders in evaluation? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651575": {
      "title": "Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE56082 Working Title Patient Relations Assistant Department Name M3030:Cancer Clinic Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3.5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motion (such as typing); walking including pushing, pulling, and/or lifting up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. The conditions of work may involve regular exposure to loud noises, intermittent exposure to blood borne/airborne pathogens and combative/violent people, and occasional exposure to cuts and punctures. Shift Days, 8:00 am-5:00 pm, Monday-Friday, and other days and hours as needed. Job Summary The Patient Relations Assistant is a first-line customer service representative for the Comprehensive Breast Care Center. This position will be responsible for respectfully acknowledging, greeting patients, and answering phones according to established guidelines. Other duties include: proactively identifying opportunities to provide a positive patient experience by anticipating patients’ needs (eg. provide directions/way finding), monitoring wait times for individual patients, communicating appropriate techniques such as “blameless apology” to manage patient wait time expectations. In addition, this position will be responsible for resolving patient complaints in an empathetic and timely manner, collaborating with teammates and leadership to prevent and resolve service failure process problems, and ensuring proficient patient registration. The Patient Relations Assistant also uses electronic tools to ensure patient insurance eligibility, and recognizes and provides initial resolution of errors in computer system. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have extensive customer service experience and able to communicate in a calm and helpful manner during stressful and/or crisis situations. Should have the ability to pay high attention to detail; work with a teamwork mindset; have data entry skills and respect for confidentiality; be able to prioritize tasks efficiently; and work in multiple systems simultaneously. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience High School diploma plus four or more years related experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your years of paid work experience in customer service. None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1, through 3 years More than 3 years * Please describe a situation when you delivered exceptional customer service to resolve a patient or physician complaint. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with customer service in an academic or other professional setting where it was necessary to deal with the public by phone and/or in-person? Yes No * Please indicate your paid employment experience with UK systems (APM, SCM and/or PM). None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Please choose the answer that best describes your amount of paid employment experience working with oncology patients. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
