    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651565": {
      "title": "Data Analyst II",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Data Analyst II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Data Analyst II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Data Analyst II Requisition Number RE56080 Working Title Department Name 7P275:Public Health Analytics and Informatics Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 44 Salary Range $44,678-71,469/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting and/or standing for long periods of time; performing repetitive motion tasks; lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs Shift Monday – Friday Between the hours of 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as needed Job Summary Turn Data into Clear, Actionable Insight The University of Kentucky is seeking a Data Analyst II to join the Public Health Analytics and Informatics department. This role supports organizational reporting, business intelligence, and data-driven decision-making by developing and maintaining dashboards, reports, and data visualizations. Working with business and technical stakeholders, the Data Analyst II will analyze and prepare data, translate reporting needs into effective solutions, and help ensure information is accurate, understandable, and useful. What You’ll Do Develop, maintain, and enhance dashboards, reports, and interactive visualizations using Tableau, Power BI, and other business intelligence and data visualization tools. Analyze data from multiple sources to identify trends, patterns, relationships, discrepancies, and other information relevant to organizational needs. Develop recurring and ad hoc reports, interpret analytical results, and communicate findings to technical and non-technical stakeholders. Use SQL and other data-access tools to retrieve, combine, filter, aggregate, and prepare data for reporting, visualization, and analysis. Validate reporting results against source systems and business rules, investigate discrepancies, and help resolve data-quality issues. Collaborate with business users, analysts, and technical staff to gather requirements and translate business questions into effective analytical and visualization solutions. Support and troubleshoot existing dashboards, reports, data sources, and scheduled refreshes, and assist users in effectively using reporting resources. Document and test dashboards, reports, SQL queries, calculations, data sources, and business rules while identifying opportunities for continuous improvement. What You’ll Bring Experience developing reports, dashboards, or data visualizations. Experience with data analysis, reporting, business intelligence, or a related area. Working knowledge of SQL and relational database concepts. Strong analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work independently on assigned projects and collaborate effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders. Minimum Requirements Master’s degree 2 years of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to work with business intelligence and data visualization technologies, including Tableau and Power BI, while continuing to build analytical and reporting expertise. Fully remote work eligibility with approval. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? Clear, accurate reporting helps organizations make informed operational and management decisions. This position strengthens that capability by connecting business needs with reliable data, thoughtful analysis, and reporting solutions that make information easier to understand and use. With its focus on business intelligence, data visualization, SQL , and stakeholder collaboration, the Data Analyst II helps turn data from multiple sources into practical insights while supporting the accuracy, usability, and continuous improvement of reporting resources. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Understanding of effective data visualization principles, including chart selection, dashboard design, usability, and accessibility. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Experience developing dashboards, reports, and visualizations using Tableau, Microsoft Power BI, or similar business intelligence and data visualization platforms. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of professional experience do you have developing dashboards, reports, or data visualizations using business intelligence tools? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years * Which business intelligence or data visualization tools have you used professionally? (Select all that apply.) None Tableau Power BI Other business intelligence/data visualization tools * How would you describe your professional experience using SQL to retrieve, join, filter, aggregate, or prepare data for reporting and analysis? None Limited experience Working proficiency Advanced proficiency * Do you have professional experience validating report or dashboard results against source data and investigating data discrepancies? Yes No * Do you have experience working directly with business users or stakeholders to gather reporting requirements and translate those requirements into dashboards, reports, or analytical solutions? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651559": {
      "title": "Nurse Clinical/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Clinical/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Clinical/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Clinical/UKHC Requisition Number NR15381 Working Title RN/Interventional Radiology Department Name H3185:Interventional Radiology Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $28.00-39.10/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education ADN Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Active Kentucky Registered Nurse (RN) license, Temporary Work Permit ( TWP ), Provisional License or active compact state Registered Nurse (RN) license that is in good standing and American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid for at least 6 months after employment date Physical Requirements The essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis and 25-50 pounds frequently; as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases, hazards of radiation, and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift Must be able to work three, 12-hour shifts (with rotating start times of 6am, 7am, and 8am) per week; will also be required to work some weekend and holidays. Job Summary The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing total, comprehensive, continuous and patient centered care which includes: assessing, documenting, planning, implementing, teaching, developing, and evaluating a comprehensive nursing plan of care; delivering direct patient care; ensuring patient satisfaction; training and delegating duties for Nursing Care Technicians (Nursing Assistant); and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. Furthermore, this environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the team of physicians to increase communication and enhance expected patient outcomes. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have the following: knowledge of Maslow’s eight Basic Human Needs and the priority within Gordon’s Functional Health Patterns Frame Work as well as Swanson’s Caring model; superb direct patient care and critical thinking skills; basic computer navigation skills and working knowledge of the internet; ability to communicate in a professional and respectful manner with patients and their families, co-workers and physicians; and strong organizational, prioritization, and delegation skill. The candidate will be highly motivated, pro-active and confident in advocating for patients and their family members. Will also enjoy working in a strong team environment and provides open, honest communication with fellow staff and physicians. In addition, the ideal candidate will possess exceptional technical skills and a proven ability to work in a team as well as independently. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BSN + AT LEAST 1 YEAR OF RN EXPERIENCE PREFERRED Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651554": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Dental Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Dental Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Dental Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE56079 Working Title Dental Therapist Senior – UK North Fork Valley Dental Clinic Department Name MG150: Medical Group-NFV Work Location Hazard, KY Grade Level 07 Salary Range $17.50-27.31/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Basic Life Support ( BLS ) at time of hire through the American Heart Association ( AHA ); must obtain Coronal Polishing and Dental X-ray competencies within 6 months of hire. Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time with repetive motion. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift; typically 8:00 am – 4:30 pm (40 hrs/wk) Job Summary This position is located off-campus in Hazard, KY at UKHC North Fork Valley Dental Clinic. The Dental Therapist Senior will assist the dentist in 4-handed dentistry during dental procedures. Will chart for the dentist in an electronic dental record. Will set up and break down dental operatories and properly disinfect. Will chart for the dentist in an electronic record and obtain patient medical info, vitals, prescribed digital radio graphs and help with overall patient flow. Will place sealants, temporary restorations, composites and amalgams with minimal adjustment by the dentist. Will pack cord, take opposing impressions, bite registration, fabricate temporary crowns and bridge work and pour and trim diagnostic models. Will be responsible for dental clinic equipment maintenance and keeping accurate and up-to-date logbooks including daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual tasks. Please attach any relevant Dental Assistant certificates or certifications as a PDF under Specific Request 1. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Four handed dentistry, multi-tasking oriented, dependability, attention to detail, ability to work with children of all ages. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Technical/Skills Training + 3 years experience Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you aware that this position is located in Hazard, KY? Yes No * Have you ever worked in a clinical setting before? Yes No * Do you have a Dental Assistant Radiology certificate? Yes No * Do you have a Dental Assistant Coronal Polishing certificate? Yes No * Have you completed an Expanded Duties Dental Assistant (EDDA) training program? Yes No * How many years of paid work experience do you have as a dental assistant? None More than 0 years, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 7 years More than 7 years * Please describe your paid employment experience working in a Dental office. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
