    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651551": {
      "title": "Optician Apprentice/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Optician Apprentice/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Optician Apprentice/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Optician Apprentice/UKHC Requisition Number RE56078 Working Title Optician Apprentice - Shriners Optical Shop Department Name MG100: Physician Based Clinics Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Ability to stand or sit for periods of time, occasional lifting of boxes up to 25 pounds. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift; 8:00am – 5:00pm (40 hrs/wk). Job Summary UK Advanced Eye Care is seeking an Apprentice Optician to join our team. The successful candidate should be prepared to work 40 hours per week, Monday through Friday. Our patients expect exceptional customer service and attention to detail. It is of utmost importance to communicate effectively and in a pleasant manner with patients and customers to provide excellent customer service. The position is expected to meet monthly sales targets. Experience in retail optical settings is preferred. Must be willing to apply for an optician apprenticeship and be trained by a licensed optician. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong customer service and the ability to learn software programs and use them effectively, MS Windows, Excel, Outlook, Word. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Optical retail sales preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your retail sales experience. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have basic computer skills (i.e Word, Excel, PowerPoint)? Yes No * Please describe a time when you provided exceptional customer service and include specific details regarding the situation. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
