    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651545": {
      "title": "Practice Manager I/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Practice Manager I/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Practice Manager I/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Practice Manager I/UKHC Requisition Number RE56076 Working Title Practice Manager I – Vascular Interventional Radiology Clinic Department Name M1200:Community Management Practice Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $48,360-81,328/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting, standing, walking, with some pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift; primarily 8:00am – 5:00pm (40 hrs/wk); other hours/schedule as needed. Job Summary The primary responsibilities of the Practice Manager I/ UKHC are to direct the clinic’s business, technical, and nursing support activities. This individual is responsible for the successful management of all assigned clinics. In conjunction with the Ambulatory Operations Director, they oversee administrative functions including operations, marketing, facilities, revenue cycle, human resources, planning and development. The Practice Manager I/ UKHC will implement adjustments to the clinic operation that will support enterprise-wide initiatives. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities none Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience none Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of paid employment experience do you have in clinic operations? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 yearsm More than 5 years * Please choose the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience with staff supervision. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be