    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651517": {
      "title": "Nuc Med Tech/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nuc Med Tech/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nuc Med Tech/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nuc Med Tech/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number DU13506 Department Name H3186: Nuclear Medicine Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $43-$59/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education Associates Degree Required Related Experience 1 year of experience Required License/Registration/Certification Temporary license required at time of hire, with official Nuclear Medicine registry obtained within 1 year of hire if not already completed; KY State Radiation License at time of hire; Basic Life Support certification via AHA within 90 days of hire Physical Requirements Lifting and pulling weight greater than 50 pounds. This position requires the ability to walk/commute to different areas within medical campus. Shift Shift opportunities will be discussed during the interview process. Depending on level, employees must work a minimum of 96 to 216 hours in a 6-week period. Job Summary This position’s primary focus is to complete a Nuclear Medicine procedure/therapy in a safe, efficient manner according to departmental, hospital, state, and federal guidelines. An experienced Nuclear Technologist is necessary to manage patient throughput, quality control, inventory, equipment evaluation and calibration, billing accuracy and regulatory compliance. This position will be responsible for executing diagnostic studies and interventional procedures by following unit policies/procedures for radiation safety, patient safety, radiopharmaceutical administration, QA, and imaging. Per diem pay is as follows: Level I – 96 hours any shift / 6-week schedule = $43/hour Level II – 144 hours any shift / 6-week schedule = $51/hour Level III – 216 hours any shift / 6-week week schedule = $59/hour Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 11/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a diploma, associates degree or higher in radiology and/or nuclear medicine? Yes No * Please indicate the number of years of paid, full-time employment experience you have as a Nuclear Medicine Technician. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years Do you have a Kentucky State Radiation Operators License or eligible to obtain this license by date of hire? Yes No Are you a Registered Nuclear Medicine Technologist? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651516": {
      "title": "Nuclear Medicine Tech/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nuclear Medicine Tech/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nuclear Medicine Tech/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nuclear Medicine Tech/UKHC Requisition Number RE55742 Working Title Nuclear Medicine Tech Department Name H3186: Nuclear Medicine Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $35.34-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Temporary license required at time of hire, with official Nuclear Medicine registry obtained within 1 year of hire if not already completed; KY State Radiation License at time of hire; Basic Life Support certification via AHA within 90 days of hire. Physical Requirements This position requires sitting, standing, and/or walking for extended periods of time. Lifting and positioning patients may also be required. Shift Flexible day shift Monday through Friday between the hours of 6:30 am – 5:00 pm. Rotational on-call is required Job Summary This position’s primary focus is to complete a Nuclear Medicine procedure/therapy in a safe, efficient manner according to departmental, hospital, state, and federal guidelines. An experienced Nuclear Technologist is necessary to manage patient throughput, quality control, inventory, equipment evaluation and calibration, billing accuracy and regulatory compliance. This position will be responsible for executing diagnostic studies and interventional procedures by following unit policies/procedures for radiation safety, patient safety, radiopharmaceutical administration, QA, and imaging. New Starting Pay Rate – The starting pay for this position was recently adjusted based on current demand for this role. The minimum hourly rate for this position will now be $ 35.34/hour. All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have effective communication, strong attention to detail, analytical thinking, customer service excellence, a willingness to learn new skills, and technological proficiency. Key strengths include problem-solving, teamwork and collaboration, customer service, clear verbal and written communication, and a proactive approach. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Degree from an accredited Nuclear Medicine Program with training in Nuclear Medicine and PET /CT preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you board certified in nuclear medicine or will be by your start date? Yes No * Please indicate the number of years of paid, full-time employment experience you have as a Nuclear Medicine Technician. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Do you have a diploma/certificate, associates degree or higher in radiology and/or nuclear medicine? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651515": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer Outreach/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Athletic Trainer Outreach/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Athletic Trainer Outreach/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Athletic Trainer Outreach/UKHC Requisition Number RE54596 Working Title Athletic Trainer Outreach Department Name MG380: Orthopaedic Surgery Work Location Frankfort, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $48,360-81,328/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 0 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Athletic Trainer Certification Physical Requirements Repetitive motion. Job-related travel. Standing or walking with objects up to 10lbs. Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs. Shift This role requires a flexible schedule based on athletic event demands. Work hours will include weekdays, evenings, and weekends depending on practice schedules, games, and special events. Some travel to away games and tournaments will be required. Job Summary UK HealthCare Sports Medicine is seeking a dedicated and dynamic Athletic Trainer. Your primary focus will be the daily medical coverage, injury prevention, assessment, rehabilitation, and return-to-play planning for athletes within the university’s athletics system. You’ll act as a liaison between players, coaches, and healthcare professionals to ensure the health, safety, and well-being of athletes. Additional duties include: Managing medical documentation and injury tracking. Coordinating with UK HealthCare’s physicians and rehabilitation specialists for athlete referrals. Assisting with emergency planning and response protocols at training and match facilities. Promoting education and awareness regarding injury prevention and performance optimization. Supporting event coverage and medical operations for events and teams as needed. We are looking for a candidate who excels in communication, adaptability, and relationship-building, with the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, team-oriented, and evolving sports environment. Benefits: Tuition waiver for employees attending the University of Kentucky, up to $5,250 per year. Access to Professional Development Funding for continuing education and certifications. Paid Kentucky Medical Licensure and BOC Certificate Maintenance Fees. Comprehensive employee insurance benefits, including Health, Dental, Vision, Prescription Drug coverage, and Flexible Spending Accounts ( FSA ). 200% employer match on retirement contributions. Accrual of 10-15 vacation days per year, increasing with years of service. Accrual of 12 sick days per year. Accrual of 13 paid holidays annually. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong understanding of sports injury prevention, evaluation, and rehabilitation techniques. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with athletes, coaches, and families. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Proficient in EMR documentation and basic administrative tasks. Commitment to continuing education and evidence-based clinical practice. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training required; Master’s degree preferred. National Athletic Trainers Association Board of Certification ( NATA BOC ) Required. Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure ( KBML ) Licensure or eligibility at time of hire. Experience working with collegiate athletes. Prior outreach/field-based AT experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently certified by the National Athletic Trainers Association (NATA) and licensed in the state of Kentucky, or eligible to obtain this licensure by date of hire? Yes No * Describe your experience working in a Sports Medicine clinic. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
