      "title": "Capital Project Management Interior Design Student Worker",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Capital Project Management Interior Design Student Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Capital Project Management Interior Design Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Capital Project Management Interior Design Student Worker Requisition Number DU15168 Department Name 3CC00:Capital Project Management Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range 15.55 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education HS Required Related Experience na Required License/Registration/Certification na Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 lbs., sitting for long periods of time, Shift Days Job Summary The position will be responsible for assisting the two UK Interior Designers 20 hours per week. Duties to include design resource library management, space planning, finish selections, furniture selections, meeting with customers, meeting with industry representatives, research new products. The position is also responsible for deliveries that need to be mad for Capital Project Management Division. Computer skills to include Auto CAD , Sketch Up, Photo Shop, Revit, Excel and Microsoft Word. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University 