    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651499": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Charging Coordinator/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Charging Coordinator/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Charging Coordinator/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Charging Coordinator/UKHC Requisition Number RE56073 Working Title Pharmacy Charging Coordinator/UKHC Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $48,360-81,328/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Nationally certified Pharmacy Technician by either PTCB ( PTCE ) or NHA (ExCPT); Registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire. Physical Requirements This position may include sitting at a computer work station for extended periods of time utilizing repetitive motions, may require standing for extended periods of time, and may require the ability to lift up to 25 pounds. Shift Primarily Monday thru Friday; 8 a- 4:30p. This is a remote position. Job Summary This position has split responsibilities for both drug charging integrity and drug pricing contract integrity for UK Healthcare Pharmacy services across UK Chandler, Good Samaritan, King’s Daughter, and St. Claire hospitals. For drug charge integrity, the position ensures accurate and compliant billing by maintaining alignment between medication administration, pharmaceutical supply utilization, and associated patient charges. Responsibilities include monitoring charging workflows, identifying discrepancies, and collaborating with operational and clinical teams to maintain revenue integrity For drug pricing contract integrity, the position oversees the accuracy of pharmaceutical pricing agreements by monitoring alignment between contracted prices, purchasing systems, and supplier invoices. Responsibilities include identifying pricing discrepancies, recovering overcharges from vendors, validating contract compliance, and ensuring accurate contract configuration within ordering and procurement systems. This position requires prior computer knowledge and multi-system knowledge, including Epic, wholesaler interfaces, Pyxis system, and SAP . Pharmacy expertise with drug or supply chain ordering, pharmacy billing, drug coding, CMS coverage guidelines, and drug knowledge to comprehend clinical documentation and interpret dosage requirements to ensure accuracy of pharmaceutical billing is also required for quality control assurance. This position is also responsible for processing invoices and working with UKHC accounting for proper vendor payment. In addition to daily duties, projects of varying time horizons will be assigned as needed. For questions regarding this position, please contact the supervisor, Felix W. Lam , at f.lam@uky.edu . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Experience utilizing the following: Cardinal Order Express, Epic, SAP , Pyxis Software, Microsoft Suite of Products. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Pharmacy Technician experience, medical and/or pharmacy billing experience highly preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a National Pharm Tech Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician or eligible to obtain by date of hire? Yes No * Please indicate the amount of paid pharmacy technician experience you have working in either an inpatient hospital and/or retail pharmacy setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate the amount of paid work experience you have in pharmacy and/or medical billing. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651496": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Requisition Number RE56072 Working Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC - ELIGIBLE FOR RECRUITMENT BONUS Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 07 Salary Range $18.50-27.31/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Nationally certified Pharmacy Technician by either PTCB ( PTCE ) or NHA (ExCPT); Registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire. Physical Requirements This position requires use of a computer workstation, completion of tasks with repetitive motions, and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 50 pounds. This position may require personnel to wear personal protective equipment to reduce risk of exposure to work-related hazards (e.g. handling of hazardous medications). Shift Primarily Monday through Friday; 7:30am – 5:00pm with some holidays possibly required. Hours and days of week are subject to change based on the needs of the service line. Remote schedule option available Job Summary This position will provide a variety of specialty pharmacy services including obtaining prior authorizations, enrolling patients’ in financial support programs, and coordinating first time dispenses and refills for specialty medications prescribed within UK HealthCare. You will work closely with nurses, physicians, and UK Specialty Pharmacy staff to improve access to medications for a variety of sub specialty disease states. This position is eligible for a recruitment bonus. Additional details will be provided during the hiring process should your application be selected to move forward. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital/retail pharmacy technician and/or healthcare customer service experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a National Pharm Tech Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician? Yes No * Please indicate the amount of paid pharmacy technician experience you have working in either an inpatient hospital and/or retail pharmacy setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
