    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651466": {
      "title": "APP Emergency Medicine Nights/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | APP Emergency Medicine Nights/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support APP Emergency Medicine Nights/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title APP Emergency Medicine Nights/UKHC Requisition Number RE56064 Working Title Department Name MG305: Emergency Medicine Work Location Lexington, KY. Grade Level 15 Salary Range $132,600-185,848/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MSN for Nurse Practitioners or BS for Physician Assistants Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr or currently completing a formal Emergency Medicine residency program. Required License/Registration/Certification Advanced Practice Registered Nurse ( APRN ) with Family Nurse Practitioner ( FNP ) certification and either enrollment or start in Acute Care Nurse Practitioner ( ACNP ) post master’s program within the first year of hire or obtain Emergency Nurse Practitioner Certification ( ENP -BC) as soon as eligible or Physician Assistant-Certified (PA-C) Physical Requirements Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds, or standing/walking for long periods of time. Shift Provide ambulatory, emergency, and urgent patient care durig 4, 10-hr night shift sessions Job Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at the University of Kentucky is currently seeking an Advanced Practice Provider to function as a Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant. This is a nights only position and will primarily provide clinical coverage and patient care in the Emergency Department. This position will improve the capacity of the clinical practice, provide enhanced monitoring of clinically complex patients, and contribute to excellence in patient care and patient satisfaction. Duties for this position include direct patient care, patient and family education, support to fast track and physician in the triage system, and serving as a critical member of the clinical care team. This includes obtaining patient health histories, reviewing outside records, and performing complete physical examinations. It also includes documenting findings and noting pertinent normal and abnormal findings. In addition, this position orders and interprets appropriate diagnostic and laboratory tests and performs approved therapeutic or diagnostic procedures based on patients’ clinical status. Patient education will also be an essential function, and this position will be required to explain the necessity, preparation, nature, and anticipated effects of therapy to patients, patients’ families, staff, and healthcare learners. In addition, this position will serve as a role model for advanced practice professional providers through conduct, appearance, communication, mutual respect, leadership, ethical decision-making, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniform