    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651465": {
      "title": "STEPS Facilities Multi-Trades Worker",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Facilities Multi-Trades Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Facilities Multi-Trades Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Facilities Multi-Trades Worker Requisition Number TE09548 Department Name 81270:Research Farms Work Location Versailles, KY Salary Range $17.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education Required Related Experience Required License/Registration/Certification Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to and possibly over 50lbs; Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs. May be exposed to loud noises, fumes, confined spaces, and/or temperature extremes while on job sites. Shift 7:00am – 4:00pm (Monday – Friday) Hours of work may vary dependent upon situational factors and may include some nights(s), weekend(s), and holiday(s) response. Job Summary The STEPS Facilities Multi-Skilled Trades Worker individually performs and/or assists: Electricians in installing and repairing electrical wiring, fixtures, and related equipment Painters in mixing and matching paints, stains, and painting Plumbers in installing, maintaining, and repairing pipes, valves, faucets, sinks, and other plumbing facilities Masons in laying brick, cement block, and sidewalks Carpenters in repairing chairs, tables, fences, doors, windows, floors, floors including carpet tile, VCT , wood, ceiling grid/tile, drywall installation/finishing, plaster repairs, various demolition, and other articles and fixtures Maintenance personnel in the repair and maintenance of buildings located at the farm HVAC mechanics in the operation, maintenance, and repair of heating, refrigeration, and air conditioning equipment Repair and maintenance of tools and equipment use of gas/electric operated equipment. In addition, this position: Models and promotes excellent customer service for internal and external customers Interacts with customers and clients in a manner which helps them reach their goals and objectives and delivers appropriate responses Inspects assigned work areas, documents findings, and initiates appropriate action to correct deficiencies though authorization and contact with supervision Ensures work in-process and upon completion complies with instructions, adherence to established practices and standards, and overall acceptability of work Ensures designated working areas are maintained in a safe and orderly manner and continuously free of trash and debris demonstrates an awareness of inventory cost control by effective and efficient use of tools and equipment. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your amount of experience in the maintenance and repair of farm equipment. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years,  up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of experience do you have with carpentry? None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years Describe your experience with plumbing, electrical, or HVAC troubleshooting, maintenance and/or repair. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
