    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651438": {
      "title": "Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Patient Relations Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE56060 Working Title Department Name M3030:Cancer Clinic Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3.5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motion (such as typing); walking including pushing, pulling, and/or lifting up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. The conditions of work may involve regular exposure to loud noises, intermittent exposure to blood borne/airborne pathogens and combative/violent people, and occasional exposure to cuts and punctures. Shift Day shift. Monday through Friday, 8:00am – 5:00pm, Other days and hours as needed. Job Summary The Patient Relations Assistant is foundational to facilitating an engaging and positive patient experience. The primary responsibilities include, but are not limited to; greeting patients, registration, insurance verification, cash handling, medical record preparation, scheduling appointments, procuring new patient records, communicating information with patients via the telephone and in person, and answering telephone. This position supports efficient patient care and clinic initiatives for improving patient attendance and keeping attendance records. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be skilled in communication, specifically in the ability to remain calm and helpful during emotionally stressful moments or crises. As someone responsible for employee records, attention to detail is critical to ensuring patient record accuracy. The ability to work in a collaborative environment with a teamwork mindset. The ability to follow processes and process data entry records. Respect for confidentiality; be able to prioritize tasks efficiently; and work in multiple systems simultaneously. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 3.5 years of experience Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe a situation when you delivered exceptional customer service to resolve a physician or patient complaint. (Open Ended Question) * Please choose the answer that best describes your amount of paid employment experience working with oncology patients. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Please choose the answer that best describes your amount of paid employment experience working with insurance and co-payments. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
