    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651414": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Plant Pathology Support Staff",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Plant Pathology Support Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Plant Pathology Support Staff Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Plant Pathology Support Staff Requisition Number DU15167 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 1405 Veteran's Dr Lexington, KY 40546 Salary Range $13.50 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High school diploma. Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Lift 25 – 50 pounds. Shift Weekdays between 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. . Job Summary Assist with general laboratory maintenance and cleanliness. Accompany Administrative Team on Surplus and/or Inventory Trips. Assist with filing and file management. Assist Administrative Team with Office Duties. Assist Administrative Team with set up for Seminars and Luncheons. Other duties as assigned. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 10/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
