      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Library Administration Library Student Assistant 3rd Shift",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Library Administration Library Student Assistant 3rd Shift Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Library Administration Library Student Assistant 3rd Shift Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Library Administration Library Student Assistant 3rd Shift Requisition Number DU15166 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 401 Hilltop Dr Lexington, KY 40506 Salary Range $13.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Be currently enrolled in the University of Kentucky. Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Be able to physically push heavy book carts weighing over 50 pounds, shelve materials on lowest and highest shelves (using step stool) and occasionally work in dusty environment. Shift Overnight shifts 11 pm to 7 am Sunday through Thursday. Some partial shift may be available. . Job Summary Produce and edit video as part of the UK PR video team. Assist with video productions on location and in studio. For inquires, please contact Steven Shaffer at steve.shaffer@uky.edu. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Customer service. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Customer service. Deadline to Apply 10/24/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination