    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651299": {
      "title": "Student: Marketing/Studio Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Marketing/Studio Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Marketing/Studio Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Marketing/Studio Assistant Requisition Number SE04484 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $15 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience - GPA 3.0 or above - Undergraduate or Graduate student - Experience with online marketing, selling, and advertising - Proficient in Canva for creating engaging digital content - Experience with TikTok, Instagram, Pinterest, and CapCut Hours per Week 15 - Starting trial period at 15 hrs per week – can lead to 20 hrs per week after evaluation (UK students encouraged to apply) - Availability to work 15 hours per week with a flexible schedule around school commitments Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply to this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Job Duties/Responsiilities: - Strong understanding of current social media trends and platform best practices - Ability to interpret social media analytics and use insights to improve content performance Creative mindset with a strong eye for aesthetics, branding, and visual storytelling - Assist with creating and scheduling engaging social media content - Help manage social media posting across multiple platforms (i.e Instagram, TikTok, FaceBook, Pinterest) - Assist with digital advertising and promotional campaigns - Support strategies to increase brand awareness, engagement, and sales conversions - Brainstorm and execute creative marketing ideas and campaigns - Maintain consistent brand voice and visual identity across all platforms - Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills - Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and collaborate effectively within a team - Strong communication, time management, and problem-solving skills Additional Information: – Work in a creative artist’s home studio alongside the artist and two additional assistants. - Studio is located in South Lexington on a quiet country road, approximately 17–18 miles from the University of Kentucky campus. - The home is shared with one friendly dog and two friendly cats, so applicants should be comfortable working around animals. - Assist with a variety of products, including handmade jewelry, ceramics, original artwork, books, vintage items, and creative supplies. - Position includes a six-week introductory/trial period, with the opportunity for continued employment through the spring/summer based on performance. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities - Familiarity with online marketing strategies and digital advertising - Strong written and verbal communication skills - Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills - Comfortable using social media platforms, including TikTok, Instagram, and Pinterest - Creative thinker with the ability to generate fresh content and marketing ideas - Understanding of online selling, e-commerce, or social commerce is preferred - Ability to analyze social media performance and apply insights to improve results - Strong organizational skills with excellent attention to detail - Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and as part of a team - Professional, positive attitude with a willingness to learn - Must have reliable transportation and a valid driver’s license Deadline to Apply 11/05/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 10/15/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
