    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651296": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Scholar",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Post-Doctoral Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Post-Doctoral Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Post-Doctoral Scholar Requisition Number DU15093 Department Name 7H364:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - RHEUMATO Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $59,000/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD/MD-PhD Required Related Experience Immunology Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Handling animal and human samples Shift Monday – Friday 8a-5p, some weekends required Job Summary The Chakravarti Immunology Laboratory in the Division of Rheumatology at the University of Kentucky is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to investigate signaling mechanisms that regulate immune cell fate decisions in health and disease. The successful candidate will lead studies focused on the role of 14-3-3 proteins and immune regulation in autoimmune and inflammatory diseases. These studies integrate molecular signaling, cellular immunology, systems immunology, and translational human immunology using both animal and human model systems. Along with the application, applicants should submit a Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter and one-page statement describing their immunology and cellular signaling related skills (Specific Request). Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Lab experience in handling immune cells, flow cytometry, cell culture and signaling is mandatory. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Immunology lab work Deadline to Apply 11/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
