    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651244": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics Requisition Number FE05059 Working Title Department Name 8E080:Mathematics Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Mathematics in the College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Kentucky in Lexington, KY seeks to fill a tenure-eligible faculty position at the Assistant Professor level or a tenured position at the Associate Professor level in Mathematics. This is a 9-month position in the regular title series with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be 25% teaching, 70% research, and 5% departmental service. The successful candidate is expected to pursue a vigorous research program in the theory of Partial Differential Equations ( PDE ) and to deliver high-quality teaching to both graduate and undergraduate students. Candidates with research interests in new interdisciplinary developments and applications related to PDE and strong funding potential are especially encouraged to apply. Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field is required at time of appointment. In order to be considered a candidate, applicants will need to complete the following two steps: 1. Submit your job market materials to MathJobs.org . Applications must include the following materials: 1) cover letter 2) CV, 3) Research Statement, 4) Teaching Statement, 5) Evidence of Effective Teaching. In addition, please provide at least three (3) letters of reference addressing the applicant’s research and one (1) letter of reference addressing the applicant’s teaching. All application materials must be submitted online at: https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/29153 2. Complete an application within the University of Kentucky employment system by visiting: https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650741 Questions about this search should be addressed to Mihai Tohaneanu, Search Committee Chair, Department of Mathematics, University of Kentucky ( mihai.tohaneanu@uky.edu ) Application review will begin on 10/30/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment at the University of Kentucky is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The University generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, the University of Kentucky offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulations concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651241": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Project Manager Requisition Number RE56049 Working Title Biosurveillance Project Manager Department Name 7P210:KY INJURY PREV & RESEARCH CTR Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 46 Salary Range $53,061-87,526/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing or pulling objects up to 50 pounds, sitting for extended periods of time, etc.) Shift Primarily days. Monday thru Friday between the hours of 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as needed. Job Summary The Kentucky Drug Overdose Biosurveillance Program Manager will develop systems, processes, and procedures for state biosurveillance programs. This position will be responsible for conducting overdose biosurveillance using multiple data sources; collaborating and developing biosurveillance program reports and grants management, including budget and grant narrative revisions; creating IRB protocols and modifications; establishing letters of agreement and consultant agreements; providing day to day leadership, supervision, coaching, and evaluation of the statewide biosurveillance program and related personnel; conducting epidemiologic analyses of biosurveillance data and developing and disseminating biosurveillance data products for stakeholders; collaborating with center faculty and staff on program evaluation and use of evaluation results to inform stakeholders and leverage sustainability funds; and analyzing population-based and other epidemiologic data on substance use, recovery, injury, and related public health topics and developing reports and other data result outputs. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Must be able to conduct data management and analysis using SAS or R/R-Studio, or other statistical analytic software. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Masters in Epidemiology Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of paid employment experience do you have with data management and data quality control? None More than 0 years up through 2 year More than 1 year up through 3 years More than 3 years up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of paid employment experience do you have disseminating research findings through presentations, briefs, publications and other venues? None More than 0 up through 1 year More than 1 year up through 3 years More than 3 years up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
