    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651239": {
      "title": "Dept Admin/Ophthalmology/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Dept Admin/Ophthalmology/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Dept Admin/Ophthalmology/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Dept Admin/Ophthalmology/UKHC Requisition Number RE55423 Working Title Ophthalmology Department Administrator Department Name MG360: Ophth & Visual Science Work Location Lexingon, KY Grade Level 15 Salary Range $95,056-185,848/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 8 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Ability to work in a sedentary position utilizing keyboard, mouse, computer and telephone. Ability to travel across campus for meetings. Shift Monday – Friday, 8am to 5pm with occasional early or late meetings as needed Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine seeks a strategic and collaborative leader to serve as Department Administrator for the Department of Ophthalmology and Visual Sciences. Reporting directly to the Department Chair, the Department Administrator serves as the department’s senior administrative leader and provides leadership for financial management, operations, human resources, faculty affairs, facilities, and strategic planning. As a key member of the department’s leadership team, the Department Administrator partners with faculty, staff, and institutional leaders to advance the department’s clinical, educational, research, and outreach missions while ensuring sound fiscal stewardship, operational excellence, and regulatory compliance. Position Overview The Department Administrator is responsible for the overall administration of a complex academic department and serves as a principal advisor to the Department Chair. This position provides leadership and oversight for departmental finances, operations, human resources, faculty affairs, facilities, and business planning activities, while supporting the department’s strategic priorities and long-term growth. Primary Responsibilities Financial Leadership & Business Operations • Direct the department’s financial and business operations, including budgeting, forecasting, financial reporting, and resource allocation. • Monitor financial performance and operational metrics to support departmental goals and long-range planning. • Ensure compliance with University, College of Medicine, UK HealthCare, and regulatory requirements. Strategic Planning & Administration • Partner with the Department Chair and leadership team to develop and implement strategic priorities. • Identify opportunities to improve operations, enhance efficiency, and support departmental growth. • Lead special initiatives and provide recommendations related to organizational structure, staffing, and resource management. Human Resources & Faculty Affairs • Provide leadership and oversight for faculty and staff affairs. • Support workforce planning, recruitment, onboarding, employee relations, performance management, and professional development activities. • Coordinate faculty recruitment, appointment, promotion, and retention processes. Operations & Facilities Management • Oversee facilities, space planning, equipment management, and administrative support functions. • Support the department’s educational, research, and clinical activities through effective operational management. • Foster a collaborative, service-oriented culture focused on continuous improvement. About the Department The Department of Ophthalmology and Visual Sciences at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine is a rapidly growing academic department dedicated to improving eye health through excellence in patient care, education, research, and community outreach. The department includes 38 faculty members representing all major ophthalmology subspecialties and supporting broad clinical, educational, and research missions across the Commonwealth. Since 2017, the department has experienced significant growth, including a 74% increase in faculty, 71% growth in patient visits, and a 93% increase in clinical productivity (wRVUs) The department maintains a substantial statewide clinical and outreach presence. During FY26, faculty and providers delivered care more than 103,000 patient encounters through UK Shriners Children’s Ophthalmology services, seven community clinic locations, and twelve outreach locations across Kentucky. In addition, the department performed nearly 4,700 surgical cases across eight operating room locations. The department’s educational programs include an ACGME -accredited ophthalmology residency program, multiple fellowship programs, and an optometry residency. Faculty and trainees also contribute to research, community outreach, telemedicine initiatives, and global ophthalmology programs that expand access to vision care in Kentucky and beyond. As a key member of the department’s leadership team, the Department Administrator will partner closely with the Department Chair and faculty leaders to support continued growth, strengthen operations, and advance the department’s strategic priorities. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The successful candidate will possess strong financial and analytical skills, strategic thinking, organizational leadership, and the ability to build collaborative relationships across diverse constituencies. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications is required. Experience with Epic, Tableau, Axiom, or similar healthcare and financial reporting systems is preferred. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Preference will be given to candidates with: • Progressive leadership experience in academic medicine, healthcare administration, higher education administration, or a similarly complex organization. • Experience supporting an academic clinical department, faculty practice, health system, or healthcare enterprise. • Demonstrated success in financial management, strategic planning, operational oversight, and organizational leadership. • Experience leading administrative teams and managing human resources functions. • Knowledge of faculty affairs, graduate medical education, and research administration. • Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships with physicians, faculty leaders, administrators, and other stakeholders. • A master’s degree in business administration, healthcare administration, public administration, higher education administration, or a related field. Deadline to Apply 11/04/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have preparing or reviewing financial data (budgets, projections, variance reports, or similar) to support leadership decision-making? None More than 0, up through 3 year More than 3 year, up through 7 years More than 7 years * Please select the option that best represents your experience with Excel or similar tools. Basic (data entry, simple calculations) Intermediate (formulas, sorting/filtering, pivot tables) Advanced (complex formulas, data analysis for reporting) No prior experience * Describe a time when you were responsible for pulling together financial or operational data for a leader or leadership group. How did you determine what information was most important to include, and how did you present it to support an informed decision or discussion? (Open Ended Question) * Provide an example of how your communication style has helped foster trust or maintain professionalism in a complex or high-pressure work environment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651232": {
      "title": "Nursing Care Technician/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Requisition Number RE54194 Working Title NCT / CNA - Surgical Oncology, MCC Department Name H7700: Cancer Services-Inpatient Pav A Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $18.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Have one or more of the following: 1. Kentucky Registered State Registered Nurse Assistant ( SRNA ), for Emergency Department (ED)- KY Registered State Registered Nurse Assistant ( SRNA ) or Emergency Medical Technician ( EMT ) 2. Registered Nurse (RN) nursing student who has completed first fundamental course and a clinical 3. Military Medic 4. current/active Licensed Practical Nurse ( LPN ) license 5. Acquired Nursing Care Technician ( NCT ) competencies through continuous employment at the University of Kentucky; 6. Successful completion of the Earn While You Learn NCT Training Program within 8 weeks of hire; plus American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid at time of hire, or completion of certification during Earn While You Learn NCT Training Program. Physical Requirements This position requires regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds; and standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasionally requires standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds and/or working in confined spaces. Also involves some exposure to risk of injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to loud noises, temperature extremes, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, radiation, burns, cuts/punctures, blood-borne or airborne pathogens, and/or combative/violent people. Shift Must be able to work three 12.5-hour shifts per week (7:00 p.m. – 7:30 a.m.) Will also be required to work some weekends and holidays. Job Summary This position works one-on-one with a Registered Nurse (RN) to complete delegated tasks and provide direct patient care such as: obtain vital signs, phlebotomy, documentation, assist with ADL’s (activities of daily living), order and stock supplies, respond to patient call lights, unit orientation, and patient admission, transfer, and discharge. Positions may also involve moving patients from bed to wheelchair or stretcher, or stretcher to treatment/surgical tables. Handling of specimens and delivery to labs and preparation of patients for surgical procedures may also be required. The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing prompt, compassionate, and patient centered care in a collaborative, team-oriented work environment. This dynamic environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the teams of physicians to increase communication, follow through, and enhance patient outcomes and satisfaction. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. In addition, the essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis, as well as stand, walk, and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Please apply for any and all positions for which you feel qualified. If you do not apply for a specific position, you cannot be considered for the position . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be compassionate, honest, trustworthy, and have a strong work ethic. Must enjoy working in a team, but also be able to take direction and communicate effectively with staff, patients, and their family members independently. In addition, must also be confident and enjoy working in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of CPR and basic concept of abnormal vital sign parameters is a must. Candidate will also need strong organizational, prioritization, basic computer navigation skills, and a working knowledge of the Internet. Valid American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider at time of hire is required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous hospital experience is preferred . Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select which of the following options best represents your related educational and/or related professional nursing experience RN Nursing student who has completed the first clinical nursing course (class and clinical) of nursing school A valid, current Kentucky State Registered Nursing Assistant Certificate Experience as a military medic Active LPN license Acquired Nursing Care Technician (NCT) competencies through continuous employment in a NCT role at University of Kentucky (For Emergency Department positions ONLY)  Emergency Medical Technician Certificate None * Are you currently a Nursing Care Technician that works at UK Chandler or Good Samaritan Hospital? Yes No * Please indicate the number of years of paid work experience you have as a Nursing Care Technician and/or a State Registered Nursing Assistant (SRNA) in which you were directly responsible for patient care in a hospital. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please describe a difficult situation you handled successfully. (Open Ended Question) * How much direct experience do you have using a computer (e.g. keyboarding, data entry, and e-mail)? None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you have a Basic Life Support (BLS) certification or eligible to obtain by hire date? Yes No * If hired, can you provide proof that you are at least 18 years of age at start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651231": {
      "title": "Nurse Clinical/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Clinical/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Clinical/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Clinical/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number NR15262 Working Title RN/Oncology Surgical Specialty/On Call Department Name H7700: Cancer Services-Inpatient Pav A Work Location Lexington Grade Level 10 Salary Range $28.00-39.10/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education ADN Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Active Kentucky Registered Nurse (RN) license, Temporary Work Permit ( TWP ), Provisional License or active compact state Registered Nurse (RN) license that is in good standing and American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid for at least 6 months after employment date Physical Requirements The essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis and 25-50 pounds frequently; as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases, hazards of radiation, and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift 7a/7p , 36 hours a month Job Summary The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing total, comprehensive, continuous and patient centered care which includes: assessing, documenting, planning, implementing, teaching, developing, and evaluating a comprehensive nursing plan of care; delivering direct patient care; ensuring patient satisfaction; training and delegating duties for Nursing Care Technicians (Nursing Assistant); and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. Furthermore, this environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the team of physicians to increase communication and enhance expected patient outcomes. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have the following: knowledge of Maslow’s eight Basic Human Needs and the priority within Gordon’s Functional Health Patterns Frame Work as well as Swanson’s Caring model; superb direct patient care and critical thinking skills; basic computer navigation skills and working knowledge of the internet; ability to communicate in a professional and respectful manner with patients and their families, co-workers and physicians; and strong organizational, prioritization, and delegation skill. The candidate will be highly motivated, pro-active and confident in advocating for patients and their family members. Will also enjoy working in a strong team environment and provides open, honest communication with fellow staff and physicians. In addition, the ideal candidate will possess exceptional technical skills and a proven ability to work in a team as well as independently. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BSN + AT LEAST 1 YEAR OF RN EXPERIENCE PREFERRED Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651229": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Postdoctoral Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Postdoctoral Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar Requisition Number DU15089 Department Name 7H700:Dept of Pharmacology & Nutritional Scien Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range Commensurate with experience Type of Position Other Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD in Neuroscience, Pharmacology, Physiology, Biology, or a closely related field Required Related Experience At least one first-author publication in a peer-reviewed journal. Research experience and strong interest in neuroscience, metabolism, diabetes, obesity, or related areas. Research experience with mouse models. Experience studying the hypothalamus or neural regulation of metabolism. Experience with neural tracing techniques. Experience performing stereotaxic surgery in mice. Excellent organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Strong written and spoken English skills. Self-motivation, scientific curiosity, and a strong commitment to research. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time; standing for long periods of time Shift Days and some weekends Job Summary We are seeking a highly motivated and enthusiastic Postdoctoral Fellow to join our research team. This position is particularly well suited for a recent PhD graduate with training in Neuroscience, Pharmacology, Physiology, or a related field who is interested in understanding the neural and cellular mechanisms regulating energy and glucose homeostasis in health and disease. The selected postdoctoral fellow will use a multidisciplinary approach combining mouse models and in vitro studies to investigate mechanisms by which the brain regulates glucose homeostasis. The research will focus on understanding these mechanisms in the context of normal metabolic physiology, diabetes, and obesity, with an emphasis on the role of the hypothalamus and neural circuits involved in metabolic regulation. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Experience with metabolic phenotyping, glucose tolerance testing, insulin sensitivity studies, or related in vivo metabolic assays. Experience with immunohistochemistry, microscopy, molecular biology, or related techniques. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Experience with metabolic phenotyping, glucose tolerance testing, insulin sensitivity studies, or related in vivo metabolic assays. Experience with immunohistochemistry, microscopy, molecular biology, or related techniques. Candidates who are recent PhD graduates and have a strong publication record, scientific motivation, and transferable research skills are particularly encouraged to apply. Training will be provided for techniques that are new to the successful candidate. Deadline to Apply 11/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651228": {
      "title": "Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE55625 Working Title Specialty Dental Assistant - KY Clinic General Dentistry Clinic Department Name MD100:DENTAL GROUP CLINICAL PRACTICE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $19.00-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Basic Life Support ( BLS ) at time of hire through the American Heart Association ( AHA ); must obtain Coronal Polishing, Dental X-ray, and IV Sedation competencies within 6 months of hire Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting, standing, walking, with some pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift; primarily 8:00 am – 5:00 pm (40 hrs/wk); other hours/schedule as needed Job Summary The Specialty Dental Assistant provides clinical support for surgical and general dental procedures performed by faculty, residents, and students. This includes four-handed chairside assisting during pediatric and adult treatments such as orthodontics, restorative, endodontics, periodontics, prosthodontics, oral surgery, and implant placement. This position may also be on a rotation to assist in the operating room setting. Responsibilities include obtaining patient consent, reviewing medical histories, initiating IVs, drawing blood for PRF preparation, and setting up or breaking down operatories. The assistant monitors and documents vital signs during oral and IV sedation, administers medications under supervision, and assists during medical emergencies. Additional duties include passing instruments during procedures, delivering post-operative instructions, escorting patients after surgery, and managing clinical inventory and supply orders. The role also involves diagnostic tasks such as taking radiographs, impressions, and intraoral scans. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail and accuracy, excellent communication and customer service skills, dependability, communication, initiative Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Expanded duties certificate, Coronal polishing certificate, Experience assisting with sedation, and working in the operating room environment. Experience in working with patients with special needs. Knowledge of implant procedures is desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a current BLS (Basic Life Support) certification through the American Heart Association (AHA), or are you eligible to obtain this by date of hire? Yes No * Do you have current Coronal Polishing, Dental X-ray, and IV Sedation certificates, or are you eligible to obtain these 6 months of hire into the Specialty Dental Assistant/UKHC job title? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651227": {
      "title": "Dental Hygienist/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Dental Hygienist/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Dental Hygienist/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Dental Hygienist/UKHC Requisition Number RE54337 Working Title Department Name MD100:DENTAL GROUP CLINICAL PRACTICE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $26.00-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Basic Life Support ( BLS ) and Registered Dental Hygienist ( RDH ) in state of Kentucky at time of hire Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting, standing, walking, with some pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. Constant repetitive motion. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift Job Summary The person in this position will provide direct patient care, including performing prophylaxis, polishing, periodontal maintenance, scaling and root planning, patient assessment of hard and soft tissues and periodontal exams. Capture radiographic image. Apply fluoride foam and varnish and sealants as ordered by dentist. Provides home care assessment and oral health instructions. Provide clinical support through disinfection, set-up and breakdown of clinical operator, instrument sharpening and equipment maintenance. Prepares and transports instruments for sterilization. Update patient’s medical history and medications. Records vital signs at each visit. Documents treatment performed and enters procedures in the clinical patient management software. Schedule patients for return appointment. This position is eligible for a Sign-on Bonus of $10,000, contingent on a 12-month employment commitment. Further details will be discussed during the hiring process. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Four handed dentistry knowledge, multi-tasking oriented, dependability, self-starter, organizational skills, attention to detail, communication skills, timeliness, ability to work with patients of all ages. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous experience as a dental hygienist preferred, with pediatric dental experience highly desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently licensed as a Registered Dental Hygienist in the state of Kentucky, or are you eligible to obtain licensure by your start date? Yes No * Do you have a current BLS (Basic Life Support) certification through the American Heart Association (AHA), or are you eligible to obtain this by date of hire? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
