    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651208": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Professor of Pediatrics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate, or Professor of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate, or Professor of Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate, or Professor of Pediatrics Requisition Number DU15070 Department Name MG340: Funds Flow Pediatrics Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $1.00 Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Minimum of 3 years in pediatric pulmonology and sleep medicine Required Related Experience Pediatric Residency, Pediatric Sleep Medicine Fellowship Required License/Registration/Certification MD, DO, or equivalent Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motion (such as typing); walking including pushing, pulling, and/or lifting up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. The conditions of work may involve regular exposure to loud noises, intermittent exposure to blood borne/airborne pathogens and combative/violent people, and occasional exposure to cuts and punctures. Shift Part-time appointment including remote sleep study reading. Job Summary The Part-time Title Series position is needed in the Department of Pediatrics, Division of Pulmonology in order to meet the academic and clinical needs of the division and the Department in education, training and service consistent with the mission of the University of Kentucky College Of Medicine. The primary responsibilities of this position are to provide quality care to children with sleep disorders in the Kentucky Children’s Hospital Pediatric Sleep Center. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 11/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
