    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651206": {
      "title": "Research &amp; Program Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research &amp; Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research & Program Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research & Program Coordinator Requisition Number RE55175 Working Title Survivorship Manager Department Name 7H025:CANCER CENTER-CORE SUPPORT Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 43 Salary Range $19.56-31.29/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time, walking long distances, manage office supplies, repetitive motion. Shift Monday – Friday (40 hrs/wk). Job Summary The Markey Cancer Center is currently hiring a Research Coordinator (Survivorship Manager) to support a new research initiative. This position will provide essential administrative, research, and technical support to Initiative leadership to advance survivorship research at Markey. As described below, duties will include providing research proposal development support, communication management and partnership building, event and program planning, and administration and strategic planning. Pre-award research support will entail assisting with the development of human subjects and clinical trial documents for research proposals and developing protocols for regulatory submissions for Just-in-Time requests from funders. Communication management and partnership building will require serving as the front-line interface between Initiative leadership and varied stakeholders (e.g. investigators, clinicians, community partners, other units on campus). Event and program planning will require conception to post-event coordination and management for speaker series, research events, and other events led by the Initiative. A successful candidate will have experience supporting or conducting human subjects research with cancer patients or other chronic or serious illness populations and knowledge of clinical trial requirements. In addition to being detail-oriented, self-motivated, and reliable, the successful candidate will exhibit maturity, customer service, excellent written and oral communication skills, an ability to prioritize and manage multiple deadlines, and good judgement. The successful candidate will have strong skills in MS software, remote meeting platforms, and online survey platforms (REDCap or Qualtrics). This position is eligible for a Hybrid work arrangement. IMPORTANT : Resumes and CVs cannot be substituted for a completed application. Incomplete applications could disqualify you from being considered for this position. If the information on your resume is not entered on the application, this will prevent us from being able to assess your education and experience when trying to determine a salary offer. To be considered you must fully complete the online application being sure to only put one (1) job title for each entry (multiple job titles for one employer must have separate entries), the # of hours worked per week and your ending salary. You will also be required to upload a cover letter and CV. To view the University of Kentucky’s exceptional benefits, please visit https://www.uky.edu/hr/benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite programs, document and file management systems (e.g. SharePoint, One Drive, Microsoft Teams file repositories), project management/workflow tools for tracking tasks, timelines, and program plans, virtual meeting platforms, online survey administration systems; strong interpersonal skills; excellent written and oral communication Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Master’s degree preferred, at least 3 years experience supporting human subjects research studies, with preference for clinically-focused research support, demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, attend to firm deadlines, and work with partners from a variety of disciplines. Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you ever managed email and schedules for someone in a leadership or high-level executive position? Yes No * Have you ever provided research/study coordination support to human subjects investigators? Yes No * Have you ever planned events in a professional capacity? Yes No * Have you ever worked in an interdisciplinary environment where you interacted with clinicians and researchers? Yes No * Have you ever designed surveys for REDCap or Qualtrics? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Writing Sample 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651205": {
      "title": "LPN/Ambulatory/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | LPN/Ambulatory/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support LPN/Ambulatory/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title LPN/Ambulatory/UKHC Requisition Number RE55689 Working Title LPN/Ambulatory/UKHC Department Name H4007:Chief Medical Office Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $21.36-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education LPN Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Practical Nurse ( LPN ) – Kentucky Licensure Physical Requirements Requires handling of average weights or objects up to 25 pounds with some sitting, standing, or walking. Shift 8:00 – 4:30pm Job Summary The LPN is a member of the multidisciplinary ambulatory team who is responsible for patient care, patient satisfaction, and clinical outcomes. The LPN performs the duties for which they are trained such as starting IVs, simple wound dressings, and notifying the RN or LIP with any changes or abnormalities in the patient’s condition. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities None Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience None Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) in the state of Kentucky or able to obtain license by date of hire? Yes No * Please indicate your paid employment experience working with patients in a clinical setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please choose the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience as an LPN. None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years, up through 10 years More than 10 years * Please describe your previous role(s) on a multidisciplinary health care team, including your specific responsibilities. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
