    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651192": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Carpenter Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Carpenter Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Carpenter Requisition Number RE55468 Working Title Department Name 81270:Research Farms Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 6 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements This position requires pushing or pulling objects over 50 pounds, working at heights above 4 feet, and climbing ladders. A full range of physical motion is required. Shift Days; Monday-Friday, typically 7:00 am-4:00 pm (40 hours per week) may require some overtime. Job Summary The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment is seeking a Carpenter to join the trades team for Research Farms, at the scenic 1,800-acre North Farm in Lexington. The Research Farms provide a vast array of teaching, research and extension opportunities for the faculty, staff and students of the college, while overseeing the engineering, Construction and Maintenance of the colleges Agriculture facilities. As an essential member of the Trades team, A Carpenter will perform construction, repairs and maintenance carpentry work across College facilities and the farms! Making this position an integral part of keeping these spaces functional, well maintained and most importantly, safe. This position offers the opportunity to work in a distinctive agricultural environment while supporting the College’s mission. This position is eligible for the University of Kentucky’s exceptional benefits package, which includes: 10 to 15 days of paid vacation per year, and up to 20 days per year with additional years of service 14 paid holidays and bonus days, plus 2 paid personal well-being days Paid parental and elder care leave 200% employer match to your retirement savings contributions Tuition-free classes for you and tuition discounts for family members Affordable health, dental, vision and life insurance including a $0 co-pay for medical and mental health telehealth visits with most plans The Big Blue Family Care program, which makes it simple for UK families to connect with UK students for occasional, part-time childcare needs Student loan savings – You might be eligible for lower payments and Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) Visit https://www.uky.edu/hr/employment/working-uk/our-benefits to explore additional benefits. The Research Farm units are part of the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment. Martin-Gatton CAFE is a welcoming workplace that offers a variety of employee enhancement initiatives, such as a formal mentoring program and a staff professional development fund. To find out more about Martin-Gatton CAFE and how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky … Click Here . For additional information about the Research Farms division, please click here . ( https://research.ca.uky.edu/content/central-ky-farms ). Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Driver’s license preferred Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience with facility management, construction and renovation. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience working on a multi-disciplinary skilled trades team to coordinate and perform job tasks required for carpentry in building and renovation construction. (Open Ended Question) * This position requires laborious and/or physically taxing work and the ability to efficiently perform any and all cumbersome duties and job tasks. Are you able to meet these requirements with or without reasonable accommodations? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651191": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology Requisition Number FE05032 Working Title Department Name 8E120:Psychology Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education A PhD in Psychology Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Psychology in the College of Arts Sciences at the University of Kentucky in Lexington, KY seeks to fill two tenure-eligible faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor level within the Psychology department. These are 9-month positions in the regular title series with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be 25% teaching, 70% research, and 5% departmental service. This position will be a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. We seek candidates who identify professionally as cognitive neuroscientists, clinical neuroscientists, or clinical neuropsychologists with expertise in neuroscience methodologies (e.g., neuroimaging, biomarkers, computational modeling, genomics, or other advanced neuroscientific research methods). The department includes a Cognitive Neuroscience area with both basic and clinically focused research programs (e.g., substance use, ADHD ), as well as an APA / PCSAS -accredited Clinical Psychology PhD training program that includes a Clinical Neuropsychology concentration. The successful candidates will join the Cognitive Neuroscience area of the experimental doctoral program and are expected to conduct research that fosters collaboration across our Cognitive Neuroscience and Clinical faculty. Candidates may also affiliate with the Clinical Psychology training program if appropriate to their interests and training. The research focus is open and may complement existing areas of expertise within the department and university—including substance use, brain injury, decision making, attentional processes, learning and memory, Alzheimer’s disease and related disorders, affective disorders, and ADHD—or introduce new areas of cognitive or behavioral neuroscience research. Candidates should have a strong research program, demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications and the potential to secure extramural funding. Successful candidates will also contribute to the department’s teaching and service missions and be prepared to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in their area of expertise. At the University of Kentucky, faculty psychologists regularly lead multidisciplinary research teams and conduct collaborative research across a range of clinical settings, including the Department of Psychiatry, Markey Cancer Center, Kentucky Clinic, Gill Heart and Vascular Institute, Kentucky Neuroscience Institute, Eastern State Hospital, and Sanders-Brown Center on Aging. Additional research infrastructure includes the Spinal Cord and Brain Injury Research Center and the Center for Clinical and Translational Science ( CCTS ), which provides resources such as biomarker analysis and an outpatient clinical research unit. The UK Magnetic Resonance Imaging and Spectroscopy Center ( MRISC ) supports structural and functional neuroimaging with a Siemens PRISMA 3T MRI scanner. A PhD in Psychology is required at time of appointment. Applicants must include the following: 1) letter of application (upload as Cover Letter) 2) CV 3) research statement (upload as specific statement 1) 4) teaching statement (upload as specific statement 2) 5) In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the academic profile. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references within the employment system. Questions about this search should be addressed to Mark Fillmore ( Fillmore@uky.edu ) or Anthony Zanesco ( anthony.zanesco@uky.edu ), Search Committee Chairs, Department of Psychology, University of Kentucky. Application Deadline is 10/07/2026. This posting will remain open until both positions are filled. Employment at the University of Kentucky is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The University generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, the University of Kentucky offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651185": {
      "title": "Nursing Assistant/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nursing Assistant/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nursing Assistant/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nursing Assistant/UKHC Requisition Number RE55936 Working Title Eastern State Hospital - MHA – Gragg 1 Department Name H1050:ESH Nursing Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 05 Salary Range $15.68-22.60/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements This position requires regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds; and standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasionally requires standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds and/or working in confined spaces. Also involves some exposure to risk of injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to loud noises, temperature extremes, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, radiation, burns, cuts/punctures, blood-borne or airborne pathogens, and/or combative/violent people. Shift Must be able to work three 12.5-hour shifts per week (7:00 a.m. – 7:30 p.m.) Will also be required to work some weekends and holidays. Job Summary Eastern State Hospital is currently recruiting for a full-time Nurse Assistant/Mental Health Associate in Gragg 1: 28-Bed All-Male Unit The Mental Health Associate will assist a licensed healthcare provider in the delivery of patient care to adult patients with a primary psychiatric diagnosis. Assists in providing age appropriate and specific needs, treatment services, and performs related tasks as required (i.e. obtain vital signs; assist with activities of daily living). Provides direct patient care by planning, organizing, and implementing psychiatric rehabilitation activities. Assists in escort of patients to and from activities, assists in screening and basic assessment of patients. Provides documentation and keeps records of patient behavior. Assists in patient supervision of patients during treatment/support activities. Leads/co-leads group activities. Implements hospital and departmental policies, procedures, rules, and regulations in assuring a safe, therapeutic environment. Please apply for any and all positions for which you feel qualified. If you do not apply for a specific position, you cannot be considered for the position. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be compassionate, honest, trustworthy, and have a strong work ethic. Must enjoy working in a team, but also be able to take direction and communicate effectively with staff, patients and their family members independently. In addition, must also be confident and enjoy working in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of CPR and basic concept of abnormal vital sign parameters is a must. Candidate will also need strong organizational, prioritization, basic computer navigation skills, and a working knowledge of the Internet. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous healthcare experience and CPR certification preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently certified as a Kentucky State Registered Nursing Assistant? Yes No * Please indicate your paid work experience in a hospital as a Behavioral Health Tech, Nursing Assistant, and/or a State Registered Nursing Assistant (SRNA). None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of mental health related experience do you have? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
