    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651179": {
      "title": "Customer Svc Rep/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Customer Svc Rep/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Customer Svc Rep/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Customer Svc Rep/UKHC Requisition Number RE55445 Working Title Customer Relations Specialist Department Name H4005:Office of Patient Experience Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $19.00-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The physical requirements of this position include: sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motions (such as typing); occasionally standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs; and regular traveling/walking through the facilities. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 4:30pm (with some flexibility). May also include some evenings, weekends and holidays per departmental needs. Job Summary The Customer Relations Specialist will provide prompt, sensitive and professional responses to patients and families regarding their complaint or grievance. This position will also collaborate and serve as a liaison between patients, families, and/or surrogates and UK HealthCare staff and departments; will research and document obstacles to the delivery of service to proactively work on developing solutions; and adhere to UK Healthcare Behavioral at all times. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate for this position will have a proven track record of providing exceptional customer service; superior communications abilities with an emphasis on patient care, diplomacy, and sensitivity; and a strong background in utilizing Microsoft systems including Windows, Word, and Excel. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree in a healthcare related field with 3 years of experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of work experience have you had related to customer service? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years * How many years of paid work experience do you have working in healthcare? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe a patient conflict that you helped to resolve.  What was the issue and what did you do to resolve it? (Open Ended Question) * Why are you interested in this position? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Writing Sample 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
