    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651178": {
      "title": "Interventional Technologist/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Interventional Technologist/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Interventional Technologist/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Interventional Technologist/UKHC Requisition Number RE55826 Working Title Interventional Technologist - Up to $30,000 sign-on bonus! Department Name H3185:Interventional Radiology Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $26.00-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Kentucky State Radiation Operators License + American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Registered Radiologic Technologist ( ARRT RT ) + Basic Life Support ( BLS ) Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs; Standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs; Standing for long periods while wearing radiation protective garments; Risk of back injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; Risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job; Radiation exposure. Shift M-F 0700-1730 with rotating days off, requires being on call for evenings, nights, weekends and holidays. Job Summary UK Healthcare is growing! We are expanding our Interventional Radiology services and are hiring for new technologists. The IR Technologist will provide clinical assistance during procedures and assist the physician in expediting needed care. The IR Tech will provide technical assistance in CT, US and fluoroscopy guided procedures. Quality, efficiency, and service excellence are all essential parts of this position. Techs will also assist as a scrub tech or circulator during procedures, and be responsible for supply charge, documentation and charging procedures. Maintaining patient efficiency by spending appropriate amounts of time for each task and interacting will be an essential job function. Adhering to the UK behavioral standards during interactions with patients, coworkers, and physicians, as well as external and internal customers will also be essential. Maintaining privacy and confidentiality are required. There will be a potential for advancement to Master Tech after obtaining advanced registry and gaining equipment proficiency. Applicants who possess the Associate’s degree & 3 years related experience (or equivalent) + ARRT or ARRT certification are eligible to be moved upon hire to the grade 12 Interventional Master Technologist/ UKHC position ($30.00/hour – $53.67/hour). Skills / Knowledge / Abilities PACS , EPIC Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred Interventional Radiology experience, but any rad tech experience is acceptable Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires you to currently hold or be eligible to obtain American Registry of Radiologic Technologists  Radiography®  Cardiovascular Interventional Radiography (CV) or American Registry of Radiologic Technologists  Radiography® Vascular Interventional Radiography (VI) by date of hire. Will you be able to meet both of these requirements? Yes No * This position requires you to currently hold or be eligible to obtain a Kentucky Radiation Operator’s License by date of hire. Will you be able to meet both of these requirements? Yes No * Do you currently hold or will be eligible to obtain a Basic Life Support (BLS) certification by date of hire? Yes No * Please choose the answer that best describes your paid employment experience in Interventional Radiology and/or General Radiology. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
