    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651175": {
      "title": "Dietetics Technician/Formula Room/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Dietetics Technician/Formula Room/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Dietetics Technician/Formula Room/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Dietetics Technician/Formula Room/UKHC Requisition Number RE55370 Working Title Infant Nutrition Diet Technician Department Name H3075:Nutritions Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $17.35-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly lifting/pushing/pulling objects up to 50lbs, regularly standing/walking with objects up to 10lbs, and repetitive motions. Shift Must work five, 8-hour variable shifts per week (8:00 am – 4:30 pm, 8:30 am – 5:00 pm, 9:00 am – 5:30 pm, or 12:00 pm – 8:30 pm). Weekend and holiday rotation required (at least one winter and one summer holiday). Job Summary Responsible for the preparation, storage and delivery of infant feedings as well as inventory, ordering, cleaning and sanitation. Performs as a member of the interdisciplinary team. Ensures customer satisfaction and good public relations through safe and efficient use of resources. Performs duties in compliance with performance improvement plans, TJC , and other licensing, accrediting, and regulatory agencies. Assists the Registered Dietitian with nutrition care of patients. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be a Dietetic Technician, Registered and/or have completed a degree in Dietetics. This individual will have the ability to manage multiple tasks and/or projects while accurately completing routine functions in a fast-paced, high-intensity, professional work environment; enjoy working independently as well as closely with co-workers in a supportive team environment; and possess proficient computer skills (including Microsoft Office), excellent customer service and active listening skills, a high regard for attention to detail, and dependability. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Current Dietetic Technician, Registered ( DTR ) credential; background in nutrition, pharmacy, and/or laboratory; and a degree in nutrition (or medically-related field) preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you completed a two year Associate's Degree Dietetic Technician program or obtained a Bachelor's Degree in Dietetics? Yes No * Are you a Dietetic Technician Registered? Yes No * Please indicate your years of paid work experience as a dietetic technician. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Briefly describe your work experience as it relates to the specific duties of this position and why you chose to apply. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
