    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651170": {
      "title": "Administrative Support Associate I",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Support Associate I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Support Associate I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Support Associate I Requisition Number RE56044 Working Title Tuition Assistance Program Coordinator Department Name 3J521:Employee Benefits Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The essential functions of this position include: occasionally lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to and over 50lbs; occasionally standing or walking with objects 10-25lbs; communicate and work cooperatively with staff, faculty and applicants from diverse backgrounds; abide by University guidelines; maintain confidentiality; prioritize and manage work effectively; provide exceptional customer service; complete work with interruptions; ensure work is detailed, accurate and completed in a timely manner; perform work in a sedentary position, utilizing computer, keyboard, mouse and telephone the majority of the day; and work successfully in a team as well as independently. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Job Summary The role oversees employee education and benefits administration across university programs. Its responsibilities span program processing, customer support, compliance, reconciliation, and enrollment accuracy. • Employee and Family Education Programs carry weights of 30% and 15% , covering eligibility checks, billing coordination, ProSam waivers or discounts, refunds, databases, and taxable tuition reporting. • Customer service carries 20% , while reconciliation duties carry 20% and include journal vouchers, benefits reports, payroll eligibility, Section 125 and Affordable Care Act compliance, dependent audits, and flexible spending reviews. • New enrollment-checking duties carry 15% and cover dental, vision, health, flexible spending, retirement, and life plans across SAP and Direct Bill. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Data entry, SAP knowledge, Excel, attention to details and customer service. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How would you describe your experience with Microsoft Excel? No experience with Microsoft Excel Beginner – Data entry, basic formatting, simple sorting and filtering Intermediate – Using formulas (e.g., SUM, IF), conditional formatting, removing duplicates Advanced – Combining data from multiple sources, using VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, creating pivot tables Expert – Advanced formulas, macros/VBA, automating processes * Describe a situation where you provided excellent customer service. (Open Ended Question) * Please tell me about a time when attention to detail was essential. What was the task or project and how did you ensure accuracy? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
