      "title": "LPN/Hospital/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | LPN/Hospital/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support LPN/Hospital/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title LPN/Hospital/UKHC Requisition Number NR15204 Working Title LPN/Hospital/UKHC Department Name H1050:ESH Nursing Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 08 Salary Range $21.40-30.09/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education LPN Required Related Experience 0 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Practical Nurse ( LPN ) – Kentucky Licensure Physical Requirements Requires handling of average weights or objects up to 25 pounds with some sitting, standing, or walking. Shift 7:00 am – 7:30 pm Job Summary Wendall 2 is a 28-bed co-ed unit. The LPN is a member of the multidisciplinary ambulatory team who is responsible for patient care, patient satisfaction, and clinical outcomes. The LPN performs the duties for which they are trained such as starting IVs, simple wound dressings, and notifying the RN or LIP with any changes or abnormalities in the patient’s condition. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities None Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience None Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does 