    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651147": {
      "title": "Radiology Tech Sr/Spec Prcdr/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Radiology Tech Sr/Spec Prcdr/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Radiology Tech Sr/Spec Prcdr/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Radiology Tech Sr/Spec Prcdr/UKHC Requisition Number RE55681 Working Title Cath Lab Technologist - Cath Lab Technologist - Sign-on bonus up to $30,000 with an 18-month commitment Department Name H3130:Gill Heart Institute Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $35.16-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Kentucky State Radiation Operators License + American Registry of Radiologic Technologists Registered Radiologic Technologist ( ARRT RT ) + Basic Life Support ( BLS ) at time of hire; plus Advanced Cardiac Life Support ( ACLS ), Pediatric Advanced Cardiac Life Support ( PALS ) and Certified EKG Technician ( CET ) within 6 months of hire Physical Requirements This position requires the ability to regularly lift, push, and/or pull objects weighing up to and over 50 lbs.; occasionally stand or walk with objects weighing up to 25 lbs.; regularly perform tasks requiring repetitive motions; and occasionally sit at a computer workstation for an extended period of time. Shift Four 10-hour weekday shifts per week, 7:00am – 5:30pm. Shift can be scheduled for any weekday. Call coverage required including weekends and holidays. The call back is 30 minutes. Job Summary Cardiac Cath and EP Technologist will demonstrate knowledge of Interventional, Structural, Pediatric, and Electrophysiology procedures. Technologist will scrub/assist the physician during diagnostic and Interventional Cardiac and Peripheral angiographic studies. The technologist is also able to record and monitor procedures and demonstrate understanding of hemodynamic measurements and readings from the valve areas. Technologist will provide adequate call coverage per departmental need. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities McKesson, EPIC , Qsight, Intellispace, Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, etc. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Cardiac Cath/EP experience preferred but any rad tech experience is acceptable. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently certified by the ARRT (American Registry of Radiologic Technologists) or eligible to obtain this certification by date of hire? Yes No * Do you currently hold a KY Radiation Operator's License (KBMIRT) or are you eligible to obtain by date of hire? Yes No * This position requires the following additional certifications within 6 months of hire: Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS); Pediatric Advanced Cardiac Life Support (PALS); and Certified EKG Technician (CET). Do you possess these certifications or are you eligible to obtain within 6 months of hire? Yes No * Please indicate your years of paid work experience working in a Cardiac Cath Lab. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Briefly describe your work experience working in a Cardiac Cath Lab. Be sure to include your role, scope of responsibilities, and duties assigned. (Open Ended Question) * As a Radiology Technologist, give an example of how you ensure you are providing good service to a patient. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
