    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651135": {
      "title": "Behavioral Health Counselor/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Behavioral Health Counselor/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Behavioral Health Counselor/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Behavioral Health Counselor/UKHC Requisition Number RE54890 Working Title Department Name MG34M:PEDS-PSYCHOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 12 Salary Range $62,400-111,634/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MSW for LCSW , MS for LPCC , LCADC , LMFT (no equivalency) Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Clinical Social Worker ( LCSW ) or Licensed Professional Clinical Counselor ( LPCC ) or Licensed Clinical Alcohol and Drug Counselor ( LCADC ) or Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist ( LMFT ) at time of hire Physical Requirements Sitting and standing for extended periods of time. Shift Monday – Friday, 40 hours per week, August-May (10 months) Job Summary The work location for this position will be in Scott, Harrison and Nicholas counties. This position is offered at a reduced FTE , with compensation prorated accordingly based on the assigned FTE and scheduled hours. The Behavioral Health Counselor will provide direct clinical counseling to help children and families deal with various personal, social, and mental health issues, such as depression, unemployment, domestic abuse, and illness, through individual, family, and group counseling. This individual will work closely with providers to provide patients and families with a comprehensive mental health evaluation and treatment plan. Job duties include evaluating, diagnosing, and treating mental health conditions. The BHC will provide timely and effective support to patients facing mental health emergencies using evidence-based screening tools, risk assessments, and clinical interventions for children and adolescents. The BHC will help patients cope with suicidal behaviors by safety planning, minimizing stressors, offering emotional support, and improving coping strategies during crisis situations. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities None Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous work experience providing clinical mental health assessments, counseling, case management and/or social services. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an MSW or Master's level degree or higher? Yes No * Do you have 3 years of experience in healthcare, clinical mental health, counseling, case management and/or social service? Yes No * Do you have current certification as a Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) or Licensed Professional Clinical Counselor (LPCC) or Licensed Clinical Alcohol and Drug Counselor (LCADC) or Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) at time of hire? Yes, Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) Yes, Licensed Professional Clinical Counselor (LPCC) Yes, Licensed Clinical Alcohol and Drug Counselor (LCADC) Yes, Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) No * How many years of experience do you have working as an independently licensed provider? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years up through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you have experience working in a integrated behavioral health setting, where the primary service is medical care related to physical health? Yes No * Please provide detail on your experience providing mental health care to children, including ages and any specific diagnosis. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience providing therapeutic interventions with children and adolescents who are experiencing a mental health crisis. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
