    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651131": {
      "title": "Administrative Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Operations Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Operations Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Operations Coordinator Requisition Number RE56010 Working Title Department Name 7H010:CoM Shared Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 43 Salary Range $40,685-65,083/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements This position will require the ability to utilized a computer, keyboard, and mouse for extended periods of time. Will also require ability to travel to various locations across campus as required for on-site meetings. Shift This position will work 40 hours per week scheduled Monday thru Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Job Summary College of Medicine | Fully Remote Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine is seeking a highly organized, resourceful, and customer-focused professional to join our team in a fully remote position supporting workforce, recruitment, onboarding, immigration sponsorship, and related employment processes. This role serves as a key partner to departments, employees, candidates, and university offices by coordinating complex, deadline-driven administrative processes throughout the employment lifecycle. The successful candidate will help ensure the timely completion of hiring, onboarding, immigration, and personnel-related activities while maintaining a strong focus on accuracy, compliance, customer service, and operational excellence. Responsibilities include coordinating administrative processes, monitoring documentation and critical deadlines, maintaining records and tracking systems, communicating with internal and external stakeholders, supporting recruitment and employment activities, maintaining SharePoint resources and process documentation, and utilizing a variety of web-based systems and technologies. This position offers a unique opportunity to support recruitment, workforce administration, immigration sponsorship, and operational processes that are essential to attracting, onboarding, and retaining talented individuals across the College of Medicine The ideal candidate is highly organized, adaptable, and resourceful, with exceptional communication skills, a collaborative mindset, and the ability to manage multiple priorities independently in a remote work environment. Why Join Our Team? Fully Remote Opportunity Enjoy the flexibility of a fully remote position while supporting departments, faculty, staff, scholars, and candidates across the College of Medicine. This role offers the opportunity to work independently while remaining closely connected to a collaborative and supportive team. Engaging and Varied Work Support a broad range of activities spanning recruitment, workforce administration, onboarding, immigration sponsorship, process improvement, systems administration, and stakeholder support. No two days are exactly alike, and you’ll have opportunities to learn, collaborate, and contribute across several critical functions within the College of Medicine. Professional Growth and Development Gain experience across multiple functional areas including employment administration, recruitment, immigration sponsorship support, onboarding, systems administration, process improvement, and operational support. This position offers exposure to a wide variety of university processes and opportunities to develop expertise in several specialized areas. Support the College’s Mission Your work directly supports the recruitment, hiring, onboarding, sponsorship, and retention of talented individuals who advance the College’s educational, research, and clinical missions. The processes you coordinate help departments attract and support the people who make those missions possible. Does This Sound Like You? You may be a great fit if you: Enjoy coordinating complex processes and keeping multiple priorities organized Thrive in a fast-paced environment with competing deadlines Take pride in accuracy, attention to detail, and high-quality work Are naturally resourceful and enjoy finding solutions to challenges Communicate professionally and confidently with a variety of stakeholders Enjoy helping others navigate complex administrative processes Excel at building collaborative working relationships Can work independently while remaining highly responsive and accountable Enjoy learning new systems, technologies, and business processes Are committed to providing exceptional service and support If you’re looking for a fully remote opportunity where you can make a meaningful impact, collaborate with a talented team, and support critical workforce and administrative functions across an academic medical center, we encourage you to apply. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities What Will Make You Successful? Successful candidates will demonstrate: Exceptional organizational and time-management skills Strong written and verbal communication abilities Professional judgment and problem-solving skills Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy Ability to manage multiple deadlines simultaneously Strong customer service and relationship-building skills Technical aptitude and ability to learn new systems quickly Ability to work independently in a remote environment Adaptability, initiative, and resourcefulness Commitment to continuous improvement and process excellence Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred Experience Candidates may come from a variety of backgrounds. Relevant experience may include: Human Resources Recruitment or Talent Acquisition Higher Education Administration Immigration or International Services Support Workforce Administration Employee Services Project or Program Coordination Operations Administration Business Administration Administrative Services Process Improvement or Operational Support Experience coordinating complex administrative processes, managing sensitive information, utilizing web-based business systems, maintaining records, and working with diverse stakeholder groups is highly desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires coordinating multiple deadlines, stakeholders, systems, and documentation requirements simultaneously while working in a fully remote environment. Please describe a situation where you successfully managed a complex process or project involving multiple parties. What was your role, what challenges did you encounter, and how did you ensure a successful outcome? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651130": {
      "title": "Nurse Clinical/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Clinical/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Clinical/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Clinical/UKHC Requisition Number NR15112 Working Title RN/Gastro & Heptology Ambulatory Clinic Department Name M3500: AMBULATORY MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 10 Salary Range $28.00-39.10/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education ADN Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Registered Nurse (RN) Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting, standing, walking, with some pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. Shift Monday – Friday, Day Shift; primarily 8:00 am – 4:30 pm (40 hrs/wk); other hours/schedule as needed Job Summary The Nurse Clinical Ambulatory provides disease-specific patient care to a group of patients who have serious acute and/or chronic health events or who are seeking healthcare to maintain their state of wellness. Responsibilities of the position include, but not limited to skilled assessments, care plans and care plan implementation, patient education and clinical evaluation or interventions. This position requires working with medical professionals who are working under time and efficiency constraints in a busy ambulatory care setting with a patient centered care focus on quality, safety, and service. A working knowledge of enterprise, nursing, departmental policies, protocols, and procedures is needed to be successful. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Basic computer knowledge, MS Windows, Word, Outlook Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience ADN or BSN Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit * Where did you first see this position advertised? AONE (American Organization of Nurse Executives) UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
