    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651112": {
      "title": "Physician - Orthopaedic Surgeon, Trauma",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Orthopaedic Surgeon, Trauma Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Orthopaedic Surgeon, Trauma Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Orthopaedic Surgeon, Trauma Requisition Number FE05044 Working Title Assistant, Associate, or Professor Department Name 7H859:ORTHOPAEDIC SURGERY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Medical Degree or Equivalent Demonstrated Ability in Clinical Teaching Required Related Experience Completion of residency as well as fellowship training in Orthopaedic Trauma Surgery Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for license to practice medicine in Kentucky Board Certified or eligible in Orthopaedic Surgery Job Summary The UK College of Medicine Department of Orthopaedic Surgery and Sports Medicine is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 150 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 46 faculty members, over 25 staff members, and over 40 learners. Our department is home to leading clinicians, educators, and researchers and is nationally recognized for advancing orthopaedic care through innovation, discovery, and education. Each year, providers in the department care for more than 80,000 patients across 11 clinical sites. The department trains 43 residents and fellows across 4 accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure, on average, over $1 million in grant funding to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in areas centering around developing and evaluating treatments and clinical decision making to enhance recovery, function, and long-term outcomes for patients following orthopedic injuries and surgeries. The department published on average 100 peer-reviewed articles and maintains numerous active clinical trials. More than 15 medical school learners along with varying undergraduate and post-graduate trainees and a core residency class of 25 trainees gain in-depth clinical research experience . 110+ alumni from the department can be found across the globe at academic medical centers, health systems, research institutions, and more. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Interested candidates should submit a CV along with their application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Ability to relate with internal and external constituencies of the Medical Center involved in related disciplines Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
