    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651110": {
      "title": "Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Requisition Number FE05042 Working Title Ashland, KY Department Name 7H854:OPHTHALMOLOGY & VISUAL SCIENCE Work Location Ashland, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. or D.O. and completion of Ophthalmology residency Required Related Experience Completion of Ophthalmology residency Required License/Registration/Certification Obtain Kentucky medical license by start date. Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine Department of Ophthalmology is seeking a Comprehensive Ophthalmologist to join our Ashland, KY practice. This position supports the department’s mission of clinical care, teaching, and scholarly activity, with opportunities for professional growth within a comprehensive academic medical center. We are seeking a Comprehensive Ophthalmology faculty to join our group of physicians that are committed to excellence in clinical care, instruction, scholarly activity and professional development. The successful candidate must have completed an Ophthalmology residency. Responsibilities include: · Providing direct patient care · Developing academic pursuits in the areas of education and research The UK College of Medicine Department of Ophthalmology is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 180 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 37 faculty members, 122 staff members and 24 learners. Each year, providers in the department see 140,000+ patient visits at 17 clinical sites. The department trains 24 residents and fellows across 8 accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Ashland is a historic river city located along the southern bank of the Ohio River in northeastern Kentucky. It sits near the borders of Ohio and West Virginia, forming a major part of the Huntington-Ashland metropolitan area. Ashland is a charming historic town, rich in its industrial history as an iron and steel center, its vibrant downtown arts scene and its scenic location along the Ohio River. Huntington, WV and Charleston, WV are the larger cities closest to Ashland with both being an hour or less in distance. Both cities provide a vibrant downtown experience, experiences in the arts and a doorway to the Appalachian foothills with multiple recreational activities. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Interested candidates should submit an updated CV along with their application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651107": {
      "title": "Philanthropy Assoc Specialist - Research",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Philanthropy Assoc Specialist - Research Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Philanthropy Assoc Specialist - Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Philanthropy Assoc Specialist - Research Requisition Number RE56043 Working Title Senior Research Analyst Department Name 14000:Office Of Philanthropy Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 45 Salary Range $48,214-79,560/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time at the desk and repetitive motion tasks. Attend meetings on and off campus. Shift Monday-Friday; 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Job Summary Drive Strategic Philanthropy Through Research, Insight, and Prospect Discovery The University of Kentucky Office of Philanthropy & Alumni Engagement ( PAE ) is seeking a Senior Research Analyst to turn research, data, and insight into opportunities that advance philanthropy across the University. As a senior member of the Prospect Research and Management team, this position will proactively identify and evaluate major-gift prospects and provide strategic intelligence that helps philanthropy professionals build meaningful relationships and strengthen the University’s fundraising pipeline. Serving as a trusted research partner to assigned colleges and units, the Senior Research Analyst will collaborate with philanthropy officers, deans, University leaders, and other partners to inform prospect identification, portfolio development, and engagement strategies. The role combines investigative research, analytical thinking, and sound judgment to uncover philanthropic capacity, interests, relationships, and networks—and translate those findings into clear, actionable recommendations. This is an opportunity for an experienced, self-directed researcher to influence fundraising strategy, contribute to the development of a high-performing prospect development operation, and use their expertise to support the University of Kentucky’s mission across the Commonwealth and beyond. The culture within the Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement ( PAE ) is built on our shared core values CoMMIT– Collaboration, Communication, Mission Driven, Mutual Respect, Innovation and Transparency. By applying for a position within UK PAE , you are indicating your commitment and expressing your agreement to our six values. It is important you share these values in order to be part of our committed team! Skills / Knowledge / Abilities • Some supervisory experience or experience providing work direction is preferred. • Proactive, goal-oriented individual with ability to plan, direct, implement and monitor programs and projects effectively. • Strategic planning skills with ability to develop fundraising strategies. • Knowledge of standard industry resources such as Wealth Engine, Lexis-Nexis, ResearchPoint, DonorScape, and Dun & Bradstreet, and proficiency with all MS Office products. • Utilize appropriate tools for visual data analysis (e.g. Excel, Tableau, Advizor, Visual Analyzer). • Experience using the database Millennium and the Reeher Platform is preferred. • Ability to work independently and with people collaboratively. Requires a self-motivator as well as the ability to work as part of a team. • High degree of integrity, ethical decision-making and sound business judgment; awareness of and adherence to APRA Code of Ethics and AFP Donor Bill of Rights. • Well-organized, with exceptional attention to detail and follow through. • Excellent problem-solving skills and ability to manage multiple priorities. • High degree of competency in writing and interpersonal communications. This is an onsite and in-person position in Lexington, KY. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Master’s degree Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your level of proficiency utilizing various software packages and reporting tools to complete data analysis, generate reports, and/or investigate areas of concern. (Open Ended Question) * Describe one or more of your major accomplishments related to your use of data analytics and/or philanthropy research. (Open Ended Question) * How many years have you worked in philanthropy research or in a similar field that uses data analysis? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years, up through 10 years More than 10 years * The Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement (PAE) recognizes a set of values that guide us in our daily interactions. These values are collaboration, communication, mission driven, mutual respect, innovation and transparency. Please choose one of the PAE values and give a specific example when you exhibited this quality in your professional experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651100": {
      "title": "Physician - Adult Inpatient Psychiatrist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Adult Inpatient Psychiatrist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Adult Inpatient Psychiatrist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Adult Inpatient Psychiatrist Requisition Number FE05039 Working Title Department Name 7H800:PSYCHIATRY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. degree or equivalent Required Related Experience -Completion of residency in Psychiatry. -Knowledge of psychiatric practices in a variety of clinical, teaching, and research environments, as well as a demonstrated ability in teaching students at all levels in an academic environment. Required License/Registration/Certification -Board eligible/board certified in Adult Psychiatry by the American Psychiatric Association. -Current licensure, or eligibility to obtain licensure, to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky. Job Summary The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine is seeking a residency-trained, board certified/board eligible Physician – Adult Inpatient Psychiatrist. The successful candidate must be committed to excellence in clinical care as well as teaching, administration, and professional development. Preferred experience includes previous experience in providing psychiatric services, as well as experience in teaching medical students, residents, and other health professionals. This position will be instrumental to expand inpatient physician coverage on the Behavioral Health Unit at Good Samaritan Hospital and to provide backup coverage for consultation-liaison and Emergency Department psychiatric care at Good Samaritan and Chandler hospitals. In addition this faculty position may provide backup clinical coverage and resident supervision for the Empath Unit located on the campus of Eastern State Hospital. This program will help create a 24-hour coverage model multiple locations to increase access to psychiatric consults and care throughout the hospitals and Emergency Departments. This position will help provide a proactive consult for patients by placing psychiatrists in medical units throughout the two hospitals for early identification and intervention for behavioral disorders, substance abuse disorders, and psychiatric conditions. The Department of Psychiatry at the University Of Kentucky College Of Medicine strives to provide the highest level of patient care, innovative educational programs, active research in mental illness and advocacy throughout the state of Kentucky and beyond. These pursuits have helped the department win the American College of Psychiatrists’ Award for Creativity in Psychiatric Education not once, but twice. The University of Kentucky provides a comprehensive beneﬁts package including health, dental, and insurance beneﬁts, a competitive 2:1 retirement match up to 5% of an employee’s base salary, discounts to local, regional and national businesses, paid vacation and temporary disability leave (sick time) and 14 paid holidays each year. For additional information on University of Kentucky’s beneﬁts, please visit https://hr.uky.edu/insurance-and-retirement . In addition, the Department of Psychiatry provides paid time and funding for professional development to include monthly Grand Rounds, didactic teaching from our faculty as part of our resident physician education programs, CEU opportunities from several behavioral health-related ﬁelds across the University as well as opportunities to collaborate on research projects, published papers and other scholarly work. If you are interested in joining our team of behavioral health providers making a difference in our community and across the State, please consider applying for this position. To be considered an applicant for the position, please submit a CV and cover letter along with application. Please also include the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the application. This information may be used to solicit reference letters within the employment system. Applications will be reviewed immediately. The position will remain open until filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated ability to relate and communicate with internal and external faculty, staff, and other clients of the department. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
