    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651099": {
      "title": "Physician - Radiation Oncologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Radiation Oncologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Radiation Oncologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Radiation Oncologist Requisition Number FE04992 Working Title Department Name 7H900:RADIATION MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, DO or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency or fellowship if appropriate Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible to obtain, or in current possession of, license to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Board-certified or board-eligible in Radiation Medicine Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine Department of Radiation Medicine is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor to join a growing team. This position supports the department’s missions of clinical care, teaching, and scholarly activity, with opportunities for professional growth within a comprehensive academic medical center. We are seeking a radiation oncologist who will provide CNS and Pediatric Cancer Care, as well as teaching. Responsibilities include: • Clinical services, focusing on CNS cancers and pediatric cancers • Teaching, including radiation oncology residents, medical physics residents, students in the Masters’ Program in Medical Physics, as well as medical students rotating through our clinic. • Clinical research, ranging from enrolling patients in clinical trials to serving as Principal Investigator of Investigator Initiated Clinical Trials. The UK College of Medicine Department of Radiation Medicine is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 120 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 21 faculty members, 65 staff members, and 34 learners. The department is home to Gamma Knife radiotherapy and nationally recognized for its brachytherapy program. Each year, providers in the department care for more than 2,500 patients across two clinical sites. The department trains 14 residents and fellows across 3 accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Our department is part of a college with robust research programs and initiatives, contributing to the advancement of health across Kentucky and beyond. Faculty, staff, and learners contribute to high-impact, transdisciplinary research projects and have access to state-of-the-art facilities and technology on campus. 35+ alumni from the department can be found across the globe at academic medical centers, health systems, research institutions, and more. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Interested candidates should submit their CV and academic transcripts along with their application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Academic Transcript Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
