    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/651051": {
      "title": "Diagnostic Technician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Diagnostic Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Diagnostic Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Diagnostic Technician Requisition Number RE55624 Working Title Department Name 81250:VETERINARY DIAGNOSTIC LABORATORY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50 lbs. Sitting/standing for extended periods of time as well as extended periods of repetitive motion and general laboratory duties required as part of this position. Shift Days: Monday – Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM (40 hrs/wk). In the event of an outbreak, overtime (including nights and weekends) may be required. Job Summary The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory ( UKVDL ) develops and applies state-of-the-art diagnostic methodology to improve animal health and marketability, to protect the public health and to assist in the preservation of the human-animal bond through the principles of One Health. For additional information on the UKVDL , please click here . This position is a vital member of the team serving as a Diagnostic Technician. The duties for this position in the Molecular Section of the UKVDL include process specimens; run diagnostic assays; evaluate results; keep proper records and report results; database management ; bioinformatics; and assist in the training of other employees as needed. The position includes exceptional benefits as a part of the University of Kentucky and is located at the Coldstream Research Campus off Newtown Pike (great location and free parking). The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment fosters a supportive workplace with professional development opportunities, including a formal mentoring program and staff development fund . To find out more about M-G CAFE and how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky, Click Here . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities MS Office including Access, Excel, Word, Outlook, and Specialty Bioinformatics Software. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor of Science. Excel, word and outlook. Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the response that best represents your amount of paid, full time employment experience in laboratory, research, and/or sterile techniques and diagnostics in molecular biology. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How much experience do you have working in medical or veterinary molecular biology diagnostics? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How much experience do you have working in molecular biology diagnostics? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years experience do you have in a diagnostic laboratory? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of experience do you have in molecular biology? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
