    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650999": {
      "title": "Event Production Technician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Event Production Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Event Production Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Event Production Technician Requisition Number RE56040 Working Title Event Production Specialist Department Name 3DH41:Aux Services - University Events Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting 20-25 lbs, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 lbs Sitting, standing, walking, pushing, climbing and crawling. Shift Multiple shifts available; 40 hours per University week to meet the event needs of the department which includes evenings and weekend. Job Summary The University Events Production team is seeking a Event Production Technician for university events and programs both on and off campus. This role operates and supports audio, video, lighting, presentation, projection, recording, livestreaming, and related digital production systems while collaborating with event stakeholders to deliver professional, reliable, and high-quality event experiences. What You Will Do • Provide live event and digital production services, including audio, video, lighting, presentation, projection, recording, livestreaming, and video playback for on-campus and off-campus events. • Set up, configure, operate, monitor, and dismantle production equipment and systems based on event specifications, technical requirements, venue conditions, and available resources. • Operate and integrate cameras, presentation systems, streaming platforms, video displays, and other digital production technologies. • Monitor audio, video, lighting, and digital production systems throughout events and independently identify, diagnose, and resolve technical issues to minimize service interruptions. • Apply technical judgment to select and configure appropriate production systems and solutions based on event needs, audience requirements, venue capabilities, and available resources. • Collaborate with event organizers, campus departments, presenters, performers, and other stakeholders to assess event needs and determine technical production requirements. • Provide professional, responsive, and solutions-oriented technical support during event planning, preparation, and execution, including responding to changing conditions and time-sensitive production needs. • Assist with the preparation, recording, streaming, delivery, and management of event content in accordance with established procedures. • Mentor and support Student Technicians during live events and office assignments, helping develop technical skills and promote professional production practices. • Maintain, organize, inventory, transport, configure, test, and properly store audio, video, lighting, presentation, streaming, and related production equipment. • Assist with evaluating, testing, implementing, and integrating new production technologies and equipment to support evolving university event and production needs. • Follow university policies, production procedures, and applicable health and safety standards while contributing to safe and effective event operations. • Assist Production Managers with event planning, special projects, equipment upgrades, process improvements, and other operational activities as assigned. What You Will Bring • Experience with live event production, digital media technology, audiovisual systems, livestreaming, or a related technical production environment. • Knowledge and hands-on experience operating audio, video, lighting, presentation, projection, recording, streaming, and related digital production equipment. • Strong technical troubleshooting and problem-solving skills, with the ability to diagnose and resolve issues in time-sensitive live event environments. • Ability to independently operate and configure complex production systems while exercising sound technical judgment. • Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with event organizers, presenters, performers, campus partners, and production teams. • Commitment to providing professional, responsive, and customer-focused technical support. • Ability to assess event requirements, venue conditions, and available resources and recommend appropriate technical solutions. • Ability to mentor and support student employees and colleagues in the safe and effective use of production technologies and equipment. • Commitment to safe equipment handling, operational practices, university policies, and applicable production and venue safety requirements. What Is In It for You • Meaningful impact: Help create engaging, reliable, and memorable event experiences for the University of Kentucky community and its audiences. • Cutting-edge technology: Work hands-on with professional audio, video, lighting, livestreaming, presentation, and digital production technologies. • Variety in your day: Enjoy a dynamic role supporting a wide range of live events, programs, venues, presenters, and production requirements. • Professional growth: Expand your expertise in live event production, digital media, technical systems, troubleshooting, and emerging production technologies. • Team and student development: Mentor Student Technicians while working alongside event professionals and campus partners in a collaborative production environment. • Comprehensive benefits: Enjoy competitive compensation, excellent benefits, and opportunities for professional growth at the University of Kentucky. Internal Employee Being Considered ( IEBC ) Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650997": {
      "title": "STEPS Kinship Navigator (Two Rivers)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Kinship Navigator (Two Rivers) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Kinship Navigator (Two Rivers) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Kinship Navigator (Two Rivers) Requisition Number TE09539 Department Name 8T110:College of Social Work Work Location Two Rivers Service Region Salary Range $25.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA or educational equivalency Required Related Experience Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Sitting for extended periods of time; Motions typical of desk work (typing/bending/twisting/etc.); lifting/pushing/pulling objects up to 20lbs. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm; some occasional weekends/evenings Job Summary The College of Social Work (CoSW) at the University of Kentucky (UK) invites applicants for an opening as a STEPS Kinship Navigator . This position will work in concert with Kentucky Kinship Resource Center ( KKRC ) program staff, Centers & Labs program administrators, Department of Community Based Services ( DCBS ), and the Kinship Navigator Supervisor to provide consultation and guidance to caregivers caring for children in a kinship (relative or fictive kin) placement. This position will be housed in a DCBS Regional Office and will be located in the Two Rivers Service Region. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a passion and commitment to kinship caregiving in Kentucky and a desire to support this population. Some travel within the region for meetings with DCBS and to the Coldstream Training Resource Center may be required. Essential Core Functions Objectively advise kinship caregivers of options regarding care of their relative/fictive kin child through the Kentucky Kinship Service Array, including the requirements, responsibilities, and expectations of each option. Provide connection to resources and programs appropriate to assist in supporting the kinship family. Complete any referrals needed to assistance programs. Review and complete all kinship-related forms with caregivers. Remain a point of contact for kinship caregivers who have questions or need future assistance. Work cooperatively with Department of Community Based staff to ensure timely services are provided to kinship families. Connect kinship families with the Kentucky Kinship Resource Center programming for continued support, resource connection, and training. Administrative Duties Complete all necessary state and university required paperwork based on caregivers decision. Complete data entry into online portals. Attend related trainings and meetings as required. Complete any required reporting or program evaluation as needed or indicated. There is a possibility the chosen candidate will assist with covering other regions as needed (travel to these regions for the additional coverage will not be required as this coverage can be done remotely). A map of the service regions is available for review here: https://www.chfs.ky.gov/agencies/dcbs/dsr/Documents/sraregionalmap.pdf Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Public relations; Excellent written and oral communication skills; Working in partnership with various and diverse groups; Excellent interpersonal skills with various and diverse groups; Critical Thinking; Planning and Coordination; Attention to Detail Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650994": {
      "title": "STEPS Research Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Research Assistant Requisition Number TE09495 Department Name 7H150:BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $17.41/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Bachelors or equivalent Required Related Experience Experience in research, community outreach, data collection, and report writing Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Sitting and/or standing at the work station for extended periods. Lifting and/or carrying light weight objects up to 20 pounds. Shift Days, Monday-Friday; occasional weekends and evenings. Job Summary The Health and Aging from Multicultural Perspectives Lab at the Center for Health, Engagement and Transformation is seeking an individual to work on a grant funded research study testing middle-to-late life adults on dementia risks. Duties include recruiting participants, collecting survey and neuropsychological data, and conducting qualitative interviews. The successful candidate will also assist with coordinating daily operations; drafting study materials; serving as a liaison; monitoring the study tracking system; performing statistical analyses; preparing reports; and performing other duties as assigned Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Data collection knowledge; basic computer skills including MS windows, Excel, Word, and PowerPoint; REDCap (or other survey platform); social media skills Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelors Degree with previous experience working in a research lab Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
