    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650991": {
      "title": "Auto Mechanic II",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Auto Mechanic II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Auto Mechanic II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Auto Mechanic II Requisition Number RE55969 Working Title Department Name 81270:Research Farms Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Requires heavy lifting, pushing or pulling of objects over 50 pounds. Shift Monday-Friday, 8:00 am-4:30 pm (37.5 hours a week) occasional overtime required. Job Summary The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment is seeking a skilled individual to join our team for Auto Mechanic II, at the beautiful off-campus 1800-acre North Farm in Lexington. In this role, you would perform an array of tasks including maintenance, service and repairs of farm vehicles and equipment, provide farm support for the crops production program, assist with research projects, farm maintenance, and other general facilities duties. A strong background in automotive/equipment maintenance and the ability to work with power tools, mechanics hand tools and diagnostic equipment is preferred. The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment fosters a welcoming work environment and offers excellent benefits, including health, vision and dental insurance. Retirement plans with high contribution match rates, sick time roll-over, paid vacation time, including holidays. Plus an extensive employee discount program. The Research Farms provide a unique workplace that supports agricultural innovation and fosters education for students and staff alike. For more details about the Research Farms division, visit: Research Farms . Join us and be part of a team at M-G CAFE and see how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky, Click Here . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Pesticide Applicator’s Certification & CDL preferred. Customer Service experience. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have safely operating and providing routine maintenance for farm equipment? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Do you have a valid Kentucky Driver's License? Yes No * Do you have an ASC (Automotive Service Excellence) Certification? No Response No, I have never been certified. No, my certification has lapsed. Yes, I am currently certified. * Do you have experience operating farm machinery? No Yes, limited experience. Yes, mid-level experience. Yes, extensive experience. * Please indicate your amount of experience in the maintenance and repair of farm equipment. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years,  up through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you have experience operating and maintaining field equipment (i.e. tractors, planters, combines, and spray equipment)? Yes No * Do you have a CDL License, or are you willing and able to get a CDL License? Yes, I have a CDL License. No, I do not have a CDL License. I am willing and able to get my CDL License. No, I do not have a CDL License. I am not willing/able to get a CDL License. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650967": {
      "title": "Nurse Division Charge/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nurse Division Charge/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nurse Division Charge/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nurse Division Charge/UKHC Requisition Number NR15260 Working Title Nurse Division Charge / UKHC Neonatal ICU / WEPP Nights 7p-7:30am Department Name H3060:Children's/Maternal/Psychiatric Svcs Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $29.12-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BSN Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Registered Nurse (RN) Physical Requirements N/A Shift Must be able to work two 12 hour night shifts (7pm-7:30am) Saturdays and Sundays each weekend. This position is a Weekend Premium Plan ( WEPP )—work 24 hours/week and receive 32-36 hours pay plus full benefits. Job Summary Division Charge Nurse ( DCN ), is responsible for assuring quality care during his/her tour of duty. He/She is responsible for efficient management of nursing resources and patient safety. Responsibilities include: 1. Resource management-ensures adequate numbers of competent nurses are available to care for patients, serves as a clinical and systems resource for nurses and assists staff in planning for appropriate patient care delivery. 2.Professional development-supervises nursing staff, provides guidance to staff during orientation and in their ongoing professional development, and in collaboration with the Director and Patient Care Managers assists with the performance reviews of staff 3. Customer Service-develops collaborative relationships with physicians, ancillary staff and the entire team. Interviews patient and families to ensure that staff are exceeding patient/family expectations, interacts with nursing staff to ensure engagement in their work and resolves conflicts and problems among personnel, patients, physicians and families 4. Facilitates quality patient care—identifies problems with patient care and initiates actions for resolution, ensures policies and guidelines are followed, facilitates staff completion of competency requirements. and coordinates quality improvement projects. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Microsoft Office, Access, Excel Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Preferred Education/Experience Neonatal ICU experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral Print Advertisement On-line Advertisement Military Connection Advertisement Job Fair \"I'm Interested\" page on Nurse Recruitment website Facebook HospitalCareers.com InsideHigherEd.com Diverseeducation.com (Diverse Issues in Higher Education) HERCjobs.org (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) InsightIntoDiversity.com Latinosinhighered.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com Institute for Diversity in Health Management None of the Above * Please indicate your current Nursing Educational Level. New Graduate Diploma ADN BSN MSN PhD or DNP * Are you currently employed as a registered nurse at UK HealthCare Chandler/UK HealthCare Samaritan Hospitals? Yes No * Please indicate your current licensure status. None Current KY RN License Current compact state RN licensure Current non-compact state RN licensure New Graduate within 6 months or Provisional License Valid KY Temporary Work Permit Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
