    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650915": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Laboratory Technician Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Laboratory Technician Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Laboratory Technician Senior Requisition Number RE55876 Working Title Department Name 81080:ENTOMOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Standing for long periods of time; Lifting objects up to 25 lbs. Shift Monday – Friday; 8:00 am – 4:30 pm. Job Summary Advance Research on Insect and Tick Biology Through Molecular Science The University of Kentucky is seeking a Laboratory Technician Senior to join the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment Department of Entomology . This position supports a research program focused on the molecular analysis of hormone action, insecticide resistance, and RNA interference in insects and ticks. The successful candidate will conduct laboratory experiments, manage research activities, support laboratory operations, and contribute to publications and presentations that advance understanding of disease vectors such as mosquitoes and ticks. What You’ll Do Assist in managing laboratory research activities under the direction of the project director. Conduct experiments involving molecular analysis of hormone action, insecticide resistance, and RNA interference in insects and ticks. Rear insects, feed ticks, and perform isolation and analysis of nucleic acids and proteins using techniques including gel electrophoresis. Collect, analyze, interpret, and prepare research data for scientific presentations and publications. Manage laboratory supplies, maintain inventory of chemicals and materials, and support efficient laboratory operations. Oversee laboratory safety practices and train students on laboratory safety procedures. Participate in professional development activities and support organizational improvement initiatives. What You’ll Bring Strong planning, organization, and time-management skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel. Knowledge of laboratory hygiene, safety practices, and research methods. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Experience with statistical analysis and graphics software. Knowledge of biochemistry, physiology, and molecular biology techniques. Ability to work collaboratively in a research environment and support student training. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree 1 year of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to contribute to research focused on the biology, endocrinology, and management of disease vectors, including mosquitoes and ticks. Access to a formal mentoring program that supports professional growth and career development. Eligibility for staff development funding to support continued learning and skill enhancement. Opportunities for professional development, including tuition credit for graduate studies. Recognition programs that celebrate employee contributions and achievements. Join a collaborative college community committed to excellence, learning, communication, flexibility, competence, and respect. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? Research on insect and tick biology plays a critical role in advancing strategies for managing disease vectors and addressing challenges related to insecticide resistance. This position provides essential support for ongoing laboratory investigations that generate scientific knowledge and contribute to the research mission of the Department of Entomology. As research activities continue to expand in molecular and physiological studies of insects and ticks, this role will help ensure high-quality laboratory operations, reliable data collection, student training, and continued progress toward scientific publications and research outcomes. Potential candidates should include a current copy of their CV and information for three references that may be contacted within the required cover letter as part of their application. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Data collection, rearing and collecting of arthropods and plants, organization of laboratory, ordering of supplies, supervision of undergraduate student workers and coordination of graduate student research projects. Knowledge of experimental design and statistical analysis, scientific writing, editing and proof reading, knowledge of molecular biology. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience BS in Biology or Entomology required, preferred MS in Entomology with emphasis on physiology; one to two years of experience in molecular methods or the equivalent combination of education and experience. Drivers license preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
