    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650891": {
      "title": "Student: After-School Sports Instructor",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: After-School Sports Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: After-School Sports Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: After-School Sports Instructor Requisition Number SE04481 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $16-$24 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience - Previous coaching, teaching, childcare, camp, or youth sports experience is a plus, but not required. - Background or interest in athletics, physical education, fitness, recreation, or youth development - Previous participation in organized sports - Experience leading groups of elementary or middle school students - CPR or First Aid certification - College coursework or degree work in education, kinesiology, exercise science, recreation, or a related field Hours per Week 7.5 Most programs take place Monday through Friday during after-school hours, generally fall between 2:30 PM and 5:00 PM. Coaches can work around their availability. This is especially well suited for college students or anyone looking to add a few consistent hours of work each week. Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Overtime Athletics is looking for energetic, dependable coaches to lead youth sports and enrichment programs at schools throughout the Lexington area. This is a great part-time opportunity for college students, education majors, athletes, former athletes, coaches, teachers, or anyone who enjoys working with kids and wants a flexible schedule. What You’ll Do Coaches lead fun, organized after-school programs for elementary and middle school students. Programs may include basketball, soccer, flag football, kickball, dodgeball, tennis, Sports Spectacular, and other youth sports and enrichment activities. Responsibilities include: - Leading approximately 1-hour sports and enrichment programs - Following OTA -provided lesson plans and activities - Creating a fun, positive, and safe environment - Managing groups of students and keeping everyone engaged - Communicating professionally with school staff and OTA leadership - Arriving on time and prepared for each program - Setting up and putting away equipment Why Coach With OTA ? OTA programs are designed to make sports fun and accessible for kids. We provide the program structure, equipment, and support. You bring the energy and leadership. It’s a great opportunity to gain hands-on experience working with children, build coaching and leadership skills, and earn extra money with a schedule that works particularly well for college students. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities What We’re Looking For You do not need to be an expert in every sport. We’re looking for people who: - Enjoy working with kids - Are energetic, patient, and dependable - Can confidently lead a group - Have reliable transportation - Communicate well - Have an interest in sports, fitness, coaching, or education - Can consistently commit to scheduled programs REQUIRED Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities - Ability to work effectively with children in a group setting - Dependable, punctual, and able to consistently report to scheduled programs - Strong communication and interpersonal skills - Ability to lead organized games, activities, and sports instruction - Ability to maintain a positive, safe, and engaging environment - Reliable transportation to program locations throughout the Lexington area - Ability to follow lesson plans, program procedures, and safety guidelines - Comfortable working independently and making appropriate decisions during programs Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 10/19/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
