    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650878": {
      "title": "Grants Accounting Assistant Director",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Grants Accounting Assistant Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Grants Accounting Assistant Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Grants Accounting Assistant Director Requisition Number RE56027 Working Title Assistant Director, Sponsored Projects Financial Administration Department Name 3A600:Research Financial Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 48 Salary Range $64,210-105,914/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 6 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements The essential job functions of this position require you to sit for extended periods of time; attend meetings in various building across campus; maintain high levels of concentration and mental attention; communicate effectively through verbal mediums; work extensively on computers; limited lifting of objects. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm. As a professional management position, additional time as needed to accomplish work goals and meet deadlines. Job Summary Research Financial Services ( RFS ) is seeking an experienced financial administration and operational leader to serve as Assistant Director, Sponsored Projects Financial Administration. This position provides strategic and operational leadership for core sponsored projects financial administration functions, including billing, financial reporting, new account creation, and related post-award financial activities. As a member of the Research Financial Services leadership team, the Assistant Director works closely with fellow Assistant Directors and cross-functional partners to coordinate operations, address complex challenges, align priorities, and support the strategic goals of the organization. The position is expected to exercise independent judgment, collaborate on office-wide initiatives, and contribute to solutions that support the overall success of Research Financial Services. The Assistant Director oversees a large and complex operational area, establishing performance expectations, setting priorities, developing supervisors and staff, and promoting accountability and operational excellence. The position is responsible for evaluating operational results, identifying process gaps and recurring issues, implementing corrective actions, and ensuring effective execution of sponsored projects financial administration activities. The successful candidate will possess strong leadership, financial, analytical, and problem-solving skills and a demonstrated ability to lead teams, improve processes, and drive organizational results in a complex environment. Experience in sponsored projects, grants management, higher education, or other highly regulated financial environments is beneficial; however, candidates with transferable experience in accounting, finance, financial operations, business administration, or operational management are encouraged to apply. Working collaboratively with stakeholders across the institution, the Assistant Director serves as a subject matter expert and resource, supporting the consistent interpretation and application of policies, procedures, and operational expectations. Through stakeholder engagement, financial stewardship, and process improvement, this position plays a key role in advancing the effectiveness of Research Financial Services and supporting the University’s sponsored projects mission. This position is eligible for a hybrid work schedule upon successful completion of the University’s orientation and on-boarding requirements and requires regular on-site presence to support operational leadership, staff development, collaboration, and stakeholder engagement. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Staff Leadership and Development; Project and Operational Management; Financial Administration; Accounting; Financial Analysis and Reporting; Advanced Microsoft Excel; SAP ; Tableau; Organizational Planning; Process Improvement; Problem Solving and Critical Thinking; Business Writing; Communication and Stakeholder Engagement. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Management and supervision; financial administration, accounting, finance, or business operations; financial reporting, analysis, and operational performance management; process improvement and project planning; experience working in higher education, sponsored projects administration, or other complex and highly regulated operational environments preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Tell me about a time when you were especially proactive in carrying out leadership responsibilities. What actions did you take and what was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) * Describe a situation where you identified a recurring operational issue, determined its root cause, and implemented a corrective action. What was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience analyzing operational or financial data to identify issues, inform decisions, or improve processes. Please include the reporting, data analysis, or business applications (for example: Excel, ERP systems, SAP, Workday, Tableau, Power BI, etc.) you have utilized and your experience level with each. (Open Ended Question) * Which of the following best describes your years of experience leading staff and/or operational functions within accounting, finance, business operations, grants administration, or a related environment? None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years * Describe your experience reviewing, interpreting, and applying policies, procedures, regulations, or organizational requirements to support operational decision-making and issue resolution. None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years * Which of the following best describes your years of experience working as part of a leadership team to resolve complex issues, make shared operational decisions, align priorities, and support the overall success of an organization beyond an individual department or functional area? None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650866": {
      "title": "Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development - Bracken County",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development - Bracken County Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development - Bracken County Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development - Bracken County Requisition Number RE55668 Working Title Department Name 81E08: KCES Region East Area 08 Work Location Brooksville, KY Grade Level 00 Salary Range Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education No set minimum requirements. Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No set minimum requirements. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Job-related travel including overnight stays; visiting clientele at sites throughout the county (including farms); standing/walking for long periods; handling of average-weight objects up to 25 lbs. Shift Monday-Friday (8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m.) with evenings and weekends as needed. Most weeks will exceed 40 hours. Job Summary Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development in Bracken County Location: Brooksville, KY The Extension Agent for 4-H Youth Development will work to provide leadership and management to the overall 4-H youth development programs for Bracken County. Agent responsibilities include: 1) implementing a well-rounded program that develops youth through school and community-based programs; 2) recruiting and training volunteers and leaders to work with youth; 3) utilizing and/or developing councils, advisory groups, and committees in programing around issues involving leadership development, community involvement, local government, community services and other forms of community economic development. All agents in a county will support the dissemination of useful and practical information on subjects relating to Agriculture, Family Consumer Sciences, 4-H and Community and Rural Development as outlined in the KRS statutes 164.605 to 164.675. State law requires a national and state criminal background check and a letter from the Cabinet for Health and Family Services stating the employee is clear to hire based on no findings of substantiated child abuse or neglect found through a background check of child abuse and neglect records as a condition of employment or involvement in this program. Resume, cover letter and transcripts are required at time of application. Visit the Extension Careers page: https://ces-personnel.ca.uky.edu/careers Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated ability to communicate orally and in writing with groups and individuals and through mass media. Ability to use the computer for program delivery and management. Ability to visit clientele at sites throughout the county. Ability to plan and teach educational programs. Demonstrated leadership and ability to serve as a positive role model. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree in Education, Agriculture, Family & Consumer Sciences, Social Science, or similar field of study. Driver’s License preferred Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree or expect to graduate within 6 months? yes no * What is your undergraduate GPA? Note: If you will receive your degree within 6 months, indicate your current GPA. If you have already completed a Master’s Degree please indicate that instead of your undergraduate GPA. Completed Master's 3.0-4.0 2.75-2.99 0- 2.74 * How many years experience (paid or non-paid) do you have working with youth? None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Indicate below the answer that best describes your experience with 4-H. Have been employed by the Cooperative Extension Service and worked with 4-H Have been a 4-H leader/4-H volunteer Was an active 4-H member Participated in some 4-H programs Have no involvement with 4-H * Describe your experience working with youth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you or a family member serve as a member on any county Extension District Board in Kentucky?  If yes, please state the family member’s name and the county for which either you or this individual serves as a member of the Extension District Board. (Open Ended Question) * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK jobs, UK's online employment system (ukjobs.uky.edu) Newspaper Handshake Received an email about the posting Social Media Friend or Family Journal of Extension Indeed.com Other online job board Other * Were you previously a UK Cooperative Extension summer intern? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver’s license and are you able to drive? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650862": {
      "title": "Student: Support Staff",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Support Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Support Staff Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Support Staff Requisition Number SE04477 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $15-$20 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience Hours per Week 10-20 Must be available for 3-5 shifts per week, with some weekend availability being a must. Shifts range anywhere from 2-6 hours. Only dinners during the week, with both brunch and dinner on Saturday and Sunday. Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Busser/Host positions available. Duties include - Greeting guests - Answering telephone - Taking reservations - Seating guests - Clearing and resetting tables - Necessary cleaning - Serving food - Assisting in a positive guest experience overall. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Applicants must - Possess excellent communication skills - Solid multi-tasking abilities - Dedicated work ethic - The ability to lift reasonably heavy items such as ice buckets and bus tubs - Be able to flourish and contribute to an extremely team-oriented environment. Candidates must react positively to being managed/coached and have the ability to remain efficient and calm during high pressure situations. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 10/12/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
