    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650845": {
      "title": "Pharmacist Clinical Staff/Shift-BSD/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacist Clinical Staff/Shift-BSD/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacist Clinical Staff/Shift-BSD/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacist Clinical Staff/Shift-BSD/UKHC Requisition Number RE54932 Working Title Pharmacist Clinical Staff/Shift-BSD/UKHC - Surgery Department Name H3330:Pharmacy Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 14 Salary Range $114,697-156,062/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Pharmacist Physical Requirements This position requires intermittently sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; and lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Also involves some exposure to risk of injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, cuts/punctures, and blood-borne or airborne pathogens. Shift This is a 7on/7off staffing model; days and evenings; Saturday through Friday. Requires some holidays in order to meet departmental needs. Job Summary This position provides decentralized patient care to a diverse and often high-acuity surgical population across trauma, emergency general surgery, vascular, colorectal, thoracic, oncologic, plastics, urology, otolaryngology, and orthopedic surgery services. Care setting includes surgical ICUs, progressive care units, acute care floors, and perioperative areas during first and second shift. Responsibilities include emergency response, pharmacokinetic and anticoagulation management, perioperative medication optimization, drug information support, and patient education. Opportunities include committee involvement and precepting of pharmacy residents and students. Candidates must graduate from an ACPE -accredited school or college of pharmacy, complete an ASHP -accredited PGY1 residency (or possess equivalent experience), and be eligible for Kentucky pharmacist licensure. Board certification in Pharmacotherapy ( BCPS ) or Critical Care Pharmacy ( BCCCP ), or board eligibility, is preferred Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong clinical skills; knowledge of inpatient drug distribution and dispensing; ability to prioritize; excellent communication skills; team mentality; desire to teach; and motivation are required to excel in this position. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience PharmD and ASHP PGY1 residency and/or PGY2 specialty residency preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you licensed or eligible to be licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have practicing as a licensed pharmacist? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Briefly describe your pharmacy experience. (Open Ended Question) * Have you completed or are you currently participating in an ASHP residency program? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650844": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Senior Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Community Pharmacy and Ryan White Services",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Senior Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Community Pharmacy and Ryan White Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Senior Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Community Pharmacy and Ryan White Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Senior Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Community Pharmacy and Ryan White Services Requisition Number DU14441 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $18.50/hr - $27.31/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education High School Required Related Experience 1 year Required License/Registration/Certification National Pharmacy Technician Certification thru either PTCB or ExCPT with CPhT designation and Registration with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire or on day one if previously registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a technician. Physical Requirements This position may require sitting at a computer workstation and performing tasks with repetitive motions; and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds. Possible exposure to hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, and blood-borne or airborne pathogens. May involve prolonged sitting or standing (often for 8–12 hour shifts), frequent walking, bending, and reaching. Must also be able to reach above or below waist level. Key requirements include having fine motor skills for handling small medication items, and clear communication/vision for dispensing and filling of medications. Shift Primarily covering shifts as needed including weekend shifts at the Community Pharmacy and Ryan White Services locations. Must be available to work during operating hours and days of operation which are subject to change based on location of assignment. Typical shifts are four to ten hour shifts and may cover day shifts and early/late evenings depending on location scheduled. May be required to work on some holidays which currently are being rotated by Ambulatory Pharmacy Services staff. Some weekend shifts are an expected part of the assignment which are typically during the hours of 8am-5pm. Shifts may be at KY Clinic Pharmacy, Beaumont Clinic Pharmacy, and Fountain Court Pharmacist Care Clinic in the Lexington, KY area. Job Summary This position provides patient care in a fast-paced community pharmacy setting across multiple Lexington, KY locations, including KY Clinic Pharmacy, Bluegrass Clinic Pharmacy at the Beaumont Center location, and the Fountain Court Pharmacist Care Team. Primary duties for the certified pharmacy technician (CPhT) include filling and distributing prescriptions in a busy retail-based setting. Certified Pharmacy Technicians may be allowed to complete other specialized duties as applicable by KY Board of Pharmacy law. These positions also support specialized programs including the Kentucky AIDS Drug Assistance Program, Ryan White Part C, Pharmacy Partners, and Mail Order services; and assist in our mission to ensure operational efficiency and high-quality customer service. The successful Pharmacy Senior Technician I will be reliable, punctual, works well within a team, and possesses exceptional communication and strong interpersonal skills. The ability and desire to work and grow in a fast-paced, complex, and ever-changing field within a dynamic and cutting-edge pharmacy is essential for individuals in this position. This role requires flexible shift coverage including weekend and may include some holiday rotations during operating hours which may vary by location. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability, excellent customer service and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Must be self-motivated and be able to stay on task. Must be reliable and punctual. This position requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and strong interpersonal skills to be applied with both patients and other medical professionals. Creates and maintains cultures where all staff delivers friendly, patient centered care. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Retail and/or Hospital pharmacy technician experience preferred but not required. Hired candidate must maintain licensure as CPhT from PTCB /ExCPT during employment in this position. The starting pay for this position was recently adjusted. The minimum hourly rate for this position will now be $18.50/hour. All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Please select the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience in a pharmacy. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your retail pharmacy and/or medicare billing experience. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have reliable transportation to get to an off-campus job? Yes No * Are you able to work evenings and weekends as needed? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650843": {
      "title": "Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Richmond Retail Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Richmond Retail Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Richmond Retail Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be sure to list all paid pharmacy technician and/or pharmacist intern work experience. Include Start and End dates for each job and average number of hour worked per week. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Richmond Retail Pharmacy Requisition Number DU14600 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $17.50 - $27.31 Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education High School plus Admitted to a College of Pharmacy Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification Registered with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacist Intern Physical Requirements May include standing for greater than 5 hours at a time and possibly walking several miles per day. May require the ability to reach items above shoulder level and be able to lift up to 25 pounds. Shift NOTE—this posting is primarily for an as needed (non-benefitted) pharmacist intern position in the new Richmond, KY location of UKHC Retail Pharmacies. Primarily covering shifts at the Richmond Retail Pharmacy located in Richmond, KY. Must be available to work during operating hours of the location which includes evening and weekend hours. Operating hours, schedule and shifts needed are subject to change based on location and scheduling needs of assignment area. Training shifts may be done in one of the Lexington, KY locations prior to opening of location. Transportation to Richmond location will be needed if selected for these locations. Job Summary Studen