      "title": "Amb/Retail Pharmacist/OnCall/UKHC - Hazard/Hindman NFV-JB Retail Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Amb/Retail Pharmacist/OnCall/UKHC - Hazard/Hindman NFV-JB Retail Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Amb/Retail Pharmacist/OnCall/UKHC - Hazard/Hindman NFV-JB Retail Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist/OnCall/UKHC - Hazard/Hindman NFV-JB Retail Pharmacy Requisition Number DU14598 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $50.34/hr -64.08/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education BS Pharmacy or Pharm D Required Related Experience 0 yrs. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed or eligible for license as a Pharmacist in Kentucky. Must be licensed in the State of KY on day one of employment and maintained in good standing throughout time in position. Physical Requirements May include standing for greater than 5 hours at a time. May require the ability to reach items above shoulder level and be able to lift up to 30 pounds. Shift NOTE —this posting is for an as needed (non-benefitted) pharmacist position in the Hazard/Hindman locations for UKHC Retail Pharmacies. Primarily covering shifts as needed including shifts at any of the Hazard(North Fork Valley) and Hindman (June Buchanan) UKHC retail pharmacy locations. Must be available to work during operating hours of the location. Operating hours, schedule and shifts needed are subject to change based on location and scheduling needs of assignment area. Job Summary Provide patient care in a fast-paced pharmacy setting. Compounds and dispenses medications and pharmaceutical supplies upon receiving written orders from physicians. Reviews and interprets prescriptions and drug profiles to ensure appropriate drug therapy has been prescribed and ensures that drug interactions are considered. Manage inventory and technician staff to provide excellent customer service. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Requires attention to detail and the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be reliable and punctual. This position also requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and interpersonal skills. Must be able to communicate and be understood in the English language. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Ambulatory/Retail Pharmacy Experience preferred. PharmD or BS from College of Pharmacy with eligibility to be licensed in KY. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a licensed pharmacist in the State of Kentucky? Yes No, but eligible for licensure No * Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your retail pharmacy and/or medicare billing experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please choose the answer that best describes your paid employment experience with any outpatient pharmacy. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
