      "title": "Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Retail  Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Retail  Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Retail  Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Retail/OnCall/UKHC - Retail  Pharmacy Requisition Number DU09964 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $18.50/hr - $27.31/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education High School Required Related Experience 1 year Required License/Registration/Certification National Pharmacy Technician Certification thru either PTCB or ExCPT with CPhT designation and Registration with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire or on day one if previously registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a technician. Physical Requirements This position may require sitting at a computer workstation and performing tasks with repetitive motions; and occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds. Must also be able to reach above or below waist level. Possible exposure to hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, and blood-borne or airborne pathogens. Shift Shifts may vary depending on location. Hours and days of week subject to change based on the needs and growth of the department. Requires occasional holiday and weekend rotations are part of the shifts. Number of hours scheduled per week may vary. Potential shifts and locations available will be discussed during the interview. Shifts may be at off campus locations in Lexington and Richmond, KY. If selected for one of these positions, reliable transportation will be needed. Job Summary Assists pharmacists in medicine preparation and distribution for the Retail Pharmacies operating under University of KY Pharmacy Services. Fills and dispenses prescriptions in a busy retail based setting. Requires attention to detail and the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be reliable and punctual. This position also requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and strong interpersonal skills. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability, excellent customer service and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Must be self-motivated and be able to stay on task. Must be reliable and punctual. This position requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and strong interpersonal skills to be applied with both patients and other medical professionals. Creates and maintains cultures where all staff delivers friendly, patient centered care. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Retail and/or Hospital pharmacy technician experience preferred but not required. Hired candidate must maintain licensure as CPhT from PTCB /ExCPT during employment in this position. The starting pay for this position was recently adjusted. The minimum hourly rate for this position will now be $18.50/hour. All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No The University of Kentucky HealthCare recognizes a set of values that guide us in our daily interactions. By applying for a position within UK Healthcare, you are indicating your commitment and expressing your agreement to our five values. These values are diversity, innovation, respect, compassion, and teamwork. Please choose one of the UK Healthcare values and give a specific example when you exhibited this quality in your professional experience. (Open Ended Question) Please select the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience in a pharmacy. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) Please describe your retail pharmacy and/or medicare billing experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650776": {
      "title": "Family Mentor",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Family Mentor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Family Mentor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Family Mentor Requisition Number RE56025 Working Title Family Mentor - Daviess Co. Department Name 8T110:College of Social Work Work Location Owensboro, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Drivers License Physical Requirements Sitting and/or standing for long periods of time; pushing, pulling, carrying objects up to 25 lbs.; performing repetitive motion tasks; regular job-related travel. Shift Monday-Friday 8:00 am – 4:30 pm (37.5 hrs/week); and flexible schedule as needed. Job Summary This position is 100% grant funded and the primary work location is in Daviess County, KY. The College of Social Work Training Resource Center is seeking a Sobriety Treatment and Recovery Team ( START ) Family Mentor to serve in Daviess County. Family Mentors, in collaboration with DCBS social workers and the Sobriety Treatment and Recovery Team ( START ), are responsible for providing mentoring to clients receiving substance abuse treatment. Family Mentors will serve as team members in planning, supporting and implementing strategies for prevention and building strong partnerships with community providers to help parents. Family Mentors assess client situations, capabilities, and problems to determine what services are required to meet their needs. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Customer service skills are necessary. Extensive driving is required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No P