    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650770": {
      "title": "Industry Extension Specialist II",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Industry Extension Specialist II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Industry Extension Specialist II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Industry Extension Specialist II Requisition Number RE56023 Working Title Instructional Lab Manager Department Name 8H090:OISTL/Engineering Distance Learning Work Location Paducah, KY Grade Level 46 Salary Range $53,061-87,526/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience More than six months, but less than one year Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements none Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm (40 hours/week) Job Summary The individual will support the educational missions at the University of Kentucky Pigman College of Engineering Paducah Campus, with primary responsibilities in instruction and laboratory development in Laser and Photonics Engineering Technology. Duties include, but are not limited to: Teaching undergraduate-level courses in Laser and Photonics Engineering and Technology, with an emphasis on hands-on, laboratory-based learning. Developing laboratory instructional materials and activities, and managing laboratory facilities to ensure safe operations and compliance with applicable safety and regulatory requirements. Managing the purchasing, inventory, maintenance, and organization of equipment, supplies, and materials associated with the laser and photonics laboratories. Participating in K–12, industry, and community outreach programs and activities hosted on campus. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Applicants should demonstrate strong technical expertise in Laser and Photonics Engineering, along with excellent written and verbal communication skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Applicants should hold an MS degree in Laser and Photonics Engineering or a closely related field. Candidates without an MS degree but with extensive relevant industrial experience will also be considered. Deadline to Apply 11/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please explain what course/s you would be interested in teaching. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
