    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650748": {
      "title": "Business Analytics Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Business Analytics Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Business Analytics Lecturer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Business Analytics Lecturer Requisition Number FE05045 Working Title Department Name 8F000:College of Business and Economics Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education A master’s degree or higher in business analytics or another appropriate discipline with substantial analytics content Required Related Experience Demonstrated knowledge of business analytics concepts and methods. The ability to teach and communicate effectively with students from varied academic and professional backgrounds. Proficiency with relevant analytics software or a demonstrated ability and commitment to develop the software expertise required for assigned courses. A commitment to effective teaching, student success, and continuous improvement. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Gatton College of Business and Economics at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a full-time Business Analytics Lecturer with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The selected candidate will be appointed to a full-time 9-month, non-tenure eligible faculty position for an initial two-year period that has the potential for renewal and for promotion to Senior Lecturer after five years. We seek an accomplished and student-focused colleague who is passionate about teaching business analytics and preparing students to solve practical, data-driven business problems. The successful candidate will contribute to business analytics instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels and support programs associated with the college’s Business Analytics Center. Teaching responsibilities total 7 to 8 courses per academic year (depending on other responsibilities). The Gatton College of Business and Economics at the University of Kentucky contains five academic units: The Von Allmen School of Accountancy, the Department of Economics, the John Maze Steward Department of Finance and Quantitative Methods, the Department of Management, and the Department of Marketing and Supply Chain. The selected candidate will be affiliated with the academic unit that most closely aligns with the candidate’s education, professional experience, and areas of expertise. Primary Responsibilities The primary responsibility of this position is high-quality instruction. Depending on the successful candidate’s expertise and college needs, teaching assignments may include: Introduction to business analytics Business intelligence and data visualization Data management and SQL Data modeling Data mining and predictive analytics Spreadsheet-based business analysis Undergraduate business analytics capstone Other analytics or business courses consistent with the candidate’s qualifications Courses may be delivered in face-to-face, online, or hybrid formats. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain relevant course content, assess student learning, provide timely feedback, and remain current with developments in business analytics practice and technology. The position also includes service responsibilities that may involve: Supporting the administration and continued development of undergraduate and graduate business analytics programs Advising or mentoring students interested in analytics careers Supporting experiential learning and industry-based analytics projects Contributing to a business analytics lab or other student-learning initiatives Providing analytics or technology instruction to faculty, staff, or students Advising a student organization related to business analytics Participating in college and university service Specific teaching and service assignments will be determined in consultation with the successful candidate and may be adjusted to reflect program needs, enrollment, and the candidate’s qualifications. Required Qualifications A master’s degree or higher in business analytics or another appropriate discipline with substantial analytics content Demonstrated knowledge of business analytics concepts and methods The ability to teach and communicate effectively with students from varied academic and professional backgrounds Proficiency with relevant analytics software or a demonstrated ability and commitment to develop the software expertise required for assigned courses A commitment to effective teaching, student success, and continuous improvement Preferred Qualifications A terminal degree in an appropriate discipline. Relevant professional experience applying analytics in business, government, consulting, or another organizational setting Prior teaching or training experience at the undergraduate, graduate, professional, or corporate level Experience teaching in face-to-face and online environments Experience developing courses, curricula, or experiential learning projects Experience working with employer partners or incorporating real-world data and business problems into instruction Proficiency with tools such as Excel, SQL , Tableau, Power BI, JMP Pro, Python, R, or other contemporary analytics technologies The Business Analytics Center The Business Analytics Center serves as an interdisciplinary resource for analytics education and engagement across the Gatton College of Business and Economics. Its academic offerings have included an undergraduate Business Analytics minor and a Graduate Certificate in Business Analytics. The lecturer will have opportunities to contribute to the continued development of these and other analytics initiatives. The Gatton College of Business and Economics The Gatton College of Business and Economics prepares principled leaders for the global economy, produces influential research, and supports economic growth in Kentucky and beyond. The AACSB -accredited college offers undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs in face-to-face and online formats. Faculty and staff contribute to the college’s mission through teaching, research, service, outreach, and engagement with the business community. Location The University of Kentucky is located in Lexington, Kentucky, in the heart of the Bluegrass Region. Lexington offers a combination of educational, cultural, recreational, and professional opportunities and is conveniently located near Louisville and Cincinnati. Appointment and Benefits This is a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty appointment with a nine-month contract. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. Application Procedure Applicants should submit (1) a letter of application describing the applicant’s interest in the position and relevant teaching or professional experience and (2) current curriculum vitae or resume. In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three professional references when prompted in the application. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references later in the selection process. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions concerning the position may be directed to: Tom Groleau Director, Business Analytics Center Gatton College of Business and Economics University of Kentucky Tom.Groleau@uky.edu Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650742": {
      "title": "Athletic Ticket Office Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Athletic Ticket Office Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Athletic Ticket Office Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Athletic Ticket Office Student Assistant Requisition Number DU11635 Department Name 12D00:UKAA - Administrative Support Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range Starting at $10.00 per hour. Higher rate possible for working special events and football game days Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High School Degree; Must be currently Enrolled/Registered student attending the University of Kentucky. Required Related Experience High School Degree & some customer service experience. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements To be able to lift, push or pull objects up to 25 lbs. Shift Office hours: Monday – Friday may be available based on office needs. Athletic Events: Weeknights and weekend athletic events: Required to work all home football games and select athletic events for all 7 other UK Athletic ticketed sports throughout the season, and other events hosted by UK Athletics. Job Summary In accordance with established policies and procedures, provide exceptional customer service over the phone and in person at the ticket office. Answer customer inquiries and process ticket sales via phone, mail, and walk-up orders. Responsible for daily reconciliation of ticket sales and payments. Other assignments may include but are not limited to mobile ticket help zones, the compliance pass entrance, will call distribution and scanning operations. Must be able/willing to work some nights and weekends as needed for events, including working all home football games. Must have reliable transportation to and from athletic events. Perform other tasks as assigned by Ticket Office staff. Please attach a resume, cover letter and a copy of your UK class schedule. Please attach a copy of your class schedule under specific request one. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Experience in a customer service position, both in person and over the phone. Familiarity with MS Office applications (Word/Excel). Applicants should be dependable, punctual, and possess effective communication and problem solving skills, as well as strong attention to detail. Must have a customer-friendly personality and project a positive image of the University and the Athletics Department to fans, donors, staff, students, alumni, and other groups. Must be able to multi-task and work in a fast-paced environment Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Some college education & 1-2 Years Customer Service Experience Deadline to Apply 03/19/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * As part of the Southeastern Conference, candidates considered for staff or coaching positions within UK Athletics are required to disclose any unethical conduct. Please answer the below questions regarding your personal NCAA record. Have you ever been charged with a violation of NCAA 10.1 Unethical Conduct by the NCAA or any NCAA member institution? Yes No * Have you ever been charged with a NCAA Level I, II or III, secondary or major violation? Yes No * Are you currently involved in any pending NCAA investigation, charges and/or violations of NCAA legislation? Yes No * Has the NCAA Committee on Infractions ever issued you show-cause penalty? Yes No * If you answered yes, to either of the previous two questions, please list all violations in which you’ve been charged or were involved. If you answered no to both of the previous questions please type: N/A (Open Ended Question) * I agree to and understand that failure to disclose any NCAA violation or false information regarding my NCAA compliance history will result in removal of my application for consideration. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650740": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Scholar (Jaramillo Lab)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Post Doctoral Scholar (Jaramillo Lab) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Post Doctoral Scholar (Jaramillo Lab) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Post Doctoral Scholar (Jaramillo Lab) Requisition Number DU15154 Department Name 7K300:PHARMACEUTICAL SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range Commensurate with Experience Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD in neuroscience, pharmacology, or equivalent field. Required Related Experience Competitive candidates will have experience using rodent behavioral models and/or the techniques listed above, as well as a record of research productivity. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time, stooping, bending, lifting, reaching; carrying/pushing/pulling up to 15 lbs., ability to use step ladder to reach above head Shift M-F , with occasional evenings and/or weekends due to experiments Job Summary The Jaramillo lab in the Pharmaceutical Sciences Department in the College of Pharmacy is recruiting a Postdoctoral Scholar to lead research investigating negative affective disturbances in abstinence. The successful candidate will contribute to NIH - NIAAA funded (AA032581) studies investigating neurocircuits and behavioral mechanisms that become dysregulated in animal models for alcohol use using in vivo fiber photometry, ex vivo slice physiology, chemogenetics, immunofluorescence, and intracranial pharmacological infusions. Current projects focus on the parabrachial extended amygdala circuit, with an emphasis on neuropeptides ( PACAP and CRF ) and stress. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, leading manuscript preparation (e.g., writing, data analysis, and interpretation), mentoring trainees, grant development, presenting at scientific conferences, and developing independent research questions. Applicants must hold a PhD in a relevant field (e.g., neuroscience, pharmacology). Competitive candidates will have experience using rodent behavioral models and/or the techniques listed above, as well as a record of research productivity. The successful candidate will receive individually tailored mentoring toward an independent career in the field of their choice. Individuals interested in industry will have opportunities to interact with industry experts (e.g., through departmental seminars). To apply, submit a CV, a cover letter briefly describing their research experience and career goals, and the contact information and email addresses of three professional references via the application website. Please add the reference contact information in your application. The position start date is flexible. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Lab experience recommended but not required: rodent behavioral models, in vivo fiber photometry, ex vivo slice physiology, chemogenetics, immunofluorescence, and/or intracranial pharmacological infusions Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650739": {
      "title": "Administrative Support Associate I",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Support Associate I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Support Associate I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Support Associate I Requisition Number RE56019 Working Title Membership Specialist Department Name 14300:Alumni Engagement Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time; and looking at computer for long periods of time. Effectively communicating with individuals from various backgrounds. Shift Monday – Friday; 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Job Summary The UK Alumni Association is seeking a qualified individual for their Administrative Support Associate I position. This position is responsible for greeting visitors to the King Alumni House, answering the main association telephone line, receiving and responding to inquiries from association members and all alumni, processing Life Member payments, creating and updating alumni records to ensure accuracy, reporting data on member acquisition and retention, providing outstanding customer service, providing staff support for various programs and activities, and staffing events when called on. The culture within the Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement ( PAE ) is built on our shared core values CoMMIT– Collaboration, Communication, Mission Driven, Mutual Respect, Innovation and Transparency. By applying for a position within UK PAE , you are indicating your commitment and expressing your agreement to our six values. It is important you share these values in order to be part of our committed team! Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Microsoft Office Suite, Excel, ability to learn new software systems and databases Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s Degree, Three Years Related Experience. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate the number of years of full time, paid work experience in which you were directly responsible for scheduling appointments and meetings. More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years None * Please indicate the number of years of full time, paid work experience in which you were directly responsible for preparing letters and spreadsheets using Microsoft Word and Excel. More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years None * Rate your level of expertise in using Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Windows, Excel, and PowerPoint). None Basic Average Proficient Expert * How many years of experience do you have in Word using the following functions: mail merge, tracking changes, creating advanced documents, etc.? None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe your work experience providing customer service to the public. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your work experience handling money and/or sensitive personal information. (Open Ended Question) * Describe a specific work experience in which you demonstrated initiative. (Open Ended Question) * The Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement (PAE) recognizes a set of values that guide us in our daily interactions. These values are collaboration, communication, mission driven, mutual respect, innovation and transparency. Please choose one of the PAE values and give a specific example when you exhibited this quality in your professional experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650667": {
      "title": "Scientist III",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Scientist III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Scientist III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Scientist III Requisition Number RE56011 Working Title Department Name 7H075:Center for Health Engagement and Transformation Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 48 Salary Range $64,210-105,914/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements May require sitting for long periods Shift Primarily Days Monday – Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm, some Evenings, Weekends are possible Job Summary The Markey Cancer Center has an opening for a Scientist III position in Dr. Laurie McLouth’s supportive oncology and cancer survivorship research lab. This position will primarily entail leading scholarly dissemination, supporting proposal development, developing new research protocols and evaluating preliminary data, and supporting project direction for ongoing and new extramurally-funded projects. Excellent written and verbal communication skills are required. Must be self-motivated, highly attentive to detail, and exercise good leadership and collaboration. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience PhD in Clinical or Health Psychology preferred. Experience conducting psych-oncology and psychosocial intervention research preferred. Experience conducting longitudinal data analyses preferred. Deadline to Apply 11/08/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list your years of experience designing and implementing research protocols for cancer research. (Open Ended Question) * Please choose the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience in grant writing. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Please indicate your amount of paid, full-time work experience with research project management. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years * Have you ever written and submitted an extramural grant application as PI? (Open Ended Question) * Please list your years of experience designing and implementing research protocols for psychosocial, health psychology, or behavioral medicine research. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Writing Sample Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
