    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650666": {
      "title": "APP Certified Nurse Midwife/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | APP Certified Nurse Midwife/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support APP Certified Nurse Midwife/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title APP Certified Nurse Midwife/UKHC Requisition Number RE55319 Working Title APP Certified Nurse Midwife Department Name MG33T:OBGYN-GEORGETOWN Work Location Georgetown, KY Grade Level 15 Salary Range $117,736-183,667/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MSN (Master’s requirement does not apply to those who completed qualifying education by July 1, 2005) Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Advanced Practice Registered Nurse ( APRN ) with Certified Nurse-Midwife ( CNM ) certification Physical Requirements sitting, standing, lifting, etc. Shift Mostly Monday-Friday, days, call coverage and weekend/evening shifts as required Job Summary Under a collaborative agreement with a physician; the certified nurse midwife ( CNM ) is an Advanced Practice Provider who, in collaboration with an attending physician, is responsible for the assessment, plan, implementation and evaluation of nurse midwifery care delivered to antepartum, intrapartum and postpartum, and newborn patients. The CNM performs physical exams, collects and documents data, manages labor and spontaneous delivery, conducts diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, orders and schedules laboratory studies and professional consultations, and prescribes appropriate interventions and medications. The CNM practice includes primary as well as specialized care provided at UK Women’s Health-Georgetown and Georgetown Community Hospital. The CNM promotes safety and quality in clinical care, contributes to research and teaching, and provides leadership in the organization. Per the OB/ GYN Practice Plan, all CNMs are required to take 8 call shifts per month. 8 call shifts is the equivalent of 4 weeknights plus one weekend per month. i.e. one weeknight per week = 4 shifts/month; All day Saturday & Sunday = 4 shifts/month. Weekday work, whether on L&D or in the outpatient location, is considered part of the normal workweek and not considered a call shift. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently licensed by the state of Kentucky as a Nurse Practitioner or eligible to obtain license within the next nine months?\n\n(In order to be eligible, applicant must have graduated from an accredited program or be scheduled to graduate within six months of the application.) Yes No * Do you have a Nurse Midwife certification or are eligible to obtain this certification by date of hire? Yes No * Per the OB/GYN Practice Plan, all CNMs are required to take 8 call shifts per month. 8 call shifts is the equivalent of 4 weeknights plus one weekend per month. i.e. one weeknight per week = 4 shifts/month; All day Saturday & Sunday = 4 shifts/month. Weekday work, whether on L&D or in the outpatient location, is considered part of the normal workweek and not considered a call shift. Are you able to meet this requirement? Yes No * Are you aware that this position is located in Georgetown, KY? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650659": {
      "title": "Truck Driver",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Truck Driver Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Truck Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Truck Driver Requisition Number RE55396 Working Title Department Name 3CP12:Phys Plt-Trucking Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects over 50lbs; Job related travel; Loud noises; Temperature extremes; Hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste; Animal handling (including carcasses); Subject to pungent smells. Shift Typically Monday – Friday: 7:30am – 4:15pm; additional hours per workload/project demands. Job Summary Reporting to the Trucking Supervisor, this position is responsible for the transport of materials (freight/recycling) to and from specified locations, including loading and unloading vehicles; manually picking up and moving various materials (i.e.) recycling, waste, surplus equipment/furniture and special events resources, etc., from locations on/off campus via stairways, elevators, and dock locations; and ensuring excellent customer service. Multiple positions available. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until the deadline date or until all positions are filled which could be prior to deadline date listed. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities MS Windows/Office; KRONOS ; Knowledge of Mechanics; Driver’s Courses Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience HS + 2 years professional driving experience Deadline to Apply 10/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires the flexibility to work varying shifts and overtime as needed. Are you able to meet this requirement? Yes No * Do you have a current valid KY driver's license and can you drive? Yes No * Do you have a valid Kentucky Commercial Driver's License (CDL)? Yes No * Please indicate your number of years of work experience as a truck driver. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please describe your experience as it relates to this job posting. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
