    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650652": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Requisition Number RE55672 Working Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC – Central Pharmacy 1st Shift - ELIGIBLE FOR RECRUITMENT BONUS Department Name H3330:Pharmacy Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 07 Salary Range $18.50-27.31/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Nationally certified Pharmacy Technician by either PTCB ( PTCE ) or NHA (ExCPT); Registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire. Physical Requirements This position requires use of a computer workstation, completion of tasks with repetitive motions, and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 50 pounds. This position may require personnel to wear personal protective equipment to reduce risk of exposure to work-related hazards (e.g. handling of hazardous medications). Shift 7 days on/7 days off; with some holiday requirements Job Summary The Inpatient Pharmacy Senior Technician is responsible for maintaining stock inventory, including participating in the ordering process and ensuring proper storage and dating; processing, dispensing and delivering patient specific orders to assigned areas with timeliness and efficiency; replenishing automated medication dispensing cabinets; assisting in the training of newly hired technicians, interns and student learners, and supporting the department with a patient-centered approach. This position is eligible for a recruitment bonus. Additional details will be provided during the hiring process should your application be selected to move forward. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital/retail pharmacy technician and/or healthcare customer service experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician? Yes No * Please indicate the amount of paid pharmacy technician experience you have working in either an inpatient hospital and/or retail pharmacy setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650631": {
      "title": "Research Operational Excellence Manager",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Operational Excellence Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Operational Excellence Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Operational Excellence Manager Requisition Number RE56007 Working Title Department Name 40100:VP of Research Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 49 Salary Range $73,861-121,888/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time. Repetitive movements common with office work. Shift Monday-Friday 8:00 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. Job Summary Lead Enterprise-Wide Continuous Improvement in Research Administration The University of Kentucky is seeking a Research Operational Excellence Manager to join the Research Administration enterprise. This position will lead the development, implementation, and sustainment of Lean principles, continuous improvement initiatives, and operational excellence strategies across Research Administration. The role serves as the organization’s internal Lean facilitator, coach, and change agent, partnering with leadership, faculty, and staff to improve service delivery, reduce administrative burden, enhance operational effectiveness, and support the university’s research mission. What You’ll Do Develop and execute a comprehensive Lean and continuous improvement strategy across Research Administration. Lead enterprise-wide improvement initiatives that enhance service delivery, reduce inefficiencies, improve cycle times, and strengthen operational effectiveness. Facilitate cross-functional process improvement efforts, fostering collaboration and scalable approaches to organizational change. Establish methodologies, standards, and governance for process mapping, analysis, redesign, and implementation. Lead complex process analyses to identify waste, bottlenecks, redundancies, and opportunities for sustainable improvement. Oversee enterprise change management efforts, including stakeholder engagement, communication planning, readiness, adoption, and reinforcement strategies. Establish performance measurement frameworks, key performance indicators, executive reporting, and benefit realization methodologies. Lead and govern a portfolio of transformation and continuous improvement projects, ensuring alignment with organizational priorities and successful implementation. Develop organizational capability in Lean methodologies through coaching, education, communities of practice, and workforce development programs. What You’ll Bring Expertise in Lean principles, continuous improvement methodologies, and organizational transformation. Strong project management, facilitation, and strategic planning skills. Experience leading complex cross-functional initiatives and influencing stakeholders at multiple organizational levels. Knowledge of process analysis, root cause analysis, process redesign, and process engineering techniques. Ability to develop and communicate performance metrics, dashboards, and data-driven recommendations. Excellent communication, leadership coaching, conflict resolution, and stakeholder engagement skills. Strong organizational, prioritization, documentation, and change management capabilities. Minimum Requirements Master’s degree 5 years of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to shape and advance operational excellence across a large and complex research administration enterprise. Ability to partner directly with research leadership and contribute to strategic institutional priorities. Opportunity to build a culture of continuous improvement and develop organizational capability in Lean methodologies. Hybrid work eligibility with approval. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? As research activity, regulatory complexity, and service expectations continue to evolve, Research Administration is focused on improving efficiency, reducing administrative burden, and delivering consistent, high-quality support to faculty and research staff. This role will help establish the frameworks, governance, and continuous improvement culture necessary to support those priorities. The Research Operational Excellence Manager will play a key role in advancing enterprise transformation initiatives, improving operational performance, and ensuring that process improvements remain sustainable and aligned with the University’s strategic research goals. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Lean Enterprise Toyota Production System Continuous Improvement Operational Excellence Process Engineering Quality Management Project Management Organizational Development Data Analytics Change Management Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 11/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe a process improvement initiative that you led or played a significant role in. What was the problem, what actions did you take, and what was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) * Describe a situation where you identified the root cause of a recurring problem. What approach did you use to analyze the issue, implement corrective actions, and ensure the improvement was sustained over time? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650598": {
      "title": "STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent Pool",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent Pool Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent Pool Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent Pool Requisition Number TE09294 Department Name 3J532:STEPS Temporary Employment Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00 - $21.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Required Related Experience At least 1 year of related experience in office/clerical duties. Required License/Registration/Certification Physical Requirements Ability to regularly sit for extended periods of time at a computer workstation and perform tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing), and walk extensively throughout the university, occasionally with objects weighing up to 25 lbs. Shift Typically Monday through Friday, varying shift hours between 8:00 am and 5:00 pm; hours and days of week subject to change to meet job and departmental business needs. Hours per week can range from 15 to 40 hours worked per week. Job Summary Looking to grow your administrative career in a dynamic and collaborative environment? We are building a pool of talented STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent to support a variety of departments with essential day-to-day operations. This is a great opportunity to showcase your organizational skills, customer service mindset, and attention to detail while keeping offices running smoothly. About the Opportunity: This is a pool position, which means qualified candidates will be considered for current and future temporary or project-based assignments across multiple departments. Assignments may vary in length, scope, and responsibilities, offering valuable experience and exposure to different teams and functions. As a STEPS Flex Office Administrative Support Talent , you would serve as a key point of contact for daily office activities and provide a wide range of administrative, operational, and customer support services. What You May Do: Serve as the first point of contact by greeting visitors, answering phones, and responding to emails and inquiries and ensure prompt, professional communication Manage calendars, schedule appointments, and coordinate meetings and events Support daily office operations, including mail and package distribution and front desk activities Route forms, requests, and communications to ensure timely processing and workflow Assist with purchasing, payment processing, and basic financial tracking Maintain organized filing systems, records, and document management processes Coordinate logistics for meetings, events, and engagement activities (e.g., scheduling, catering, communications) Assist with onboarding activities, including workspace readiness and basic access coordination Maintain office supplies, promotional materials, and inventory Support general administrative projects What You Bring: Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Excellent customer service and communication skills Ability to prioritize tasks and manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) Professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment Ability to work both independently and collaboratively If you enjoy supporting others, staying organized, and being part of a team that keeps things running efficiently, we encourage you to apply! Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Excellent customer service and communication skills Ability to prioritize tasks and manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) Professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment Ability to work both independently and collaboratively Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 2+ years of related experience in office/clerical duties. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This application is for a temporary pool position. STEPS temporary positions can end at any point in time and schedules could vary from 15 to 40 hours per week. Are you willing/able to work in this capacity? Yes No * Rate your level of expertise in using Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Windows, Excel, and PowerPoint). None Basic Average Proficient Expert * How many years of paid administrative work experience do you have? (i.e. responsible for administrative tasks of data entry, mailings, greeting guests, or other activities requiring organization and communication). None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Exceptional customer service is a key part of all STEPS positions. What does exceptional customer service mean to you? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650581": {
      "title": "Nursing Care Technician/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Nursing Care Technician/UKHC Requisition Number RE55412 Working Title NCT / CNA - MCC FLR 11T2 PAV A Department Name H7700: Cancer Services-Inpatient Pav A Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $18.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Have one or more of the following: 1. Kentucky Registered State Registered Nurse Assistant ( SRNA ), for Emergency Department (ED)- KY Registered State Registered Nurse Assistant ( SRNA ) or Emergency Medical Technician ( EMT ) 2. Registered Nurse (RN) nursing student who has completed first fundamental course and a clinical 3. Military Medic 4. current/active Licensed Practical Nurse ( LPN ) license 5. Acquired Nursing Care Technician ( NCT ) competencies through continuous employment at the University of Kentucky; 6. Successful completion of the Earn While You Learn NCT Training Program within 8 weeks of hire; plus American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid at time of hire, or completion of certification during Earn While You Learn NCT Training Program. Physical Requirements This position requires regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds; and standing or walking with objects weighing up to 10 pounds; occasionally requires standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds and/or working in confined spaces. Also involves some exposure to risk of injury from moving, lifting, or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to loud noises, temperature extremes, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, radiation, burns, cuts/punctures, blood-borne or airborne pathogens, and/or combative/violent people. Shift Must be able to work three 12.5-hour shifts per week (7:00 a.m. – 7:30 p.m.) Will also be required to work some weekends and holidays. Job Summary This position works one-on-one with a Registered Nurse (RN) to complete delegated tasks and provide direct patient care such as: obtain vital signs, phlebotomy, documentation, assist with ADL’s (activities of daily living), order and stock supplies, respond to patient call lights, unit orientation, and patient admission, transfer, and discharge. Positions may also involve moving patients from bed to wheelchair or stretcher, or stretcher to treatment/surgical tables. Handling of specimens and delivery to labs and preparation of patients for surgical procedures may also be required. The primary responsibilities for this position consist of providing prompt, compassionate, and patient centered care in a collaborative, team-oriented work environment. This dynamic environment supports collaborative efforts among the nursing staff and the teams of physicians to increase communication, follow through, and enhance patient outcomes and satisfaction. This includes utilization of the nursing process in conjunction with a comprehensive patient-centered plan of care, ensuring patient satisfaction and adhering to University policies and procedures as well as federal, state and local regulations. In addition, the essential functions for this position include the ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis, as well as stand, walk, and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Please apply for any and all positions for which you feel qualified. If you do not apply for a specific position, you cannot be considered for the position . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be compassionate, honest, trustworthy, and have a strong work ethic. Must enjoy working in a team, but also be able to take direction and communicate effectively with staff, patients, and their family members independently. In addition, must also be confident and enjoy working in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of CPR and basic concept of abnormal vital sign parameters is a must. Candidate will also need strong organizational, prioritization, basic computer navigation skills, and a working knowledge of the Internet. Valid American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider at time of hire is required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Previous hospital experience is preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select which of the following options best represents your related educational and/or related professional nursing experience RN Nursing student who has completed the first clinical nursing course (class and clinical) of nursing school A valid, current Kentucky State Registered Nursing Assistant Certificate Experience as a military medic Active LPN license Acquired Nursing Care Technician (NCT) competencies through continuous employment in a NCT role at University of Kentucky (For Emergency Department positions ONLY)  Emergency Medical Technician Certificate None * Are you currently a Nursing Care Technician that works at UK Chandler or Good Samaritan Hospital? Yes No * Please indicate the number of years of paid work experience you have as a Nursing Care Technician and/or a State Registered Nursing Assistant (SRNA) in which you were directly responsible for patient care in a hospital. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please describe a difficult situation you handled successfully. (Open Ended Question) * How much direct experience do you have using a computer (e.g. keyboarding, data entry, and e-mail)? None More than 0, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Will you be able to obtain a Basic Life Support (BLS) certification prior to your start date? Yes No * If hired, can you provide proof that you are at least 18 years of age at start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
