    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650540": {
      "title": "Research Analyst",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Analyst Requisition Number RE56006 Working Title Department Name 81060:PLANT AND SOIL SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 42 Salary Range $17.76-28.43/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 lbs. Sitting for long periods of time. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00-4:30 37.5 hours/week Job Summary Advance Data-Driven Solutions for Sustainable Agriculture and Environmental Stewardship The University of Kentucky is seeking a Research Analyst to join the Agriculture and Environmental Informatics Laboratory . This position will support innovative research focused on precision agriculture, digital soil mapping, soil health, and environmental informatics. The Research Analyst will contribute to the development and implementation of data-driven solutions by collecting, managing, and analyzing complex soil, landscape, and plant datasets while collaborating with researchers, stakeholders, and trainees on a variety of projects, publications, and grant initiatives. What You’ll Do Conduct research experiments and collect data from laboratory, field, proximal sensing, and remote sensing sources. Prepare samples and analyze laboratory, field, and geospatial datasets to support research objectives. Develop and maintain project databases and metadata to ensure high-quality data management and accessibility. Assist with grant proposal development, manuscript preparation, and dissemination of research findings. Support laboratory and field operations, including equipment, workflow coordination, and safety compliance. Coordinate and supervise student workers and trainees, providing guidance on laboratory procedures, field activities, and safety practices. Collaborate with faculty, researchers, industry partners, and other stakeholders on projects related to sustainable agriculture and natural resource management. What You’ll Bring Knowledge of precision agriculture, digital soil mapping, soil health research, or related agricultural and environmental applications. Experience with programming and data analysis tools such as R, Python, Shell scripting, GIS , or related technologies. Ability to collect, manage, and interpret large, high-resolution datasets from multiple sources. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow experimental protocols and research procedures. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Planning, organization, and laboratory management skills. Knowledge of laboratory safety practices and commitment to maintaining a safe research environment. Ability to mentor and support students and trainees while promoting accuracy, timeliness, and compliance with procedures. Minimum Requirements Master’s degree No related experience required What’s In It for You Opportunity to contribute to impactful research addressing real-world challenges in sustainable agriculture and environmental stewardship. Exposure to a broad portfolio of projects involving precision agriculture, geospatial modeling, soil health, soil carbon and nutrient modeling, spectroscopy, and remote sensing. Opportunities to collaborate with farmers, crop consultants, industry partners, government agencies, and researchers from other institutions. Professional growth through participation in scientific publications, grant development, training, and research innovation. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? The Agriculture and Environmental Informatics Laboratory is expanding efforts to develop data-driven tools that support sustainable agricultural production and natural resource management. As research initiatives continue to grow across precision agriculture, soil health, digital soil mapping, and environmental monitoring, this role provides critical support for advancing research goals and translating data into practical solutions. This position offers an opportunity to contribute across multiple innovative projects rather than a single research initiative, helping strengthen collaborations, accelerate scientific discovery, and support the development of technologies that benefit producers, researchers, and communities. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Handling remote sensing data using GIS Coding machine learning algorithms Effective communication and teamwork mindset Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience PhD degree or postdoc training in Precision Agriculture, Soil Science, Computer Science, Earth Science or closely related fields Experience in writing publications/grant applications Experience in field work (soil, water, and/or crop sampling, and/or proximal sensing data in field) Proficiency using open-source geospatial libraries in Python or R Experience in supercomputing Proficiency in developing machine learning algorithms or infrastructure Experience with cloud computing/ API infrastructure (Google Earth Engine, OpenGeo etc.) Part 107 Certificate Experience in designing a flight path, operating drone flights, processing drone data Experience in remote sensing analysis Experience with machine learning / artificial intelligence applications and coding Deadline to Apply 11/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid  Driver's License, and can you drive? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650524": {
      "title": "Administrative Research Assistant Pr",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Research Assistant Pr Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Research Assistant Pr Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Research Assistant Pr Requisition Number RE56004 Working Title Department Name 40526:Interdisciplinary Human Develo Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 43 Salary Range $19.56-31.29/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements While there are physical, psychosocial and cognitive requirements of the position, the job duties can be accommodated for essential functions being completed in a variety of ways. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm (40 hrs/wk) Job Summary The Human Development Institute ( HDI ) at the University of Kentucky is Kentucky’s Center on Disability. HDI is seeking an Administrative Research Assistant Pr to join our team and support the Kentucky Alternate Assessment Project. The Kentucky Alternate Assessment Project ( KAAP ) manages statewide academic and career-readiness assessments for Kentucky students with significant cognitive disabilities. The project supports compliance with ESSA and IDEA requirements, research-based instruction, and participation in Kentucky’s school accountability system. The responsibilities of this position include: Technical Editing & Quality Assurance: Edit, proofread, format, and quality-check assessment materials and project resources for accuracy, clarity, accessibility, and compliance. Technical Assistance & Customer Support: Provide technical assistance and support to educators, district personnel, and other stakeholders. Resource and Training Material Development: Develop and maintain user-friendly training materials, guides, FAQs, presentations, and online resources. Assessment Program Support and Documentation: Support statewide assessment activities through document preparation, tracking, records maintenance, and project documentation. Project Coordination and Other Duties: Coordinate with project partners and assist with meetings, scheduled assessment activities, and special projects. This position will work remotely from a home office and must be available to report to HDI’s Lexington campus location for scheduled project-related work. Advance notice will be provided when practicable. The preferred candidate will reside within commuting distance of Lexington, Kentucky, and have strong writing, editing, customer support, and organizational skills suited to a collaborative, fast-paced environment. This position is contingent upon the successful allocation and receipt of funds from federal and/or state agencies. IMPORTANT : A resume or CV does not replace a completed application. To support accurate review of your education and related experience for salary determination, complete every application field. For each Work Experience entry, include one job title, hours worked per week, ending pay rate or salary, and detailed job duties. If you held multiple titles with the same employer, create a separate entry for each title. Please submit all required attachments in an accessible format. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Work experience using Microsoft Office skills, particularly Word, PowerPoint, and Excel Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position is primarily remote but requires reporting to HDI’s Lexington campus location for scheduled project-related work. Are you able to meet this requirement? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650517": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor of Physics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor of Physics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor of Physics Requisition Number FE05020 Working Title Department Name 8E100:Physics And Astronomy Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in Astronomy, Physics, or a closely related field Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Physics and Astronomy ( https://pa.as.uky.edu/ ) in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-eligible faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in computational astrophysics, with expertise in either theory or observation. The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research is data-driven and leverages modern computational techniques, including artificial intelligence and machine learning, to maximize the scientific return from large astronomical datasets. Relevant research areas may include, but are not limited to, projects utilizing data from NASA -, NSF -, and DOE -supported supercomputing facilities and observatories, such as the Athena Supercomputer, Rubin Observatory, Roman Space Telescope, and Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument. Candidates whose research complements and strengthens existing astronomy and astrophysics programs at the University of Kentucky ( https://pa.as.uky.edu/astro ) are especially encouraged to apply. Current departmental strengths include galaxy formation, stellar evolution, and the interstellar medium. The University is also home to the Cloudy Project, a widely used open-source spectral simulation code. The successful candidate will demonstrate the potential to establish a sustained, externally funded research program and will be expected to contribute effectively to teaching, mentoring, and research training at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will also participate actively in departmental and university service. This is a nine-month appointment in the regular title series. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be approximately 65% research, 25% teaching, and 10% departmental service. A Ph.D. in Astronomy, Physics, or a closely related field is required and must be completed by August 1, 2027. In order to be considered a candidate, applicants will need to complete the following two steps: 1. Submit application materials to Academic Jobs Online at this link: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/UK/PhysicsandAstronomy/APASTRO2027 · Cover letter · Curriculum vitae (including publication list) · Research statement · Teaching statement including experience and philosophy · At least three letters of recommendation 2. Complete an Academic Profile within the University of Kentucky employment system by selecting apply for this job. The application deadline is December 1, 2026. This position will be open until filled. Questions about the search may be directed to Dr. Yuanyuan Su (ysu262@g.uky.edu), Search Committee Chair, Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Kentucky. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ medical coverage and in addition, offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650499": {
      "title": "Kentucky 4-H Camp Staff 2027",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Kentucky 4-H Camp Staff 2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Kentucky 4-H Camp Staff 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Kentucky 4-H Camp Staff 2027 Requisition Number DU15153 Department Name 81360:4-H CENTRAL OPERATIONS Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $1,700 - $2,800 per month, meals, and housing. Visit www.4hcampjobs.com to see a more precise salary based on job duties. Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education High school diploma or GED required; College experience preferred Required Related Experience Applicants must be 18 years of age or older by May 10, 2027 for employment. Experience in the position for which the applicant is applying is preferred. Required License/Registration/Certification Applicants applying for an aquatics or Camp Program Educator position must possess a lifeguard certification from a nationally recognized organization valid through the entirety of summer and/or complete an aquatics training and certification session with 4-H staff. Lifeguards must be able to swim up to 500 yards lap swim without stopping, tread water for 2 minutes without use of hands, and retrieve a 10 pound object from 10 feet of water without goggles. Physical Requirements Applicant must be available to work long hours in a noisy environment, work in outside/hot conditions, and be on feet for long periods of time. Shift Days, nights, and some weekends. Staff are expected to live on the camp property and follow safety recommendations while on and off duty. Internship positions are mid-May 2027 through early August 2027. Job Summary Kentucky 4-H Camping is seeking summer staff who can provide exceptional customer service, high-quality educational programming, and endless fun for the 13,000+ campers and volunteers attending four residential 4-H camp facilities for summer 2026: (Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp, Nancy, KY; Feltner 4- H Camp, London, KY; North Central 4-H Camp, Carlisle, KY; West Kentucky 4-H Camp, Dawson Springs, KY). Available intern positions include (varies by locations): Program Educator, Shooting Sports, Leadership Development, Challenge Course, Environmental Education, and Aquatics. To view job descriptions and responsibilities visit www.4hcampjobs.com. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 02/22/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * At which camp location do you wish to work? J.M Feltner 4-H Camp, London, KY Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp, Nancy, KY North Central 4-H Camp, Carlisle, KY West Kentucky 4-H Camp, Dawson Springs, KY Any of the locations above * If your first camp choice location is not available, is there a 2nd camp at which you would be willing to work? No. I only wish to be considered for the camp I selected above. J.M. Feltner 4-H Camp Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp North Central 4-H Camp West Kentucky 4-H Camp * If your second camp choice is not an option, is there a 3rd camp choice you'd like to consider? No. I only wish to be considered for my first two choices. J.M Feltner 4-H Camp Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp North Central 4-H Camp West Kentucky 4-H Camp * Why are you interested in this position? (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience in working with youth 9 to 14 years of age and teens ages 15-17 years of age. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
