      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | 4-H Camp Support Staff 2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support 4-H Camp Support Staff 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title 4-H Camp Support Staff 2027 Requisition Number DU15152 Department Name 81360:4-H CENTRAL OPERATIONS Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00+ per hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education None Required Related Experience Experience preferred in the area for which applicant is applying (food service, maintenance, ropes, shooting sports, aquatics). Required License/Registration/Certification Appropriate certification in the area for which individual is working (food service, maintenance, ropes, shooting sports, aquatics). Physical Requirements Ability to work long hours in a noisy environment and stand for long periods of time. Shift Temporary employment Job Summary Support for seasonal camp events in the areas of food service, maintenance, or programming: high ropes, low ropes, swimming, canoeing, archery, or rifles. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 09/30/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * At which camp location do you wish to work? J.M Feltner 4-H Camp, London, KY Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp, Nancy, KY North Central 4-H Camp, Carlisle, KY West Kentucky 4-H Camp, Dawson Springs, KY Any of the locations above Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
