    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650497": {
      "title": "4-H Camp Health Care Provider 2027",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | 4-H Camp Health Care Provider 2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support 4-H Camp Health Care Provider 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. New Applicants must furnish three (3) letters of reference. This is not required for staff from the previous summer. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title 4-H Camp Health Care Provider 2027 Requisition Number DU15151 Department Name 81360:4-H CENTRAL OPERATIONS Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $2,800- $4,900 per month, meals and housing. Visit www.4hcampjobs.com to see a more precise salary based on job duties. Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education High School Diploma or GED required College course work preferred. Required Related Experience Applicants preferred to be 19 years of age or older by August 1, 2026 for employment. Experience in the position for which the applicant is applying for is preferred. Required License/Registration/Certification Applicants must possess an EMT certification (or higher) from a nationally recognized organization valid through the entirety of summer. Physical Requirements Applicant must be available to work long hours in a noisy environment, work in outside/hot conditions, and be on feet for long periods of time Shift Days, nights, and some weekends. Staff are expected to live on the camp property and follow safety recommendations while on and off duty. Internship positions are mid-May 2027 through early August 2027. Job Summary Kentucky 4-H Camping is seeking camp healthcare providers who can provide exceptional customer service, high-quality interactions when performing first aid, react to emergency situations, and dispense prescribed and OTC medication for the 14,000+ campers and volunteers attending four residential 4-H camp facilities for summer 2027: (Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp [Nancy, KY]; Feltner 4-H Camp [London, KY]; North Central 4-H Camp [Carlisle, KY]; West Kentucky 4-H Camp [Dawson Springs, KY]). Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Prefer 21 years of age or older. Prefer 1 to 2 years of experience in patient care. Deadline to Apply 08/02/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * At which camp location do you wish to work? J.M Feltner 4-H Camp, London, KY Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp, Nancy, KY North Central 4-H Camp, Carlisle, KY West Kentucky 4-H Camp, Dawson Springs, KY Any of the locations above Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
