    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650495": {
      "title": "STEPS PB CODER",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | STEPS PB CODER Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support STEPS PB CODER Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title STEPS PB CODER Requisition Number TE09545 Department Name H4021: Revenue Management - Coding & Documentation Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $25.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Required Related Experience Required License/Registration/Certification Must be certified certified coders through AAPC and/or AHIMA . Physical Requirements Long term sitting, lifting up to 5 pounds Shift Standard Business Hours (M-F, 5a-9p). Flexible shift available.; 20 hours per week Job Summary The professional coding team is currently seeking a STEPS Surgical Coder to provide standardization, quality, expertise and customer service focus to the UK Healthcare system. The Surgical Coder will have frequent contact with customers/patients, faculty, physicians, vendors, and University personnel.  This position will analyze and extract data from clinical documentation and diagnostic results for complex surgical procedures and assign correct CPT , HCPCS , and ICD -10 CM codes and modifier for professional reimbursement. Primary responsibilities include performing highly technical professional billing and coding, correlating multispecialty coding, and ensuring adherence to all regulatory billing and coding guidelines. Utilize 3M data abstraction, encoder, and computer-assisted coding software to complete coding. Achieve productivity and quality standards set by the organization. Responsible for serving as expert-level resource for assigned surgical service lines, requiring regular interaction with surgeons and various revenue cycle stakeholders.   This position will require the ability to sit at a computer for extended periods of time and work in a fast-paced environment. The qualified individual must enjoy working in a team-oriented environment and be able to communicate with a diverse patient/customer population. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail, accuracy, CPT and ICD -10 knowledge, knowledge of coding and billing software, HIPAA , and regulatory compliance and time management skills Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
