    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650494": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Technician/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Technician/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Technician/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Technician/UKHC Requisition Number RE56001 Working Title Pharmacy Technician/UKHC - Specialty Operations Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, Ky Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire. Must maintain annual registration thereafter and remain in good standing. Physical Requirements This position requires use of a computer workstation, completion of tasks with repetitive motions, and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 50 pounds. This position may require personnel to wear personal protective equipment to reduce risk of exposure to work-related hazards (e.g. handling of hazardous medications). Shift Primarily day shift. Job Summary UK Healthcare is seeking a Pharmacy Technician to assist pharmacists in medication preparation and distribution at UK Specialty Pharmacy. This position will be a vital part of our growing team serving UK HealthCare patients and staff. The selected candidate will fill prescriptions and package orders for delivery in a busy retail-based pharmacy setting. May include standing for greater than 5 hours at a time. May require the ability to reach items above shoulder level and be able to lift up to 30 pounds. Requires attention to detail and the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be reliable and punctual. This position also requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and interpersonal skills. Applicants who possess a National Pharmacy Technician Certification through PTCB ( PTCE ) or NHA (ExCPT) are eligible to be hired into a Pharmacy Senior Technician I/ UKHC position, which is a grade 7 ($18.50/hour – $27.31/hour). All pay rates will be based on candidate’s experience. UK Healthcare offers candidates who do not currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician certification the opportunity to gain the 500 hours of on-the-job experience required to be able to obtain your certification. Applicants who are not certified at time of hire are eligible to receive a pay increase and be moved into Pharmacy Senior Technician/ UKHC , grade 7 role once certification has been obtained and 90 days of successful employment have been completed. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital/retail pharmacy technician and/or healthcare customer service experience preferred Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold a National Pharm Tech Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician? Yes No * Please select the response that best represents your full years paid, full-time, employment experience in customer service. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate the amount of paid pharmacy technician experience you have working in either an inpatient hospital and/or retail pharmacy setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650488": {
      "title": "The Study Hub Undergraduate Student Employee",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | The Study Hub Undergraduate Student Employee Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support The Study Hub Undergraduate Student Employee Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title The Study Hub Undergraduate Student Employee Requisition Number DU15149 Department Name 1B140: Transformative Learning Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range All positions $12/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Qualified applicants must have and maintain a cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher. Some positions also require successful completion of course(s) with a B or better and/or a higher GPA . Please view TSH job descriptions link below to see additional educational requirements for specific roles. Required Related Experience Please provide your UK unofficial transcript Required License/Registration/Certification Please provide your UK unofficial transcript Physical Requirements Sitting and standing for long periods of time. Shift Student employees may have shifts during any time The Study Hub ( TSH ) spaces and services are open, and shifts are usually 2-4 hours in length. Monday-Thursday 9am – 10pm Fridays 9am-5pm Sundays 4pm-8pm. Occasional additional weekend hours for training. Required training prior to the beginning of the semester Job Summary Please note that this is a general application for all undergraduate student positions within TSH . You may be invited to interview for any available role based on your qualifications and program needs. TSH employs undergraduate students in the following positions: Front Desk Ambassador TSH Ambassador Peer Tutor Success Mentor Supplemental Instruction (SI) Leader For additional information about all of The Study Hub’s positions please go to: https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/study-hub/join-team All TSH positions are also Federal Work-Study eligible! The Study Hub ( TSH ), housed in the Office of Student Success, is UK’s centralized learning center and strives to create opportunities for student success through academic support initiatives. As a member of the TSH team, undergraduate student employees will serve as peer leaders who contribute to TSH’s mission of creating opportunities for student success through academic support initiatives and foster a welcoming learning environment. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities time management; problem solving; resilience; ability to work autonomously and in a group; active listening; empathy; role-modeling positive academic behaviors Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Please provide your UK unofficial transcript Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). While it is not possible to apply for a specific position, such as a Front Desk Ambassador or an MA 123 Peer Tutor at The Study, we encourage you to share your qualifications for a particular role below if you feel especially suited for it. (Open Ended Question) If you would like to be considered for a position with our Marketing team, please outline your education or experience with design, social media, and/or customer service. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Academic Transcript Optional Documents Resume 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
