    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650487": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC Requisition Number RE54346 Working Title Pharmacy Senior Technician I/UKHC - Specialty Operations Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 07 Salary Range $18.50-27.31/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification Nationally certified Pharmacy Technician by either PTCB ( PTCE ) or NHA (ExCPT); Registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy within 30 days of hire. Physical Requirements This position requires use of a computer workstation, completion of tasks with repetitive motions, and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects weighing up to 50 pounds. This position may require personnel to wear personal protective equipment to reduce risk of exposure to work-related hazards (e.g. handling of hazardous medications) Shift Monday through Friday; variable shifts, primarily 1230p-9p. Shift hours and days are subject to change based on departmental growth and needs. Job Summary This position will provide a variety of specialty pharmacy services including obtaining prior authorizations, enrolling patients’ in financial support programs, and coordinating first time dispenses and refills for specialty medications prescribed within UK HealthCare. You will work closely with nurses, physicians, and UK Specialty Pharmacy staff to improve access to medications for a variety of sub specialty disease states. Effective 4/1/09, the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy requires all pharmacy technicians to be registered with the state and pay a $25 fee within 30 days of hire. This registration must be renewed annually. Primary focus is to follow URAC standards not limited to but including PHARMCore, Patient Management, and Operations. Follow scope of standards and polices of Specialty Pharmacy Services in relation to at minimum dispensing, procurement, mail order shipping, cold chain distribution, storage, and supply management. Person is responsible for following appropriate shipping requirements, providing quality measures testing of cold chain packaging, monitoring complaints regarding shipping errors, turnaround times, and tracking of products after leaving facility, if available. This position will support inventory processes by unpacking deliveries, putting away medications, performing counts and expiration checks. They are responsible for maintaining proper storage requirements of medications, accountability, and security of inventory per URAC standards. This position is eligible for a recruitment bonus. Additional details will be provided during the hiring process should your application be selected to move forward. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital/retail pharmacy technician and/or healthcare customer service experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No * Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician? Yes No * Please indicate the amount of paid pharmacy technician experience you have working in either an inpatient hospital and/or retail pharmacy setting. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650467": {
      "title": "Student: After-School Assistant STEM Instructors",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: After-School Assistant STEM Instructors Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: After-School Assistant STEM Instructors Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: After-School Assistant STEM Instructors Requisition Number SE04480 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $18 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience Hours per Week 5-10 Classes will begin Monday, September 14, 2026. Current availability is needed on Mondays and Wednesdays between approximately 2:30 p.m. and 5:00 p.m. Training and lesson materials will be provided. Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Young Engineers is seeking an energetic and dependable Assistant Enrichment Instructor to help deliver hands-on, LEGO -based STEM classes for elementary students at Sayre Lower School in Lexington. The instructor will work alongside a Lead Instructor to help students build motorized LEGO models while exploring engineering, science, technology, and math concepts. Responsibilities include preparing materials, assisting students with building activities, supporting classroom routines and behavior expectations, taking attendance, helping with student arrival and dismissal, organizing equipment, and cleaning the instructional space after class. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities REQUIRED Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities • Ability to communicate clearly and respectfully with elementary-aged students, families, school staff, and coworkers • Ability to follow lesson plans, safety procedures, and instructions from the Lead Instructor • Ability to supervise students actively and maintain a safe, positive, and well-organized learning environment • Dependability, punctuality, and consistent availability during scheduled program hours • Patience and the ability to encourage students with different learning needs and experience levels • Ability to work collaboratively as part of an instructional team • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail • Ability to learn basic LEGO building and engineering concepts during training • Ability to complete required training and pass applicable background screening requirements • Reliable transportation to and from local school sites PREFERRED Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities • Experience working with children through tutoring, mentoring, coaching, childcare, camps, after-school programs, or classroom instruction • Interest in education, engineering, mathematics, science, technology, robotics, or youth development • Coursework or a major in education, STEM , child development, psychology, social work, or a related field • Knowledge of positive behavior-management and student-engagement strategies • Ability to explain directions using clear, age-appropriate language • Experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and with different learning needs • Enthusiasm for hands-on learning, creativity, problem-solving, and teamwork • Interest in growing into a Lead Enrichment Instructor position Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 10/09/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
