    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650458": {
      "title": "Student: Clinical Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Clinical Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Clinical Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Clinical Assistant Requisition Number SE04476 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range 14 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience - Ideal candidates will be pursuing medical degrees, such as nursing, pre-med, or in preparation of PA school. - Prefer student be in at least their sophomore year. - CPR certification required. Hours per Week 15-20 Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Primary duties include working in the clinic setting to - Assist in rooming patients - Assisting with physician orders - Ensuring patient flow with ancillary staff - Patient care to include wound care and obtaining vital signs. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veter