    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650429": {
      "title": "Student: Archery Coach",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Archery Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Archery Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Archery Coach Requisition Number SE04473 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range 25 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience - Previous coaching or teaching experience, particularly with youth or middle school students. - Competitive archery experience or participation in an organized archery program. - Experience with NASP (National Archery in the Schools Program) or similar school-based archery programs. - Experience developing practice plans and progressive skill-development programs. Hours per Week 6 Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. The Lexington School is currently searching for an archery coach for their 4th-8th grade team! This individual would be responsible for: - Teaching and demonstrating proper archery form, technique, and safety procedures - Properly and safely, inspect, maintain, and use archery equipment - Other duties as necessary Skills / Knowledge / Abilities REQUIRED Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities – Knowledge of archery fundamentals, including proper shooting technique, range safety, equipment use, and scoring. - Ability to teach and demonstrate proper archery form, technique, and safety procedures to student-athletes of varying skill levels. - Strong understanding of and commitment to archery range safety protocols and appropriate supervision of students. - Ability to safely inspect, maintain, and properly use archery equipment, including bows, arrows, targets, and related gear. - Ability to develop and lead organized, age-appropriate practices that promote skill development and teamwork. - Ability to identify areas for improvement and provide constructive, encouraging feedback to athletes. - Strong communication and interpersonal skills with students, parents, coaches, and school staff. - Ability to create a positive, inclusive, and supportive team environment. - Ability to manage student-athletes effectively and maintain appropriate discipline and expectations. - Ability to remain calm, attentive, and safety-conscious in a range setting. - Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage practices, competitions, equipment, and team logistics. - Ability to motivate and encourage student-athletes while emphasizing sportsmanship, responsibility, and personal growth. - Commitment to supporting the school’s athletics program and representing the school in a professional manner. - Ability to work collaboratively with the Athletic Director, other coaches, and school personnel. - Ability to attend scheduled practices, competitions, meetings, and other team-related activities. PREFERRED Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities - Knowledge of archery scoring, tournament procedures, and competition formats. - Familiarity with a variety of archery equipment and basic equipment troubleshooting and maintenance. - A passion for archery and a desire to introduce students to the sport in a positive and encouraging environment. - Willingness to pursue additional archery coaching or safety certifications as appropriate. Deadline to Apply 10/16/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 11/08/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
