    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650417": {
      "title": "MoveWell Part-Time Fitness Instructor",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | MoveWell Part-Time Fitness Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support MoveWell Part-Time Fitness Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title MoveWell Part-Time Fitness Instructor Requisition Number DU15148 Department Name 1B310:Campus Recreation Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12 - $20/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education NCCA Accredited Personal Training or Group Fitness Certification Required Related Experience Personal or Group Fitness Training Required License/Registration/Certification NCCA Accredited Personal Training or Group Fitness Certification Physical Requirements The position may require lifting or pushing objects up to 50 lbs. or extended amount of time walking or standing. Shift varies based on clients schedule Job Summary We are looking for a PT Personal Trainer to work in our Export Street location.  This person must have a NCCA Accredited Personal Training or Group Fitness Certification. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Time Management, Social Interaction, Initiative, Observant Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 05/01/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please describe your experience in teaching or leading a group fitness or personal training session. (Open Ended Question) Do you currently hold any certifications in the fitness / wellness field? Please attach in Specific Request 1. Yes No What is your training philosophy? (Open Ended Question) Are you available to work weekends? Yes No No Response Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
