    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650414": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Security Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Security Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Security Officer Requisition Number RE55996 Working Title Department Name 3HL00:UK Police Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 40 Salary Range $15.61-24.99/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 100 lbs.; sitting/ walking/standing for long periods of time; handling intermittent periods of high levels of stress; engaging with potentially violent or combative patients, visitors or other individuals. Shift 8 hour shifts, assignments to be determined. Must be able to work any of the following: 1st shift: 6:00 am – 2:30 pm 2nd shift: 2:00 pm – 10:30 pm 3rd shift: 10:00 pm – 06:30 am Days, Evenings, Nights, Weekends, Holidays, and mandatory overtime to include special events such as UK home football games. Security officers must be able to work overtime with short notice for extended periods of time. Location assignment will be determined at time of hire. Job Summary The University of Kentucky Police Department prioritizes its investment of professional development and offer a competitive starting pay of $17.60/hour for Security Officers. We are looking for individuals who are eager to grow their careers while contributing to the safety and security of our University community. In concert with UK Police Officers, Security Officers maintain a safe and secure environment at the University of Kentucky’s HealthCare facilities’ by protecting guests, visitors, staff, and property. They serve as the frontline for security across the UK HealthCare enterprise and during University-sponsored events. In those efforts, Security Officers conduct patrols and use knowledge of their assigned area to actively provide high visibility and presence concentrating on high traffic areas to detect possible suspicious activities or assist visitors with needs for service. They identify, report, and respond quickly, calmly, and professionally to suspicious activities, sensitive situations, emergency alarms, and assistance calls. Security Officers also work collaboratively by monitoring radio broadcasts by Communications and other Security Officers to ensure awareness of activities in the area and to aid as needed. They also respond to assistance calls for disorderly patients and visitors, provide services including crisis intervention, conflict resolution, and diffuse potentially volatile situations with due regard for the safety of all involved. Security Officers experience both high pace activity in response to high stress situations and repetitive/routine activity to proactively serve and protect. They perform basic investigative reviews and prioritize information for the completion of University forms and security reports. They meet and talk with staff, hospital patients, visitors, and vendors, providing information, advising of safety measures, and building rapport. The position also requires providing coverage for individuals on 72 hour holds, performing repetitive duties like relocking and unlocking doors, and monitoring video camera footage and the security badge access and alarm systems. Security Officers escalate situations to UK Police as needed. To learn more about who we are and what we do for the University and our community, Click Here . Feel free to reach out with any additional questions at JoinUKPD@uky.edu Multiple positions available. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until the deadline date or until all positions are filled which could be prior to deadline date listed. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Customer Service, Communication, and De-escalation Skills preferred. This position will require candidates to take a polygraph examination as part of the University Police Department’s employment process. Additionally, any position working in one of the hospitals/clinics owned or operated by the University of Kentucky is required to undergo a drug screen as part of the pre-employment screening process. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/21/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires you to take a polygraph examination as part of the University of Kentucky Police Department employment process. Are you aware of this requirement? Yes No * This position requires you to take a drug-screen as part of the University of Kentucky’s pre-employment screening process. Are you aware of this requirement? Yes No * All security officers are employees of the University of Kentucky Police Department; therefore we must conduct an initial background check to ensure your eligibility to be employed by a police department. Are you aware of this requirement? Yes No * Do you have any felony convictions or other criminal convictions for drugs, domestic violence, theft/shoplifting, or multiple alcohol violations? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650376": {
      "title": "Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Requisition Number RE55904 Working Title Respiratory Therapist Senior - Pediatric Sleep Center Department Name M4000:Pediatrics Clinic Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $30.00-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensure through the Kentucky Board of Respiratory Care and Registered Respiratory Therapist ( RRT ) through the National Board of Respiratory Care at time of hire. Physical Requirements Regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motions (such as typing); occasionally lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to and over 50lbs; and occasionally standing or walking with objects up to 25lbs Shift Nightshift; 3x 12-hour shifts per week (Monday – Saturday); 6:00 pm – 6:30 am Job Summary The Respiratory Therapist Senior provides competent care of patients through airway management, various CPAP / BIPAP therapies, oxygen administration, and performing polysomnography studies in accordance with The Joint Commission ( TJC ) and departmental policies and procedures. General duties will include: registering patients; gathering patient pre-study paperwork; preparing patients and equipment for procedures; explaining procedures and interactions to patients; completing follow-up notes as needed; performing polysomnography studies and analyzing data to assist in obtaining proper diagnosis; entering charges; and cleaning all study equipment. This position will also have some administrative and clerical responsibilities for the department’s daily operations. The starting pay for this position was recently adjusted. The minimum hourly rate for this position will now be $30.00/hour. All pay rates will be based on the candidate’s experience. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Communicate technical information about test results to physicians, family members, or researchers. The ability to work interdependently within a healthcare clinic team. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Sleep Center experience preferred but not required. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently credentialed as a Registered Respiratory Therapist through the National Board of Respiratory Care (NBRC)? Yes Eligible to obtain within 6 months of hire No Do you currently hold a Kentucky Respiratory Care Practitioner License through the Kentucky Board of Respiratory Care (KBRC) or are you eligible to obtain by date of hire? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650373": {
      "title": "Administrative Support Associate I",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Support Associate I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Support Associate I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Support Associate I Requisition Number RE55994 Working Title Department Name 40420:Office of Technology Commercialization Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time; and repetitive motion related to computer work. Shift Monday-Friday; 8:00 am-5:00 pm Job Summary Support Innovation Through Exceptional Administrative Coordination and Operational Excellence The University of Kentucky is seeking an Administrative Support Associate I to join the UK Innovate Technology Commercialization team. This position provides essential administrative and operational support to a dynamic team responsible for advancing University innovations. The successful candidate will support daily office operations, coordinate meetings and events, assist with travel and onboarding activities, and serve as a key resource for administrative processes while maintaining a high level of professionalism, confidentiality, and customer service. What You’ll Do Assist with scheduling and calendar management for the Technology Commercialization Director, including coordination with university and external stakeholders. Provide administrative and clerical support to the Director and professional staff, including preparation of agendas, meeting materials, minutes, correspondence, and confidential documents. Coordinate travel arrangements, expense documentation, and administrative requirements for faculty and staff. Serve as an internal resource for office procedures related to travel, remote work, onboarding, reporting, and other business operations. Coordinate meetings, workshops, seminars, interviews, and events sponsored by Technology Commercialization, UK Innovate, and Research units. Support onboarding, orientation, employee transition activities, and candidate interview processes. Assist with special projects and provide follow-up to help ensure initiatives remain on schedule and progress effectively. Maintain office supplies and support administrative needs for on-campus, hybrid, and remote personnel. Serve as a liaison between Technology Commercialization and other University administrative and executive offices. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes, efficiency, communication, and customer service. What You’ll Bring Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Proven organizational and time management abilities with the capacity to manage multiple priorities. Ability to work independently while contributing positively to a collaborative team environment. Professional judgment and discretion when handling sensitive or confidential information. Strong planning, customer service, and problem-solving skills. Initiative and adaptability in a fast-paced administrative setting. Minimum Requirements Associate’s degree 3 years of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to support innovative research and technology commercialization efforts that help advance University discoveries. Exposure to a wide range of university stakeholders, faculty innovators, administrative leaders, and external partners. Professional development opportunities through continuing education, seminars, and industry best-practice learning. Hybrid work eligibility with approval. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? As UK Innovate continues supporting the commercialization of University discoveries, strong administrative coordination is essential to maintaining efficient operations and delivering responsive service to faculty, staff, and external partners. This position provides critical support that helps ensure projects, events, communications, and administrative processes are managed effectively. The Administrative Support Associate I will play an important role in strengthening office operations, supporting organizational continuity, and helping Technology Commercialization maintain a high level of service while advancing its mission to bring University innovations to broader impact. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Excellent organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong interpersonal and customer-service skills and the ability to interact professionally with faculty, staff, University leadership, and external stakeholders. Ability to exercise sound judgment and appropriately handle confidential and sensitive information. Ability to interpret and consistently apply policies, procedures, and administrative requirements. Initiative and demonstrated ability to independently identify and resolve routine administrative issues. Experience with financial or expense administration, purchasing, travel, or related business processes. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, Teams, and PowerPoint. Ability and willingness to learn University systems and processes. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preference will be given to candidates with experience in higher education, research administration, financial administration, office management, or a similarly complex professional environment. Experience with University of Kentucky administrative and financial systems, travel and expense processes, Procard administration, or related University business procedures is particularly desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience planning and coordinating workshops, seminars, and events. Include examples of how you communicated and interacted with participants at those events. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience with managing calendars, including your process for finding suitable times for larger groups (10+ people) to meet. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650328": {
      "title": "APP Neurology Ambulatory/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | APP Neurology Ambulatory/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support APP Neurology Ambulatory/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title APP Neurology Ambulatory/UKHC Requisition Number RE55057 Working Title APP Neurology Ambulatory Department Name MG350: Neurology Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 14 Salary Range $99,535-156,062/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MSN for Nurse Practitioners or BS for Physician Assistants Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Advanced Practice Registered Nurse ( APRN ) or Physician Assistant-Certified (PA-C) Physical Requirements May lift up to 50 lbs occasionally, sitting or standing for long periods. Shift Primarily Monday-Friday, with occasional evenings and weekends depending on departmental needs Job Summary The Advanced Practice Provider ( APP ) in the Memory Disorders clinic will provide comprehensive evaluation and management of patients with cognitive and memory concerns. Working collaboratively with physicians, nursing staff, and other interdisciplinary team members, the APP will conduct detailed patient assessments, perform neurological and cognitive screenings, formulate differential diagnoses, and develop evidence-based care plans. Responsibilities include managing ongoing treatment, coordinating referrals, educating patients and families about disease progression and care options, and contributing to clinical research or quality improvement initiatives related to memory disorders. The APP will play an integral role in optimizing patient outcomes and supporting the mission of providing compassionate, specialized care for individuals with memory and cognitive impairments. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently licensed by the state of Kentucky as a Nurse Practitioner or eligible to obtain license within the next nine months, or are you currently certified as a Physician Assistant by the (NCCPA) National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants or eligible to obtain certification within the next nine months? (In order to be eligible, applicant must have graduated from an accredited program or be scheduled to graduate within six months of the application.) Yes No * Please describe your experience working with neurology patients. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
