    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650283": {
      "title": "Patient Relations Asst/Bilingual/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Patient Relations Asst/Bilingual/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Patient Relations Asst/Bilingual/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Patient Relations Asst/Bilingual/UKHC Requisition Number RE55767 Working Title Patient Relations Asst/Bilingual/UKHC Department Name MD100:DENTAL GROUP CLINICAL PRACTICE Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 06 Salary Range $16.20-24.82/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3.5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification Language proficiency proven by high school or college diploma from Spanish speaking country or third party proficiency evaluation or test. Physical Requirements The physical requirements for this position include regularly sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time with repetitive motion (such as typing); walking including pushing, pulling, and/or lifting up to 10lbs and occasional pushing, pulling, and/or lifting objects up to 50lbs. The conditions of work may involve regular exposure to loud noises, intermittent exposure to blood borne/airborne pathogens and combative/violent people, and occasional exposure to cuts and punctures. Shift Days, 8:00 am-5:00 pm, Monday-Friday, and other days and hours as needed. Job Summary This position will provide patient registration, scheduling, and financial counseling to the DMD Dental Clinic and coordinate cross clinic coverage. The successful candidate will, on occasion, provide fill-in and backup coverage for patient relations positions at various levels at other UK Dental Clinics both on and off campus. This position will provide services to English and Spanish speakers, fluency in written and verbal communication in both English and Spanish are required. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will be fluent in both English and Spanish languages; have excellent attention to detail; exceptional planning and organizational skills; effective written and verbal communication skills; ability to solve routine problems and manage resources; demonstrated ability to provide superior customer service, time management, and judgment; and respect for confidentiality and patients from various backgrounds. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Verbal Fluency in Spanish is highly preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you meet the language proficiency requirement by having a high school or college diploma from a Spanish-speaking country OR by providing documentation of Spanish proficiency through a third-party language proficiency evaluation or test? Yes No * Please indicate your paid employment experience working in a medical or dental office. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years, up through 10 years More than 10 years * How many providers have you worked for at one time in a dental/medical officer? None 1 2 3-4 5-10 11+ * Please describe a time when you had an angry, frustrated patient and how you approached and resolved the patient's issue. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe how you would handle a patient who arrives 20 minutes late for an appointment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
