    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650229": {
      "title": "Postdoctotal Scholar (Paducah Campus)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Postdoctotal Scholar (Paducah Campus) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Postdoctotal Scholar (Paducah Campus) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Postdoctotal Scholar (Paducah Campus) Requisition Number DU15146 Department Name 8H090:OISTL/Engineering Distance Learning Work Location Paducah, KY Salary Range Commensurate with Abilites and Experience Type of Position Student Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD in Physics, Engineering or related fields Required Related Experience See Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Some standing or walking,. Sitting at computer workstation for extended peirods. Repetitve motion. Lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 lbs. Shift Monday – Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm (40 hours/week) Job Summary The Postdoctoral Scholar will support the educational missions at the University of Kentucky Pigman College of Engineering Paducah Campus, with primary responsibilities in instruction and laboratory development in Laser and Photonics Engineering Technology . The position will serve as an instructional faculty member within the Paducah program and contribute to the development, delivery, and expansion of laser and photonics education for students and industry partners. Primary responsibilities include teaching courses related to optics, lasers, and photonics, with a strong emphasis on hands-on, laboratory-based learning . The Postdoctoral Scholar will develop instructional and laboratory materials, experiments, demonstrations, and other learning activities that provide students with practical experience using laser, photonics, optical, and related technologies. The position will also assist with the management and operation of laser and photonics laboratory facilities and help ensure compliance with applicable laboratory safety procedures and regulatory requirements. The position will collaborate with faculty to develop and integrate laser and photonics courses and laboratory experiences as electives within existing engineering and engineering technology programs. The position will also support the University’s engagement with regional industry by developing and delivering engineering and technology instruction and workforce training for industry partners. Although not required, the Postdoctoral Scholar is highly encouraged to engage in research and grant development. Funding will be renewed yearly, contingent upon performance and funding availability. Employment may be subject to U.S. export control regulations. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Applicants should demonstrate strong technical expertise in laser and photonics science and engineering, along with excellent written and verbal communication skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience PhD in Physics, Engineering or related fields Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
