    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650088": {
      "title": "First-Year Experience Ambassador",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | First-Year Experience Ambassador Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support First-Year Experience Ambassador Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title First-Year Experience Ambassador Requisition Number DU15133 Department Name 1B540:Prospective and New Student Programs Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00/hour and On-Campus Housing provided during summer orientation Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Must be currently enrolled as a student at UK. Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing and pulling objects up to 50 Ibs. Shift The First-Year Experience Ambassador position is a Spring 2027 – Spring 2028 commitment with ranges of required hours as explained in more detail below: Spring 2027/Fall 2027/Spring 2028: During the Academic Year, First-Year Experience Ambassadors will work to support incoming students through office shifts that will take place based on their availability and around their class schedules Monday – Friday between the hours of 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. In the spring semesters, there will also be occasional weekend support. Summer 2027: From June 1 to July 9, 2027, FYE Ambassadors will serve as orientation leaders and will be full time, in-person, on campus, Monday – Friday during these June and July dates. On campus housing will be provided beginning May 31, with check-out on July 10. Most hours will be worked between 6 a.m. and 6 p.m. each day. Job Summary First-Year Experience ( FYE ) Ambassadors play a critical role in shaping a student’s first-year experience at UK. FYE Ambassadors are the face of orientations and assist in facilitating the Big Blue Nation Orientations, Merit Days, Kentucky Science Olympiad, and Bluegrass Days. FYEAs lead small-group sessions for new students, provide guidance throughout orientation programming, support event logistics such as check-in and navigation around campus, and help create an exciting and engaging environment to facilitate incoming students’ transition to campus life. Students who are offered the First-Year Experience Ambassador position will receive extensive training in public speaking, group facilitation, campus resource information, and other leadership skills. As cross-trained student leaders with a deep understanding of campus resources, FYE Ambassadors may also be offered opportunities during the academic year to assist areas within Enrollment Management or the Office for Student Success. Preferred applicants will have demonstrated skills in customer service and communication. While some public speaking and leadership experiences are helpful, training and support are provided to help FYE Ambassadors grow in confidence and effectiveness. Candidates should be proactive, detail-oriented, reliable, and motivated to make a positive impact on the campus community. Successful FYEAs are enthusiastic about UK, passionate about helping others, and dedicated to helping every new student feel welcomed and supported. This position is also Federal Work-Study eligible, if you qualify . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience n/a Deadline to Apply 10/27/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What piece of advice would you give to a new UK student or their family? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650057": {
      "title": "Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - OR/ICU Satellite",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - OR/ICU Satellite Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - OR/ICU Satellite Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - OR/ICU Satellite Requisition Number DU12271 Department Name H3330:Pharmacy Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $50.34-$64.08 Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education B.S. Pharmacy or PharmD Required Related Experience none Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed pharmacist or license eligible in Kentucky Physical Requirements May require standing or sitting for greater than 5 hours at a time. Shift Varies Job Summary In this position the candidate will provide pharmaceutical care to patients admitted to the University of Kentucky Healthcare Albert B. Chandler Medical Center. Responsibilities include: reviewing and perfecting medication orders, reviewing drug profiles to ensure appropriateness of therapy and contacting and conferring with physicians and other practitioners to optimize medication therapy. Actively participating in all aspects of the medication reconciliation process and promotion of economically conscientious use of medication. Daily activities may include active participation on patient care rounds, review of patient profiles, and provision of pharmacokinetic evaluation of therapeutic regimens. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities knowledge of inpatient pharmacy practice, strong clinical skills, ability to prioritize Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital experience preferred Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky (or another state) and are eligible for licensure in KY? Yes No How many years of experience do you have as a pharmacist? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650050": {
      "title": "Resident Advisor",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Resident Advisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Resident Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Resident Advisor Requisition Number DU15098 Department Name 1B450:Residence Life Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12 per hour for eligible front desk shifts Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education In order to be eligible for the position, a candidate must: 1. Be a full time undergraduate student, in good academic standing 2. Be in good disciplinary standing with the university 3. Have a cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher by the end of the Fall 2026 semester to be considered for placement. 4. Be a sophomore, junior, or senior in the fall of 2027. Required Related Experience None Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting for long periods of time while working at the front desk (4-hour shifts), completing rounds of the building during on-call coverage. Shift Days, Evenings, Nights, Weekends, On-Call Job Summary Position to begin in August 2027. Resident Advisors (RAs) are integral members of the Office of Residence Life who contribute to building vibrant, inclusive communities through our residential curriculum, The Wildcat Way . RAs play a key role in supporting student well-being and cultivating a sense of belonging by fostering engaging living and learning experiences. The RA position balances community-building, student support, administrative responsibilities, and leadership development. Core responsibilities include facilitating student engagement opportunities, serving as a resource and referral point for residents, covering front desk shifts, responding to incidents as part of the on-call rotation, and serving as a positive role model within the residence hall. RAs also represent the University of Kentucky both inside and outside of the residence halls and are expected to model the values of the institution at all times. Key Areas of Responsibility The Wildcat Way Support student well-being and belonging by implementing strategies from the Wildcat Way curriculum. This includes facilitating CATS UP intentional conversations, hosting signature and community events, and encouraging meaningful connections within the hall. Leadership Development Contribute to a collaborative team environment by engaging in all trainings, meetings, and professional development opportunities. Selected candidates will also complete a leadership development series during the Spring 2026 semester prior to official appointment as an RA. Resident Support & Community Standards Serve as a role model by promoting positive behavior, addressing concerns, and ensuring safety and security within the hall. RAs uphold University Housing Community Standards and the Code of Student Conduct through education, accountability, and consistent policy enforcement. RAs are also mandated reporters, meaning they are required to share any disclosures of harm, discrimination, or safety concerns with the appropriate university offices to ensure residents are supported and connected with resources. Communication & Administration Maintain regular communication with the Resident Director and fulfill key administrative tasks such as hall opening/closing, weekly staff meetings, one-on-one check-ins, on-call coverage, and accurate incident reporting. Support residence hall operations by covering assigned front desk shifts. This includes responsibilities such as welcoming residents and guests, managing mail and packages, monitoring building security, and providing excellent customer service Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Resident Advisors come from many different backgrounds, but successful RAs often share these skills and qualities: Strong communication and listening skills Ability to make responsible decisions Self-awareness and professionalism Comfort working with a dynamic student population Desire to help and motivate others Solid time management and organization Teamwork and collaboration skills Confidence in handling conflict and crisis situations Knowledge of campus resources Commitment to being a leader and positive role model Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience At least one semester of experience living on campus either in the UK residence halls or at a previous school. Deadline to Apply 10/26/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your current year in school? No Response Freshman/First year Sophomore/Second year Junior/Third year Senior/Fourth year Senior/More than four years Graduate Student * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a specific need for break housing and would need employment in a break housing hall? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/650007": {
      "title": "Student Lab Technician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Lab Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Lab Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Lab Technician Requisition Number DU15141 Department Name 81240:REGULATORY SERVICES Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $14.00-$16.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High school/some college Required Related Experience None Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Standing for periods of time, lifting 50lbs Shift M-F up to 20 hours. Job Summary The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment – Division of Regulatory Services is seeking a Student to support its mission of ensuring the quality and regulation of animal feed, fertilizer, seed, and raw milk for Kentucky consumers and to provide educational analysis for its service programs of soil, seed, hemp, lime and forage testing. This position is responsible for performing soil grinding, log in help, soil weighing, help with tests such as texture class. Additional duties include assist or participate in interdepartmental laboratory work, cross-training with similar positions may be necessary and assigned as needed. As a key team member, the student will contribute to upholding regulatory standards and ensuring the delivery of superior agricultural products. The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment fosters a supportive workplace with professional development opportunities, including a formal mentoring program and staff development fund . For additional information on Regulatory Services please Click Here . To find out more about Martin-Gatton CAFE and how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky, Click Here . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail and basic math and chemistry, Excel, and general computer skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Science or agriculture major (in-process) Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
