    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649993": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Administrative Assistant Requisition Number RE55954 Working Title Department Name 81360:4-H CENTRAL OPERATIONS Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 1 yr Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Must be able to walk carrying up to 25 pounds; and must be able to sit for extended periods of time. Shift Monday-Friday; 8:00 am-4:30 pm. Job Summary Support Kentucky 4-H Programs Through Administrative Excellence and Statewide Service The University of Kentucky is seeking an Administrative Assistant for 4-H Online and 4-H Programming to join the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food & Environment’s 4-H units . This position provides essential administrative and operational support for Kentucky 4-H programs, helping ensure effective service delivery to youth, families, Extension personnel, and program leaders across the state. The role supports 4-H Online operations, financial and registration processes, travel coordination, and program initiatives including Volunteerism and State Fair activities while maintaining a strong commitment to customer service and organizational excellence. What You’ll Do Coordinate travel arrangements, calendar management, meeting scheduling, and administrative support for the Director and Associate Program Leader. Prepare and analyze monthly travel expenses and maintain related records. Support financial operations through purchasing card reconciliation, SAP transactions, cash transmittals, and other assigned financial processes. Provide first-line customer service and technical support for 4-H Online users, including Extension agents and 4-H families. Assist with planning, coordination, and implementation of 4-H Online trainings and events. Maintain registration and event tracking spreadsheets for conferences, trainings, and program activities. Collect, track, deposit, and receipt registration fees in accordance with university cash-handling policies and procedures. Coordinate statewide communications, mailings, and information distribution to Kentucky 4-H Extension personnel. Provide administrative and programmatic support for multiple 4-H specialists and programming areas. Assist with event registration, on-site fee collection, printing projects, and conference support as needed. What You’ll Bring Strong customer service skills and a commitment to providing timely, professional support. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and related administrative systems. Excellent organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and adapt quickly to changing needs. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Experience maintaining detailed records, spreadsheets, and financial documentation. Strong time management skills and attention to detail. Ability to collaborate with colleagues, Extension personnel, and members of the public. Event coordination and administrative support experience. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree 1 year of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to support positive youth development initiatives that impact young people and communities throughout Kentucky. Access to professional development opportunities, training programs, and seminars. Participation in a formal mentoring program. Access to a staff development fund that supports continued learning and growth. UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? Kentucky 4-H continues to provide meaningful youth development experiences across the Commonwealth, creating opportunities for young people to develop skills, build connections, and contribute to their communities. This role is critical to supporting the administrative systems, customer service functions, and program operations that help those experiences run smoothly. As 4-H programs, events, and online engagement continue to serve participants statewide, the Administrative Assistant will play an important role in maintaining efficient operations, supporting specialists and program leaders, and ensuring excellent service for Extension personnel, volunteers, families, and youth participants. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Microsoft Office, 4-H Online Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Driver’s license preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/25/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Rate your level of expertise in using Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Windows, Excel, and PowerPoint). None Basic Average Proficient Expert * How many years of experience do you have in utilizing Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of paid work experience do you have in a customer service position? None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Describe your experiences with 4-H Youth Development. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649934": {
      "title": "Data Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Data Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Data Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Data Coordinator Requisition Number DU15134 Department Name 40546:Center for the Environment Work Location Various locations Salary Range $25,000 - $35,000/year Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Master’s Degree Required Related Experience 3 years Required License/Registration/Certification Driver’s License Physical Requirements Sitting at a computer for extended periods, carrying up to 10 pounds. Shift To be determined. 20 hours per week. Job Summary The University of Kentucky Center for the Environment seeks a Data Coordinator for a large multi-site research project. Duties will include but are not limited to data coordination, data monitoring, and data entry. The position will ensure record completion, identify missing reports and data, collaborate on a cross walk exercise of project data and protocols with the All of Us research study, communicate findings with research staff and field sites, write summary reports, and enter data into Redcap. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Scientific writing, ability to find missing data, data entry, Microsoft Office, and REDcap experience preferred. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Master’s in scientific field plus 3 years of experience in research, scientific writing, and community education. Deadline to Apply 12/31/9999 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience with data coordination, ensuring report completeness, and identifying missing data. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your paid work experience with communicating with research and field staff. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience with writing summary reports. (Open Ended Question) * Rate your level of experise with REDCap: None Some knowledge Data entry experience Expert Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649903": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Internal Medicine &amp; Divisions Undergraduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Internal Medicine &amp; Divisions Undergraduate Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Internal Medicine & Divisions Undergraduate Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Internal Medicine & Divisions Undergraduate Research Assistant Requisition Number DU15138 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 800 Rose St Lexington, KY 40536 Salary Range $12.00 -$15.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education N/A Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Able to conduct physical activity program and exercises 2x per week (60mins/week) for the duration of the study. Shift Weekdays between 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Evenings . Job Summary Exercise Session Support: Assist the PI in leading twice-weekly, ~30-minute Zoom-delivered exercise sessions following the study’s standardized three-phase protocol (warm-up/safety briefing, main circuit, cool-down/stretching). Help demonstrate and cue exercises (body-weight resistance movements, balance and core work) and offer real-time modifications (progression/regression) for participants based on tolerance and Rating of Perceived Exertion ( RPE ). Monitor participants via video for signs of intolerance and immediately alert the supervising staff member if a session needs to be paused or stopped per protocol. Track and log exercise session attendance and adherence for each participant. Conduct the post-session check-in and reinforce recovery guidance. Questionnaire Administration: Administer the Brief Fatigue Inventory ( BFI ) and any other patient-reported outcome ( PRO ) instruments to participants at baseline and each follow-up visit (Months 2, 4, and 6). Ensure questionnaires are completed accurately and in full, answer participant procedural questions, and escalate any concerning responses to the PI or Co-Investigator per protocol. Enter completed questionnaire data into REDCap in a timely and accurate manner. Physical Fitness Testing Support: Assist with administration of the standardized physical function battery at each assessment visit: the 6-Minute Walk Test (6MWT), Timed Up and Go ( TUG ), and handgrip strength testing. Prepare testing space and equipment, time and record trial results, and ensure tests are conducted per standardized instructions for consistency across participants and timepoints. Stop testing immediately at the participant’s request or per assessor judgment, and document any adverse events or deviations the same day. Data Management: Enter and manage study data (questionnaire responses, functional test results, attendance/adherence logs) in REDCap, maintaining accuracy and participant confidentiality. Assist with routine data quality checks and flag discrepancies to the PI. Compliance and Professionalism: Complete required human subjects research ( CITI ) training and any institution-specific onboarding prior to participant contact. Maintain participant confidentiality and comply with all IRB -approved protocol procedures, HIPAA requirements, and Markey Cancer Center policies. Attend regular check-ins with the PI/Co-Investigator to report progress, raise questions, and receive protocol updates. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience in human research or hospital/patient care experience. Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Nutrition, or Human Health Sciences majors preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649832": {
      "title": "Data Coordinator Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Data Coordinator Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Data Coordinator Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Data Coordinator Senior Requisition Number RE55946 Working Title Department Name 7H090:CENTER ON DRUG & ALCOHOL RESEA Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 41 Salary Range $16.15-25.81/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 4 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting at computer workstation for extended periods. Intermittent repetitive motion. Shift Monday through Friday, 8:00am – 5:00pm. Job Summary The Center on Drug and Alcohol Research is seeking a Data Coordinator Senior. The Data Coordinator Senior is needed to collect data, locate and track individuals for phone interviews, assist with data management, and support other project activities in order to meet the requirements of the funding agency. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Data collection, locating and tracking, interviewing research subjects, MS Access, SPSS . Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree plus six or more years related experience with data collection, locating and tracking, interviewing research subjects preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your paid employment experience interviewing research subjects. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate your years of paid work experience with interviewing and data management. None More than 0, through 1 year More than 1 year, through 3 years More than 3 years, through 5 years More than 5 years * Please describe your experience working with data collection systems or database management. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Curriculum Vita 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
