    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649825": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Child Development Center of the Bluegrass Assistant Teacher",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Child Development Center of the Bluegrass Assistant Teacher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Child Development Center of the Bluegrass Assistant Teacher Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Child Development Center of the Bluegrass Assistant Teacher Requisition Number DU15136 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 290 Alumni Dr Lexington, KY, 40503 Salary Range $13.50 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High school diploma. Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Lifting children. Shift 4:00 – 5:30 and other times as needed. Job Summary Help assist children in the classroom, serve snack, and sit on the floor and play with children. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Patient with children. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 12/10/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study?\r\n(If you are unsure, or you have not yet been awarded Federal Work Study, please contact the Student Financial Aid office at (859) 257-3172 and ask to speak with your counselor.) Yes No * Please state your current 8-digit UKID number and LinkBlue ID (Open Ended Question) * Kentucky state law requires anyone who works after 10:30 p.m. on school nights (Sunday - Thursday), and after 1:00 a.m. on non-school nights (Friday - Sunday), to be 18+ years of age. Are you over the age of 18 or will you be 18 before August 1st of the fall semester or January 1st for the spring term (or before employment)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
