    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649768": {
      "title": "Student Assistant - Plant and Soil Sciences",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Assistant - Plant and Soil Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Assistant - Plant and Soil Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Assistant - Plant and Soil Sciences Requisition Number DU12421 Department Name 81060:PLANT AND SOIL SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $13.00-$17.00/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Student pursuing a degree at UK Required Related Experience Willingness to learn new skills and follow detailed protocols Output-oriented Ability to work well as part of a team Clear written and verbal communication skills Reliability and attention to detail Required License/Registration/Certification Driver’s license Physical Requirements Office space will be provided Work takes place in both office, laboratory and outdoor settings Moving may involve walking, working in hot or cold weather, and lifting Shift 1–20 hours per week Flexible schedule (up to candidate) Job Summary Part-Time Student Assistant Setting: In-person Hourly 1–20 hours per week | Flexible schedule (up to candidate) Hourly rate: $13~17/hr depending on experience About the Lab The Agricultural, Computational, and Environmental Lab ( ACE ) at the University of Kentucky, led by Dr. Katsutoshi Mizuta, studies soil health and agroecosystem using various cutting-edge data-driven methods with AI and a big data to improve soil management and precision agriculture. Our team combines laboratory analysis, field sampling, and data science to address practical problems for growers and land managers. About the Position We are seeking a dependable, motivated student assistant to support laboratory and research-support activities. You will work closely with a PhD student and the faculty lead, and you’ll gain hands-on experience in how soil research is carried out from sample collection through publication. No prior research experience is required, and training will be provided. Key Responsibilities Laboratory support: Assist a PhD student with sample preparation, processing, and analysis, following established protocols and lab safety procedures Sample and lab organization: Label, catalog, and store samples; keep inventory of supplies; maintain a clean, organized lab space Data management: Enter, organize, and quality-check research data and keep records accurate Publication support: Help prepare research papers and book materials (e.g., formatting, managing references, preparing figures and tables) Vehicle upkeep: Help with routine care of lab vehicles (e.g., cleaning, scheduling service, tracking maintenance) Team support: Assist other lab members with research activities as needed Michellaneous: Assist to move to a new building: preparing, packing, and transporting equipment and samples…etc Required Qualifications Willingness to learn new skills and follow detailed protocols Output-oriented Ability to work well as part of a team Clear written and verbal communication skills Reliability and attention to detail Preferred Qualifications Undergraduate chemistry laboratory experience Coursework in soil science, agriculture, environmental science, chemistry, or a related field Valid driver’s license Basic familiarity with spreadsheets (e.g., Excel) Working Conditions Office space will be provided Work takes place in both office, laboratory and outdoor settings Moving may involve walking, working in hot or cold weather, and lifting What You’ll Gain Hands-on training in soil laboratory methods and field sampling Experience with real research projects, from data collection to publication Mentoring from a faculty member and graduate student A strong reference for graduate school, internships, or future jobs Start date: ASAP Duration: However long possible depending on candidates’ schedule and funding situations. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail; ability to work independently; excellent communication skills. Experience in coding and/or GIS if possible. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Undergraduate chemistry laboratory experience Coursework in soil science, agriculture, environmental science, chemistry, or a related field Valid driver’s license Basic familiarity with spreadsheets (e.g., Excel) Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
