    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649522": {
      "title": "Student: Resident Experience Coordinator- Memory Care",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Resident Experience Coordinator- Memory Care Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Resident Experience Coordinator- Memory Care Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Resident Experience Coordinator- Memory Care Requisition Number SE04472 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $15+ Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience - High school diploma or equivalent. - Minimum of one year of experience working with dementia residents in long-term care. - At least minimal experience in planning and directing activities for elderly residents, and in planning and organizing special programs for residents, families and staff. Hours per Week 20-40 Able to work full-time or part-time as agreed upon with Resident Experience Director, with some evening and weekend work Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Assist Resident Experience Director in planning and providing activities that support and maintain the residents’ quality of life, and that meet state requirements for addressing the residents’ social, physical, spiritual and mental health. Essential Job Functions: - Plans, coordinates and implements programming to address the needs of residents with varying abilities. - Provides supportive programming in a comfortable environment to residents who are not able to tolerate stimulation of a group program. - Assist Resident Experience Director in creating displaying and distributing a monthly Activity Calendar that is both informative and attractive. - Assists the Resident Experience Director in maintaining an updated social history file on each resident. - Meets all new residents and families upon arrival, informing them of the activity program and encouraging participation. - As directed, coordinates with the Dietary Department regarding food-related needs. - Assist with inventory of supplies and equipment and submits monthly list of needs to the Resident Experience Director. - Coordinates all programming in conjunction with the Resident Experience Director. - Role models Meaningful Moments program and philosophy to all staff. The job description provides a framework for the job; other duties may be assigned as necessary. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities - Basic knowledge of current dementia-care practices and communication strategies. - Good verbal communication skills, including ability to give directions to others in a manner that is pleasant and easily understood. - Ability to display enthusiasm and a positive attitude in promoting activities, and in enlisting the support of facility team members for activity programming. - Must have a valid state driver’s license Working Conditions: - Ability to travel locally if necessary, to purchase supplies and participate in resident outings. Physical/Sensory Requirements: - Medium work – Ability to exert 20-50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 10-25 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. - Must be able to see well enough to write and read English, use computer, and visually interact with residents, families, visitors and staff. - Must be able to speak and hear well enough to verbally interact with residents, families, visitors and staff. Deadline to Apply 10/13/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 09/30/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649502": {
      "title": "Student: Part-Time Teller (The Health and Education Credit Union)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Part-Time Teller (The Health and Education Credit Union) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Part-Time Teller (The Health and Education Credit Union) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Part-Time Teller (The Health and Education Credit Union) Requisition Number SE04471 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $15 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience Hours per Week Looking to hire some part time tellers who are available 20 hrs a week during school. Would be required to work at least 2 Saturdays per month Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off-campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Receives and processes member financial transactions, including deposits, withdrawals, and loan payments; sells money orders. Balances cash drawer and daily transactions. Verifies and posts transactions to member accounts and maintains member and Credit Union records. Greets members and provides routine information concerning services, and directs members to appropriate department for specific information and service. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Excellent communication skills, customer service oriented Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 09/30/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
