    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649494": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Teaching Scholar - School of Information Science",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Postdoctoral Teaching Scholar - School of Information Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Postdoctoral Teaching Scholar - School of Information Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Postdoctoral Teaching Scholar - School of Information Science Requisition Number DU15126 Department Name 8M300:Center for Instructional Communication Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $50,000 / year Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education Ph.D. in Communication or a related area. Required Related Experience NA Required License/Registration/Certification NA Physical Requirements Present in a classroom; regular use of computer Shift Per course schedule Job Summary The School of Information Science ( SIS ) in the College of Communication and Information at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a Postdoctoral Teaching Scholar in Communication with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027. Qualifications/Responsibilities : Duties include teaching up to eight courses in the academic year and working with a faculty mentor on a special project during the summer months. Courses will include required courses for undergraduates in composition and communication ( CIS 110 Composition and Communication I, CIS 111 Composition and Communication II, CIS 112 Accelerated Composition and Communication, as well as business communication ( CIS 300 Strategic Business and Professional Communication). Each course has a course coordinator who develops the base course syllabus and Canvas shell for use by all instructors. Additionally, ICR has a Program Coordinator who helps support all faculty. The twelve-month contract begins January 1, 2027, and ends December 31, 2027; the contract may be renewed for one additional year. A Ph.D. in Communication or a related area, earned within the past two years, is required by the time the appointment begins. Teaching experience, especially in writing-intensive courses, is preferred. Application : To apply, please complete this application and include the following attachments: A letter of application (attach as cover letter), a curriculum vita, evidence of teaching excellence (attach as specific request 1), and contact information for three references (attach as specific request 2). Please note that references will not be contacted without prior consent. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Assistant Director of the School, Dr. Will Buntin, will.buntin@uky.edu. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Teaching experience, especially in writing-intensive courses, is preferred. Deadline to Apply 11/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
