    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649402": {
      "title": "UK Innovate Fellow",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | UK Innovate Fellow Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support UK Innovate Fellow Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title UK Innovate Fellow Requisition Number DU15123 Department Name 40420:Office of Technology Commercialization Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Enrollment at the University of Kentucky as an Undergraduate, Graduate, or Postgraduate Student Required Related Experience Essential Qualifications: •Enrolled in a related Bachelor’s, Master’s, PhD, or Post-Doctorate degree program at UK •Required Dashboard Experience (PowerBi or Tableau) •Required Data analysis and visualization experience •Strong desire to learn along with professional drive in support of UKI’s mission statement •Must demonstrate the ability to communicate technical knowledge and translate into visual tools for real-world applications. •Must demonstrate effective written and verbal communication skills •Proficient in Microsoft Copilot, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Repetitive motion related to computer use. Shift 10 hours a week. The specific work schedule will be determined in collaboration between the student employee and supervisor. Job Summary Essential Functions: The UK Innovate Fellow will report to the UK R&D Partnerships Manager for College of Engineering as a dedicated resource supporting the corporate partnership team – UK R&D Parnterships. • Laboratory Engagement, Data Collection, and Capability Mapping • Research Infrastructure Dashboard Development • AI and Process Automation Development • Research Analytics, Benchmarking, and Reporting • Statement of Work ( SOW ) Automation and Process Improvement • Industry Intelligence and Partnership Development • Administrative Support and Professional Engagement Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Preferred Qualifications: •Experience working in or with industry (internship, co-op, industry sponsored research or collaboration, etc.) •Preferred Agentic AI Developer/Automation Engineer •Preferred Programming Experience or ability (Python, PowerApp, Xcode, etc). •Preferred general understanding of research life cycle (equipment, testing, validation, industry sponsored research/grants, statements of work, proposal development, budgeting, etc.) Opportunities for Skill Development on the Job: This position will provide opportunities to develop skills and gain relevant work experience including the following areas. Responsibility/Accountability •Provide high-level Gantt chart status on several key projects and individual progress. •Self driven and confident to find missing information or collect information and organize into a form that is visual. •Takes ownership of work duties and responsibilities, and ensures they are completed accurately and on time •Presents himself/herself in a friendly and professional mannerPerforms assigned duties and responsibilities consistently and correctly Independence/Interdependence •Seeks instruction from supervisor and asks when unclear of tasks, procedures or how to correct errors •Demonstrates clear and effective communication with supervisor and team members •Works independently when needed; seeks assistance to find unknown information Goal Orientation •Manages time to complete all required and/or assigned duties and tasks •Seeks guidance from supervisor to make improvements in job knowledge and performance •Seeks to improve oneself at work as well as the working environment Self-Awareness •Displays friendly and helpful attitude with customers and peers •Can separate the demands of the job and customers from personal concerns and ego •Acknowledges own strengths and weaknesses Resilience •Able to work through difficulties when they arise •Recovers from and continues to work successfully following disappointments •Accepts direction and constructive criticism from supervisor Appreciation of Differences •Respects the values and beliefs of others •Appreciates the uniqueness in each client, coworker, supervisor •Treats all clients, peers and supervisor respectfully Tolerance of Ambiguity •Demonstrates a willingness to attempt new tasks •Employs basic problem-solving skills and looks to supervisor for guidance as needed •Maintains composure and professionalism when faced with difficult or new situations Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/19/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
