    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649311": {
      "title": "Physician - Division Chief of Trauma Surgery",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Division Chief of Trauma Surgery Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Division Chief of Trauma Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Division Chief of Trauma Surgery Requisition Number FE05027 Working Title Department Name 7H85T:SURGERY-TRAUMA & ACUTE CARE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency and a Critical Care/ Trauma Fellowship Proven success in Leadership Required License/Registration/Certification Board Certified in General Surgery and Surgical Critical Care/Trauma Active and unencumbered DEA Current, or eligibility to obtain, medical licensure in the state of Kentucky Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine Department of Surgery is seeking a Division Chief of Acute Care Surgery, Trauma and Critical Care Surgery to provide strategic direction for one of the region’s premier trauma programs while advancing the Division’s clinical, educational, and research missions. The Division Chief will oversee a comprehensive program built around UK HealthCare’s American College of Surgeons-accredited Level I Trauma Center, one of only two Level I Trauma Centers serving the Commonwealth of Kentucky. The Division serves as a regional referral center for central and southeastern Kentucky, providing tertiary trauma care to a service area encompassing 60 counties, approximately 20,000 square miles, and a population of more than 1.4 million people. The person in this position will maintain an active clinical practice while fostering excellence in trauma surgery, acute care surgery, and surgical critical care. The Division Chief will be expected to grow the Division’s regional and national reputation through innovation in clinical care, education, quality improvement, outreach, and scholarly activity. The UK College of Medicine Department of Surgery is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 275 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 101 faculty members, 118 APPs, 56 staff members, and more than 400 learners annually. The department is home to a broad multidisciplinary scope of surgical practice and nationally recognized for its contributions to the advancement of clinical care, surgical education, research, and innovations in medical technology . Each year, providers in the department care for more than 14,000 patients across multiple clinical sites. The department trains 78 residents and 10 fellows across 9 accredited programs and 1 unaccredited program, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure over $6 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in areas such as aging, surgical device development, colorectal cancer, neuroblastoma, oncology, sepsis, thrombosis, and solid organ transplant and transplant rejection. The department has published 152 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains 20 active clinical trials. Multiple biomedical learners, including PhD and master’s students, gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs. 1005+ alumni from the department can be found across the globe at academic medical centers, health systems, research institutions, and more. Please include an updated CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649307": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Surgical Infomatics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor of Surgical Infomatics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor of Surgical Infomatics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor of Surgical Infomatics Requisition Number FE05017 Working Title Surgical Data Scientist Department Name 7H851:SURGERY/DEPARTMENT Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Master’s degree in Data Science, Statistics, Biostatistics, Computer Science, Epidemiology, Public Health or another quantitative discipline with demonstrated experience supporting research, quality improvement, operational improvement, or healthcare-related analytic initiatives. OR Doctoral degree in a quantitative discipline with demonstrated expertise in statistical modeling, machine learning, data science, research methodology, or related analytical fields. Required Related Experience • Demonstrated experience conducting statistical analyses, predictive modeling, and quantitative research using large and complex datasets. • Experience programming in one or more analytical languages such as R, Python, SQL , SAS , or equivalent. • Experience supporting research, quality improvement, operational improvement, or healthcare-related analytic initiatives. • Ability to communicate complex analytical findings effectively to clinical, operational, and administrative stakeholders. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Surgery at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine seeks a highly motivated Data Scientist to support the Division of Surgical Informatics, Analytics, and Data Science in the Research Title Series . This position will partner with surgeons, researchers, quality leaders, and health system stakeholders to develop advanced analytic solutions that improve patient outcomes, operational performance, surgical quality, and research productivity. The Data Scientist will leverage large-scale clinical, operational, financial, registry, and electronic health record datasets to generate actionable insights, develop predictive models, support quality improvement initiatives, and advance the use of artificial intelligence and machine learning throughout the Department of Surgery. This position serves as a key member of the Department’s growing analytics and informatics infrastructure and will contribute to clinical operations, quality improvement, translational research, and educational initiatives. This position will be filled by an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the Department of Surgery. The UK College of Medicine Department of Surgery is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 275 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 101 faculty members, 118 APPs, 56 staff members, and more than 400 learners annually. The department is home to a broad multidisciplinary scope of surgical practice and nationally recognized for its contributions to the advancement of clinical care, surgical education, research, and innovations in medical technology . Each year, providers in the department care for more than 14,000 patients across multiple clinical sites. The department trains 78 residents and 10 fellows across 9 accredited programs and 1 unaccredited program, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure over $6 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in areas such as aging, surgical device development, colorectal cancer, neuroblastoma, oncology, sepsis, thrombosis, and solid organ transplant and transplant rejection. The department has published 152 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains 20 active clinical trials. Multiple biomedical learners, including PhD and master’s students, gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs. 1005+ alumni from the department can be found across the globe at academic medical centers, health systems, research institutions, and more. To be considered an applicant for the position, please submit a CV with your application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience • PhD or other doctoral degree in Data Science, Statistics, Biostatistics, Computer Science, Biomedical Informatics, Health Services Research, Public Health, or a related quantitative field. • Experience working in academic medicine, healthcare systems, clinical research, or translational research environments. • Experience collaborating with physicians, clinical researchers, quality leaders, or healthcare administrators. • Experience analyzing clinical, operational, financial, registry, claims, or population health data. • Experience supporting grants, scientific publications, presentations, and research protocols. • Record of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications, funded research, or national presentations. • Experience developing dashboards, reports, data visualizations, or decision-support tools. • Familiarity with electronic health record data sources, clinical registries, data warehouses, or healthcare informatics platforms. • Experience teaching, mentoring, or providing analytical consultation to faculty, trainees, and staff. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649293": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Civil and Infrastructure Systems Engineering",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor of Civil and Infrastructure Systems Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor of Civil and Infrastructure Systems Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor of Civil and Infrastructure Systems Engineering Requisition Number FE05031 Working Title Department Name 8H300:Civil Engineering Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in Civil Engineering, Systems Engineering, Operations Research, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment Required Related Experience Candidates must demonstrate deep technical proficiency in fields such as network optimization, machine learning, control theory, or stochastic modeling. Crucially, the ideal candidate must have a proven track record of viewing civil infrastructure through a holistic, interconnected “system of systems” perspective, showing a clear capacity to bridge the gap between traditional engineering disciplines and modern systems-level complexities. Required License/Registration/Certification State law requires faculty members teaching engineering design to become licensed as Professional Engineers in Kentucky within four years of being employed. Job Summary Position Overview The Department of Civil Engineering at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible, 9-month appointment (Regular Title Series) faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. We seek an innovative and collaborative candidate who applies systems engineering, operations research, and advanced computational modeling to the design, management, and protection of complex, non-transportation interdependent civil infrastructure networks. We seek candidates with particular interests in water distribution systems and networks. Core Responsibilities The faculty member will be expected to establish and sustain a vibrant, externally funded research program focused on systems-level analysis, modeling, and protection of critical infrastructure assets. Educational duties include developing and delivering high-quality undergraduate and graduate courses in civil systems engineering (including fluid mechanics, water resources engineering, water distribution network analysis), risk and reliability analysis, and/or network optimization, alongside mentoring Ph.D. and Master’s students in computational infrastructure research. Additionally, the candidate will engage in professional service by participating in departmental committees and actively collaborating with ASCE / EWRI and prominent international systems engineering societies such as INCOSE , INFORMS , iEMSs, and IEEE . Additional collaborative opportunities exist with the Kentucky Energy and Environment Cabinet. The initial Distribution of Effort ( DOE ) expectations are 50% research, 45% instruction, 3% service and 2% professional development. Targeted Research Areas We welcome candidates with demonstrated technical expertise in modeling, optimizing, or securing critical non-transportation systems. In the domain of water and wastewater networks, this includes advancing smart water grids, optimizing hydraulic distribution, modeling contaminant propagation, and analyzing the water-energy nexus. For smart power grids and energy systems, research should focus on integrating renewable energy into municipal grids, designing decentralized energy architectures, and strengthening microgrid resilience. Key areas of interest also encompass interdependent cyber-physical networks, specifically analyzing cascading failures across telecommunication, data, water, and power networks. Furthermore, the position emphasizes disaster resilience and adaptation, leveraging algorithmic decision-making for real-time infrastructure recovery and efficient resource allocation during extreme events. Required Qualifications Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in Civil Engineering, Systems Engineering, Operations Research, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. Candidates must demonstrate deep technical proficiency in fields such as network optimization, machine learning, control theory, or stochastic modeling. Crucially, the ideal candidate must have a proven track record of viewing civil infrastructure through a holistic, interconnected “system of systems” perspective, showing a clear capacity to bridge the gap between traditional engineering disciplines and modern systems-level complexities. Note, State law requires faculty members teaching engineering design to become licensed as Professional Engineers in Kentucky within four years of being employed. The city of Lexington is ranked #3 Best City to Raise a Family, #21 Best Places to Live in America, and #31 Most Educated City in America. The University of Kentucky is the flagship university for the Commonwealth and is one of only eight universities in the United States that house colleges of agriculture, law, business, engineering, medicine, and pharmacy on a single campus. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. To apply, please visit the UK Jobs site. Applicants should submit a cover letter, a full curriculum vitae, a research statement (3-page limit; upload as Specific Request 1), a teaching statement (2-page limit; upload as Specific Request 2), and contact information for 3 references. The priority application deadline is October 30, 2026. Review of applications will begin shortly thereafter and will continue until the position is filled. The desired starting date for this position is August 1, 2027. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649164": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Part Time Faculty - Clinical Instructor (Clinical Privileges Required)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Undergraduate Part Time Faculty - Clinical Instructor (Clinical Privileges Required) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Undergraduate Part Time Faculty - Clinical Instructor (Clinical Privileges Required) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Undergraduate Part Time Faculty - Clinical Instructor (Clinical Privileges Required) Requisition Number DU13537 Department Name 7E000:College of Nursing Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range compensation based upon course load Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Master’s degree or higher in nursing OR Bachelor’s degree in nursing with 2 years of BSN prepared nursing experience within the last 5 years with evidence of competence in clinical area of teaching. Required Related Experience Two years of full-time BSN prepared nursing employment or the equivalent within the last 5 years with evidence of competence in clinical area. Required License/Registration/Certification Current unencumbered license or privilege to practice as a Registered Nurse in the Commonwealth of Kentucky and American Heart Association ( AHA ) Basic Life Support certification for the Healthcare Provider valid for at least 6 months after employment date Physical Requirements Moving about while instructing and demonstrating skills to students as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 50-100 pounds on a daily basis and 25-50 pounds frequently. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases, hazards of radiation, and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift varies Job Summary The part-time Clinical Instructor for the University of Kentucky Bachelors of Nursing Program plays a pivotal role in bridging the gap between theoretical knowledge and practical application for nursing students. This position involves interpreting the mission and aims of the College of Nursing to plan and deliver nursing care within healthcare agencies, serving as a role model, and maintaining current clinical competency and knowledge. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Instruction and Supervision: Provide hands-on clinical instruction and supervision to nursing students, ensuring the delivery of safe patient care. Facilitate valuable learning experiences, including the use of the nursing process and clinical judgment. Student Orientation and Evaluation: Orient students to clinical settings, reinforcing concepts from the BSN curriculum, and helping them develop professional skills, clinical reasoning, and effective communication. Plan and assign student tasks, and guide students in acquiring necessary nursing skills. Conduct student evaluations weekly, at mid-term, and at the end of the term, providing timely feedback to promote student success. Collaboration and Communication: Work closely with course faculty, healthcare agency staff, and other faculty members to ensure effective clinical learning experiences. Serve as a positive liaison between the College of Nursing and healthcare agencies, and maintain open communication with all stakeholders. Professional Development: Attend mandatory orientation and training sessions; maintain compliance with clinical site requirements; participate in faculty meetings and ongoing program evaluation activities, as required; provide update professional portfolio annually. **Specific Request #1- Please upload 2 recommendation letters in one PDF . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstration of clinical competence; strong communication skills; able to provide evidence of effective teaching ability; possess creative, innovative, and diverse approaches to teaching; ability to develop interpersonal relationships with faculty, students, and cooperating agencies. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Master’s degree or higher in Nursing Deadline to Apply Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Academic Transcript Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649015": {
      "title": "Digital Mobile Dental – Rural Health Transformational Project",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Digital Mobile Dental – Rural Health Transformational Project Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Digital Mobile Dental – Rural Health Transformational Project Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Digital Mobile Dental – Rural Health Transformational Project Requisition Number FE05024 Working Title Department Name 7A880:Division of Public Health Dent Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education DMD or DDS degree from a CODA accredited institution or proof of graduation from a non- CODA accredited dental school and evidence that the degree makes the candidate eligible to practice dentistry in the jurisdiction from which the applicant graduated. Required Related Experience Experience in dental practice Required License/Registration/Certification Evidence that the candidate is eligible to receive an unrestricted Kentucky dental license or a Kentucky dental faculty license. Job Summary The Rural Health Transformational Project ( RHTP ) is a strategic initiative designed to improve access to comprehensive oral health services, enhance interprofessional education, and strengthen the healthcare workforce in rural and underserved communities throughout Eastern Kentucky. A key component of the project is the operation and expansion of a Mobile Dental Unit ( MDU ) that delivers digitally fabricated dentures to underserved populations across the service region. This Clinical Title Series Faculty position is required to provide clinical leadership, patient care services, educational activities, community engagement, and support for Mobile Dental Unit operations in support of the Rural Health Transformational Project. The faculty member will work collaboratively with College of Dentistry leadership, community partners, healthcare providers, students, residents, and stakeholders to advance the oral health objectives of the project and improve the health outcomes of rural populations. Primary Funding Source: Rural Health Transformational Project ( RHTP ) This position is supported by external grant funding and is expected to continue through the duration of the grant, currently funded for a five-year period, subject to funding availability. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will work closely with the Department of Oral Health Science, the Center for Rural Health at Hazard, and Rural Health Transformational Project leadership to develop and maintain clinical, community-based, and Mobile Dental Unit oral health initiatives throughout the service region. Primary responsibilities include providing direct patient care and delivery of digitally fabricated prosthetics through mobile clinical and/or fixed-site settings, supporting Mobile Dental Unit operations, participating in community outreach activities, assisting with program development, and engaging in scholarly and service activities consistent with a Clinical Title Series faculty appointment. The faculty member is expected to establish productive working relationships with a broad range of constituencies including dental and medical faculty, healthcare professionals, community organizations, local health departments, school systems, hospital administrators, government agencies, and regional leaders. The individual will contribute to the advancement of innovative care delivery models, including the Mobile Dental Unit, and participate in activities that support the sustainability and growth of the Rural Health Transformational Project. Working directly with administrative staff, the faculty member is expected to participate in data collection, quality improvement, outcomes assessment, and reporting activities related to Mobile Dental Unit services. Additionally, the faculty member is responsible for ensuring Mobile Dental Unit activities comply with applicable clinical, operational, safety, regulatory, and accreditation requirements. The distribution of effort ( DOE ) for this position will include Instruction 0%, Research and Scholarly, Activity 5%, Service 75-85% Patient Care and Clinical Instruction (including Mobile Dental Unit activities, Administration 5-10% Rural Health Transformational Project and Mobile Dental Unit Administration/Community Engagement, & Professional Development 5%. Clinical Title Series – Non-Tenure Track Clinical Faculty (Clinical Title Series), from UKDC Promotion and Tenure guidelines Assistant Professor DMD / DDS or other professional clinical degree, with important commitment to clinical service and academic community. Evidence of or potential for a high level of clinical competence in a clinical area and use of innovative approaches, technologies, instrumentation, or systems of patient care in a clinical discipline. Evidence of or potential for recognition by peers and patients as an excellent clinician. Evidence of or potential for developing a leadership role in a clinical division or discipline and active participation in local, regional, or national professional clinical organizations. Evidence of or potential for recognition by dental students, residents, fellows, continuing dental education attendees, affiliated health professionals, and peers for excellence in clinical teaching. Associate Professor Evidence of or potential for recognition by dental students, residents, fellows, continuing dental education attendees, affiliated health professionals, and peers for excellence in clinical teaching. Provides service to the college, university academic community, and/or profession on committees, boards, programs, or centers. Development of greater than local reputation in clinical practice and emerging reputation as an authority in a clinical field. Continuing evidence of peer recognition as an excellent clinical teacher at regional level. Demonstrated creative contributions to the instructional and clinical service programs of the University, and/or has scholarly activities of important or original clinical investigations appropriate for the research allocation described on the individual’s DOE . Professor Outstanding service as associate professor at UKCD (or its equivalent elsewhere) with important accomplishments as clinician and teacher, as well as service to academic community supported through contracts, grants or clinical income. Evidence of advancement of skills/knowledge in the field as recognized by peers, programs, certification or advanced degree(s). Significant leadership role in provision of dental health care. Development of national reputation for excellence in clinical practice, and as an authority in a clinical field. Established recognition as an outstanding clinical teacher beyond regional level. Scholarly activities of important and original clinical investigations appropriate for the research allocation described on the individual’s DOE . In a discipline that aligns with the needs of the Department or College. These guidelines are to be used in conjunction with the definitions and examples of scholarship and excellence, and the Statements of Evidence provided in the College of Dentistry Appointment, Promotion, and Tenure procedures. The University of Kentucky’s Statement on Benefits: Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should submit an application as well as include: • Letter of interest • Curriculum vitae • Names and contact information for three references when prompted in the application Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Experience with the fabrication of removable prosthetics by utilizing a digital workflow. Experience providing dental services through mobile clinics, community outreach programs, school-based dental programs, public health initiatives, or other non-traditional care delivery settings. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/649013": {
      "title": "Comprehensive Mobile Dental Unit Director – Rural Health Transformational Project",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Comprehensive Mobile Dental Unit Director – Rural Health Transformational Project Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Comprehensive Mobile Dental Unit Director – Rural Health Transformational Project Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Comprehensive Mobile Dental Unit Director – Rural Health Transformational Project Requisition Number FE05021 Working Title Department Name 7A880:Division of Public Health Dent Work Location Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education DMD or DDS degree from a CODA accredited institution or proof of graduation from a non- CODA accredited dental school and evidence that the degree makes the candidate eligible to practice dentistry in the jurisdiction from which the applicant graduated. Required Related Experience Experience in dental practice Required License/Registration/Certification Evidence that the candidate is eligible to receive an unrestricted Kentucky dental license or a Kentucky dental faculty license. Job Summary The Rural Health Transformational Project ( RHTP ) is a strategic initiative designed to improve access to comprehensive oral health services, enhance interprofessional education, and strengthen the healthcare workforce in rural and underserved communities throughout Eastern Kentucky. A key component of the project is the operation and expansion of a Mobile Dental Unit ( MDU ) that delivers preventive, diagnostic, and restorative dental services directly to schools, community settings, and underserved populations across the service region. This Clinical Title Series Faculty position is required to provide clinical leadership, patient care services, educational activities, community engagement, and support for Mobile Dental Unit operations in support of the Rural Health Transformational Project. The faculty member will work collaboratively with College of Dentistry leadership, community partners, healthcare providers, students, residents, and stakeholders to advance the oral health objectives of the project and improve the health outcomes of rural populations. Primary Funding Source: Rural Health Transformational Project ( RHTP ) This position is supported by external grant funding and is expected to continue through the duration of the grant, currently funded for a five-year period, subject to funding availability. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will work closely with the Department of Oral Health Science, the Center for Rural Health at Hazard, and Rural Health Transformational Project leadership to develop and maintain clinical, community-based, and Mobile Dental Unit oral health initiatives throughout the service region. Primary responsibilities include providing direct patient care through mobile clinical and/or fixed-site settings, supporting Mobile Dental Unit operations, participating in community outreach activities, assisting with program development, and engaging in scholarly and service activities consistent with a Clinical Title Series faculty appointment. The faculty member is expected to establish productive working relationships with a broad range of constituencies including dental and medical faculty, healthcare professionals, community organizations, local health departments, school systems, hospital administrators, government agencies, and regional leaders. The individual will contribute to the advancement of innovative care delivery models, including the Mobile Dental Unit, and participate in activities that support the sustainability and growth of the Rural Health Transformational Project. Working directly with administrative staff, the faculty member is expected to participate in data collection, quality improvement, outcomes assessment, and reporting activities related to Mobile Dental Unit services. Additionally, the faculty member is responsible for ensuring Mobile Dental Unit activities comply with applicable clinical, operational, safety, regulatory, and accreditation requirements. The distribution of effort ( DOE ) for this position will include Instruction 0%, Research and Scholarly, Activity 5%, Service 75-85% Patient Care and Clinical Instruction (including Mobile Dental Unit activities, Administration 5-10% Rural Health Transformational Project and Mobile Dental Unit Administration/Community Engagement, & Professional Development 5%. Clinical Title Series – Non-Tenure Track Clinical Faculty (Clinical Title Series), from UKDC Promotion and Tenure guidelines Assistant Professor DMD / DDS or other professional clinical degree, with important commitment to clinical service and academic community. Evidence of or potential for a high level of clinical competence in a clinical area and use of innovative approaches, technologies, instrumentation, or systems of patient care in a clinical discipline. Evidence of or potential for recognition by peers and patients as an excellent clinician. Evidence of or potential for developing a leadership role in a clinical division or discipline and active participation in local, regional, or national professional clinical organizations. Evidence of or potential for recognition by dental students, residents, fellows, continuing dental education attendees, affiliated health professionals, and peers for excellence in clinical teaching. Associate Professor Evidence of or potential for recognition by dental students, residents, fellows, continuing dental education attendees, affiliated health professionals, and peers for excellence in clinical teaching. Provides service to the college, university academic community, and/or profession on committees, boards, programs, or centers. Development of greater than local reputation in clinical practice and emerging reputation as an authority in a clinical field. Continuing evidence of peer recognition as an excellent clinical teacher at regional level. Demonstrated creative contributions to the instructional and clinical service programs of the University, and/or has scholarly activities of important or original clinical investigations appropriate for the research allocation described on the individual’s DOE . Professor Outstanding service as associate professor at UKCD (or its equivalent elsewhere) with important accomplishments as clinician and teacher, as well as service to academic community supported through contracts, grants or clinical income. Evidence of advancement of skills/knowledge in the field as recognized by peers, programs, certification or advanced degree(s). Significant leadership role in provision of dental health care. Development of national reputation for excellence in clinical practice, and as an authority in a clinical field. Established recognition as an outstanding clinical teacher beyond regional level. Scholarly activities of important and original clinical investigations appropriate for the research allocation described on the individual’s DOE . In a discipline that aligns with the needs of the Department or College. These guidelines are to be used in conjunction with the definitions and examples of scholarship and excellence, and the Statements of Evidence provided in the College of Dentistry Appointment, Promotion, and Tenure procedures. The University of Kentucky’s Statement on Benefits: Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Interested applicants should submit an application as well as include: • Letter of interest • Curriculum vitae • Names and contact information for three references when prompted in the application Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Experience providing dental services through mobile clinics, community outreach programs, school-based dental programs, public health initiatives, or other non-traditional care delivery settings. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
