    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648869": {
      "title": "Academic Dermatologist - Residency Program Director",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Academic Dermatologist - Residency Program Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Academic Dermatologist - Residency Program Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Academic Dermatologist - Residency Program Director Requisition Number FE05022 Working Title Residency Program Director Department Name 7H377:Internal Medicine-Dermatology Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD or DO degree with board certification in Dermatology Required Related Experience ACGME Requirements Applicants must meet the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education ( ACGME ) Dermatology Program Director requirements outlined in Section 2.5, Qualifications of the Program Director, including: ACGME Program Requirements Current board certification in Dermatology by the American Board of Dermatology or American Osteopathic Board of Dermatology Specialty expertise in Dermatology Minimum of one year of documented experience serving as a core faculty member for an ACGME -accredited dermatology program Minimum of three years of documented educational and/or administrative experience Demonstrated ongoing clinical activity in Dermatology Required Experience Completion of an ACGME -accredited Dermatology Residency Program Experience in academic or teaching environments, preferably Track record of peer-reviewed publications or scholarly presentations in dermatology Demonstrated ability to collaborate across specialties and participate in multidisciplinary care. Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for licensure in the Commonwealth of Kentucky Job Summary The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine invites applications for a full-time Academic Dermatologist to join the Division of Dermatology. The ideal candidate will be board-certified or board-eligible in dermatology and have demonstrated excellence in clinical care, dermatopathology, medical education, program development, and scholarly activity. Candidates with experience leading or developing residency training programs, including serving as a Residency Program Director for a new or inaugural residency program, are particularly encouraged to apply. This position includes opportunities for clinical practice, teaching medical students and residents, curriculum development, residency program leadership, and participation in research and academic endeavors. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the growth of academic dermatology at one of the Commonwealth’s leading academic health centers, with access to NIH -supported infrastructure, multidisciplinary partners, and patients from varied backgrounds. The Department of Internal Medicine is the largest in the College of Medicine and at the University of Kentucky with approximately 334 faculty, 157 staff, 214 residents and fellows, and 203 advanced practice providers. The department has 14 clinical divisions and 2 non-clinical divisions within its scope. The department of internal medicine is led by Dr. Darwin L. Conwell, MD, MS, FACG and departmental leaders including Vice Chairs, Associate Vice Chairs, and the Office of the Chair Administration team. Internal Medicine faculty secure over $35 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in all internal medicine subspecialties. The department has published 287 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains more than 50 active clinical trials and 240 active grants and contracts. The Department of Internal Medicine has 211 faculty who are actively involved in research activities and supervise biomedical learners, including PhD and master’s students, to gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs . This position will provide an opportunity for advancement with generous benefit package including: Professional Development Funding Relocation Assistance Malpractice Insurance 200% 403b Retirement Match Educational Benefits for Family Members Rank and Compensation Commensurate with Experience. Lexington is a vibrant and welcoming city that offers the cultural amenities of a vibrant metropolitan area while maintaining the charm, beauty, and hospitality of Kentucky’s Bluegrass region. Situated in the heart of horse country and known as the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque rolling landscapes and world-renowned thoroughbred farms. The University of Kentucky is deeply woven into the fabric of the city, serving as a major driver of innovation, healthcare, education, commerce, and culture. As the flagship institution of the Commonwealth and a member of the Southeastern Conference ( SEC ), UK contributes to a dynamic and spirited community. Lexington offers safe neighborhoods, highly regarded schools, an affordable cost of living, and a quality of life that appeals to individuals, couples, and families alike. Additionally, Louisville and Cincinnati are just over an hour away, providing easy access to an even broader array of cultural, culinary, entertainment, and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Confidential inquiries, nominations and expressions of interest should be submitted via email to RaShaun West at rashaun.west@uky.edu Please include an CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position. Job posting will remain open until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Experience serving in a leadership role (e.g., Chief Resident) Prior involvement in educational content development or curriculum design Participation in professional societies such as the American Academy of Dermatology ( AAD ) and American Society of Dermatopathology ( ASDP ) Interest in or experience with community engagement or committee service (e.g., melanoma/skin cancer programs) Experience serving as a Residency Program Director, Associate Program Director, or other leadership role in the development, accreditation, implementation, or administration of a new or inaugural residency training program. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
