    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648777": {
      "title": "Student: Church Nursery Worker",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student: Church Nursery Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student: Church Nursery Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student: Church Nursery Worker Requisition Number SE04469 Department Name 3J5SE: Student Employment Work Location Lexington, KY On Campus/Off Campus Off Campus Salary Range $15.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Preferred Education/Experience Hours per Week 3+ Must be available to work Wednesday evenings 5:30-8pm Job Summary You must be a current UK student to apply for this position. This position is located off campus with a local Lexington employer and is not affiliated with UK. Centenary is seeking a loving, dependable, and responsible Nursery Worker to provide a safe, nurturing, and welcoming environment for infants and toddlers during our worship services and events. The ideal candidate has a heart for children and a commitment to providing care. Responsibilities: • Provide attentive and loving care to infants and toddlers (typically ages 0-4) • Maintain a clean, safe, and organized nursery environment • Follow all church safety and check-in/check-out procedures • Engage children in age-appropriate play, stories, and activities • Communicate effectively with parents and guardians • Work alongside volunteers or other staff as scheduled • Report any incidents or concerns to appropriate staff Skills / Knowledge / Abilities • Experience caring for young children (formal or informal) • Warm, patient, and energetic personality • CPR /First Aid certification (or willingness to obtain) • Must be at least 18 years old • Pass a background check and provide references • Punctual and reliable Must be available to work Wednesday evenings 5:30-8pm Deadline to Apply 10/15/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Anticipated Start Date 10/14/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position is located off campus and is not associated with the University of Kentucky. Are you eligible to work an off campus job? Yes No * This position requires additional steps after submitting your application. You will receive an email with instructions to apply directly with a third-party non-UK employer. Do you understand that you must follow the instructions in that email to complete your application? Yes No * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
