    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648763": {
      "title": "Big Blue Family Care- Child/Pet Caregiver 2026-27",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Big Blue Family Care- Child/Pet Caregiver 2026-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Big Blue Family Care- Child/Pet Caregiver 2026-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Complete the application for review and consideration. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Big Blue Family Care- Child/Pet Caregiver 2026-27 Requisition Number DU15105 Department Name 3JHRW:Work Life Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00-$22.00/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education No specific education is required- all current UK students and recent alumni are eligible to apply. Required Related Experience No previous experience of paid childcare is required to apply. Required License/Registration/Certification No specific license, registration, or certification is required to apply. Physical Requirements Applicants must be able to lift (children) up to 50 lbs. if needed. Shift Shifts/work schedules and pay rate for applicants will be determined and agreed upon by the student-caregiver and the UK family for which they are providing child or pet care. Job Summary Big Blue Family Care ( BBFC ) is a child/pet care referral network that offers current UK undergraduate, graduate students and recent alumni of the program the opportunity to offer occasional (part-time or full-time) care-giving (i.e. child care, pet care) to UK families. By submitting this application you are applying to become a care-giver in the BBFC program. A standard background check (pre-employment screening) will be completed for all applicants before they are referred to parents. -Caregivers are welcome to provide care for as many families as their schedule allows and work as many hours as they are available. -Successful applicants are welcome to participate in the BBFC program the entire time they are a UK student. Each semester that the caregiver participates in the BBFC program, a new schedule of work availability is required. -There is no minimum or maximum required work hours. Referrals are made on an “as needed” or “by request” basis with a UK family once an online BBFC request form is submitted. Payment rates and type of payment (cash, electronic, check) is determined and agreed upon by both the UK family and the UK student-caregiver. The UK family will pay the UK student-caregiver directly. All majors are welcome to apply. Previous childcare experience is recommended. Parents may require proof of driving license, CPR , BLS and references (optional). Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Desire to care for children (ages vary). Ability to problem solve, offer positive feedback and manage behavior of children. Ability to provide basic care for the children including engage in healthy play, offer meals. Ability to assist children with school work is helpful but not required. Ability to transport children to activities is sometimes desired but not required. Familiarity with childhood behavior is helpful. Interest and experience with pets are desired, but not required if seeking to be a pet sitter. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience for applicants is +1 year of child/youth care-giving. Previous paid or unpaid childcare related experience is desired and acceptable. Deadline to Apply 06/30/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No * Please describe any experience you have related to care-giving; including the duration of care-giving experience, age, and number of child(ren). (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any professional training/certification for caregiving? (e.g., CPR, First Aid, special needs care training, Teaching Assistant Certificate, early childhood education training, Child Development Associate Credential, etc.) If yes, please describe. (Open Ended Question) Please provide up to 2 references that can talk about your care-giving or employment history. (Open Ended Question) * How many children are you comfortable caring for at a given time? 0 1 2 3 4+ * Are you willing to care for mildly ill children? Yes No * Do you have any experience caring for special needs children? Yes No * Are you able to provide back-up/emergency child-care? (E.g. providing child-care with little notice beforehand.) Yes No * What is your preferred hourly rate? (Open Ended Question) * Are you comfortable with pets? If no, please state which animals. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648719": {
      "title": "Physician - Critical Care Pediatrician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Critical Care Pediatrician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Critical Care Pediatrician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Critical Care Pediatrician Requisition Number FE05023 Working Title Department Name 7H654:PEDIATRICS - WERNER CRITICAL CARE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D., DO or the foreign equivalent Required Related Experience Minimum residency training of three years in Pediatrics and fellowship training in Pediatric Critical Care Required License/Registration/Certification Board certified or board eligible in Pediatrics, board certified or board eligible in Critical Care Medicine Eligible for or licensed to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Job Summary The Department of Pediatrics at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine is committed to advancing healthcare, education, and research to improve lives across the Commonwealth and beyond. We foster a collaborative environment where innovation thrives, and every team member’s contribution makes a meaningful impact. About the Role The faculty member appointed to this position will be responsible for supervision of clinical services and will also participate in the teaching activities of the division as well as in clinical research projects and quality improvement initiatives. Bedside teaching will be integrated with clinical responsibilities. About the Department Golisano Children’s at UK, part of UK HealthCare and the University of Kentucky College of Medicine, is a leading academic pediatric referral center serving Central and Eastern Kentucky and surrounding regions. The hospital delivers comprehensive, multidisciplinary care across more than 24 pediatric specialties and serves as a tertiary and quaternary care center for complex conditions. Key clinical capabilities include a Level IV NICU , Level I Pediatric Trauma Center, and dedicated pediatric intensive care units. The University of Kentucky Department of Pediatrics plays a central role in advancing pediatric care, education, and research across the institution. Faculty are actively engaged in medical education, clinical research, and program development, working within a highly collaborative environment alongside experienced pediatric specialists, advanced practice providers, and multidisciplinary teams. The department is committed to innovation, mentorship, and improving child health outcomes across the Commonwealth through clinical excellence and outreach. Located in the heart of the Bluegrass region, Lexington is a vibrant, mid-sized city known for its blend of academic excellence, cultural amenities, and scenic beauty. As home to the University of Kentucky, the city offers a dynamic environment supported by strong healthcare, education, and research communities. Often referred to as the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque horse farms and a thriving equine industry, including world-renowned venues such as Keeneland. Residents enjoy a high quality of life with access to outdoor recreation, a growing culinary and arts scene, and a welcoming, community-oriented atmosphere. Surrounding communities—including Georgetown, Versailles, Nicholasville, and Winchester—offer additional living options ranging from charming small towns to scenic countryside, all within a short drive of the city. Work Location & Flexibility This position is fully on-site in Lexington, KY, based on departmental needs and university policies. Why Join Us Joining Golisano Children’s at UK and the University of Kentucky Department of Pediatrics offers a unique opportunity to practice in a collaborative, mission-driven academic environment while making a meaningful impact on pediatric health across the region. Physicians benefit from a strong institutional commitment to clinical excellence, innovation, and program growth, with the support needed to develop and expand specialized services. Faculty enjoy: Academic engagement through teaching, mentorship, and involvement with trainees at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine Opportunities to participate in clinical and translational research, quality improvement, and program development A collaborative, multidisciplinary care model with experienced colleagues and strong APP support The ability to serve a varied and high-acuity patient population, including complex tertiary and quaternary cases Institutional support for career advancement, leadership development, and professional growth Located in Lexington, physicians and their families also benefit from a high quality of life, with access to a vibrant community, excellent schools, and the natural beauty of the Bluegrass region. We invite you to join our team and become part of the reason Golisano Children’s at UK and the UK Department of Pediatrics are the People, Purpose and Place for pediatric healthcare in Kentucky. Please include curriculum vitae and cover letter along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648713": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Requisition Number FE05018 Working Title Department Name 8H700:Mechanical Engineering Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Applicants should hold a Ph.D. degree in mechanical, aerospace, electrical, or computer engineering, or a closely related field. Required Related Experience The successful candidate will have expertise in high-speed computational fluid dynamics with interest in turbulence and transitional flows. We welcome a broad range of related expertise, including but not limited to fluid-structure interaction, uncertainty quantification, and inference methods. Exceptional candidates at the associate- or full-professor level may also be considered. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering ( https://www.engr.uky.edu/mae ) at the University of Kentucky seeks to expand its strengths in hypersonics. The Department invites qualified candidates to apply for a tenure-eligible, 9-month appointment (Regular Title Series) faculty position at the assistant-professor level with an anticipated start date of fall 2027. The successful candidate will have expertise in high-speed computational fluid dynamics with interest in turbulence and transitional flows. We welcome a broad range of related expertise, including but not limited to fluid-structure interaction, uncertainty quantification, and inference methods. Exceptional candidates at the associate- or full-professor level may also be considered. The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering is the largest in the Stanley and Karen Pigman College of Engineering with 41 faculty members, over 1,250 undergraduate students, and over 140 graduate students. The Department offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in mechanical engineering and aerospace engineering, and a master’s degree program in manufacturing systems engineering. The Department is engaged in federally funded research projects from agencies such as NSF , NIH , NASA , DOE , DOW , DARPA , FAA , NIST , and USDA . The Department’s externally funded research currently averages over $22 million/year in new awards. The Department also houses the NASA Kentucky Space Grant and EPSCoR programs and has research centers and consortiums that collaborate extensively with industry. This faculty search is part of the Department’s plan to expand in the strategic focus areas of hypersonics and aerodynamics, advanced manufacturing, autonomous systems and AI, biomechanics and biomaterials, and sustainable energy. Candidates must have a strong record of academic scholarship and high potential for building an externally funded research program, conducting high-impact research, advising graduate students, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. The city of Lexington is ranked #3 Best City to Raise a Family, #21 Best Places to Live in America, and #31 Most Educated City in America. The University of Kentucky is the flagship university for the Commonwealth and is one of only eight universities in the United States that house colleges of agriculture, law, business, engineering, medicine, and pharmacy on a single campus. Employment at UK comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/ . Applicants should submit a cover letter, a full curriculum vitae, a research statement (3-page limit), a teaching statement (2-page limit), and contact information for 3 professional references. We request that the teaching statement specifically address undergraduate and graduate teaching interests relevant to aerospace and mechanical engineering. The priority application deadline is November 30, 2026. Review of applications will begin shortly thereafter and will continue until the position is filled. The desired starting date for this position is August 1, 2027. Requests for further information regarding application procedures may be directed to Mr. Troy Howell (Senior Business Officer) at (859) 218-0650 or troy.howell@uky.edu . Questions for the chair of the search committee can be directed to Dr. Savio Poovathingal (Associate Professor of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering) at saviopoovathingal@uky.edu . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents Specific Request 3 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648704": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Requisition Number FE05012 Working Title Department Name 8E110:Political Science Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education PhD in Political Science Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-eligible faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the field of law, courts, and democracy. Preference will be given to scholars whose research and teaching bridge traditional subfield boundaries. This is a nine-month appointment in the regular title series with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be 45% teaching, 45% research, and 10% departmental service. The successful candidate will demonstrate either an established record or strong potential for producing high-quality research, securing extramural funding, employing rigorous quantitative and methodological approaches, and providing effective instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in the Law and Justice major, a rapidly growing program housed within the Department of Political Science, as well as Political Science courses in law and courts. A PhD in Political Science is required at time of appointment. Applicants must include the following: 1) letter of application (upload as Cover Letter) 2) Curriculum Vita 3) Two publications or writing samples 4) Research Statement (upload as specific statement 1) 5) Teaching statement and evidence of teaching experience (upload as specific statement 2) 6) Transcript 7) In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the academic profile. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references within the employment system. Questions about the search may be directed to Dr. Bridgett King, Search Committee Chair, Department of Political Science, University of Kentucky, at bridgett.king@uky.edu. Application Deadline is 09/29/2026. This position will remain open until filled. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ medical coverage and in addition, offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulations concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Writing Sample Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
