    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648673": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Scholar",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Post Doctoral Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Post Doctoral Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Post Doctoral Scholar Requisition Number DU15102 Department Name 7H018:Toxicology and Cancer Biology Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $63,480 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education A Ph.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent degree in cancer biology, immunology, molecular/cellular biology, or a related field Required Related Experience Hands-on experience with mouse models and in vivo experiments Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Check all that apply: ☒Sitting at computer work station for long periods of time ☒Standing for long periods of time ☐Risk of back injury from moving/lifting, equipment, or materials ☒Repetitive motion ☒Lifting/Carrying up to _25____lbs. ☒Pushing/Pulling up to __25_____ lbs. ☐Job Related Travel ☐Loud Noises ☒Hazardous Chemicals or fumes ☐Temperature extremes ☐Radiation ☒Burns/Cuts/Punctures ☐Bloodborne/Airborne Pathogens/Recombinant DNA /Viral Vectors ☐___________________________________ Shift 40 hours a week. Some evenings and/or weekends may be necessary. Job Summary A fully funded Postdoctoral Scholar position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Xia Li u at the Department of Toxicology and Cancer biology. The position is supported by recently funded NIH / NCI R01 and American Cancer Society ( ACS ) Research Scholar Grant awards and is available immediately. Research Focus The Liu Laboratory investigates how neutrophils and other myeloid cells regulate breast cancer progression, metastasis, and response to cancer immunotherapy, with a particular focus on triple-negative breast cancer ( TNBC ). Our research focuses on the interplay between tumors and the systemic tumor macroenvironment, particularly how tumor-derived signals reprogram hematopoiesis and neutrophil development and function to promote cancer progression and therapeutic resistance. The successful candidate will have opportunities to work on projects investigating: Molecular mechanisms regulating emergency granulopoiesis and neutrophil development during cancer progression Systemic tumor–host interactions within the tumor macroenvironment Functional and molecular heterogeneity of circulating and tumor-associated neutrophils Signaling pathways regulating the generation and immunosuppressive functions of immature neutrophils/ PMN -MDSCs Mechanisms by which neutrophils promote breast cancer progression and metastasis Mechanisms underlying neutrophil-mediated resistance to anti-PD-1 immunotherapy Metabolic and functional reprogramming of neutrophils during cancer progression Novel therapeutic strategies targeting tumor–myeloid interactions to inhibit metastasis and overcome immunotherapy resistance The projects combine mechanistic studies with clinically relevant questions and provide opportunities to identify novel therapeutic targets within both the local tumor microenvironment and systemic tumor macroenvironment. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Applicants should have: A Ph.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent degree in cancer biology, immunology, molecular/cellular biology, or a related field Hands-on experience with mouse models and in vivo experiments Experience with molecular and cellular biology techniques Strong motivation to pursue research in cancer biology, tumor immunology, and myeloid cell biology Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment Strong written and oral communication skills Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Experience with mouse tumor models is particularly important for this position. Experience with single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data analysis is preferred. Additional experience in cancer immunology, neutrophil/myeloid cell biology, flow cytometry, bone marrow transplantation, bioinformatics, or immunotherapy studies is highly desirable. Deadline to Apply 10/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648645": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Political Science Requisition Number FE05014 Working Title Department Name 8E110:Political Science Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education A Ph.D. in Political Science Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-eligible faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the field of international conflict and cooperation. Preference will be given to scholars whose research and teaching focus on terrorism, transitional and restorative justice, or civil conflict, and whose work bridges traditional subfield boundaries. This is a nine-month appointment in the regular title series with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be 45% teaching, 45% research, and 10% departmental service. The successful candidate will demonstrate either an established record or strong potential for producing high-quality research, securing extramural funding, employing rigorous quantitative and methodological approaches, and providing effective instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in Political Science related to international conflict and cooperation and will preferably be able to contribute to the Law and Justice major, a rapidly growing program housed within the Department of Political Science. A Ph.D. in Political Science is required and must be completed by August 1, 2027. Applicants must include the following: 1) letter of application (upload as Cover Letter) 2) Curriculum Vita 3) Two publications or writing samples 4) Research Statement (upload as specific statement 1) 5) Teaching statement and evidence of teaching experience (upload as specific statement 2) 6) Transcript 7) In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the academic profile. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references within the employment system. Questions about the search may be directed to Dr. Daniel Morey, Search Committee Chair, Department of Political Science, University of Kentucky, at daniel-morey@uky.edu Application Deadline is 09/29/2026. This position will remain open until filled. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ medical coverage and in addition, offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulations concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Writing Sample Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
