    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648639": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Retailing and Tourism Management",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Lecturer in Retailing and Tourism Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Lecturer in Retailing and Tourism Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Lecturer in Retailing and Tourism Management Requisition Number FE05007 Working Title Department Name 81700:Retailing & Tourism Management Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Masters’ degree with a min. of 3-5 years extensive professional experience or Ph.D in Hospitality Management, Event Management, Retailing Management or related field. Required Related Experience Applicants must possess an earned master’s degree with a min. of 3-5 years extensive professional experience in the event industry or Ph.D (preferred) in Hospitality Management, Event Management, Tourism , or related field by the date of appointment in order to be credentialed by our university’s accrediting body. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in the HMT and MAT programs, and contribute to departmental, college, and university service activities. The department is particularly interested in candidates with expertise in event management and related fields, who can contribute to the continued expansion of event-related courses, experiential learning opportunities, and interdisciplinary initiatives. The successful candidate will also be expected to cultivate and strengthen relationships with industry partners, nonprofit organizations, community leaders, government agencies, alumni, and other stakeholders to create meaningful opportunities for student engagement, internships, applied learning and collaborative projects. In addition to supporting the department’s growing emphasis on event management, the successful candidate will contribute to student learning across a broad range of subject areas, including customer service, emerging technologies, and professional development. The candidate must demonstrate excellence in oral and written communication and the ability to work effectively in a collaborative, team-based environment. The position includes teaching twelve credit hours (four courses) during one academic semester and nine credit hours (three courses) during the other semester and may also include summer teaching assignments. Applicants must submit a letter of application (cover letter), curriculum vitae, academic transcripts, contact information for three professional references (including telephone numbers, mailing addresses, and email addresses), a teaching portfolio, project/work samples, and a statement of career goals. Please upload the following documents in the Specific Request Documents section: Specific Request 1: Teaching Portfolio Specific Request 2: Project/Work Samples Specific Request 3: Statement of Career Goals (maximum 3 pages) Letters of recommendation are not required as part of the initial application. The search committee may request letters of recommendation from selected candidates, which will be solicited electronically through the system. This position will remain open until filled. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027 . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The successful candidate will be expected to cultivate and strengthen relationships with industry partners, nonprofit organizations, community leaders, government agencies, alumni, and other stakeholders to create meaningful opportunities for student engagement, interships, applied learning, and collaborative projects. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Applicants must possess an earned master’s degree with a min. of 3-5 years extensive professional experience in the event industry or PhD (preferred) in Hospitality Management, Event Management, Retailing Management or related field, by the date of appointment in order to be credentialed by our university’s accrediting body . Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Specific Request 3 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648621": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Regular Title Series",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor - Regular Title Series Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor - Regular Title Series Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor - Regular Title Series Requisition Number FE05010 Working Title Department Name 7K300:PHARMACEUTICAL SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education PharmD, PhD, MD, PharmD/PhD, MD/PhD, or an equivalent advanced degree in pharmaceutical sciences or a related discipline Required Related Experience Candidates must provide evidence of outstanding scholarship, research productivity, and their commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and service Required License/Registration/Certification none Job Summary The Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences at the University of Kentucky College of Pharmacy invites applications for 12-month tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, with an anticipated Fall 2027 start date. We seek who can help grow our translational program and align with the COP’s P20 Center of Biomedical Research Excellence for Translational Chemical Biology . This would include, but is not limited to: innovative approaches to chemical biology and/or medicinal/natural products chemistry in translational drug discovery and development; pharmaceutics, pharmacology, targeted drug delivery and/or PKPD in the drug development process; or pharmacogenomics and/or novel tools to improve personalized diagnostics and therapeutics. Special consideration will be given to candidates whose research interests complement the existing and emerging research at the College (including substance use disorders, infectious disease, cancer, neurological disorders, metabolic syndrome, and immune modulation of disease). Motivated applicants with research expertise related to other health problems are also encouraged to apply. Candidates must have a PharmD, PhD, MD, PharmD/PhD, MD/PhD, or an equivalent advanced degree in pharmaceutical sciences or a related discipline. Candidates must also provide evidence for outstanding scholarship, research productivity, and their commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and service. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an extramurally funded, nationally recognized, collaborative research program. The selected candidate will also be expected to contribute to the teaching, advising, and mentoring of Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD), graduate and undergraduate students in a manner that supports a positive learning environment. A primary mission of The University of Kentucky College of Pharmacy is to improve health by developing innovative approaches for the treatment of disease. Our faculty create and lead collaborative, interdisciplinary efforts within our University’s dynamic and growing research and clinical enterprises, with a particular focus on translating discoveries to impact patients. The College of Pharmacy resides in a 286,000 sq. ft. building located next to the Biomedical Biological Sciences Research Building and the recently opened Healthy Kentucky Research Building that also house pharmacy faculty. All three buildings are at the center of the combined medical and academic campus, facilitating close interactions with other departments and centers at the University of Kentucky. These include nationally recognized centers of excellence in neuroscience (Sanders-Brown Center on Aging, Spinal Cord and Brain Injury Research Center, Kentucky Neuroscience Institute), cancer ( NCI -designated Markey Cancer Center), cardiovascular disease (Saha Cardiovascular Research Center, Gill Heart and Vascular Institute), and clinical/translational research (Center for Clinical and Translational Science). In addition, the College houses research centers that cultivate and provide expertise in all aspects of drug discovery and development as well as translational science. These include the Molecular Modeling and Biopharmaceuticals Center, the Center for the Advancement of Pharmacy Practice, and the Center for Pharmaceutical Research and Innovation. The College of Pharmacy is also home to the COBRE in Translational and Chemical Biology, a primary mission of which is to support junior faculty in their research and career development. In addition, the College of Pharmacy financially supports various initiatives to foster interdepartmental and inter-collegiate collaborations. Application materials must include: 1) Curriculum vitae 2) Research statement including a summary of research goals (under specific request #1) 3) Teaching and mentoring philosophy statement (under specific request #2) 4) Names of three persons who may be contacted for reference letters. For questions about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Vincent Venditto (vincent.venditto@uky.edu). Application review will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. To assure full consideration, application materials should be received by December 4, 2026. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648607": {
      "title": "University Press Director",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | University Press Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support University Press Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title University Press Director Requisition Number RE55849 Working Title Director Department Name 88400:University Press Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 51 Salary Range $95,826-162,947/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education MA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 8 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Sitting and/or standing at a computer for long periods of time; performing repetitive motion tasks; occasionally lifting up to 25 pounds; effectively communicating with individuals from various backgrounds and varied professional levels; and intermittent job-related travel. Shift Weekdays with occasional nights and weekends. Job Summary The University Press of Kentucky has a dual mission—the publication of academic books of high scholarly merit in a variety of fields and the publication of significant books about the history and culture of Kentucky, the Ohio Valley region, the Upper South, and Appalachia. The Press is the statewide nonprofit scholarly publisher for the Commonwealth of Kentucky, serving all Kentucky state-sponsored institutions of higher learning as well as nine private colleges and Kentucky’s two major historical societies. The Press now seeks an innovative and mission-driven Director to lead a dedicated team of 15-17 and set the strategic path for the Press going forward. The position is based in Lexington, KY and reports to the Dean of Libraries. Relocation assistance is available. Lexington is a bustling and culturally rich city, which was ranked #15 by U.S. News and World Report among the Best Places to Live in America, while the University of Kentucky has been recognized as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For. Primary Responsibilities Administration and Leadership Provide strategic and operational leadership for the University Press of Kentucky, ensuring that publishing programs, policies, operations, and priorities align with the missions of the University of Kentucky and the statewide consortium. Direct all publishing activities, including acquisitions, editorial, production, marketing, sales, and partnerships, while assessing program quality, financial performance, and emerging opportunities. Financial and Business Management Develop and oversee the Press’s budget, financial strategy, and revenue streams to support publishing priorities and long-term sustainability. Monitor financial and operational performance, evaluate new business and partnership opportunities, oversee major contracts, and ensure compliance with university policies and financial controls. External Relations, Fundraising, and Statewide Engagement Represent the Press and cultivate relationships with university, statewide, regional, and national partners, including authors, scholars, cultural organizations, donors, and publishing professionals. Advance fundraising, donor stewardship, and public support through collaboration with university and external stakeholders. Personnel and Organizational Leadership Lead and support Press personnel by supervising and evaluating direct reports, establishing clear expectations, and promoting accountability and collaboration across departments. Assess staffing needs and support recruitment, employee development, retention, succession planning, and a respectful and inclusive workplace culture. Professional Development and Service Maintain knowledge of developments and best practices in scholarly and university publishing through ongoing professional development. Participate in professional organizations and serve on relevant university, consortium, and industry committees. Required Education: Graduate degree in a discipline related to the Press’s areas of publishing emphasis or to one of its operational departments, such as marketing or business, or an equivalent combination of education and experience from which comparable knowledge and abilities can be acquired. Required Related Experience 8 years Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Competencies/Skills/Requirements More than 8 years of experience in university press, scholarly, or academic publishing with increasing leadership responsibilities. Demonstrated success in strategic planning and organizational leadership. Experience managing budgets, business operations, and revenue-generating activities. Success securing grants, gifts, sponsorships, or other external funding. Experience building partnerships with external organizations and stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and lead high-performing teams. History & Organization The University Press of Kentucky is the scholarly publisher for the Commonwealth of Kentucky. It was organized in 1969 as successor to the University of Kentucky Press. Since then, the Press has represented a consortium that now includes all of Kentucky’s state universities, nine of its private colleges, and two historical societies. Each constituent institution is represented on a statewide editorial board, which supervises the University Press of Kentucky imprint. The Press serves: Bellarmine University Berea College Centre College of Kentucky Eastern Kentucky University The Filson Historical Society Georgetown College Kentucky Historical Society Kentucky State University Morehead State University Murray State University Northern Kentucky University Simmons College of Kentucky Spalding University Transylvania University University of Kentucky University of Louisville University of Pikeville Western Kentucky University Current Operation & Areas of Focus From its offices on the UK campus, the Press’s full-time staff of 15-17 publishes approximately 50 titles per year in print and electronic formats. The Press has over 2,100 titles in print with annual sales of approximately $1.75 million. University Press of Kentucky books are available through all major retail and wholesale channels, libraries, and online platforms, both domestic and international. The Press’s editorial program focuses on the humanities and the social sciences. Its publications in film and military studies have earned the Press a national reputation in these fields, with reviews in such media as the Wall Street Journal, New York Times, Los Angeles Times, Chicago Tribune, and NPR . Notable awards for Press titles include: thirteen Frederick Jackson Turner Awards (history); six Weatherford Awards (Appalachian studies); three Lillian Smith Book Awards (African American studies); and the Lannan Literary Award. Memberships & Partnerships In 2007, the Press entered into a partnership with the Association of the United States Army ( AUSA ) to co-publish outstanding works in military history and to exhibit at the association’s annual conference. The Press also regularly exhibits titles and works to cultivate authors at the annual meetings of the Appalachian Studies Association, the Popular Culture Association/American Culture Association, the the Association of Writers & Writing Programs, the Society for Military History, the Society for Cinema and Media Studies, and others. Current book imprints and series of note include: Screen Door Press, edited by Crystal Wilkinson; Fox Hill Books, edited by Silas House; Appalachian Futures: Black, Native, and Queer Voices; Asia in the New Millennium; Aviation and Air Power; Civil Rights and the Struggle for Black Equality in the Twentieth Century; Horses in History; New Directions in Southern History; New Poetry & Prose, in partnership with Centre College; Racing Royalty; Screen Classics; Topics in Kentucky History; and the AUSA American Warriors, Battles & Campaigns, and Foreign Military Studies series. The Press also publishes a large list in bourbon, spirits, and foodways. The University Press of Kentucky is a longstanding member of the international professional group the Association of University Presses (AUPresses) . Over the years, Press staff have served in a variety of capacities on AUPresses committees and working groups. The Press has also collaborated on books and events with statewide and community partners such as the Kentucky Humanities Council (this collaboration produced the outstanding New Books for New Readers Series, titles designed to enhance adult literacy through Kentucky-based subjects); the Kentucky Arts Council; Kentucky State Parks; the Kentucky Department of Libraries and Archives; the Kentucky Department of Fish and Wildlife; the Kentucky State Nature Preserves Commission; the Bluegrass Trust; and the Frazier History Museum, among others. NOTE : The University of Kentucky Libraries has exclusively retained Jack Farrell & Associates ( www.jackfarrell.com ) to find the winning candidate for this important hire. A resume and 2-page cover letter are required. The cover letter should address 1) why they are interested in the position; 2) how they are qualified; 3) their vision for the UPK going forward. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Ability to manage staff in various functions to produce a cohesive publishing effort. Evidence of innovative thinking in resolving publishing challenges and emerging trends. Understanding of current issues and trends in scholarly publication. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills and ability to work well with faculty, students, and colleagues. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience More than 8 years of experience in university press, scholarly, or academic publishing with increasing leadership responsibilities. Demonstrated success in strategic planning and organizational leadership. Experience managing budgets, business operations, and revenue-generating activities. Success securing grants, gifts, sponsorships, or other external funding. Experience building partnerships with external organizations and stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and lead high-performing teams. Deadline to Apply 10/23/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648526": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science, Regular Title Series",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science, Regular Title Series Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science, Regular Title Series Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science, Regular Title Series Requisition Number FE05011 Working Title Department Name 8G040:Kinesiology - Health Promotion Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education PhD or equivalent in field of Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Kinesiology, or a related field. Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification CSCS preferred Job Summary The Department of Kinesiology and Health Promotion invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor position in Exercise Science. The position is Regular Title Series, tenure-eligible. This is a 9-month appointment, effective August 16, 2027. The selected candidate will be expected to be actively committed to our departmental vision and mission by pursuing excellence in teaching, research and scholarship, and service. Successful candidates will be expected to teach graduate and undergraduate exercise science courses, with faculty in this position typically expected to teach a 2-2 course load. Responsibilities include the following: Teach 2 courses each semester (fall and spring), such as undergraduate courses in Strength and Conditioning for Sports, Physiology of Exercise, Introduction to Exercise Testing and Prescription, Practicum in Kinesiology and Health Promotion, Laboratory Methods in Exercise Science, or other exercise science/exercise physiology courses as assigned. Provide support for the undergraduate Exercise Science and Strength and Conditioning major and minor programs; Develop and maintain an active, interdisciplinary research agenda involving human subjects, showcasing a strong record of academic scholarship and potential for extramural support, as demonstrated by an independent research trajectory, peer-reviewed research publications, presentations, and/or grant support; Advise and mentor master’s and doctoral students in the exercise science program; Seek and be competitive for extramural research funding; and Provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. Interested applicants should apply at www.uky.edu/ukjobs and include the following materials: a detailed cover letter noting academic credentials and professional experience related to the responsibilities for this position — upload under Cover Letter; a curriculum vita (no photos) — upload under Curriculum Vita; a statement on teaching that includes reflections on the candidate’s teaching experiences, mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and copies of evaluations of the candidate’s teaching, if available — upload under Specific Request 1; a statement on research describing the candidate’s research interests and areas of expertise, dissemination of research, and current/potential funding agencies — upload under Specific Request 2; writing samples – up to three representative publications (first or corresponding author preferred) — upload under Writing Sample; names and contact information for three professional references – upload under References. References will be contacted to upload a letter once finalists have been selected. Review of applications will be conducted on a rolling basis. Preference will be given to applicants who have submitted their applications by October 16, 2026. Questions regarding the position or application materials may be directed to the search committee chair Dr. Lance Bollinger ( lance.bollinger@uky.edu ). Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities An earned doctorate in exercise science, exercise physiology, kinesiology, or a related field before the employment start date; A commitment to, and record of, successful college or university teaching excellence in areas related to exercise science, exercise physiology, kinesiology, or a related field; A strong record of academic scholarship as demonstrated by peer-reviewed research publications, a record of successful grant funding, or the ability to actively pursue extramural research funding; A commitment to and experience mentoring student research and career development; Potential for, or history of, active service participation and/or leadership roles in campus, community, and professional organizations; and The ability to work collegially and effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Demonstrated excellence in university-level teaching and student mentorship in relevant disciplinary areas, including experience with applied, laboratory-based, and experiential learning environments. Evidence of success in curriculum and course development at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Strong record of interdisciplinary collaboration and the ability to engage effectively with colleagues across academic and professional disciplines. Established record of scholarly productivity commensurate with career stage. Demonstrated potential to secure extramural funding and sustain an independent research program. Postdoctoral research experience is preferred. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Writing Sample Academic Transcript Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648368": {
      "title": "Physician - Academic Dermatologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Academic Dermatologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Academic Dermatologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Academic Dermatologist Requisition Number FE04710 Working Title Department Name 7H350:INTERNAL MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD or DO degree with board certification in Dermatology Required Related Experience Completion of an ACGME -accredited Dermatology Residency Program Completion of an ACGME -accredited Dermatopathology Fellowship Board-certified or board-eligible in Dermatology and Dermatopathology Experience in academic or teaching environments, preferably with internal medicine or family medicine residents and medical students Track record of peer-reviewed publications or scholarly presentations in dermatology and/or dermatopathology Demonstrated ability to collaborate across specialties and participate in multidisciplinary care Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for licensure in the Commonwealth of Kentucky Job Summary The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine invites applications for a full-time Academic Dermatologist to join the Division of Dermatology. The ideal candidate will be board-certified or board-eligible in dermatology and have demonstrated excellence in clinical care, dermatopathology, medical education, and scholarly activity. This position includes opportunities for clinical practice, teaching medical students and residents, and participating in research and academic endeavors. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the growth of academic dermatology at one of the Commonwealth’s leading academic health centers, with access to NIH -supported infrastructure, multidisciplinary partners, and patients from varied backgrounds. Please include an updated CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position. Job posting will remain open until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Experience serving in a leadership role (e.g., Chief Resident) Prior involvement in educational content development or curriculum design Participation in professional societies such as the American Academy of Dermatology ( AAD ) and American Society of Dermatopathology ( ASDP ) Interest in or experience with community engagement or committee service (e.g., melanoma/skin cancer programs) Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
