    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648355": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Police Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Police Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Police Officer Requisition Number RE55827 Working Title Department Name 3HL00:UK Police Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 45 Salary Range $23.18-38.25/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education HS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Police Certification Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 100 lbs., sitting for long periods of time, walking for long periods of time, standing for long periods of time, handling intermittent periods of high levels of stress. Shift Police Officers will be assigned to one of the following 12 hour shifts to include rotating weekends off: 7 am – 7 pm 7 pm – 7 am Officers work days, nights, weekends, holidays, and mandatory overtime to include UK sports and other university events. Job Summary University of Kentucky Police Officers are responsible for providing the UK community with a safe and secure environment in which to work, live, and learn. The department is service oriented and specializes in meeting the needs of the campus’ population of students, faculty, staff, hospital guests, and visitors. The major job responsibilities of the UK Police Officer include patrol and investigations, public relations and service, professional development and training, and report writing. Specific duties include patrol, law enforcement, criminal investigation, community relations, preparing and presenting testimony in court, completing trainings and professional development, and completing University documents including but not limited to reports, tickets, daily logs, and property/person receipts. Officers shall positively interact, enhance relations, and represent the University with local law enforcement, community partners, and UK HealthCare officials. To learn more about our who we are and what we do for the University and our community, Click Here . Feel free to reach out with any additional questions at JoinUKPD@uky.edu Multiple positions available. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until the deadline date or until all positions are filled which could be prior to deadline date listed. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Per Kentucky Regulations, this position has several minimum requirements to qualify as indicated below. • Citizen of the United States • At least twenty-one (21) years of age • High school graduate or has successfully completed a General Education Development (G.E.D.) examination • Possess a valid driver’s license to operate a motor vehicle • Has not been convicted of a felony • Has not been convicted of any misdemeanor or inchoate offenses under KRS Chapter 510 • Has not received a dishonorable discharge, bad conduct discharge, or general discharge under other than honorable conditions • Not prohibited by federal or state law from possessing a firearm • Not had certification as a peace officer permanently revoked in another state Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Per Kentucky regulations, this position requires several qualifications. These qualifications are in the posting within the \"Skills / Knowledge / Abilities\" section. Do you meet these minimum requirements? Yes No * Are you currently or have you previously been a certified police officer? Yes No * Have you obtained your Police Officer Professional Standards Certification through the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council (KLEC)? Yes No * Have you obtained a police officer certification through another state? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648342": {
      "title": "Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clinical Staf/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clinical Staf/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clinical Staf/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clinical Staf/UKHC Requisition Number RE55822 Working Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clinical Staff/UKHC - Education and Academic Detailing Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 14 Salary Range $114.911-156,062/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Pharmacist Physical Requirements This position requires intermittently sitting at a computer workstation and performing tasks with repetitive motions (such as typing); occasionally standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Also involves risk of injuries from use of equipment on the job; working in confined spaces; and exposure to blood-borne or airborne pathogens, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, and cuts/punctures. Shift Day shift; varies 7:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Hours and days of the week are subject to change based on needs and growth of department. Job Summary This position will help establish and lead the delivery of a new pharmacist-led academic detailing program across UK HealthCare, providing individualized, evidence-based education and clinical outreach to healthcare providers to promote appropriate medication use, support guideline implementation, improve medication safety and patient outcomes, and advance cost-effective prescribing practices. This position will serve as a clinical liaison between UK Specialty Pharmacy and Infusion Services and healthcare providers, establishing collaborative relationships, assessing provider-specific educational needs and prescribing practices, and translating clinical evidence, formulary information, and medication-use data into actionable recommendations. This position will support prescribing optimization and the integration of evidence-based practices into clinical workflows. The pharmacist will also develop educational materials, track and evaluate program outcomes, and use provider feedback and prescribing data to refine academic detailing strategies and identify opportunities for quality improvement. This position will also support pharmacy education, training, competency initiatives, accreditation readiness, continuing education, experiential education, and the development of educational resources for UKSPIS staff, students, residents, and other healthcare professionals. This position will expand the reach of UKSPIS clinical expertise, strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration, and support the delivery of high-quality, safe, and cost-effective patient care across the health system. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong clinical skills; knowledge of inpatient drug distribution and dispensing; ability to prioritize; excellent communication skills; a “team” mentality; desire to teach; and motivation are required to excel in this position. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience PharmD and completion of an ASHP -accredited PGY1 residency program (or equivalent experience) preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you licensed or eligible to be licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have practicing as a licensed pharmacist? None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Briefly describe your pharmacy experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience in working with physicians, nurses, and pharmacists to secure Prior Authorizations. (Open Ended Question) * Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide excellent customer service. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648319": {
      "title": "Study Ambassador",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Study Ambassador Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Study Ambassador Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Study Ambassador Requisition Number DU15096 Department Name 40546:Center for the Environment Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education HS Required Related Experience none Required License/Registration/Certification none Physical Requirements carrying objects up to 25 pounds Shift days, evenings, and weekends. 4 to 5 hours per week. Job Summary The East Palestine Train Derailment Health Research Program is seeking five Study Ambassadors to serve as trusted voices for the research in their own communities. Ambassadors will help connect residents of East Palestine, Ohio, and the surrounding region, including Western Pennsylvania with learning about and taking part in the study. They will also play an active role in communication about the ongoing research and it’s findings with the communities. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Required Lives in, works in, or has strong ties to East Palestine or the surrounding Ohio and Pennsylvania communities. Known and trusted within the community, with a genuine interest in the health of friends and neighbors. Comfortable starting conversations and speaking with people from all walks of life. Reliable, organized, and able to follow through on commitments. Able to respect participant privacy and handle sensitive information with discretion. Willing to complete required training before beginning outreach. At least 18 years of age. Preferred Experience in community volunteering, civic or faith-based leadership, or local advocacy. Existing connections to local schools, churches, businesses, or community groups. Comfort using social media, email, and text messaging for outreach. Personal experience with the derailment and its aftermath is valued but not required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience some college or paid experience Deadline to Apply 12/31/9999 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648214": {
      "title": "Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Respiratory Therapist Senior/UKHC Requisition Number RE54175 Working Title Respiratory Therapist Senior Department Name H3410:Respiratory Services Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 11 Salary Range $30.00-45.70/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education AS Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience No experience required. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensure through the Kentucky Board of Respiratory Care and Registered Respiratory Therapist ( RRT ) through the National Board of Respiratory Care at time of hire. Physical Requirements The ability to lift, carry, push, and pull 25-100 pounds on a daily basis, as well as stand, walk and sit for long periods of time. The conditions of work may involve exposure to communicable diseases and injury from intractable patients or sharp instruments. Shift Must be able to work three 12.5-hour shifts per week (7:00 p.m. – 7:30 a.m.) Will also be required to work weekends and holidays. Job Summary UK HealthCare is seeking registered respiratory therapists dedicated to wellness, safety, and patient-centered care. The Respiratory Therapist Senior ensures competent care of patients through airway management, mechanical ventilator management, blood gases, oxygen therapy, aerosol therapy, and other duties as it relates to assure the quality of patient care. The ideal candidate will perform proper documentation of patient care activities and interventions; record therapy and results as required by hospital policy and regulatory agencies; and communicate with other healthcare teams to ensure the quality care of patients. Albert B. Chandler Hospital remains the No. 1 hospital in Kentucky and the Bluegrass Region, according to U.S. News & World Report’s Best Hospitals Rankings and offers a large, state-of-the-art (569-bed) teaching hospital with over 100gunn ICU beds across multiple service lines. Chandler hosts the region’s only Level 1 trauma center and is also home to the Markey Cancer Center which has earned designation by the National Cancer Institute. Respiratory therapists at Chandler will have the excellent opportunity to deliver a considerable range of services covered under their RT license. Multiple positions available. Review of applications will begin immediately, and applications will be accepted until the deadline date or until all positions are filled which could be prior to deadline date listed. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will have patient care experience, strong computer skills, and excellent communication skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital experience is preferred. Deadline to Apply 10/22/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently credentialed as a Registered Respiratory Therapist through the National Board of Respiratory Care (NBRC)? Yes Eligible to obtain within 6 months of hire No * Do you currently hold a Kentucky Respiratory Care Practitioner License through the Kentucky Board of Respiratory Care (KBRC) or are you eligible to obtain by date of hire? Yes No * Please indicate your years of paid work experience with respiratory care. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years * Do you have hospital experience in pediatric respiratory care? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648197": {
      "title": "Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Requisition Number FE05015 Working Title Department Name 7H503:OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY - MATERNAL FETAL Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN as well as fellowship in Maternal-Fetal Medicine Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for, or currently licensed, to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Board Certified/Board Eligible in OB/ GYN Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky, College of Medicine, Lexington, Kentucky is seeking a Board Certified/Board Eligible physician to join the Division of Maternal-Fetal Medicine ( MFM ) for a full-time faculty position.This position supports the department’s missions of clinical care, teaching, and scholarly activity, with opportunities for professional growth within a comprehensive academic medical center. Responsibilities include clinical care (prenatal diagnosis and treatment, advanced obstetric ultrasound, invasive procedure and high-risk pregnancy consultation and care); teaching our outstanding residents and medical students, perinatal outreach, as well as involvement with clinical outcomes or basic research. We offer PhD supported research programs, and our faculty members coordinate grants. Dedicated research time is available and will be consistent with the applicant’s research experience and interest. The Division of Maternal-Fetal Medicine has a Board-Approved three-year Fellowship which takes one fellow each year. Experience in teaching and supervising medical students and resident physicians is desirable. Applicants should also have an interest in clinical care and research. A competitive salary and benefits package is being offered. The UK College of Medicine Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology is a strong, multidisciplinary team dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 47 faculty members, 30 Advanced Practice Providers, and more than 225 learners. UK HealthCare’s Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB- GYN ) specialty ranked No. 28 in the nation in the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Hospitals rankings. This marks the third consecutive year our program has been recognized as a top national specialty, reflecting the continued dedication of our faculty, staff, and care teams to excellence in women’s health. The Joint Commission’s Maternal Levels of Care ( MLC ) Verification program, offered in collaboration with the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists ( ACOG ), named UK HealthCare as a Level IV maternal care verified facility. As a Level IV facility, UK HealthCare provides expert and compassionate care for critically ill and high-risk maternity patients. The MLC Verification program provides an objective assessment of a facility’s capabilities, and verifies that a hospital has the expertise, equipment, and resources in place for a patient’s specific needs and risk level. As a top hospital in Kentucky, UK HealthCare provides the highest level of maternity care and receives patients from other hospitals who have high-risk pregnancies or experience complications during labor. UK HealthCare underwent a comprehensive onsite review in early 2025 to verify the level of care provided. Each year, providers in the department care for thousands of patients across several clinical sites around the state. Currently, the department offers outreach services in ovarian cancer screening, gynecologic oncology, general gynecology, and high-risk obstetrics at more than 24 locations throughout the state. Additionally, 22 new sites are in the planning stages, with some current locations adding more clinic days to better serve patients. The department trains 28 residents and fellows across ACGME accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure over $75 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries. Our research division offers a dynamic and collaborative environment spanning three key areas of women’s health: reproductive endocrinology and infertility, gynecologic oncology, and maternal fetal medicine. Our research team explores critical questions in ovarian function, hormone regulation, inflammation, and the impact of endocrine-disrupting chemicals. We also lead epidemiologic investigations into the health effects of intimate partner violence, sexual violence, and related adverse outcomes—bridging science with real-world health challenges. With longstanding support from federal agencies such as the NIH and CDC , and a strong record of publication in leading medical and scientific journals, our work reflects a commitment to high-impact, translational research. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Please include an updated CV when applying for the position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648194": {
      "title": "Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Requisition Number FE05016 Working Title Department Name 7H508:OB/GYN  Subspecialties Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN Required License/Registration/Certification Eligibility for or current medical license in the state of Kentucky Board certified or eligibility in OB/ GYN Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky, is seeking a Board Certified/Board Eligible Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility ( REI ) fellowship trained Physician to join the Division of Gynecologic Surgery for a full-time faculty position. The successful candidate will have completed a residency in OBGYN and completed or be completing a fellowship in Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility. Recent graduates are encouraged to apply. Enjoy an active role caring for patients and performing research while educating residents and medical students. The UK College of Medicine Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology is a strong, multidisciplinary team dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 47 faculty members, 30 Advanced Practice Providers, and more than 225 learners. UK HealthCare’s Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB- GYN ) specialty ranked No. 28 in the nation in the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Hospitals rankings. This marks the third consecutive year our program has been recognized as a top national specialty, reflecting the continued dedication of our faculty, staff, and care teams to excellence in women’s health. The Joint Commission’s Maternal Levels of Care ( MLC ) Verification program, offered in collaboration with the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists ( ACOG ), named UK HealthCare as a Level IV maternal care verified facility. As a Level IV facility, UK HealthCare provides expert and compassionate care for critically ill and high-risk maternity patients. The MLC Verification program provides an objective assessment of a facility’s capabilities, and verifies that a hospital has the expertise, equipment, and resources in place for a patient’s specific needs and risk level. As a top hospital in Kentucky, UK HealthCare provides the highest level of maternity care and receives patients from other hospitals who have high-risk pregnancies or experience complications during labor. UK HealthCare underwent a comprehensive onsite review in early 2025 to verify the level of care provided. Each year, providers in the department care for thousands of patients across several clinical sites around the state. Currently, the department offers outreach services in ovarian cancer screening, gynecologic oncology, general gynecology, and high-risk obstetrics at more than 24 locations throughout the state. Additionally, 22 new sites are in the planning stages, with some current locations adding more clinic days to better serve patients. The department trains 28 residents and fellows across ACGME accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure over $75 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries. Our research division offers a dynamic and collaborative environment spanning three key areas of women’s health: reproductive endocrinology and infertility, gynecologic oncology, and maternal fetal medicine. Our research team explores critical questions in ovarian function, hormone regulation, inflammation, and the impact of endocrine-disrupting chemicals. We also lead epidemiologic investigations into the health effects of intimate partner violence, sexual violence, and related adverse outcomes—bridging science with real-world health challenges. With longstanding support from federal agencies such as the NIH and CDC , and a strong record of publication in leading medical and scientific journals, our work reflects a commitment to high-impact, translational research. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Please include a CV along with the application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience in teaching and supervising medical students Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
