    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/648010": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Opera Office Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Opera Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Opera Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Opera Office Assistant Requisition Number DU15083 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 412 Rose St Lexington, KY 40506 Salary Range $12.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education N/A Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Lift 50 pounds. Shift Weekdays between 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Some evenings. . Job Summary The School of Music Opera Theatre department is looking for an individual to assist the production manager with a variety of production and administrative duties: Scan and digitize archival documents Distribute production marketing materials Assist with loading and unloading van for events and productions Assist with gear transport, setup and breakdown for events Accompany on trips to warehouse and surplus Organize office and storage spaces Support social media efforts and strategy Weekly kitchen cleaning Seasonal building decorating Other duties as assigned Skills / Knowledge / Abilities N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply 12/12/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
