    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647966": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Requisition Number FE05009 Working Title Department Name 8E000:College of Arts & Sciences Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education A PhD in Biology, Neuroscience, or a related field is required at time of appointment. Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Biology at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, with expertise in the field of Cell and Molecular Neuroscience. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research incorporates induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC)-derived neural cells, organ-on-chip, and/or cerebral organoid models to study mechanisms of neurodevelopment, neurodevelopmental or neurodegenerative disorders, neuronal function, neural circuit development, or related areas of neuroscience. We encourage applications from candidates using iPSC/organoid models in conjunction with complementary experimental approaches such as genome editing, imaging, transcriptomics, proteomics, and electrophysiology, as well as computational approaches. Consideration will also be given to strong research programs using invertebrate model systems focused on the topic areas listed above. The successful candidate will demonstrate evidence of an ability to obtain extramural grant support, communicate their research, and effectively teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Responsibilities for the successful candidate will include: (1) establishment of an independent research program that is supported by awards from extramural agencies; (2) contribution to the teaching mission of the undergraduate program, which will include the development and teaching of a course on Developmental Neurobiology; (3) teaching and mentoring of graduate students and postdoctoral fellows; and (4) service to the department, university, and profession. We will offer a competitive start-up package and laboratory space for this faculty position. The Department of Biology is a highly collaborative with research strengths in neuroscience, regenerative and developmental biology, ecology and evolutionary biology, and circadian rhythms and biological timing. Our faculty and trainees use a diverse array of biological model systems and mathematical and computational tools. Our faculty also collaborate with life science faculty in the Colleges of Medicine, Pharmacy, Engineering, Agriculture, Public Health, and Arts and Sciences, as well as the Markey Cancer Center, the Sanders Brown Center on Aging, and the Center for Clinical and Translational Science. The anticipated Distribution of Effort will be 30% teaching, 60% research, and 10% departmental service. This position will be a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. A PhD in Biology, Neuroscience, or a related field is required at time of appointment. Applicants must include the following: 1) letter of application (upload as Cover Letter) 2) CV 3) research statement (upload as Specific Request 1) 4) teaching statement (upload as Specific Request 2) 5) In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the academic profile. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references within the employment system. Questions about this search should be addressed to Ann Morris, Professor and Chair, Department of Biology, University of Kentucky ann.morris@uky.edu . Application review will begin on 10/15/2026. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ medical coverage and in addition, offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulations concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647947": {
      "title": "Clinician - Ambulatory Psychologist/Researcher",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Clinician - Ambulatory Psychologist/Researcher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Clinician - Ambulatory Psychologist/Researcher Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinician - Ambulatory Psychologist/Researcher Requisition Number FE05008 Working Title Department Name 7H800:PSYCHIATRY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Doctoral degree in a clinical field, such as social work, psychology, or counseling, or related field. Required Related Experience Required Clinical Experience Applicants will have previous experience providing psychological services through evidence-based psychotherapy, psychological testing and/or related services. Demonstrated experience collaborating with physicians and other clinicians in diagnosing and treating patients with mental health conditions. Demonstrated ability in teaching students or trainees is strongly preferred. Required Research Experience Applicants will have an established track record in conducting independent research, publishing novel scientific findings, and obtaining extramural funding. Experience doing community and stakeholder-engaged research is preferred. This position will have significant research effort so that an extramurally funded research program can be established in the context of the Department’s core research areas, which include substance use, trauma, HIV , mood disorders, and suicide prevention. Experience in working with children, adolescents, and young adults is preferred. Required License/Registration/Certification Current licensure ( LCSW , Ph.D., LPP , LPCC , or the equivalent), or eligibility to obtain licensure and/or industry-standard board certification in the field of psychotherapy, psychological testing or related services to practice in the state of Kentucky. Job Summary The UK College of Medicine Department of Psychiatry is seeking a faculty member to serve as a clinician and researcher in its Research Division. The Department employs physicians, psychologists, therapists and other mental health professionals to provide a wide variety of behavioral health and substance use treatment services at multiple locations. Our clinicians provide care at our UK Psychiatric & Behavioral Health Care Clinic at Fountain Court, Albert B. Chandler Hospital, Good Samaritan Hospital, Eastern State Hospital, and various other clinics and departments throughout the UK HealthCare system and outside organizations throughout Kentucky. Our team of researchers are working to advance the understanding of behavioral health and how behavioral health conditions are managed and treated. Our department has five ACGME -certified residency training programs which focus on training more than 50 physicians each year to become the future leaders in psychiatry. Our Department strives to provide the highest level of patient care, innovative educational programs, active research in mental illness and advocacy throughout the state of Kentucky and beyond. These pursuits have helped the department win the American College of Psychiatrists’ Award for Creativity in Psychiatric Education not once, but twice. The successful candidate must be committed to excellence in clinical care providing psychotherapy, psychological testing, and related services to adults or children and adolescents. Additionally the candidate must have an emerging or sustained track record of success in research including a history of submitting and/or receiving intramural or extramural funding as well as publishing articles in peer reviewed journals. The Department of Psychiatry’s a Behavioral Health Care Clinic is located near the Hamburg area of Lexington at 245 Fountain Ct., Lexington, KY, 40509. This off-campus location provides free onsite parking for employees and patients as well as a primary care/urgent care clinic and retail pharmacy that is accessible for both patients and employees. In addition, the University of Kentucky provides a comprehensive beneﬁts package including health, dental, and insurance beneﬁts, a competitive 2:1 retirement match up to 5% of an employee’s base salary, discounts to local, regional and national businesses, paid vacation and temporary disability leave (sick time) and 14 paid holidays each year. For additional information on University of Kentucky’s beneﬁts, please visit https://hr.uky.edu/insurance-and-retirement . In addition, the Department of Psychiatry provides paid time and funding for professional development to include monthly Grand Rounds, didactic teaching from our faculty as part of our resident physician education programs, CEU opportunities from several behavioral health-related ﬁelds across the University, and opportunities to collaborate on research projects, published papers and other scholarly work. If you are interested in joining our team of behavioral health providers making a difference in our community and across the State, please consider applying for this position. To be considered an applicant for the position, please submit a CV and cover letter with your application. Please also include the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the application. This information may be used to solicit reference letters within the employment system. Applications will be reviewed immediately. The position will remain open until filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities -Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills and the ability to interact effectively with colleagues, supervisors, stakeholders, and the public. -Collaborative work ethic, with a commitment to fostering a respectful work environment. -Strong organizational and time-management skills, attention to detail, adaptability, and the ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. -Dependability, punctuality, initiative, and a positive, solution-oriented approach to work. -Confidentiality when handling sensitive information and a keen sense of integrity. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647944": {
      "title": "Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Obstetrician / Gynecologist (OB/GYN) Requisition Number FE05013 Working Title Department Name 7H511: OB-GYN/GEORGETOWN Work Location Georgetown, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for, or currently licensed, to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Board Certified/Board Eligible in OB/ GYN Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky, College of Medicine is seeking a Board Certified/Board Eligible general OBGYN for a full-time position at the UK Women’s Georgetown OBGYN Practice and Georgetown Community Hospital in Georgetown, Kentucky. Major responsibilities of this position include comprehensive Obstetrics and Gynecology practice and participation in teaching activities with medical students. Development and participation in educational and community activities and involvement in hospital and university committees is strongly encouraged. Experience and enthusiasm in teaching and supervising medical students is desirable. A competitive salary and benefits package is being offered, and opportunities for faculty development are available and encouraged. Job responsibilities include: Building a comprehensive OB/ GYN clinical practice. Expectation is for nine half-days per week of clinical practice with some combination of Clinic, Operating room-surgery, and Labor and Delivery. Night, weekend, and holiday call will be shared equally among the UK Georgetown practice and UKHC faculty. Excellence in Clinical teaching with medical students and potentially other health care students is expected. In addition, working in partnership with UKCOM and the OBGYN Clerkship Director to build a strong educational clinical site for the UKCOM OBGYN -clerkship. The UK College of Medicine Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology is a strong, multidisciplinary team dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 47 faculty members, 30 Advanced Practice Providers, and more than 225 learners. UK HealthCare’s Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB- GYN ) specialty ranked No. 28 in the nation in the 2025–2026 U.S. News & World Report Best Hospitals rankings. This marks the third consecutive year our program has been recognized as a top national specialty, reflecting the continued dedication of our faculty, staff, and care teams to excellence in women’s health. The Joint Commission’s Maternal Levels of Care ( MLC ) Verification program, offered in collaboration with the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists ( ACOG ), named UK HealthCare as a Level IV maternal care verified facility. As a Level IV facility, UK HealthCare provides expert and compassionate care for critically ill and high-risk maternity patients. The MLC Verification program provides an objective assessment of a facility’s capabilities, and verifies that a hospital has the expertise, equipment, and resources in place for a patient’s specific needs and risk level. As a top hospital in Kentucky, UK HealthCare provides the highest level of maternity care and receives patients from other hospitals who have high-risk pregnancies or experience complications during labor. UK HealthCare underwent a comprehensive onsite review in early 2025 to verify the level of care provided. Each year, providers in the department care for thousands of patients across several clinical sites around the state. Currently, the department offers outreach services in ovarian cancer screening, gynecologic oncology, general gynecology, and high-risk obstetrics at more than 24 locations throughout the state. Additionally, 22 new sites are in the planning stages, with some current locations adding more clinic days to better serve patients. The department trains 28 residents and fellows across ACGME accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Faculty secure over $75 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries. Our research division offers a dynamic and collaborative environment spanning three key areas of women’s health: reproductive endocrinology and infertility, gynecologic oncology, and maternal fetal medicine. Our research team explores critical questions in ovarian function, hormone regulation, inflammation, and the impact of endocrine-disrupting chemicals. We also lead epidemiologic investigations into the health effects of intimate partner violence, sexual violence, and related adverse outcomes—bridging science with real-world health challenges. With longstanding support from federal agencies such as the NIH and CDC , and a strong record of publication in leading medical and scientific journals, our work reflects a commitment to high-impact, translational research. The University of Kentucky plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Georgetown and Lexington combine safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Georgetown and Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Please include an updated CV when applying for the position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience in teaching or supervising medical students Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647943": {
      "title": "Major Campus Programming Student Event Manager",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Major Campus Programming Student Event Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Major Campus Programming Student Event Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Major Campus Programming Student Event Manager Requisition Number DU15081 Department Name 1B430:Student Organizations and Activities Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00/hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Currently enrolled at UK as an Undergrad Required Related Experience Involvement in UK campus organizations (Registered Student Organization, Student Sponsored Organization, Club Sports, etc.), event management and execution, hospitality Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 lbs., sitting for long periods of time Shift Mon-Fri 4p-after, some weekends; 5-10 hours/week Job Summary Overview: The MCP Student Event Manager , at the guidance of the Major Campus Programming Coordinator, Senior Specialist, and/or Associate Director, will assist in executing semesterly Major Campus Programming events hosted by the Office of Student Organizations & Activities. Events include: SOA Cinema Series, Bingo, Trivia, Game Watches, tabling events, and other duties as assigned. Key Responsibilities: This position includes various tasks relating to in-person event management and execution including event set-up, check-in of attendees, event clean-up. This position is also subject to a minimum number of shifts per semester. Facilitation/hosting of events, engaging with guests, discussing involvement opportunities with students, and other duties as assigned. Candidates considered should have strong interpersonal skills and be able to actively engage with students, peers, or staff at events. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong customer service and hospitality, engaging with guests at events, strong communication and logistical skills, effective time management Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Currently enrolled at UK as an Undergrad; Involvement in UK campus organizations (Registered Student Organization, Student Sponsored Organization, Club Sports, etc.), event management and execution, hospitality Deadline to Apply 10/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position works with large scale events and programming.  What has been your experience  helping to plan and manage events? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
