    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647159": {
      "title": "Geologist III",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Geologist III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Geologist III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Geologist III Requisition Number RE55730 Working Title Department Name 40520:KY Geological Survey Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 46 Salary Range $53,061-87,526/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 3 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Independently traverse rough terrain for field work. Periodic lifting of 50lbs or less. Sitting or standing for long periods of time. Shift Monday – Friday; 8:00am to 5:00pm. Job Summary Advance Energy Geoscience Research to Support Kentucky’s Subsurface Resource Future The University of Kentucky is seeking a Geologist III to join the Kentucky Geological Survey ( KGS ) . This position will contribute to KGS’s subsurface and energy geology research program through the investigation of energy resources, basin analysis, geophysics, and related geoscience disciplines. The successful candidate will develop research projects, publish findings, engage with stakeholders, manage projects and personnel, and help advance KGS’s mission of supporting informed decisions about Kentucky’s subsurface resources. What You’ll Do Perform independent geologic research focused on subsurface energy resources, basin analysis, geophysics, petrophysics, stratigraphy, structural geology, and related topics. Compile, analyze, and interpret geological, geophysical, and petrophysical datasets to create maps, cross sections, and regional subsurface characterizations. Conduct field investigations, collect geological samples, and apply established data collection and safety standards. Publish research results in peer-reviewed outlets and present findings at professional conferences and meetings. Manage research projects, including project planning, budgeting, reporting, database maintenance, and coordination with collaborators and sponsors. Develop new research opportunities through stakeholder engagement, networking, proposal development, and pursuit of external funding. Supervise research staff, assign work, monitor progress, and provide mentoring and professional development support. Collaborate with KGS colleagues, external partners, state agencies, landowners, and stakeholders to support successful project outcomes and public engagement efforts. What You’ll Bring Strong technical expertise in one or more areas such as petrophysics, stratigraphy, structural geology, geophysics, geofluids, or subsurface energy resources. Experience interpreting complex geological and geophysical datasets using industry-standard software tools. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including scientific publication and presentation experience. Ability to manage multiple projects, maintain organized datasets, and oversee project deliverables. Strong attention to detail, sound professional judgment, and analytical problem-solving skills. Collaborative approach to teamwork, mentoring, stakeholder engagement, and relationship building. Knowledge of Kentucky geology is beneficial. Minimum Requirements PhD 3 years of related experience What’s In It for You Opportunity to build and lead a research program focused on emerging and traditional energy resources important to the Commonwealth of Kentucky. Access to extensive KGS resources, including drill cores, well logs, seismic reflection data, and potential fields datasets. Opportunities to collaborate with researchers, government agencies, industry partners, and stakeholders across the region. Potential opportunities for adjunct faculty appointments and involvement in mentoring and education. Support for professional growth through research, publications, conferences, workshops, and proposal development. Hybrid work eligibility, with approval UK’s Exceptional Benefits Why Now? Kentucky continues to experience strong interest in both established and emerging energy resources, creating opportunities for research that informs responsible resource development and long-term resilience for the Commonwealth. KGS is investing in expanded understanding of subsurface systems, energy resources, and geologic storage opportunities that support statewide needs. This role provides an opportunity to help shape future research initiatives, develop externally funded projects, and contribute scientific expertise that supports stakeholders, policymakers, and communities across Kentucky and the broader region. For more information, please contact Dr. Michael McGlue ( michael.mcglue@uky.edu ). The first review of application materials (CV, cover letter, and writing sample of a peer reviewed scientific paper) will begin on October 19 , 2026. References will be requested after the first review of applications; references will be contacted as one component of the evaluation. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities ESRI ArcGIS, MS Office, experience with field sampling, 5+ years of Driver’s license. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Writing Sample Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/647040": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Public and Nonprofit Management",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Public and Nonprofit Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Public and Nonprofit Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Public and Nonprofit Management Requisition Number FE04998 Working Title Department Name 8W100:Martin School of Public Administration Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in Public Administration, Public Policy, Public Affairs, Political Science, Management, or a closely related field completed by the time of appointment ( ABD candidates with a defined completion timeline may be considered for appointment at the Assistant Professor rank, contingent on degree conferral). Required Related Experience Research agenda in public management and nonprofit management, broadly construed. Ability or potential to teach online and in-person graduate and undergraduate courses in public and nonprofit management. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Martin School of Public Policy and Administration at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Public and Nonprofit Management, open to appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank. We welcome applicants working in any major area of public and nonprofit management, including but not limited to organizational behavior, human resource management, nonprofit governance, nonprofit finance, behavioral public administration, and collaborative or networked governance. Junior applicants are expected to demonstrate a promising research agenda and the potential for excellence in graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentoring. For appointment at the Associate Professor rank, applicants should have an established record of high-quality peer-reviewed research, effective graduate and/or undergraduate teaching and mentoring, and a demonstrated capacity for leadership in the field. This is a 9-month appointment to begin August 1, 2027. About the School The Martin School of Public Policy and Administration is a comprehensive school of policy and administration, offering degrees at the bachelor’s, master’s and doctoral level, as well as graduate certificates. Consistently ranked among the top public policy and administration schools in the nation, the Martin School is celebrating 50 years since its founding in 1976. Excelling in research, education and public service, it provides an innovative environment reflective of commitment, strategic thinking and integrity. It prepares graduates for a variety of public service careers including those in local, state, or federal government, nonprofit agencies, and advocacy organizations, as well as for advanced studies in fields such as law, public policy, management, and public finance. Interested applicants should submit an application online at https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646348 and include: · Letter of interest detailing qualifications (upload under Cover Letter ) · Current curriculum vita (upload under Curriculum Vita ) · Sample research writing (upload under Specific Request 1 ) · Names and contact information for three professional references (Upload under Specific Request 2 ) Inquiries regarding the position may be submitted to Dr. Taha Hameduddin, search committee chair, at ta.ha@uky.edu . For more information about the Martin School, please visit Martin School of Public Policy and Administration Review of applications will begin October 9, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Ph.D in Public Administration, Public Policy, Public Affairs, Political Science, Management , or a closely related field completed by time of appointment. Research expertise in one or more of the following areas: nonprofit governance, nonprofit financial management, philanthropy, volunteering, organizational behavior, strategic management, behavioral public administration, cross-sector collaboration, coproduction, or networked governance. Experience conducting community-engaged and public impact research with relevance for public and nonprofit management. Experience applying novel research approaches and methodologies to scholarship, including but not limited to, experimental/behavioral, qualitative, mixed-methods, and network approaches. Evidence of, or strong potential to secure, extramural research funding. Experience teaching or willingness to teach in areas complementary to the School’s existing curriculum in public financial management and policy analysis. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
