    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646864": {
      "title": "MRI Technologist/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | MRI Technologist/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support MRI Technologist/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title MRI Technologist/MS Pool/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number DU13503 Department Name H3184: MRI Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $43-$67/hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education Associates Degree Required Related Experience 18 months of related experience required Required License/Registration/Certification American Registry of Radiologic Technologists ( ARRT ) at time of hire; Basic Life Support certification via AHA within 90 days of hire, MRI registry within one year of hire. Physical Requirements This position requires regularly lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects weighing up to or over 50 pounds; and performing tasks with repetitive motions; intermittently standing or walking with objects weighing up to 25 pounds; and sitting at a computer workstation for extended periods of time; and occasionally working at heights above four feet and/or in confined spaces. Also involves regular to occasional risk of injury from moving, lifting or positioning patients, equipment, or materials; and exposure to loud noises, temperature extremes, hazardous chemicals and fumes including waste, radiation, burns, cuts/punctures, blood-borne or airborne pathogens, and combative/violent people. Shift Shift opportunities will be discussed during the interview process. Depending on level, employees must work a minimum of 96 to 216 hours in a 6-week period. Job Summary The MRI Technologist will be responsible for performing Magnetic Resonance Imaging procedures in accordance with standards and practice set forth by ARRT and Department Policies and Procedures; and will demonstrate a knowledge of the human structure and functions, patient care, positioning, principles of electromagnetic and computer sciences, magnetic protection, and specialized techniques. The individual in this role is expected to be able to apply appropriate patient care and recognize patient conditions essential for successful completion of procedures. Per diem pay is as follows: Level I – 96 hours any shift / 6-week schedule = $43/hour Level II – 144 hours any shift / 6-week schedule = $51/hour Level III – 216 hours any shift / 6-week week schedule = $59/hour Level IV – 216 hours on nights / 6-week week schedule = $67/hour Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 09/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires you to currently hold or eligible to obtain ARRT (American Registry of Radiologic Technologists) certification. Will you be able to meet these requirements? Yes No * This position requires MRI (Magnetic Resonance Imaging) registry within one year of hire. Are you aware of this requirement? Yes No * Basic Life Support (BLS) certification through the American Heart Association (AHA) is required within 90 days of hire. Are you aware of this requirement? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646852": {
      "title": "Physician - Musculoskeletal Radiologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Musculoskeletal Radiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Musculoskeletal Radiologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Musculoskeletal Radiologist Requisition Number FE05005 Working Title Musculoskeletal Radiologist Department Name 7H300:RADIOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD degree or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency and fellowship as appropriate Required License/Registration/Certification Board certified/board eligible by the American Board of Radiology. Must obtain Kentucky medical licensure upon appointment and maintain throughout the term of the appointment. Must be appropriately credentialed and accepted as a member of the active staff at the University Chandler and Good Samaritan Hospitals, Kentucky Clinic and other sites deemed necessary by the Chair of Radiology. Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine seeks an exceptional full-time Musculoskeletal Radiologist for a clinical faculty position in the Division of Musculoskeletal Radiology. The MSK division has a mature ACGME accredited fellowship program with one position every year. Two dynamic radiology residents rotate on service each month. The division covers a comprehensive blend of sports, orthopedic trauma, tumor, rheumatology, plastics, and emergency imaging studies and procedures. The UK College of Medicine Department of Radiology is a strong, multidisciplinary team that is dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together through world-class clinical care, innovation and research, and educating the next generation of physicians. Our department encompasses more than 60 faculty members and more than 500 staff. The Department of Radiology is home to nationally recognized leaders in their fields that drive the mission of the institution forward. Radiologists interpreted more than 700,000 studies during the last year, covering our Level I Trauma Center with a census of approximately 700 beds, our NCCN -accredited Comprehensive Cancer Center, Kentucky Children’s Hospital, and our outpatient imaging facilities. This recruitment will support our continued growth, including: opening of a Cancer and Advanced Ambulatory Building, a new multi-disciplinary ambulatory care site, an expansion of our main hospital, and a new tower for Kentucky Children’s Hospital. The Department is active in education. The Diagnostic Radiology residency program has 32 residents (8 per class). The Integrated Interventional Radiology residency has 10 residents (2 per class). The Department has both the Early Specialization in IR ( ESIR ) pathway and the Independent Interventional Radiology residency. The Department also boasts a Medical Physics Residency. Fellowships in Abdominal Imaging, Chest and Cardiovascular Imaging, Breast Imaging, Musculoskeletal Imaging, Neuroradiology, Emergency Radiology, and Oncologic Imaging are available. For those interested in Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, the accelerated pathway to dual ABNM and ABR certification is available. The Department also supports learners on the ABR alternate pathway. There are many opportunities to teach and interact with medical students as well. The Department of Radiology participates in more than 50 on-going clinical trials across a variety of areas including, but not limited to, molecular imaging, oncology, theranostics, fMRI and neuro-imaging, interventional radiology, and AI. Faculty from the Department of Radiology published more than 50 manuscripts during the last academic year and were invited speakers at over 100 national or international conferences. This position will provide an opportunity for advancement with generous benefit package including: · Professional Development Funding · Relocation Assistance · Malpractice Insurance · 200% 403b Retirement Match · Educational Benefits for Family Members · Rank and Compensation Commensurate with Experience. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, and an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Please include an updated CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position.  Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646850": {
      "title": "Physician - Neuroradiologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Neuroradiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Neuroradiologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Neuroradiologist Requisition Number FE05004 Working Title Department Name 7H300:RADIOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D or D.O Equivalent Required Related Experience The successful candidate must have an MD/DO degree (or equivalent) and be board-certified or board-eligible by The American Board of Radiology. Subspecialty training and/or experience would be a plus. Required License/Registration/Certification Eligibility for, or in possession of, a Kentucky Medical License and DEA license. The successful candidate must be board-certified or board-eligible by The American Board of Radiology. Subspecialty training and/or experience would be a plus. Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine, located in Lexington, KY, seeks an exceptional full-time Assistant, Associate, or Professor in Neuroradiology for a full-time clinical faculty position in the Division of Neuroradiology at the Albert B. Chandler Medical Center. The UK College of Medicine Department of Radiology is a strong, multidisciplinary team that is dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together through world-class clinical care, innovation and research, and educating the next generation of physicians. Our department encompasses more than 60 faculty members and more than 500 staff. The Department of Radiology is home to nationally recognized leaders in their fields that drive the mission of the institution forward. Radiologists interpreted more than 700,000 studies during the last year, covering our Level I Trauma Center with a census of approximately 700 beds, our NCCN -accredited Comprehensive Cancer Center, Kentucky Children’s Hospital, and our outpatient imaging facilities. This recruitment will support our continued growth, including: opening of a Cancer and Advanced Ambulatory Building, a new multi-disciplinary ambulatory care site, an expansion of our main hospital, and a new tower for Kentucky Children’s Hospital. The Department is active in education. The Diagnostic Radiology residency program has 32 residents (8 per class). The Integrated Interventional Radiology residency has 10 residents (2 per class). The Department has both the Early Specialization in IR ( ESIR ) pathway and the Independent Interventional Radiology residency. The Department also boasts a Medical Physics Residency. Fellowships in Abdominal Imaging, Chest and Cardiovascular Imaging, Breast Imaging, Musculoskeletal Imaging, Neuroradiology, Emergency Radiology, and Oncologic Imaging are available. For those interested in Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, the accelerated pathway to dual ABNM and ABR certification is available. The Department also supports learners on the ABR alternate pathway. There are many opportunities to teach and interact with medical students as well. The Department of Radiology participates in more than 50 on-going clinical trials across a variety of areas including, but not limited to, molecular imaging, oncology, theranostics, fMRI and neuro-imaging, interventional radiology, and AI. Faculty from the Department of Radiology published more than 50 manuscripts during the last academic year and were invited speakers at over 100 national or international conferences. This position will provide an opportunity for advancement with generous benefit package including: · Professional Development Funding · Relocation Assistance · Malpractice Insurance · 200% 403b Retirement Match · Educational Benefits for Family Members · Rank and Compensation Commensurate with Experience. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World,” Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, and an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples, and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Please include an updated CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646801": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Marketing and Supply Chain",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Lecturer in Marketing and Supply Chain Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Lecturer in Marketing and Supply Chain Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Lecturer in Marketing and Supply Chain Requisition Number FE04997 Working Title Department Name 8F240:Dept of Marketing and Supply Chain Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education PhD or Master’s degree in marketing, business or a related field Required Related Experience Classroom (or similar training) experience is preferred Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Department of Marketing and Supply Chain in the Gatton College of Business and Economics at the University of Kentucky in Lexington, KY is pleased to invite applications for a Lecturer position beginning January 1, 2027. The selected candidate will be appointed to a full-time 9-month, non-tenure eligible faculty position for an initial two-year period that has the potential for renewal and for promotion to Senior Lecturer after five years. Candidates must hold a PhD or Master’s degree in marketing, business or a related field, and classroom (or similar training) experience is preferred. This position involves teaching 3-4 courses per semester and being involved in a departmental service activity. We are looking for an individual with the ability to design and teach courses in the Marketing Strategy, Sales, or Digital Marketing areas. Interest in other topics will also be considered. Applicants should submit a letter of interest and current curriculum vitae. In addition, please provide the names and contact information for three references when prompted in the academic profile. This information may be utilized to solicit recommendation letters from your references within the employment system. Applications will begin to be reviewed immediately, and the position will remain open until filled, with interviews beginning in mid-to-late October. Questions concerning the position may be directed to: Daniel Sheehan Kincaid Endowed Associate Professor of Marketing Department of Marketing and Supply Chain Chair University of Kentucky Gatton College of Business & Economics dan.sheehan@uky.edu Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. The Gatton College of Business and Economics recently celebrated its 100th anniversary. Over that time, we have been preparing principled leaders for the global economy, producing high quality, influential research, and supporting economic growth in Kentucky and beyond. Accredited by the AACSB , Gatton proudly offers a full range of undergraduate, graduate and professional business and economics degrees and certificates in both a face to face and online format. We are housed in a 220,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility where the college accommodates the fastest growing student enrollment on UK’s campus, reaching over 5,000 students. Through teaching, research, and outreach, the Gatton College has a direct, tangible influence on the lives of Kentucky’s citizens and people around the world. We are looking for professionals who embody the College’s tagline of “Blue Means Business”. Located in central Kentucky, Lexington (pop. 329,000) is widely known as the “horse capital of the world” and is roughly an hour’s drive from Louisville and Cincinnati. Lexington has a number of desirable amenities, a vibrant dining and nightlife, and plenty of outdoor activities and is regularly cited as one of the top places to live in the US. Please consider joining our team. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646797": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor in Physical Therapy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor in Physical Therapy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor in Physical Therapy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor in Physical Therapy Requisition Number FE04996 Working Title Department Name 7N640:Physical Therapy Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Terminal academic doctoral degree (i.e., PhD or similar terminal degree) in relevant field Required Related Experience 1. Research expertise in content areas relevant to physical therapy practice with focus on neuroscience, rehabilitation, musculoskeletal, or movement science research. 2. Record of research productivity with a strong potential for funding Required License/Registration/Certification Current physical therapy license or privilege to practice in Kentucky or eligibility for licensure with licensure completed within 90 days of start date. Job Summary The Department of Physical Therapy (PT), College of Health Sciences ( CHS ) at the University of Kentucky is currently accepting applications for two (2) full-time 11-month appointment, tenure-eligible faculty members at rank determined by qualifications, to begin employment at the Lexington campus by July 1, 2027. Primary duties of each position include advancing a research agenda in rehabilitation and/or movement science that synergizes with and enhances the research portfolio of the Department and College, teaching in the content areas related to their expertise, building and maintaining strong relationships with internal and external constituents, and mentoring students in the Doctor of Physical Therapy program. The distribution of effort for this position will be approximately 30-40% instruction, 50-60% research, and 10% service. Faculty may also assume an active role in the CHS Rehabilitation and Health Sciences PhD Program , a multi-disciplinary, multi-institutional Ph.D. program with faculty and students from disciplines such as Athletic Training & Clinical Nutrition, Occupational Therapy, Physician Assistant, Physical Therapy and Speech-Language Pathology. About the Physical Therapy Program The Physical Therapy program at UK has been educating physical therapists since 1967. Our program is conducted at the Lexington, Kentucky campus and at the Center of Excellence in Rural Health in Hazard, Kentucky. The qualified candidate will join an outstanding academic faculty devoted to teaching, research, clinical practice, and service. Our faculty is comprised of numerous physical therapists with post professional doctoral training who are involved in clinical, bench, and educational research, and clinical faculty involved in delivery of patient care services. Our research portfolio is diverse and places a high value on translational and interdisciplinary science. The qualified candidate will have access to several significant resources including the College’s state-of-the-art teaching and research facilities, widespread UK Healthcare facilities and other partners within the academic medical center, and those incorporated into our developing Health Education Building . The College of Health Sciences research centers and institutes include the Biomotion Laboratory , Center for Muscle Biology , and Sports Medicine Research Institute . The candidate may also have access to the UK Core Facilities and the UK’s Center for Clinical Translational Sciences ( CCTS ), and develop partnerships within the Kentucky Appalachian Rural Rehabilitation Network , the Spinal Cord and Brain Injury Research Center , the Sanders-Brown Center on Aging , Barnstable Brown Diabetes & Obesity Research Center , Veteran’s Affairs Medical Center, Kentucky Neuroscience Institute , and our UK Human Development Institute . The University of Kentucky and the College of Health Sciences are committed to ensuring that all students, faculty, and staff operate in an environment of openness and acceptance. We strive to bring together many people into one community, ensuring everyone feels valued and welcome. The mission of the Physical Therapy Program at the University of Kentucky is foremost to meet the physical therapy needs of Kentucky and contribute to global needs through education, research and service. It aspires for excellence, aiming to the highest standards of education, clinical practice, research, professional duty, and social responsibility. For more information, please visit http://www.uky.edu/healthsciences/academic-programs/physical-therapy . Candidates should submit a complete UK application, a curriculum vita, and a letter of interest outlining how your research agenda will enhance or synergize with those of the College of Health Sciences and leverage partnerships within the University or UK Healthcare . Questions should be directed to the search committee co-chairs, Nathan Johnson and Patrick Kitzman College of Health Sciences, Department of Physical Therapy, Wethington Building, 900 S. Limestone Street, Lexington, KY 40536-0200, or email at Nathan.johnson@uky.edu and Patrick.Kitzman@uky.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Upon offer of employment, successful applicants must undergo a national background check and pre-employment drug screen as required by University of Kentucky Human Resources. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 1. History of extramural funding 2. Teaching experience with potential for course management and design Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? UK Jobs Website Employee Referral HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Indeed APTAEducation.org Chronicle of Higher Education APTA - Red Hot Jobs APTA - Orthopedics A Colleague, Friend and/or Family member None of the above Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646790": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Exercise Science",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Lecturer in Exercise Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Lecturer in Exercise Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Lecturer in Exercise Science Requisition Number FE05003 Working Title Department Name 8G040:Kinesiology - Health Promotion Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. or equivalent in field of Exercise Science or related field Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Department of Kinesiology and Health Promotion within the College of Education at the University of Kentucky is seeking candidates for a non-tenure-eligible Lecturer position, effective August 16, 2027 . Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application reviews will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The flagship university of the Commonwealth of Kentucky, the University of Kentucky is home to more than 35,000 students and nearly 2,500 faculty members. Located in Lexington, the Horse Capital of the World, UK is a major employer in a city of approximately 330,000. The Department of Kinesiology and Health Promotion ( KHP ), housed in the College of Education, is comprised of 30 full-time faculty members, and offers undergraduate, masters, and doctoral programs in the academic areas of exercise science, physical education, health promotion, and sport leadership. KHP serves as the academic focus for more than 1,000 undergraduate and graduate students. Job Responsibilities Pursue excellence in teaching and service. Successful candidates will be expected to: Teach a four-four course load (i.e., 12 credits per semester) each academic year, consisting of primarily undergraduate courses serving most of our KHP majors and minors; Provide support across departmental undergraduate programs; Provide service to the department, college, and University of Kentucky. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. Applications Interested applicants should submit a UK Online Application at www.uky.edu/ukjobs . Applicants should include: a detailed cover letter (upload under Cover Letter); a curriculum vita (upload under Curriculum Vita); student evaluations of the candidate’s teaching (upload under Specific Request 1); and a teaching philosophy/statement including reflections on experiences with teaching and mentoring diverse student populations (upload under Specific Request 2); detailed contact information for three or more professional references that can speak to the applicant’s qualifications (upload under References). References will be contacted for finalists only. Academic transcripts – required for finalists. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Mark Abel, at mark.abel@uky.edu . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The successful candidate will possess an earned doctorate (Ph.D., Ed.D., or equivalent) in Exercise Science, or a related field, but the start date in August 2027. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Successful teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646789": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Elementary STEM Education--Science, Regular Title Series",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor of Elementary STEM Education--Science, Regular Title Series Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor of Elementary STEM Education--Science, Regular Title Series Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor of Elementary STEM Education--Science, Regular Title Series Requisition Number FE04999 Working Title Department Name 8G020:Education Curriculum & Instr Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in Curriculum & Instruction – Science, Science Education, STEM Education, Engineering Education, OR a similar, equivalent degree and area of concentration. Required Related Experience Preference given to candidates with experience teaching elementary science methods and working with preservice and/or practicing teachers, as well as evidence of scholarly productivity, including refereed publications and/or presentations, that demonstrates potential for future success in developing and carrying out a productive research program in STEM /Science Education. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Department of Teaching and Learning in the College of Education at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-eligible, Regular Title Series Assistant Professor of Elementary STEM Education with an emphasis in Science Education. This is a 9-month appointment, effective August 16, 2027. We seek a colleague with a promising research agenda focused on elementary science teaching and learning, elementary science teacher education, and/or related areas of STEM education. The successful candidate will contribute to elementary teacher preparation, and to undergraduate and graduate programs in science and STEM education, while developing an active program of research, scholarship, and external funding. Responsibilities will be divided among research, teaching, and service, with faculty in this position typically expected to teach a 2-2 course load. The ideal candidate will have a demonstrated ability to integrate their teaching and service with research that aligns with the department, college, and university’s mission. Responsibilities include the following: Teach two courses each semester (fall and spring) such as: SEM 328 – Teaching Science in the Elementary School SEM 448 – Applications of Teaching Middle Level Science SEM 604 – History of STEM Education SEM 613 – Effective Use of Technology for Modeling-based Inquiry in STEM Ed. SEM 708 – Engineering in STEM Education Collaborate with school partners; Conduct a line of research relevant to the department and university’s mission (e.g., peer reviewed publications, grant proposals, presentations); Seek extramural funding; Serve on masters and doctoral committees; and Provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. The Distribution of Effort ( DOE ) for this position is approximately: 50% Instruction (12 credit hours each academic year) 30% Research 20% Service Interested applicants should submit an application at www.uky.edu/ukjobs and include the following materials: Detailed Cover Letter – Note academic credentials and professional experience related to the responsibilities for this position. Curriculum Vita – Please include contact information for 3 professional references. Research & Teaching Statement – (Upload a single document under “Specific Request 1”.) Teaching Evaluations and/or other evidence of excellence in teaching (upload under “Specific Request 2”). Writing Sample – Provide one writing sample or scholarly publication representative of your research (upload under “Writing Sample”). Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026. Questions regarding the position or application materials may be directed to search committee co-chairs Dr. Cindy Jong ( cindy.Jong@uky.edu ) and Dr. Sahar Alameh ( sahar@uky.edu ). For institutional information, visit the following websites: University of Kentucky – http://www.uky.edu College of Education – http://education.uky.edu Department of Teaching and Learning – https://education.uky.edu/academics/departments/dtl Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Preference given to candidates with: Experience with interdisciplinary STEM education, and Experience in building school partnerships, supervising teacher candidates, and collaborating with schools, universities, and colleagues across institutions. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Active research record and extramural funding Experience teaching science at the K-8 level Experience as an instructor of record in undergraduate and graduate courses. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Writing Sample Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646787": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Special Education - Learning &amp; Behavior Disorders, Regular Title Series",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor in Special Education - Learning &amp; Behavior Disorders, Regular Title Series Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor in Special Education - Learning & Behavior Disorders, Regular Title Series Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor in Special Education - Learning & Behavior Disorders, Regular Title Series Requisition Number FE04995 Working Title Department Name 8G070:Early Childhood, Spec Ed & Counselor Ed Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Doctorate in Special Education, earned (or expected) prior to start date. Required Related Experience A minimum of three years of direct experience as a special education teacher serving school-aged students with Learning and Behavior Disorders ( LBD ) in K-12 educational settings in the United States Demonstrated commitment to innovative, inclusive educational practices for students with disabilities Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with K-12 partners in education Demonstrated use of effective, evidence-based practices in school settings Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Department of Early Childhood, Special Education, and Counselor Education ( EDSCE ) invites applications for an Assistant Professor position in Special Education – Learning and Behavior Disorders ( LBD ). This faculty member will provide expertise in support of the LBD program across elementary and secondary school levels. The position is Regular Title Series, Tenure Eligible. This is a 9-month appointment, effective August 16, 2027. Responsibilities include the following: Maintain a productive research agenda, including applying for external funding; Teach two courses each semester (fall and spring), particularly coursework and fieldwork supervision within our undergraduate program; Advise current and incoming students; Engage with K-12 and university faculty in program planning, implementation, and evaluation; Serve on masters and doctoral committees; and Provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. The Distribution of Effort ( DOE ) for this position is approximately: — 50% Instruction (12 credit hours each academic year), — 30% Research, and — 20% Service (service to the college, department, institution, and the profession). Interested applicants should submit an application at www.uky.edu/ukjobs and include the following materials: Detailed cover letter noting academic credentials and professional experience related to the responsibilities for this position, including the required and preferred experiences and expertise (upload under Cover Letter); Curriculum vita – (upload under Curriculum Vita); Combined statement on research, teaching, and service (upload under Specific Request 1); 2-3 professional writing samples (upload under Writing Sample); Names and contact information for three professional references (upload under References). References will be contacted for finalists. Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026. Questions regarding the position or application materials may be directed to search committee chair Dr. Mark Samudre ( mark.samudre@uky.edu ). Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The ideal candidate will possess in-depth knowledge of evidence-based practices for teaching K-12 students with Learning Disabilities. They should have strong instructional and assessment skills, the ability to teach and supervise teacher candidates, along with excellent collaboration and communication abilities to foster an inclusive learning environment. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preference will be given to applicants who have direct experience providing academic instruction and special education services to students with Learning Disabilities in K-12 educational environments, and whose research focuses on academic interventions, or related areas of effective instruction. Additional preference will be given to applicants with experience supervising practicum and student teaching in K-12 schools for university teacher candidates. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Specific Request 1 Writing Sample Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/646323": {
      "title": "Radiology Tech Assistant/On-Call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Radiology Tech Assistant/On-Call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Radiology Tech Assistant/On-Call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Radiology Tech Assistant/On-Call/UKHC Requisition Number DU15053 Department Name H6250:Imaging Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00-22.60/hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education HS Required Related Experience 1 year Required License/Registration/Certification Basic Life Support ( BLS ) Certified within 90 days of hire Physical Requirements Heavy lifting, pushing, and pulling of objects over 50 lbs. Shift Varies Job Summary This position provides clinical support and patient care functions alongside the Radiology staff at UKHC Good Samaritan Hospital. This employee will assist with facilitating patient throughput in the department by performing functions such as preparing patients for their exam, room turnover, answering phones, cleaning, transporting patients, stocking supplies, interacting with the RIS system, and assisting with patient transfers. This position will also be responsible for rounding throughout the department to ensure cleanliness and appropriate patient communication. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 12/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * University of Kentucky HealthCare seeks to attract, develop and retain highly skilled and competent employees, to provide the best experience for every patient, every time.  If selected for a position, do you agree to abide by the UK HealthCare Values of diversity, innovation, respect, compassion, and teamwork? Yes No University of Kentucky HealthCare recognizes a set of values that guide us in our daily interactions. By applying for a position within UK Healthcare, you are indicating your commitment and expressing your agreement to our five values. These values are diversity, innovation, respect, compassion, and teamwork. Please choose one of the UK Healthcare values and give a specific example when you exhibited this quality in your professional experience. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a current Kentucky BLS (Basic Life Support) certification or are you eligible to obtain by date of hire? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
