    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645986": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Requisition Number FE04647 Working Title Program Director for Doctorate in Audiology Program Department Name 7N620:Communication Sciences and Disorders Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education A minimum of a Doctoral Degree in Audiology (PhD, AuD, EdD) or related area Required Related Experience At least two years of related experience. Qualified applicants in all areas of Audiology expertise will be considered, but preference will be given to those with experience in program administration. Required License/Registration/Certification ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence in Audiology Kentucky audiology licensure or eligibility Job Summary The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders ( CSD ) in the University of Kentucky’s College of Health Sciences is currently accepting applications for a full-time (12-month), Faculty Member to serve as the Doctor of Audiology degree Program Director. We invite you to become part of a dynamic department to meet instructional and administrative needs within the newly approved three year program organized in collaboration with the Department of Otolaryngology- Head and Neck Surgery in the College of Medicine . Rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. This is a tenure eligible position. The primary responsibilities of the Program Director will be to provide visionary and strategic leadership for our Doctor of Audiology (AuD) program, ensuring academic excellence, innovation in clinical education, and continued accreditation compliance. This individual will be responsible for overseeing curriculum development, faculty coordination, student advising, and clinical partnerships in collaboration with Director of Clinical Education. The Program Director will also mentor faculty, engage in scholarly activities and recruit students while fostering a collaborative environment. This is an on-site, in-person position. The specific instructional assignments will be based on program needs as well as areas of expertise and negotiated with the Chair of the Department of Communicative Sciences and Disorders annually. Qualified applicants must possess a minimum of a Doctoral Degree in Audiology (PhD, AuD or related area, EdD) ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence in Audiology, Kentucky audiology licensure or eligibility. Qualified applicants in all areas of Audiology expertise will be considered, but preference will be given to those with experience in program administration. Candidates should apply online with a curriculum vita, letter of interest, and other specific requests listed on the UK HR employment website. Questions about the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Anne Olson, PhD, CCC /A., by email to: aolso2@uky.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Preferred start date for this position is July 1, 2027. The University of Kentucky and College of Health Sciences are dedicated to creating an environment where students, faculty and staff collaborate openly and treat one another with respect. We bring together many people into one community as we work toward our shared goal of advancing Kentucky through education, research, service and care. About the Audiology Program in Communication Sciences and Disorders The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders ( CSD ) administers a doctoral program in audiology, a master’s level graduate program in Speech-Language Pathology and a pre-professional undergraduate program. The qualified candidate will join an outstanding academic faculty devoted to teaching, research, clinical practice, and service. Our faculty is comprised of three audiologists, nine speech-language pathologists, and one speech physiologist. Program development plans include the addition of two more faculty in audiology. The UK CSD program has had a strong faculty history with two ASHA Honors recipients, eight ASHA Fellows, four state DiCarlo recipients, one national DiCarlo winner, one past president of ASHA , one past president of AAA , and recipients of multiple teaching awards. In addition to program faculty within CSD , physicians and audiologists in the Department of Otolaryngology provide didactic and practical instruction as part of the Doctorate in Audiology (AuD) degree program. The UK HealthCare’s Otolaryngology Department provides hearing care services with a faculty of 20 otolaryngologists (four neurotologists), six advanced practice providers and 17 doctoral level audiologists. The Audiology program will be expanding from its current location to a new state of the art Rankin Heath Education Building (currently under construction) which will be the largest academic building in the history of UK. Our research portfolio places a high value on translational, interdisciplinary, and collaborative science. The College of Health Sciences is home to a variety of research laboratories and maintains strong collaborative ties with colleagues across campus. The successful candidate will have access to several significant clinical, instructional and research resources including the College’s state-of-the-art teaching facilities, the UK Center for the Enhancement of Learning and Teaching, the CSD Academic Clinic , the Human Development Institute, the MRISC Neuroimaging Center, the Center for Clinical Translational Sciences, the Sanders-Brown Center on Aging, a contiguous Veteran’s Affairs Hospital, the Kentucky Neuroscience Institute, the Sports Medicine Research Institute , the Molecular Genetics of Hearing and Hearing Loss Lab , and the Center for Telehealth Education, Research, and Outreach . About the University of Kentucky Founded in 1865 as a land-grant institution, UK is nestled in the scenic heart of the Bluegrass region of Kentucky. Recently ranked as one of the safest, most creative, and brainiest cities in the nation, Lexington is an ideal location to experience the work-life balance that the University strives to provide to its employees. Visit the University’s website and see for yourself what makes UK the perfect place to work. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645829": {
      "title": "Physician - Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine Requisition Number FE04990 Working Title Cardiologist Department Name 7H354:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - CARDIOLO Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, MD/PhD, DO, or equivalent degree. Required Related Experience The ideal candidate for the Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine will possess the following background, experience, and skills: Strong, visionary, inspirational leader who can artfully convey a long-term vision for the division yet is equally skilled at implementing a detailed plan to achieve that vision. Highly approachable and compassionate; a record of promoting a culture of innovation, collaboration, teamwork, respect, and honesty; a professional and personal demeanor characterized by integrity, graciousness, humility, genuineness, empathy, and sincerity; and a passion for the organization’s mission and objectives. Exceptionally team-oriented; skilled at working well and partnering with providers across the care continuum to identify, build, and negotiate “win-win” relationships; politically astute yet apolitical with an ability to break down silos and ensure a collegial and productive work environment. Highly adept and at ease managing the day-to-day operational details with the ability to make strong and decisive decisions when needed while at the same time creating unity within the division. Required License/Registration/Certification Board certification in Cardiovascular Medicine. Board certification in Internal Medicine. Eligible for Medical licensure in the State of Kentucky. Job Summary The Opportunity The University of Kentucky College of Medicine, Department of Internal Medicine seeks their next Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine. Exceptional accomplishments as an academic leader and investigator will prepare the candidate for success in guiding the division’s busy clinical practice and supporting growing academic careers. The division chief reports directly to the Department Chair of Internal Medicine and collaborates closely with other leaders across UK HealthCare and the College of Medicine. The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine is committed to achieving the highest standards in the diagnosis and treatment of heart and vascular disease. Through dedication to scholarly pursuits, they aim to improve the future of heart health across Kentucky and beyond. To this end, they provide clinical services based on the latest evidence and technology, by advancing knowledge through research and by educating those in training, in practice, and their patients. UK seeks a division chief who is a leader committed to the tri-partite academic mission, excels at building and guiding teams, collaborates effectively with hospital partners, and the ability to mentor early career faculty and trainees. Experience as a division or section chief, medical director, program director, or in leadership within national professional societies or major journals is especially valuable. Highly competitive candidates will bring a history of achievement as an academic cardiologist including clinical expertise, meaningful research contributions supported by a successful track record of promoting scholarship, securing extramural funding, progressive leadership experience, and recognition at the national and/or international level. The predominant criteria for the appointment as division chief include a respected academic physician with a high-level of emotional intelligence and demonstrated ability to deliver exceptional patient care while training the future leaders in cardiovascular medicine. The successful candidate should demonstrate strong leadership skills as a listener, decision-maker and effective advocate for the division and the department. The candidate will encourage and participate in collaborative initiatives; communicate effectively, demonstrate integrity and foster the trust of colleagues across the University. The division is poised to achieve regional and national recognition in clinical care delivery, medical education and research. It serves an integral role in a vibrant and robust academic environment within UK HealthCare, which brings state-of-the-art facilities and technology to the Lexington, Kentucky campus and broader region as UK HealthCare and College of Medicine moves toward its goal of becoming a top 25 academic medical center. UK is constructing a new hospital tower, to bring total beds on the main campus to 1,500 by 2029. Position Summary The Division Chief of Cardiovascular Medicine will play a central role in advancing the organization’s highest-priority strategies and in driving excellence across all quality measures. Serving as the leader across the clinical, educational, and research missions, the Division Chief will champion the continued growth of medical training, scientific discovery, and clinical integration in collaboration with the cardiovascular service line director. The Division Chief serves at the discretion of the Department Chair and works in close partnership with leaders throughout UK HealthCare, the Gill Heart and Vascular Institute, and the College of Medicine. Key Responsibilities Oversee and develop an exceptional cardiovascular program, with a commitment to teaching and research. Lead strategic planning, budgeting, and resource allocation for the division. Oversee faculty recruitment, retention, career development, and promotion/tenure processes. Manage clinical scheduling, workforce planning, and operational performance. Provide leadership for the division’s teaching programs and fellowship training. Collaborate closely with the cardiovascular service line leader to advance cardiovascular services. Promote academic excellence within the division, with emphasis on faculty development, scholarly productivity, and mentorship. Strengthen the division’s academic profile through programmatic growth, interdisciplinary collaboration, and faculty support. Advance the division’s research mission, including clinical, translational, and basic science initiatives. Develop and expand translational research programs that connect the Saha Cardiovascular Research Center with divisional activities. Maintain an active personal research program. Support faculty in securing extramural funding and building research careers. Serve on division, department, college, hospital, and university committees as appropriate. Represent the division in institutional planning, interdisciplinary initiatives, and strategic collaborations. Provide high‑quality clinical care, which may include outpatient clinics, inpatient attending service, and on‑call responsibilities. Model excellence in patient care and support continuous improvement in quality, safety, and access. Teach medical students, residents, and fellows in both inpatient and outpatient settings. Participate in didactic teaching, seminars, and curriculum development. Support the fellowship program and ensure high‑quality training experiences. Department of Internal Medicine The Department of Internal Medicine is the largest in the College of Medicine and at the University of Kentucky with approximately 367 faculty, 171 staff, 222 residents and fellows, and 212 advanced practice providers. The department has 14 clinical divisions and 2 non-clinical divisions within its scope. The department of internal medicine is led by Dr. Darwin Conwell, MD and departmental leaders including Vice Chairs, Associate Vice Chairs, and the Office of the Chair Administration team. Internal Medicine faculty secure over $35 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in all internal medicine subspecialties. The department has published 287 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains more than 50 active clinical trials and 240 active grants and contracts. The Department of Internal Medicine has 211 faculty who are actively involved in research activities and supervise biomedical learners, including PhD and master’s students, to gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs. Interested Applicants To be considered for the position, interested applicants should submit application materials (CV, Letter of Interest) addressed to the Search Advisory Committee to Amber Gornik, Managing Associate at Korn Ferry, at amber.gornik@kornferry.com . Additionally, interested applicants must apply through the University of Kentucky Division Chief posting and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter when prompted in the application process: https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644747 For inquiries or questions, please direct them to Jenny Seaver, Principal at Korn Ferry jenny.seaver@kornferry.com and Cassandra Rogers, Internal Medicine Faculty Affairs Administrator cassandra.rogers@uky.edu to the attention of Darwin Conwell, MD, Department Chair. All applications and inquiries will be handled in a secure, sensitive, and confidential manner. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong clinical skills and ability to continue to practice their field of expertise while serving as Chief; should have skills in collaboration and the ability to learn and share. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Strong record of clinical excellence, academic achievement, and leadership experience. Demonstrated success in research, education, and program development. Meet university criteria for appointment of Associate or Full Professor. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645726": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Plant Pathology",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor of Plant Pathology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor of Plant Pathology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor of Plant Pathology Requisition Number FE04989 Working Title Extension Plant Pathologist, Specialty Crops: Assistant Extension Professor of Plant Pathology Department Name 81120:PLANT PATHOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education PhD in Plant Pathology or related discipline Required Related Experience Demonstrated experience in applied plant pathology research and plant pathology extension and outreach Required License/Registration/Certification None Job Summary Assistant Extension Professor of Plant Pathology, Specialty Crops Disease Management, twelve-month, tenure-eligible appointment, extension/service (75%), research (25%). The Department of Plant Pathology at the University of Kentucky invites applicants for a tenure-eligible extension/research faculty position focused on field-grown fruit, vegetable, and tobacco pathology. The position is located on the main campus of the University of Kentucky in Lexington, KY. The successful candidate will develop a nationally recognized Extension program and conduct translational research on pathogens of these crops. We seek candidates that will use innovative and interdisciplinary approaches to conduct impactful applied research relevant to stakeholder needs. As part of a team of Extension personnel within the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment and statewide, this individual will develop and implement educational/outreach programs that complement and enhance existing extension and research programs, supporting statewide county-based extension professionals and other stakeholder groups pertaining to specialty crop disease management. The successful candidate will actively seek external and competitive funding opportunities and conduct problem-solving research to provide research-based disease management recommendations to stakeholders, cooperating in multi-disciplinary teams with relevant collaborators. The faculty member will be responsive to the educational and applied research needs of Kentucky farmers, commodity groups, Extension agents, and industry. The incumbent will participate in mentoring graduate students in the Integrated Plant and Soils Sciences graduate program, will be expected to contribute to institutional service and the missions of the Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment. The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment ( MGCAFE ) is fulfilling the land-grant promise of educational excellence, civic leadership, transformational research, and shared knowledge serving the common good. We serve the people of the Commonwealth and across the world through education, outreach, service, and research by finding solutions to improve lives today and create a sustainable future. We integrate teaching, research, and extension in our work. We recruit, retain, and graduate students who are competent, responsible, and workforce ready. For more than 130 years, MGCAFE has provided research results to the community. From traditional labs and research farms to high-tech diagnostic and research centers, we offer science-based, practical solutions that affect the everyday lives of Kentuckians and people around the world. Our Cooperative Extension programs are engaged in Kentucky’s 120 counties, identifying and addressing needs not only in agriculture and natural resources, but also 4-H and youth development, family and consumer sciences, as well as community & economic development. The University of Kentucky is an institution with over 30,000 undergraduate and 10,000 graduate students. UK is Kentucky’s flagship university and a land grant institution. We have a university commitment to improve the lives of Kentuckians and beyond and that is why environmental stewardship and sustainability are core parts of our institution’s legacy. We are recognized as a Tree Campus USA by the Arbor Day Foundation, a Gold level Bicycle Friendly University by The League of American Bicyclists , and are recognized as a STARS (Sustainability Tracking, Assessment & Rating System) Silver Rating by the Association for the Advancement of Sustainability in Higher Education. The university is geographically near downtown Lexington, which offers the vibrancy of an urban location while being in close proximity to working landscapes and recognized wilderness areas. It is a thriving community of 320,000+ with a strong commitment to quality of life, education, and the arts. Lexington is in the Bluegrass Region, an internationally acclaimed cultural landscape and agricultural region. QUESTIONS AND /OR NOMINATIONS : Dr. Kiersten Wise Professor and Search Committee Chair 348 University Dr, PO Box 469 Princeton, KY 42445 Email: Kiersten.wise@uky.edu Phone: 859-562-1338 OR: Dr. Gary Munkvold Professor and Department Chair 1405 Veterans Drive University of Kentucky Lexington, KY 40546 Email: Gary.Munkvold@uky.edu APPLICATION : Applications should be submitted by October 9, 2026, for full consideration while the position will remain open until filled. The anticipated interview period is early November to mid-December. The anticipated start date is March 2027. Please upload the following documents: (1) A cover letter that outlines your experience and qualifications (2) A statement that describes your vision for developing and implementing an innovative, impactful Extension and applied research program that addresses existing and emerging issues affecting fruit, vegetable, and tobacco crops in Kentucky ( Writing Sample ) (3) The names, addresses, emails, and phone numbers for three references ( Specific Request 1 ) (4) Curriculum Vita Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The successful applicant must have a PhD in Plant Pathology or a related discipline with demonstrated experience in applied research in disease management; excellent oral and written communication skills; use of common computer technologies and social media; and experience with extension and outreach. Post-doctoral training, experience as a member of a multidisciplinary team, and expertise in specialty crops are desirable, but not essential. Applicants should have experience in scientific communication and the complementarity of research and Extension programming. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Writing Sample Specific Request 1 Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Resume Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645708": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Translational Neurorehabilitation Research",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Postdoctoral Scholar in Translational Neurorehabilitation Research Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Postdoctoral Scholar in Translational Neurorehabilitation Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Postdoctoral Scholar in Translational Neurorehabilitation Research Requisition Number DU14996 Department Name 7H951:PHYSICAL MEDICINE & REHAB - RESEARCH DIV Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $54,000/year Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education PhD in Neuroscience or related discipline. Required Related Experience No experience required Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds, or sitting for long periods of time. Shift Monday – Friday 8:30 am – 5:00 pm Job Summary Physical Medicine Post-Doctoral Fellow position is utilized to support Dr. Sachdeva’s clinical research on effects of transcutaneous spinal cord stimulation on motor, autonomic and metabolic function in individuals with various neurological conditions. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Excellent written and verbal communication skills; strong organizational and time management abilities; ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Experience with human participant research, data collection and analysis, statistical software, and scientific manuscript preparation. Familiarity with neurological rehabilitation, spinal cord injury research, and neuromodulation techniques is desirable. Willingness to interact with research participants and coordinate study activities across clinical and laboratory settings. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience PhD in Neuroscience or related discipline with minimum two first author publications in peer-reviewed journals. Preferred but not required: experience working with individuals with disability; Physical Therapy degree; Phlebotomy Certification; experience with Matlab, Python or R. Deadline to Apply Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
