    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645600": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Finance",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Finance Requisition Number FE04991 Working Title Department Name 8F200:Dept of Finance & Quantitative Methods Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in finance or a related field by the start date; ABD candidates who expect to complete their degree before the start date may also be considered. Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The John Maze Stewart Department of Finance and Quantitative Methods at the University of Kentucky in Lexington, KY is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-eligible, Regular Title Series, position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level. This is a 9-month position with a preferred start date of August 1, 2027. The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. in finance or a related field by the start date; ABD candidates who expect to complete their degree before the start date may also be considered. The research agenda is open, and the anticipated teaching load is three courses per year. The anticipated initial distribution of effort ( DOE ) will be 30% teaching, 60% research, and 10% service. The successful candidate will be expected to mentor and advise students and to provide service to the department, college, university, and profession. The Finance Department has a highly productive group of research-oriented faculty who publish in top finance journals. The department has strong research support, a vibrant Ph.D. program, and hosts a top-quality boutique finance conference ( https://gatton.uky.edu/financeconference ). The Gatton College building also houses the Kentucky Research Data Center, part of the U.S. Census Bureau’s Federal Statistical Research Data Center network, providing approved researchers with secure access to restricted federal microdata. We encourage you to learn more about the department by visiting the department website: https://gatton.uky.edu/faculty-research/departments/john-maze-stewart-finance-quantitative-methods For full consideration, applications should be submitted by November 15, 2026, though the position will remain open until filled. We expect first-round Zoom interviews to occur in December 2026 and campus visits to occur in early 2027. Applications must include the following: 1) Letter of application (upload as Cover Letter), 2) Curriculum Vitae, 3) job-market paper or primary working paper (upload as Specific Request 1), and 4) second working paper (optional – upload as Specific Request 2). In addition, please provide the names and contact information for at least three, no more than four, references when prompted in the academic profile. This information will be used to solicit recommendation letters from all applicants’ references through the employment system. For additional information about this search, please contact Taylor Begley (begley@uky.edu), Chair of the Finance Faculty Search Committee, John Maze Stewart Department of Finance and Quantitative Methods. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. The Gatton College recently celebrated its 100th anniversary. Over that time, we have been preparing principled leaders for the global economy, producing high-quality, influential research, and supporting economic growth in Kentucky and beyond. Accredited by the AACSB , Gatton proudly offers a full range of undergraduate, graduate, and professional business and economics degrees and certificates in both face-to-face and online formats. We are housed in a 220,000-square-foot state-of-the-art facility, and are the fastest growing college on UK’s campus, with more than 5,000 students. Through teaching, research, and outreach, the Gatton College has a direct, tangible influence on the lives of Kentucky’s citizens and people around the world. We are looking for faculty who embody the College’s tagline of “Blue Means Business.” Located in central Kentucky, Lexington (pop. 329,000) is widely known as the “horse capital of the world” and is roughly an hour’s drive from Louisville and Cincinnati. Lexington has a number of desirable amenities, a vibrant dining and nightlife, and plenty of outdoor activities and is regularly cited as one of the top places to live in the US. Please consider joining our team. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Specific Request 2 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
