    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645583": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist/On-call/UKHC",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Occupational Therapist/On-call/UKHC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Occupational Therapist/On-call/UKHC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Occupational Therapist/On-call/UKHC Requisition Number DU15034 Department Name H3411:Therapeutic Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $45.00 per hour Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education Bachelor’s degree or higher in Occupational Therapy Required Related Experience Hospital/acute care, trauma, neuro and ortho experience preferred. Required License/Registration/Certification Current Kentucky State Occupational Therapy License Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing or pulling objects greater than 50 pounds, standing and walking for long periods of time Shift Day-Shift: Primarily weekends, some hours may be available M-F, some holidays Job Summary This position will perform Occupational therapy evaluations and render occupational therapy treatments following a physician’s order. Will treat patients with a variety of diagnoses. Will perform appropriate documentation in the medical record. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Excellent communication and computer skills, necessary. Must be able to work in a fast paced environment Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 10/30/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Can you work flexible hours or days to accommodate patient needs and work flow? Yes No * Do you work well in a high stress, fast paced, and multi-tasking working environment? Yes No * Are you currently registered or eligible to be registered as an occupational therapist in the state of Kentucky? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
