    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/645150": {
      "title": "College Philanthropy Officer Senior",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | College Philanthropy Officer Senior Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support College Philanthropy Officer Senior Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title College Philanthropy Officer Senior Requisition Number RE55189 Working Title College Philanthropy Officer Senior - Major Gifts Department Name 8F004:B&E Development & Advance Work Location Lexington, KY Grade Level 48 Salary Range $64,210-105,914/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 7 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Lifting, pushing and/or pulling of objects up to 10 lbs.; Sitting and/or standing for extended periods of time; Performing repetitive motion tasks; Effectively communicating with individuals from varying backgrounds and professional levels; Extensive travel. Shift Typically Monday – Friday; 8:00am – 5:00pm; nights and weekends as needed for work and travel. Job Summary The Gatton College of Business and Economics is recruiting two College Philanthropy Officer Senior positions for fundraising of major gifts. Each position is responsible for managing an active portfolio of 75–100 donors and prospects and raise $1.5 million to $3 million annually. Reporting to the College Philanthropy Director Senior, the successful candidate will conduct 100–125 face-to-face visits, deliver 20–30 proposals, and close 15–20 major gifts ($25,000+ capacity) per year while generating at least five planned giving leads. This results-driven role requires a professional with a proven fundraising track record and exceptional communication skills. The Gatton College of Business and Economics offers a unique opportunity for fundraising professionals to create transformational impact while building relationships with an extraordinary network of alumni, donors, and corporate leaders. Fundraisers work with passionate and highly successful Gatton graduates, including executives, entrepreneurs, and industry innovators who are committed to investing in the next generation of business leaders. The role also provides meaningful engagement with prominent Kentucky and nationally recognized companies that partner with Gatton to advance student success, workforce development, experiential learning, and research. Every philanthropic investment directly impacts students by expanding access to scholarships, supporting hands-on learning opportunities, enhancing global experiences, and attracting world-class faculty. The Gatton College of Business and Economics just celebrated its 100th anniversary. Over that time, we have been preparing principled leaders for the global economy, producing high quality, influential research, and supporting economic growth in Kentucky and beyond. Accredited by the AACSB , Gatton proudly offers a full range of undergraduate, graduate and professional business and economics degrees and certificates in both a face to face an online format. We are housed in a 220,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility where the college accommodates the fastest growing student enrollment on UK’s campus, reaching over 4,000 students in Fall 2022. Through teaching, research, and outreach, the Gatton College has a direct, tangible influence on the lives of Kentucky’s citizens and people around the world. We are looking for professionals who embody the College’s tagline of “Blue Means Business”. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Philanthropic fundraising and/or graduate degree preferred. 5+ years of direct fundraising experience, preferably in higher education. Deadline to Apply 10/20/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of fundraising/sales or related experience do you have? None More than 0 years, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 4 years More than 4 years, up through 6 years More than 6 years * Please describe the two largest major gifts you identified, cultivated and successfully secured. Include the amounts and the steps taken to successfully secure them. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of paid work experience do you have developing and managing a portfolio of major gift prospects? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
