    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644632": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Health Sciences Education and Engagement",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Associate Director for Health Sciences Education and Engagement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Associate Director for Health Sciences Education and Engagement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Associate Director for Health Sciences Education and Engagement Requisition Number FE04984 Working Title Department Name 88000:LIBRARY ADMINISTRATION Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA accredited program accredited program Required Related Experience ● Relevant professional experience in an academic or health sciences library ● Demonstrated experience with instruction, teaching, or educational programming ● Supervisory or leadership experience Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Medical Center Library invites applications for the position of Associate Director for Health Sciences Education and Engagement, a leadership role responsible for advancing library instruction, outreach, and engagement across the six allied health colleges served by the Medical Center Library: Dentistry, Health Sciences, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, and Public Health. Reporting to the Director of the Medical Center Library, the Associate Director provides strategic leadership for educational programming, liaison services, and engagement initiatives that support teaching, learning, and research on the medical campus. The Associate Director will serve in a team-based liaison model and supervise faculty librarians. Responsibilities ● Provide strategic leadership for library education, instruction, and engagement programs supporting all six health colleges ● Perform liaison duties within a team model, including instruction, literature searching, evidence synthesis support, research support, and building faculty partnership, while collaborating with library colleagues to ensure consistency and shared expertise across disciplines ● Supervise a team of faculty librarians and foster a collaborative, cross-library approach to service development and delivery ● Coordinate instruction, workshops, and orientation programs across the medical campus, aligning with broader UK Libraries initiatives and partnerships ● Lead the planning, development, and delivery of the UK Libraries Research Workshop Series ● Integrate outreach and engagement into educational programs to increase awareness and impact of library services ● Support the development of online learning objects, tutorials, and instructional materials ● Promote learner centered teaching practices that address a range of different learning needs ● Assess educational and engagement activities to inform continuous improvement contribute to Libraries-wide assessment efforts ● Serve as a member of the Medical Center Library Leadership Team Required Qualifications ● Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA accredited program accredited program ● Relevant professional experience in an academic or health sciences library ● Demonstrated experience with instruction, teaching, or educational programming ● Supervisory or leadership experience ● Strong interpersonal, communication, and project management skills Preferred Qualifications ● Experience coordinating instruction programs or supervising librarians with instruction responsibilities ● Familiarity with instructional design, educational technologies, or online learning environments ● Experience with instructional effectiveness and/or program impact ● Experience working in collaborative, team-based service models This position participates in planning, shared governance, and UK Libraries-wide faculty activities. This is a full-time, 12-month, tenure eligible position in the Librarian Title Series (open rank) which requires scholarship, professional development, and service that contributes to the effectiveness of UK Libraries, the university, and the profession as outlined in Administrative Regulation 2:7 ( https://regs.uky.edu/administrative-regulation/ar-27 ). Your Distribution of Effort ( DOE ) range: Primary assignment: 70-80%, Service/Prof. development and scholarship 20-30% and is reviewed at minimum annually each year. Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications. The minimum salary for a Librarian IV is $57,000 and for a Librarian III is $62,500. All career levels are encouraged to apply. This position is not eligible for immigration sponsorship. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with comprehensive rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Library tenure-track faculty are also eligible to receive a generous relocation allowance, start-up funding for research, and annual professional development/travel funds. To apply, interested applicants must complete a UK Online Academic Profile at https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings and attach the below documents: Curriculum vitae Cover letter Please include contact information for three references when prompted in the application. We ask that one of the references be your current supervisor. Please note, the current supervisor will only be contacted if you are selected for a final round of interviews on campus. If you have any questions, contact UK Human Resources employment at (859) 257-9555, select option 2. Review of applications will begin on 9/19/2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated position start date will be on or after 2/01/2027. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Strong interpersonal, communication, and project management skills Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience ● Experience coordinating instruction programs or supervising librarians with instruction responsibilities ● Familiarity with instructional design, educational technologies, or online learning environments ● Experience with instructional effectiveness and/or program impact ● Experience working in collaborative, team-based service models Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644558": {
      "title": "4-H Camp Director",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | 4-H Camp Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support 4-H Camp Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title 4-H Camp Director Requisition Number RE55490 Working Title Department Name 81361:Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp Work Location Nancy, KY Grade Level 45 Salary Range $48,214-79,560/year Type of Position Staff Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education BA Click here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies Required Related Experience 5 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Must be able to lift up to 25lbs, and walk, sit and stand for periods of time. Shift Monday-Friday; and some nights and weekends. Job Summary This position is located in Nancy, Ky. The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture Food and Environment, Lake Cumberland 4-H Camp seeks an energetic self-motivated candidate that possesses a strong work ethic with skills in program development, financial management, and supervision for the 4-H Camp Director position. The 4-H Camp Director will be responsible for direct oversight, budgeting, planning, and preparing for summer camp programs. Responsible for recruiting, hiring seasonal camp staff and direct day to day management of all camp programs. Responsible for direct supervision for 25+ temporary, full-time employees. Continually evaluate and monitor risk management practices to ensure health and safety of participants and staff. Responsible for the day-to-day management of the camp budget. Research and pursue fund development opportunities as appropriate (e.g., fundraisers and grants). Work with the Maintenance Supervisor and Camp Maintenance and Operations Supervisor to evaluate facilities and set maintenance priorities and work plans. On-site housing is available. Valid driver’s license preferred and completion of the 12-passenger van training upon employment. This position includes excellent benefits and provides opportunities for professional development. For additional information on 4-H please Click Here . The Martin-Gatton College of Agriculture, Food and Environment offers a variety of employee enhancement initiatives, such as a formal mentoring program and a staff professional development fund. To find out more about Martin-Gatton CAFE and how the college supports the mission of this being the University of, for, and with Kentucky, Click Here . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Computer skills Supervision skills Experience in agriculture and/or Cooperative Extension Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Prefer experience in summer camp leadership, knowledge of 4-H programs, and experience working with youth. Driver’s License preferred Deadline to Apply 10/23/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your leadership experience with summer camp operations, financial oversight, and facility management, which may include volunteer and paid experience. (Open Ended Question) * Indicate below the answer that best describes your experience with 4-H. Have been employed by the Cooperative Extension Service and worked with 4-H Have been a 4-H leader/4-H volunteer Was an active 4-H member Participated in some 4-H programs Have no involvement with 4-H * Describe your supervisory experience. Include the number of employees whom you have supervised and the level of supervision you provided (i.e. hiring, discipline, training, delegation, performance management, etc.). (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience in and knowledge of 4-H Summer Camp, may include teen/adult volunteer and staff experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644490": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor, Department of Health &amp; Clinical Sciences",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor, Department of Health &amp; Clinical Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor, Department of Health & Clinical Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor, Department of Health & Clinical Sciences Requisition Number FE04980 Working Title Department Name 7N630:Health and Clinical Sciences Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Doctoral degree in a health sciences related field with relevant experience; ABD considered. Related fields include, but are not limited to, public health, health psychology, health communication, health administration, medical sociology, medical anthropology, health education or social work. Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary Special Title Series (tenure eligible) Faculty Position – Department of Health & Clinical Sciences The Human Health Sciences ( HHS ) program, Department of Health & Clinical Sciences, College of Health Sciences ( CHS ) at the University of Kentucky is currently accepting applications for a full-time 11-month teaching-focused special title (tenure eligible) faculty member with a preferred start date of July 1, 2027. We invite you to become part of a supportive community of dynamic and dedicated faculty focused on being national leaders in instruction, research, and service to positively impact others. This will be our second new faculty position this year to support robust growth in the department. The Human Health Sciences ( HHS ) degree is a pre-professional program for students interested in healthcare careers. The HHS degree offers a liberal arts foundation designed to provide students with a comprehensive look at health care practices to complement a solid foundation in basic science. HHS graduates are prepared to pursue advanced professional degrees in healthcare, such as medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, physician assistant studies, physical therapy, occupational therapy, optometry, athletic training, medical research, and more. Students are also being prepared for careers in patient navigation and leadership as well as other graduate studies. For more information about the HHS program, please visit: https://www.uky.edu/chs/human-health-sciences . Primary duties of this faculty position will include teaching undergraduate courses in the HHS program such as ethics, health policy, research in health sciences, social determinants of health, and/or cultural humility, depending on the candidate’s area(s) of expertise. The faculty member will also participate in curriculum development, advising/mentoring students, student admission activities, and other activities as assigned by the Program Director or Department Chair. Additional duties include participating in service across the department, college and university levels and scholarship and research activities as appropriate for special title series. The anticipated effort for this position is Instruction 65-75%, Research/Scholarship 10-20%, Service 8-10%, Professional Development 2-5% and will be determined based on an annual agreement with the Department Chair. The University of Kentucky and the College of Health Sciences are dedicated to fostering a professional and collaborative environment for students, faculty, and staff. We aim to support a strong community where individuals can thrive in their academic and professional pursuits. In your letter of interest, please describe the ways in which your past or current teaching, mentorship, and/or community service have supported the values of the University of Kentucky College of Health Sciences and the Human Health Sciences Program: https://www.uky.edu/chs/human-health-sciences . Candidates should apply online with a curriculum vitae, letter of interest, and complete UK job application. Applicants are also asked to submit an overview of their teaching experience which should include their teaching philosophy and sample teaching evaluations (if available). Please upload the overview and sample teaching evaluations as Specific Request 1 in the Applicant Documents section. Questions should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Jami Warren by email at jami.warren@uky.edu. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . About the University of Kentucky Founded in 1865 as a land-grant institution, UK is nestled in the scenic heart of the Bluegrass region of Kentucky. Recently ranked as one of the safest, most creative, and brainiest cities in the nation, Lexington is an ideal location to experience the work-life balance that the University strives to provide to its employees. Visit the University’s website and see for yourself what makes UK the perfect place to work. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 2-3 years instructional experience in health sciences related course work in post-secondary education (especially undergraduate instruction) Teaching experience in ethics, health policy, research in the health sciences, social determinants of health, cultural humility, and related classes Demonstrated record of scholarship and/or research presentations and/or publications Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised other than on UK's online employment system? HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Indeed American Public Health Association Association of Schools of Allied Health Professions AcademyHealth Society for Medical Anthropology Interprofessional Education Collaborative Kentucky Public Health Association A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member None of the above Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644114": {
      "title": "Clinical Physician - General Internist Medicine Women&#39;s Health",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Clinical Physician - General Internist Medicine Women&#39;s Health Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Clinical Physician - General Internist Medicine Women's Health Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinical Physician - General Internist Medicine Women's Health Requisition Number FE04976 Working Title Department Name 7H359:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - GENERAL Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD Degree or Equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency training in Internal Medicine Required License/Registration/Certification Internal Medicine Board certified or eligible Eligible for, or in current possession of, license to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Job Summary The University of Kentucky, Department of Internal Medicine is seeking an Assistant Professor in Internal Medicine for an opportunity in an academically oriented ambulatory position in the Women’s Health Section of the Division of General internal Medicine. The primary responsibilities are to provide ambulatory clinical services at the University of Kentucky Health Enterprise for women of all ages; an interest in specialty women’s care is required. The position will also provide clinical teaching and advising for trainees in the College of Medicine. This position will have a full clinical faculty appointment, competitive compensation and benefits. Qualified applicants must be board eligible or board certified in internal medicine. UK HealthCare is located in the beautiful Bluegrass Region of Lexington and is an ideal location to experience the work-life balance we strive to provide for all our employees. Lexington, KY is consistently ranked nationally in the top sectors for Business and Careers (Forbes), Young Professionals (Kiplinger), and Education (Parenting). The Department of Internal Medicine is the largest in the College of Medicine and at the University of Kentucky with approximately 367 faculty, 171 staff, 222 residents and fellows, and 212 advanced practice providers. The department has 14 clinical divisions and 2 non-clinical divisions within its scope. The department of internal medicine is led by Darwin Conwell, MD and departmental leaders including Vice Chairs, Associate Vice Chairs, and the Office of the Chair Administration team. Internal Medicine faculty secure over $35 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in all internal medicine subspecialties. The department has published 287 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains more than 50 active clinical trials and 240 active grants and contracts. The Department of Internal Medicine has 211 faculty who are actively involved in research activities and supervise biomedical learners, including Ph.D. and master’s students, to gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs . Please include CV along with application. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities An interest in providing specialty women’s care is required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preference will be given to providers with an interest in providing primary care services to women of all ages, and an interest in specialty women’s care. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644111": {
      "title": "Clinical Physician - General Internist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Clinical Physician - General Internist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Clinical Physician - General Internist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinical Physician - General Internist Requisition Number FE04977 Working Title MedPeds Ambulatory Department Name 7H359:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - GENERAL Work Location Frankfort, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency program and board certification Required License/Registration/Certification Kentucky Medical License Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine, Department of Internal Medicine, is seeking a qualified Med-Peds trained physician to join our Frankfort-based offsite clinic. UK HealthCare is working to provide primary care services to faculty, staff and patients closer to home. This clinic will serve as an extension of our General Internal Medicine clinic. Care will be provided in a team-based model with APPs and a physicians collaborating to care for a panel of patients. Additional responsibilities can include participation in community outreach programs and health education initiatives and participation in our mission of educating healthcare professionals for the state of Kentucky. Qualified applicants must be board eligible or board certified in Internal Medicine/Med-Peds, capable of fulfilling the requirements of a primary care physician, and committed to upholding the values and standards of the University of Kentucky and the Department of Internal Medicine. We offer competitive compensation based on rank and experience and an excellent benefits package that includes health, dental and life insurance; disability and malpractice insurance; a generous retirement plan; continuing education; paid time off and more. The Department of Internal Medicine is the largest in the College of Medicine and at the University of Kentucky with approximately 367 faculty, 171 staff, 222 residents and fellows, and 212 advanced practice providers. The department has 14 clinical divisions and 2 non-clinical divisions within its scope. The department of internal medicine is led by Darwin Conwell, MD and departmental leaders including Vice Chairs, Associate Vice Chairs, and the Office of the Chair Administration team. Internal Medicine faculty secure over $35 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in all internal medicine subspecialties. The department has published 287 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains more than 50 active clinical trials and 240 active grants and contracts. The Department of Internal Medicine has 211 faculty who are actively involved in research activities and supervise biomedical learners, including Ph.D. and master’s students, to gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs . Please include cover letter and CV along with application. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
