    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/644089": {
      "title": "Technology Support Assistant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Technology Support Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Technology Support Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Technology Support Assistant Requisition Number DU15001 Department Name 8X000:College of Fine Arts Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range 15.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Prior technical support experience is a plus but not required. Required Related Experience Prior technical support experience is a plus but not required. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements N/A Shift 10-20 per week Job Summary The College of Fine Arts is seeking a student for a Technology Support Assistant position which will provide friendly, prompt technology support for classrooms, faculty computers, and intake of help request calls across the college. This position is ideal for a student employee interested in gaining hands-on experience with classroom technology, Mac and Windows systems, and hands-on computer support. Work Setting: On-site support for classrooms, offices, and faculty workspaces Primary Responsibilities Provide classroom AV support, including basic troubleshooting for projectors, displays, audio systems, presentation systems, and related classroom technology. Respond to help desk tickets; assist faculty and staff with technology support requests. Support faculty computers and workstations using both Mac and Windows operating systems. Assist with break/fix, testing, and maintenance of classroom and instructional technology. Communicate clearly and professionally with faculty and staff when resolving technology issues. Document support activity, update tickets, and escalate complex technical issues to technology staff when appropriate. Qualifications Must be currently enrolled as a student at UK and eligible for student employment. Prior technical support experience is a plus but not required. General interest in computer technology, classroom systems, and helping others solve problems. Ability to communicate professionally and provide courteous customer service. Willingness to learn Mac and Windows support tasks and the UK ticketing system. Dependability, attention to detail, and ability to follow instructions. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 12/01/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
