    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/643904": {
      "title": "Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Comprehensive Ophthalmologist Requisition Number FE04958 Working Title Cataract Surgery Academic Faculty Department Name 7H854:OPHTHALMOLOGY & VISUAL SCIENCE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD plus Ophthalmology residency completion Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification Able to obtain Kentucky medical license Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine, Department of Ophthalmology, is seeking a Comprehensive Ophthalmologist to join our growing academic faculty. This is a unique opportunity for a clinician who is passionate about delivering exceptional patient care while shaping the next generation of ophthalmologists. What sets this position apart is the opportunity to dedicate approximately 50% of your professional effort to teaching and mentoring ophthalmology residents in cataract clinics and the operating room. This intentionally balanced role allows you to make a lasting impact on resident surgical education while maintaining an active and rewarding comprehensive ophthalmology practice. As a faculty member, you will join a collaborative academic department committed to excellence in patient care, education, and scholarly activity, with opportunities for professional growth and academic advancement. Position Responsibilities Provide comprehensive ophthalmic care to adult patients. Supervise and teach ophthalmology residents in cataract clinics and the operating room, with approximately 50% of the position dedicated to resident cataract education and surgical supervision. Educate and mentor ophthalmology residents and medical students through clinical instruction and hands-on surgical teaching. Participate in scholarly and academic activities aligned with your professional interests. Collaborate with faculty and multidisciplinary colleagues to advance the Department’s missions of clinical care, education, and research. Why Join the University of Kentucky? A unique clinician-educator opportunity with approximately 50% of the position dedicated to resident cataract education and surgical supervision. The opportunity to mentor and train future cataract surgeons in both the clinic and operating room. A balanced academic career that combines clinical excellence with meaningful teaching. Faculty appointment within a thriving academic medical center. Opportunities for academic advancement, professional development, and scholarly pursuits. A collegial and collaborative department committed to innovation, education, and exceptional patient care. The UK College of Medicine Department of Ophthalmology is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 180 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 37 faculty members, 122 staff members and 24 learners. Each year, providers in the department see 140,000+ patient visits at 17 clinical sites. The department trains 24 residents and fellows across 8 accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World”, Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Interested candidates should submit an updated CV along with their application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
