    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/643626": {
      "title": "Student Worker Video",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Worker Video Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Worker Video Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Worker Video Requisition Number DU12273 Department Name 12F00:UKAA - Support Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range 10.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education None required. Required Related Experience None required. Required License/Registration/Certification None required. Physical Requirements None required. Shift Days, Nights, Weekends Job Summary Work with our Sports Video Creative team to learn how to create engaging video content that showcases our athletic programs. You will gain hands-on experience with various cinema-style digital cameras, as well as sound, lighting, and editing equipment. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities None required. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience None required. Deadline to Apply 10/23/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * As part of the Southeastern Conference, candidates considered for staff or coaching positions within UK Athletics are required to disclose any unethical conduct. Please answer the below questions regarding your personal NCAA record. Have you ever been charged with a violation of NCAA 10.1 Unethical Conduct by the NCAA or any NCAA member institution? Yes No * Have you ever been charged with a NCAA Level I, II or III, secondary or major violation? Yes No * Are you currently involved in any pending NCAA investigation, charges and/or violations of NCAA legislation? Yes No * Has the NCAA Committee on Infractions ever issued you show-cause penalty? Yes No * If you answered yes, to either of the previous two questions, please list all violations in which you’ve been charged or were involved. If you answered no to both of the previous questions please type: N/A (Open Ended Question) * I agree to and understand that failure to disclose any NCAA violation or false information regarding my NCAA compliance history will result in removal of my application for consideration. Yes No * NCAA Bylaw 13.12.2 restricts institutional employment of an “Individual Associated with a Recruited Prospective Student-Athlete” (IAWRP) at any camp or clinic, including those consisting only of non-prospect-aged individuals. In order to certify you are not an IAWRP, the following questions must be answered in their entirety. (Open Ended Question) * I certify that I am not associated with any prospective student-athlete(s) that UK is currently recruiting. Yes No * Please list any basketball teams that you have been associated with in the past 4 years (e.g. high school, prep school, AAU, 2-year college): (Open Ended Question) * Are you associated with any prospect whose presence at a UK camp has been solicited by UK staff or a representative of UK’s athletics interests (e.g. booster)? Yes No * Are you associated with any prospect that has been provided with recruiting materials by UK? Yes No * Are you associated with any prospect with whom a UK staff member has had any recruiting contact [in-person or electronic contact (e.g. telephone call, email, text)]? Yes No * Are you associated with any prospect that has received a verbal offer of athletically related financial aid from UK? Yes No * Are you associated with any prospect that has verbally committed to attend UK? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/643468": {
      "title": "Research Data Analysis Librarian",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Data Analysis Librarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Data Analysis Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Data Analysis Librarian Requisition Number FE04975 Working Title Department Name 88000:LIBRARY ADMINISTRATION Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA -accredited program by start date or a relevant, advanced degree. Required Related Experience Experience working with data such as analysis, visualization, or wrangling in a professional or academic setting using any of (but not limited to) the following tools: REDCap, Python, R, Qualtrics, SAS , SPSS , NVIVO , Stata, or MATLAB . Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary University of Kentucky Libraries is vital to fulfilling the goals of enhancing and expanding the university’s research enterprise, and we are seeking a Research Data Analysis Librarian to strengthen and expand UK Libraries’ research data services, particularly in data refinement, analysis, and visualization. This position is part of Digital Scholarship and Data, a collaborative department with expertise in research data management, digital scholarship, scholarly communication, and GIS . Serving all academic disciplines, the Research Data Analysis Librarian supports robust, reproducible, and impactful research across campus by providing expertise in data analysis methods and workflows, while also engaging with emerging approaches, including the responsible use of artificial intelligence in research and scholarship. Responsibilities ● Provides data analysis instruction, workshops, and consultations for students, faculty, and researchers across disciplines, supporting both qualitative and quantitative methods. ● Develops and shares best practices for data refinement, analysis, visualization, and modeling, with an emphasis on reproducibility and responsible research workflows. ● Supports the use of tools, programming environments, and emerging technologies, including AI-enabled approaches, that enhance data analysis and research processes. ● Collaborates with subject liaisons and campus partners to provide responsive and customized data-related instruction. ● Actively engages with research coordinators and early career researchers to build capacity for responsible data practices. ● Remains current on trends and issues related to digital scholarship, scholarly communication, and open scholarship, particularly in the context of research data. Shares advancements with colleagues on campus and within the profession through scholarship and service. Required Qualifications ● Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA -accredited program by start date or a relevant, advanced degree. ● Experience working with data such as analysis, visualization, or wrangling in a professional or academic setting using any of (but not limited to) the following tools: REDCap, Python, R, Qualtrics, SAS , SPSS , NVIVO , Stata, or MATLAB . ● Demonstrated ability to learn and apply new tools and methods, including emerging data and AI technologies. ● Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, both written and oral. ● Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. ● Ability to meet the requirements of tenure. Preferred Qualifications ● Experience providing instruction or consultations related to data analysis or research methods. ● Familiarity with a range of data analysis tools and workflows. ● Experience working in an academic or research environment. ● Awareness of ethical, legal, and practical considerations in the use of data and AI in research. This position participates in planning, shared governance, and UK Libraries-wide faculty activities. This is a full-time, 12-month, tenure eligible position in the Librarian Title Series (open rank) which requires scholarship, professional development, and service that contributes to the effectiveness of UK Libraries, the university, and the profession as outlined in Administrative Regulation 2:7 (https://regs.uky.edu/administrative-regulation/ar-27). Your Distribution of Effort ( DOE ) range: Primary assignment: 70-80%, Service/Prof. development and scholarship 20-30% and is reviewed at minimum annually each year. Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications. The minimum salary for a Librarian IV is $57,000 and for a Librarian III is $62,500. All career levels are encouraged to apply. This position is not eligible for immigration sponsorship. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with comprehensive rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits. Library tenure-track faculty are also eligible to receive a generous relocation allowance, start-up funding for research, and annual professional development/travel funds. To apply, interested applicants must complete a UK Online Academic Profile at https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings and attach the below documents: Curriculum vitae Cover letter Please include contact information for three references when prompted in the application. We ask that one of the references be your current supervisor. Please note, the current supervisor will only be contacted if you are selected for a final round of interviews on campus. If you have any questions, contact UK Human Resources employment at (859) 257-9555, select option 2. Review of applications will begin on 9/14/2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated position start date will be on or after 2/01/2027 . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Demonstrated ability to learn and apply new skills and tools; evidence of ongoing, self-directed learning. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, both written and oral. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Instructional or consultation experience with a range of constituents, especially the teaching of technical skills. Experience working in a research environment, academic library, or similar setting (including but not limited to internships, practica, and student employment). Familiarity with a broad range of data analysis tools. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/643364": {
      "title": "Chair and Executive Director - Associate or Professor in Social Work",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Chair and Executive Director - Associate or Professor in Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Chair and Executive Director - Associate or Professor in Social Work Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Chair and Executive Director - Associate or Professor in Social Work Requisition Number FE04968 Working Title Chair and Executive Director in Social Work Department Name 8T110:College of Social Work Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education An earned doctorate in Social Work from an accredited institution An earned Master of Social Work degree from a CSWE -accredited program Required Related Experience A record of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure. Strong potential for securing external funding and producing high-quality scholarship. Ability to foster, develop, and/or maintain positive professional relationships with local, state, federal, and private social work focused agencies/organizations/associations. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary THE UNIVERSITY OF KENTUCKY , COLLEGE OF SOCIAL WORK (CoSW) is a renowned leader in higher education. Our mission is clear: Through rigorous research, excellence in instruction, and steadfast service, the CoSW works to improve the human condition. Always, in all ways. As the state’s flagship university, CoSW is committed to actualizing our mission through innovative, accessible academic programming. CoSW is home to several undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs, including: Bachelor of Arts in Criminal Justice (traditional and online), Bachelor of Science in Criminal Justice (traditional and online), Bachelor of Arts in Social Work (traditional and online), Master of Science in Criminal Justice (online), Master of Social Work (hybrid and online), Doctorate of Social Work (online), Ph.D. in Social Work (traditional), and multiple certificate programs. In addition to Lexington’s main campus, we have a satellite campus at Fort Sam Houston in San Antonio, Texas. The Chair and Executive Director of Social Work Programs serves as the chief academic and administrative leader for the College’s social work educational enterprise. The Chair provides visionary leadership and strategic oversight for all aspects of the College’s social work programs, including the Bachelor of Arts in Social Work, Master of Social Work, Doctorate of Social Work, Doctor of Philosophy in Social Work, and related certificate programs. Reporting directly to the Dean and serving as a member of the College leadership team, the Chair and Executive Director advances the College’s strategic vision through academic leadership, faculty development, student success, community engagement, operational excellence, and organizational growth. Primary responsibilities of this position include but are not limited to: Leads Strategic Growth and Innovation Develops and implements the strategic vision for the College’s social work programs. Guides academic innovation and program growth across modalities. Uses workforce, enrollment, and market data to inform planning. Identifies opportunities for new educational initiatives. Advances Faculty Success Recruits, mentors, supervises, and evaluates faculty and instructional personnel. Supports promotion, tenure, annual review, and workload planning. Supports faculty leadership development. Cultivates a collaborative faculty culture. Promotes Academic Excellence Oversees BASW , MSW , DSW , PhD, and certificate programs. Supports curriculum innovation. Ensures compliance with CSWE and SACSCOC . Promotes instructional quality across all modalities. Supports Student Success Partners with admissions, advising, practicum, recruitment, and student success. Advances recruitment, retention, persistence, and graduation initiatives. Strengthens Community Impact Develops relationships with agencies, alumni, professional organizations, and community partners. Supports fundraising and workforce partnerships. Expands community-engaged scholarship and education. Manages Resources for Organizational Success Oversees personnel, budgeting, operational planning, and resource allocation. Collaborates with College leadership to advance strategic priorities. The University’s mission involves three primary functions across our faculty cohort: instruction, research, and service. Each year, various ranking faculty work with the Office of the Dean to delineate their distribution of effort ( DOE ). This DOE outlines how faculty will spend their time. In general, DOE for faculty members in the Regular Title Series typically includes allocations in the areas of instruction, research, and service. The DOE for the Chair and Executive Director is subject to negotiation but we anticipate roughly 70% Administration, 25% research and 5% service. Of course, the DOE can fluctuate depending on an array of factors (e.g., grant funding, new course development, service to the college, etc.). It is expected that work in this faculty appointment, including but not limited to course instruction, office hours, administrative meetings, and attending college-wide events such as faculty meetings, will occur on-site. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with many rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . Applicants should submit: • Curriculum Vitae (upload as resume) • Letter of Interest describing qualifications, leadership philosophy, and alignment with the position (upload as cover letter) • Contact information for at least three professional references (upload as Special Request #1) • Statement addressing administrative leadership, program development, and commitment to excellence and collaboration (upload as Special Request #2) We anticipate this search will run from October 2026 through April 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Inquiries about the position can be emailed to UKCOSW@uky.edu. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience WE ARE SEEKING AN INDIVIDUAL WHO POSSESSES : Demonstrated leadership experience in higher education, academic administration, community-engaged organizations, or related professional settings Experience providing executive-level leadership, including strategic planning, operational oversight, organizational leadership, and collaborative decision-making Evidence of successful collaboration across interdisciplinary, professional, and community contexts Experience supporting faculty development, mentorship, leadership cultivation, and program growth A commitment to fostering excellence through a wide range of perspectives, methodologies, lived experiences, and approaches to scholarship, teaching, and service Experience with CSWE accreditation standards and processes Experience overseeing curriculum assessment, instructional coordination, and supervision of instructional personnel Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/643319": {
      "title": "FWS Fall 2026, Law Library Student Desk Attendant",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | FWS Fall 2026, Law Library Student Desk Attendant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support FWS Fall 2026, Law Library Student Desk Attendant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title FWS Fall 2026, Law Library Student Desk Attendant Requisition Number DU14961 Department Name 1B531:Federal Work Study Work Location 602 S Limestone Lexington, KY, 40506 Salary Range $12.00 - $20.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Must be enrolled in the University of Kentucky and eligible for Federal Work Study. Required Related Experience Library work experience preferred. Library Information Sciences or Law majors preferred, but other majors and undergraduates welcome to apply. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Must be able to lift 30 lbs. and sit or stand for a period of 2 hours or more. Shift Maximum is 20 hours per week. Most shifts are 2 – 6 hours each and occur between 7:00 AM – 10:00 PM. Job Summary Student Desk Attendants answer library-related questions in-person and over the phone, check desk materials in and out to patrons assist with hold shelf items, and direct patrons to our Reference librarians. They also open and close the library, depending on their availability and selected weekly shifts. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Good attention to detail and ability to work independently. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Library experience preferred, but not necessary. Deadline to Apply 12/18/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? (If you are unsure, or you have not yet been awarded Federal Work Study, please contact the Student Financial Aid office at (859) 257-3172 and ask to speak with your counselor.) Yes No * Please state your current 8-digit UKID number and LinkBlue ID (Open Ended Question) * Kentucky state law requires anyone who works after 10:30 p.m. on school nights (Sunday - Thursday), and after 1:00 a.m. on non-school nights (Friday - Sunday), to be 18+ years of age. Are you over the age of 18 or will you be 18 before August 1st of the fall semester or January 1st for the spring term (or before employment)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
