    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642977": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor in Interior Design",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Associate or Full Professor in Interior Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Associate or Full Professor in Interior Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Associate or Full Professor in Interior Design Requisition Number FE04974 Working Title Director, School of Interiors Department Name 8N500:Sch of Interiors:Planning/Strategy/Desig Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Terminal degree in Interior Design or a closely related field Required Related Experience Record of excellence in teaching, research, or creative practice sufficient for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor Demonstrated academic leadership experience Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills Commitment to collaboration, shared governance, and student success Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The College of Design at the University of Kentucky invites applications and nominations for the position of Director of the School of Interiors. The Director will lead the next phase of the school’s development, working closely with faculty to articulate and advance a clear and compelling vision for the future of interior design education, one that builds on the school’s strengths in material exploration, interdisciplinary design, and human-centered inquiry while expanding its research impact, global reach, and national visibility. We are seeking an outward-facing, service-oriented leader who listens, advocates, and positions the school within evolving conversations across design, higher education, and the profession. The Director will enter at a moment when the school is well-positioned for new opportunities. We are in a new building, have made significant faculty hires in recent years, will have completed reaccreditation in spring 2027, and have a curriculum transformation underway. The school is in an energetic and malleable phase with significant opportunity to shape its trajectory. Job Description The Director of the School of Interiors is a full-time faculty position with administrative responsibilities. Administration is anticipated to be 45% of the Director’s distribution of effort, with the remaining 55% allocated to teaching and research. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Design, the Director is responsible for the overall academic, administrative, and fiscal leadership of the School. They will provide leadership in defining the program’s strategic priorities and vision and in enhancing its visibility, brand, and reputation. In this role, the Director will be responsible for continuing to advance and strengthen curricular offerings; fostering excellence in teaching, research, and engagement ; strategically managing the program’s enrollment; overseeing the hiring of new full-time and part-time faculty; supporting the career advancement of faculty members; advancing innovation and multidisciplinary activities; and working collaboratively with College leadership and departmental faculty to effectively manage program resources. The Director should promote a work and learning environment that fosters entrepreneurship, growth, collaboration, and shared governance. The position will commence on July 1, 2027. This is a 12-month appointment at the rank of associate or full professor with tenure. The term of the administrative appointment is four years and is renewable for an additional four years. Salary is competitive and based on qualifications and experience. A complete application must include and will be evaluated based on the following materials: a cover letter addressing experience and vision related to leadership, research and creative scholarship, service, teaching, as well as the future of design education and the industry a current curriculum vitae or resume highlighting relevant academic and/or professional experience names and contact information for at least three references (who will not be contacted unless/until a candidate is invited to an on-campus interview) sample of scholarly or creative work (10 pages max.; upload under Specific Request 1 ) Applications only accepted via https://ukjobs.uky.edu/. Review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Leadership Profile The ideal candidate will be an outward-facing, strategic leader who works closely with faculty to articulate and advance a shared vision for the school. They will be a strong listener, a clear communicator, and an advocate for the program. They will be able to build consensus, set direction, and make decisions that move the school forward. This includes strengthening its intellectual contributions, expanding its reach, and positioning it within evolving conversations in design, culture, and the built environment. An effective Director will support people while also challenging the program to grow. They will recognize the School’s current momentum and guide it through this next phase with clarity, focus, and purpose. Key Responsibilities and Leadership Priorities: External Engagement and Visibility • Serve as the public face of the School and position it within national and international design conversations • Expand partnerships with industry, alumni, peer institutions, and community organizations • Grow the School’s global footprint through study abroad and international research initiatives • Build upon and activate an Advisory Board and contribute to philanthropic efforts • Elevate the visibility of faculty research and creative work through strategic communication and outreach Student Experience and Outcomes • Champion a rigorous, engaging, and supportive student experience • Encourage intellectual risk-taking and critical engagement in student work • Strengthen connections to professional practice, graduate education, and interdisciplinary opportunities • Support pathways that connect undergraduate and graduate research and learning Faculty Leadership and Development • Build alignment across School faculty while supporting individual trajectories • Oversee review, promotion, and mentoring processes • Support and elevate faculty research, creative activity, and external recognition • Build upon a culture of shared governance, collaboration, and mutual accountability Academic and Intellectual Leadership • Lead the intellectual and pedagogical direction of the school • Support a cohesive curricular vision aligned with the school’s mission and future trajectory • Advance a culture of critical inquiry, experimentation, and design rigor • Guide curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation • Strengthen the integration of research across studios, seminars, and graduate work Operations and Program Management • Oversee budgets, staffing, and day-to-day operations • Develop course schedules and faculty teaching assignments • Align resources with strategic priorities • Collaborate with College leadership on hiring, planning, and resource allocation About the School of Interiors The School of Interiors is a nationally respected program known for its strong and multidisciplinary faculty-led research program, collaborative culture, and commitment to design as a human-centered and materially grounded practice. The school emphasizes areas of inquiry such as material experimentation, soft making, and interdisciplinary methodologies, supported by fabrication facilities and an expanding research environment. Faculty are engaged in creative practice, scholarship, and community-based work that contributes to both local impact and broader disciplinary conversations. The program is distinguished by its graduate offerings, which position it among a limited number of interior design programs with advanced research pathways. This creates opportunities to further define areas of distinction and deepen research contributions. The school is actively evolving. It is expanding its global footprint through study abroad and international research, strengthening connections to industry and professional practice, and building new partnerships that extend its reach. A key priority for the Director will be to expand and engage an Advisory Board and support philanthropic development. This is a moment of transition and opportunity. With new faculty, new facilities, and a curriculum revision underway, the school is entering a new era that invites strategic leadership, alignment, and growth. About the College of Design The College of Design is a dynamic, transdisciplinary environment that supports innovation across architecture, interiors, historic preservation, and product design. Housed in a new facility within a growing arts district, the College fosters collaboration, experimentation, and outward-facing work. The College is actively engaged in shaping a forward-looking vision for design education and research. Faculty and leadership are invested in building new models of practice that connect design to pressing environmental, social, and cultural issues. The Director of the School of Interiors will play a central role in this visioning process. We value design as a human-centered, inherently optimistic activity and embrace the unique strengths of our disciplines while collaborating in a transdisciplinary environment. Our programs balance theoretical foundations, conceptual design thinking, technical understanding, and the act of making as crucial elements of an iterative process leading to impactful design. Learning, teaching, and research in the College of Design explore the interconnected relationships between human experience, built and natural environments, and designed objects and systems. Our areas of research specialization include history, theory, and criticism; digital fabrication and simulation; materials innovation; community resiliency; sustainability and preservation; and design for health and well-being. The College of Design’s home, the Gray Design Building, is 100,000 square feet of open studio space, state-of-the-art fabrication lab facilities, classrooms, offices, and event spaces — a place where students of architecture, interiors, historic preservation, product design, and landscape architecture — can all learn and work together in a modern, cross-disciplinary environment. Built in 1917, the former tobacco warehouse has been transformed into an open, dynamic space that encourages interaction and collaboration between students and faculty of various disciplines. The Gray Design Building was more than a renovation project — it serves as a prime example of adaptive reuse and sustainable building practices, effective collaboration between global and local design teams, and symbolizes a bridge between the building’s industrial past and its innovative future as a hub for design education. This transformative renovation was completed in 2024, and the College moved into its new home that spring. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience • National or international recognition in design research or practice • Experience leading program development or curricular transformation • Record of externally funded research or sustained professional engagement • Experience building strategic partnerships across academic, industry, or community contexts • Ability to elevate program visibility and reputation Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642969": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Research Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Research Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Research Assistant Professor Requisition Number FE04961 Working Title Department Name 8H007:Biomedical Engineering Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related field. Required Related Experience PhD + 3 years experience Required License/Registration/Certification None Job Summary The successful candidate will contribute to an active research program in biomedical engineering, with emphasis on nanomedicine, genome editing, and cancer immunotherapy. Primary responsibilities will include planning and designing experiments, generating and analyzing complex experimental data, preparing manuscripts, and contributing to research grant applications. Additional responsibilities will include mentoring and training graduate students in experimental design, operation of specialized scientific equipment, data analysis, and scientific writing. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related field. Candidates with strong experience in nanomedicine, genome editing, cancer immunotherapy, biomaterials, drug/gene delivery, correlated areas are especially encouraged to apply. Applicants should also have strong written and oral communication skills, a record of research productivity, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. The candidate will need to provide a curriculum vitae, a cover letter, a research statement ( Specific Request 1 ) and the names of three references ( Specific Request 2) . This posting will remain open until filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Cancer immunology; and Gene Editing. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Candidates with strong experience in nanomedicine, genome editing, cancer immunotherapy, biomaterials, drug/gene delivery, or related areas are especially encouraged to apply. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642898": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant or Associate Professor of Law Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant or Associate Professor of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Law Requisition Number FE04962 Working Title Department Name 8K100:Law Instruction Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education J.D. or equivalent law degree Required Related Experience Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in teaching and in scholarly productivity in one or more areas as needed. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary THE UNIVERSITY OF KENTUCKY ROSENBERG COLLEGE OF LAW invites applications to fill two regular title series tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning in August 2027. The positions will be 9-month appointments corresponding with the University’s fall and spring semesters. The College welcomes applications from candidates across all areas of law, but some areas of need include the fields of commercial law (including bankruptcy), business law, and property. We may also consider an applicant for a full Professor position. The Rosenberg College of Law is an important part of a major research university and offers a collegial and supportive atmosphere for its faculty, staff, and students. Applicants should have a J.D. or equivalent law degree, a record of high academic achievement, and a demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and in scholarly productivity. We are interested in applicants with a wide variety of professional and academic experiences and backgrounds. Salary for this position will be commensurate with experience. To receive consideration for this position, applicants must apply through the University of Kentucky’s Integrated Employment System where they can submit a letter of application and resume. Please send any questions to Faculty Appointments Committee Chair John Blevins, jbl272@uky.edu, or by mail at the University of Kentucky Rosenberg College of Law, 620 South Limestone, Lexington, KY 40506-0048. This posting will remain open until all positions are filled. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and includes a comprehensive benefits package that supports employee well-being and career development. Leadership is committed to promoting work life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. Additional optional benefits include dental and vision insurance, supplemental retirement plans, and much more. To learn more about these benefits, click here . Lexington is in the center of the Bluegrass, an internationally acclaimed cultural landscape, and in close proximity to Louisville and Cincinnati. It is a community of 300,000 and is distinguished by its rating as one of the top 10 most educated cities in the nation (according to the U.S. Census), top 5 cities for young professionals (Kiplinger), top 3 mid-sized cities for lowest cost of living ( KPMG LLP ), and top 5 cities to raise a family (Forbes). More information on Lexington is available at http://www.visitlex.com . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience N/A Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642729": {
      "title": "Physician - Dermatologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Dermatologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Dermatologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Dermatologist Requisition Number FE04963 Working Title Department Name 7H350:INTERNAL MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD or DO degree with board certification in Dermatology Required Related Experience Completion of an ACGME -accredited Dermatology Residency Program Completion of an ACGME -accredited Dermatopathology Fellowship Board-certified or board-eligible in Dermatology and Dermatopathology Experience in academic or teaching environments, preferably with internal medicine or family medicine residents and medical students Track record of peer-reviewed publications or scholarly presentations in dermatology and/or dermatopathology Demonstrated ability to collaborate across specialties and participate in multidisciplinary care Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for licensure in the Commonwealth of Kentucky Job Summary The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine invites applications for a full-time Dermatologist to join the Division of Dermatology as an Assistant, Associate or Professor of Dermatology. The ideal candidate will be board-certified or board-eligible in dermatology and have demonstrated excellence in clinical care, dermatopathology, medical education, and scholarly activity. This position includes opportunities for clinical practice, teaching medical students and residents, and participating in research and academic endeavors. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the growth of academic dermatology at one of the Commonwealth’s leading academic health centers, with access to NIH -supported infrastructure, multidisciplinary partners, and patients from varied backgrounds. About the Department of Internal Medicine The Department of Internal Medicine is the largest in the College of Medicine and at the University of Kentucky with approximately 334 faculty, 157 staff, 214 residents and fellows, and 203 advanced practice providers. The department has 14 clinical divisions and 2 non-clinical divisions within its scope. The department of internal medicine is led by Dr. Darwin L. Conwell, MD, MS, FACG and departmental leaders including Vice Chairs, Associate Vice Chairs, and the Office of the Chair Administration team. Internal Medicine faculty secure over $35 million in grant funding annually to pursue cutting-edge research and discoveries, supporting projects in all internal medicine subspecialties. The department has published 287 peer-reviewed articles in the past year and maintains more than 50 active clinical trials and 240 active grants and contracts. The Department of Internal Medicine has 211 faculty who are actively involved in research activities and supervise biomedical learners, including PhD and master’s students, to gain in-depth experience in high-impact research labs . Please include an updated CV and Cover Letter when applying to this position. Job posting will remain open until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642728": {
      "title": "Faculty in Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Faculty in Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Faculty in Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Faculty in Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry Requisition Number FE04965 Working Title Department Name 7H180:Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Ph.D., M.D. or equivalent degree Required Related Experience Research areas of interest include structural and cellular biology of cardiovascular, muscle, neurological, and metabolic diseases, cancer (including interest in pediatric oncology) and developmental biology. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Job Summary The Department of Molecular & Cellular Biochemistry at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the assistant professor level. Candidates must possess a Ph.D., M.D. or equivalent degree. Extramural funding is not required; however applicants should have potential to develop a robust, extramurally funded research program. Competitive start-up funds and appropriate space will be offered. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research area complements existing departmental strengths in the structural and cellular biology of cardiovascular, muscle, neurological, and metabolic diseases, cancer (including interest in pediatric oncology) and developmental biology. Translational research programs that encompass aspects of both basic and clinical research are of special interest, particularly those that make use of mass spectroscopy-based approaches, advanced organoid models or single-cell/spatial —omics and bioinformatic approaches. The Department offers a stimulating and collaborative environment, with a strong graduate program, and extensive shared, state-of-the-art equipment. The University of Kentucky houses an NCI -designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, a federally supported Alzheimer’s Disease Center, and a Center for Clinical and Translational Science. In addition, the University is undergoing a significant expansion of its biomedical research program. Initial evaluation of applicants will begin September 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should visit https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642068 to access the online faculty application. Required application materials include a cover letter, curriculum vitae , description of current and future research (≤ 3 pages) (specific request 1), teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) (specific request 2), and contact information for three references. Inquiries may be directed to the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee at: biochem@uky.edu For further information about the Department, please visit: https://medicine.uky.edu/departments/biochemistry/ Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? Yes Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
