    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/642060": {
      "title": "Campus Recreation STUDENT Personal Trainer or STUDENT Group Fitness Instructor Fall 2026",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Campus Recreation STUDENT Personal Trainer or STUDENT Group Fitness Instructor Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Campus Recreation STUDENT Personal Trainer or STUDENT Group Fitness Instructor Fall 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Campus Recreation STUDENT Personal Trainer or STUDENT Group Fitness Instructor Fall 2026 Requisition Number DU14920 Department Name 1B310:Campus Recreation Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12-$20 / Hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Must be a current student at the University of Kentucky Required Related Experience none Required License/Registration/Certification Personal Training or Group Fitness Certification Physical Requirements The position may require lifting or pushing objects up to 50lbs, or extended amounts of time walking or standing. Shift As scheduled Job Summary Designing and leading personal training and group fitness sessions. This position is also Federal Work-Study eligible, if you qualify. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Time Management, Social Interaction, Initiative, Observant Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Certified Personal Trainer or Group Fitness Instructor Deadline to Apply 05/31/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure Are you interested in working as a Personal Trainer or Group Fitness Instructor? Yes No What certification do you hold? (Open Ended Question) Please describe your experience in teaching or leading a group fitness or personal training session. (Open Ended Question) What is your training philosophy? (Open Ended Question) Are you available to work weekends? Yes No No Response To help us understand your availability for the applicable semester, please provide the specific times when you are NOT available to work. Our hours of operation are: Monday - Friday 6:00 a.m. to 12:00 a.m., Saturday 10:00 a.m. to 9:00 p.m., and Sunday 11:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m. (EXAMPLE: 'I cannot work M/W/F 11:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. because I have class.') (Open Ended Question) You must be a UK student to hold this position. Are you a UK student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click