    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/641961": {
      "title": "Athletics Operations Student Worker",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Athletics Operations Student Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Athletics Operations Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Athletics Operations Student Worker Requisition Number DU13614 Department Name 12G00:UKAA - Facilities Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00/hr Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High School diploma or GED Required Related Experience NA Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements Ability to lift, push, and pull objects up to 50 lbs. Some jobs require extensive walking and /or lengthy periods of standing, along with exposure to indoor and outdoor weather elements. Shift Days, Evenings, Nights, and Weekends Job Summary This position assists our Operations Staff in all event and facility-related areas (e.g., event setup/breakdown, general facility upkeep, and other assigned duties). The position collaborates with our full-time staff on weekdays from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. and works at home sporting events on nights and weekends throughout the fall, winter, and spring seasons. This includes mandatory participation in all home football games in the fall semester. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Ability to excel in a fast-paced setting; exceptional communication and adaptability; team player with professionalism, leadership, and practical time management skills. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 05/31/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * As part of the Southeastern Conference, candidates considered for staff or coaching positions within UK Athletics are required to disclose any unethical conduct. Please answer the below questions regarding your prior collegiate employment. Have you ever been charged with a violation of NCAA 10.1 Unethical Conduct by the NCAA or any NCAA member institution? Yes No * Have you ever been charged with a NCAA Level I, II or III, secondary or major violation or any violations with the Collegiate Sports Commission (CSC) and/or SEC? Yes No * Are you currently involved in any pending NCAA, CSC, or SEC investigation, charges and/or violations of NCAA, CSC or SEC legislation? Yes No * If you answered yes, to either of the previous three questions, please list all violations in which you’ve been charged or were involved. If you answered no to all three of the previous questions please type: N/A (Open Ended Question) * Has the NCAA Committee on Infractions ever issued you show-cause penalty? Yes No * I agree to and understand that failure to disclose any NCAA violation or false information regarding my NCAA compliance history will result in removal of my application for consideration. Yes No * I certify that I am not associated with any prospective student-athlete(s) UK is currently recruiting. Yes No * Please select “Yes” for the games you are available for and “No” for the games you are not available for I understand * Saturday, September 5th – Youngstown State Yes No * Saturday, September 12th – Alabama Yes No * Saturday, September 26th– South Alabama Yes No * Saturday, October 10th – LSU Yes No * Saturday, October 24th – Vanderbilt Yes No * Saturday, November 14th-Florida Yes No Saturday, November 28th – Louisville Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/641796": {
      "title": "Student Facilitator",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Facilitator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Facilitator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Facilitator Requisition Number DU12391 Department Name 8G040:Kinesiology - Health Promotion Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.50-$16.50/ hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education undergraduate student Required Related Experience • Experience working with youth in school or community setting is preferred, but not required. . • Experience in public speaking is preferred. • Experience successfully utilizing tools such as Microsoft PowerPoint, Word, and Excel. • Be highly motivated, energetic, dependable and knowledgeable. Required License/Registration/Certification none Physical Requirements none Shift 10-15 hours a week, M-F, times will vary Applicant must have one day of full availability in order to facilitate presentations. Please include your weekly availability. Job Summary NOTE : No prior knowledge on the topic of tobacco use or public health is needed. The program will provide comprehensive training. NOTE : The position may be used to fulfill practicum hours if needed. Position Objective: To provide tobacco use prevention services to youth, families and community members across Kentucky. Position Description: Supervised by the Program Director, the Youth Prevention Specialist works in schools and communities to facilitate tobacco use prevention services based on the #iCANendthetrend framework, which include: 1. Prevention Education 2. Information Dissemination 3. Youth Empowerment 4. Professional Development Position Responsibilities: • Collaborate with schools, parent-teacher groups, civic organizations, church groups, and other youth and community organizations to provide information and awareness on youth tobacco use, including e-cigarettes. • Implement peer-to-peer prevention program to provide information and awareness on youth tobacco use, including e-cigarettes. • Assist in providing orientation or information sessions for parents, teachers, staff or administrators in target area school and community sites when requested. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director to meet program objectives. *Applicants must have reliable transportation. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience • Pre-employment criminal background check, employment background check, as required by school districts. • Evidence-based curriculum training must be obtained within 1 month of employment, and prior to in-school or related program delivery. This will be provided through the position. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Writing Sample Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
