    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/641174": {
      "title": "Physician - Oculoplastics Surgeon",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Oculoplastics Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Oculoplastics Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Oculoplastics Surgeon Requisition Number FE03357 Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Oculoplastic Surgery Department Name 7H854:OPHTHALMOLOGY & VISUAL SCIENCE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. Required Related Experience M.D. Required License/Registration/Certification M.D. Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine Department of Ophthalmology is seeking an Assistant Professor to join our Oculoplastics practice. This position supports the department’s mission of clinical care, teaching, and scholarly activity, with opportunities for professional growth within a comprehensive academic medical center. We are seeking an Oculplastics faculty to join our group of physicians that are committed to excellence in clinical care, instruction, scholarly activity and professional development. The successful candidate must have completed an accredited American Society of Ophthalmic Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery ( ASOPRS ) fellowship. Responsibilities include: Providing direct patient care Teaching an ASOPRS fellow, residents and medical students Developing academic pursuits in the areas of education and research The UK College of Medicine Department of Ophthalmology is a strong, multidisciplinary team of more than 180 people dedicated to advancing Kentucky health care together. Our department encompasses 37 faculty members, 122 staff members and 24 learners. Each year, providers in the department see 140,000+ patient visits at 17 clinical sites. The department trains 24 residents and fellows across 8 accredited programs, while also contributing to the education of medical students and graduate trainees. Lexington is an understated and sophisticated city in the southeast. Situated in the heart of the Bluegrass and rightfully called the “Horse Capital of the World”, Lexington is surrounded by picturesque landscapes and horse farms. The University of Kentucky is central to the city and plays a major role in commerce and culture. As an SEC school, the university boasts one of the most unique and competitive collegiate sports teams in the nation. Lexington combines safe neighborhoods, excellent schools, an affordable cost of living, and a vibrant community that appeals to individuals, couples and families. Louisville and Cincinnati are a little over an hour’s drive and complement Lexington as larger, vibrant cities with many cultural and recreational opportunities year-round. https://medicine.uky.edu/visit-college-medicine Interested candidates should submit an updated CV along with their application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/641168": {
      "title": "Economic Development Student Worker",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Economic Development Student Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Economic Development Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Economic Development Student Worker Requisition Number DU14891 Department Name 37500:Economic Development Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Full-time University of Kentucky Student in good standing. Required Related Experience None Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements May require sitting or standing for long periods of time. Shift Flexible, up to 15 hours per week, to be agreed upon with supervisor. Job Summary The Office of Economic Development and Real Estate at the University of Kentucky is seeking a student intern to support program storytelling, digital content development, and event coordination. This position will assist with capturing and sharing the impact of UK’s economic development and real estate initiatives through written stories, photography, video, and digital content. The intern will also provide support for the Economic Development Collaborative’s quarterly convening by assisting with planning, logistics, on-site execution, and post-event reporting. Working closely with university and community partners, the intern will help document program outcomes, develop engaging content, and contribute to initiatives that highlight the office’s work and impact. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Pursuing a degree in journalism, public relations, business, design, English, integrated strategic communication, or a related field. Strong writing, editing, and storytelling skills with the ability to communicate complex topics to a broad audience. Experience creating digital content, including photography, graphics, and short-form video using Canva or Adobe Creative Cloud. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Interest in event planning and providing logistical support for meetings, conferences, and community engagement activities. Familiarity with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace for organizing information and basic reporting. Self-motivated, detail-oriented, and comfortable collaborating with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Pursuing a degree in journalism, public relations, business, design, English, integrated strategic communication, or a related field Deadline to Apply Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
