    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/640652": {
      "title": "Lecturer - College of Nursing - Clinical Instruction",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Lecturer - College of Nursing - Clinical Instruction Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Lecturer - College of Nursing - Clinical Instruction Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Lecturer - College of Nursing - Clinical Instruction Requisition Number FE04884 Working Title Lecturer Department Name 7E100:NURSING INSTRUCTION Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education Master’s degree in Nursing required Required Related Experience Minimum of two (2) years of BSN nursing experience within the last five (5) years required Required License/Registration/Certification Active unencumbered Kentucky license as a registered nurse Job Summary The University of Kentucky, College of Nursing Undergraduate Program is seeking a Lecturer Title Series (non-tenure track) Lecturer. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated Distribution of Effort of about 90% Teaching and Advising, and 10% Service/Professional Development which will be reviewed annually. We anticipate a start date of August 16, 2026. This position, onsite and based in Lexington, KY, will assist and resource the Undergraduate BSN program within the College of Nursing. This position will provide clinical instruction to students in the Traditional and Accelerated BSN ( ABSN ) tracks and help develop, coordinate, teach, and evaluate nursing content and current nursing interventions to keep the curriculum up to date. This position requires expertise in medical surgical nursing, clinical nursing instruction, clinical coordination, and use of interactive and simulated technology in nursing education. Additional responsibilities include mentoring students, participation in course and curriculum development, and service on college committees. Engagement in professional development, scholarship related to teaching, and membership in relevant professional organizations are expected. Ideal applicants will have clinical teaching experience with undergraduate health professions or nursing students and the ability to connect nursing concepts to clinical reasoning and patient care. The required education and experience includes an earned Master’s Degree in Nursing. Doctorate (PhD, DNP , or related terminal degree) is preferred. An active unencumbered Kentucky license as a registered nurse and a minimum of two years of BSN nursing experience within the last five years required. Please apply to both Lecturer – College of Nursing – Clinical Instructor positions to be considered. Employment at UK is subject to fund availability and comes with comprehensive rewards, focusing on your total well-being and career development, with leadership striving to provide a strong work-life integration. The university generously contributes to employees’ retirement plans, medical coverage, and life insurance. In addition, UK offers optional benefits such as dental and vision insurance, additional retirement plans and much more. To learn more about these benefits, please visit: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/our-benefits . **For specific request #1, please upload recommendation letters as one PDF (minimum: 3, maximum: 6) Skills / Knowledge / Abilities • Excellent interpersonal communication and organizational skills. • Demonstrated clinical proficiency and clinical experience in medical surgical nursing. • Experience in clinical simulation with low- and high-fidelity simulators preferred. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Doctorate (PhD, DNP , or related terminal degree) is preferred. Successful teaching of baccalaureate nursing students, clinical coordination, and simulation experience is preferred Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Specific Request 1 Optional Documents Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
