    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/640433": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Scholar in Immunology",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Post-Doctoral Scholar in Immunology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Post-Doctoral Scholar in Immunology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Post-Doctoral Scholar in Immunology Requisition Number DU14837 Department Name 81140:Veterinary Science Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience but competitive. Type of Position Student Position Time Status Full-Time Required Education Ph.D. in Immunology, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Sciences, Microbiology, Stem Cell Biology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry, or a closely related discipline. Candidates with experience in bioinformatics and omics data analysis are encouraged to apply. Required Related Experience The successful candidate should demonstrate a strong first-author publication record in peer-reviewed journals and possess experience in one or more areas, including cellular immunology, mammalian cell biology, advanced two-dimensional (2D) and three-dimensional (3D) cell culture systems, primary cell isolation and culture, epithelial biology, stem cell-based culture systems, immune cell culture and co-culture models, host–pathogen interactions, and molecular and cellular immunology. Experience with immunological techniques such as flow cytometry, cytokine analysis, multiplex immunoassays, ELISA , immunofluorescence microscopy, confocal microscopy, Western blotting, and immune signaling pathway analysis is highly desirable. Candidates with experience in next-generation sequencing workflows, including RNA isolation, sequencing library preparation, quality control, transcriptomic analysis, or other omics-based approaches, are strongly encouraged to apply. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, scientific rigor, analytical thinking, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively are essential. Required License/Registration/Certification N/A Physical Requirements Work in the laboratory may require long periods of standing or sitting. Shift Monday to Friday 8 am to 5 pm (40 hrs/week), plus evenings & weekends as needed. Job Summary The Department of Veterinary Science at the University of Kentucky invites applications for a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar/Research Associate to join an interdisciplinary research program investigating cellular immune responses to bacterial pathogens and the molecular mechanisms governing host–pathogen interactions. The successful candidate will lead innovative research utilizing advanced cellular and molecular biology approaches, sophisticated two-dimensional and three-dimensional cell culture systems, immunological assays, high-resolution imaging, and next-generation sequencing technologies to investigate epithelial and immune cell responses to infection and evaluate novel therapeutic strategies. This position offers outstanding opportunities to conduct high-impact research, publish in leading journals, mentor trainees, and develop independent research projects. Questions about this position can be directed to yahe223@uky.edu . Skills / Knowledge / Abilities The successful candidate will: · Design, develop, and lead independent and collaborative research projects focused on cellular immunology and host responses to infection. · Develop and optimize advanced mammalian cell culture systems, including complex 2D and 3D cellular models. · Perform immunological assays, including flow cytometry, cytokine profiling, ELISA , immunofluorescence microscopy, Western blotting, and immune signaling analyses. · Conduct molecular biology experiments, including RNA isolation, quantitative PCR , and sequencing library preparation. · Analyze transcriptomic and other omics datasets in collaboration with bioinformatics teams. · Interpret experimental data, troubleshoot assays, and optimize laboratory protocols. · Prepare manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals. · Present research findings at scientific meetings. · Contribute to the preparation of competitive grant proposals. · Mentor graduate and undergraduate students. Maintain compliance with institutional biosafety and research regulations. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Demonstrated enthusiasm for research, excellent written and verbal communication skills, professionalism, strong interpersonal and teamwork abilities, a solid academic record, and a commitment to scientific rigor. Deadline to Apply 10/14/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
