    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/640330": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Policy Studies &amp; Evaluation--Qualitative Research Design &amp; Methods, Regular Title Series",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor of Educational Policy Studies &amp; Evaluation--Qualitative Research Design &amp; Methods, Regular Title Series Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor of Educational Policy Studies & Evaluation--Qualitative Research Design & Methods, Regular Title Series Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor of Educational Policy Studies & Evaluation--Qualitative Research Design & Methods, Regular Title Series Requisition Number FE04955 Working Title Department Name 8G060:Educational Policy Studies and Evaluatio Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Tenure Track Required Education Earned doctorate in qualitative research design and methods or related area, or an earned doctorate in disciplinary areas such as education policy, public policy, higher education, or a closely related field with extensive preparation in qualitative research design and methods. Required Related Experience Required qualifications include: Experience in conducting qualitative research; Demonstrated or evidenced potential to teach qualitative methods and methodologies at the graduate level; Evidence of scholarly productivity; Experience working with student populations; and Excellent oral and written communication skills. Required License/Registration/Certification n/a Job Summary The Department of Educational Policy Studies and Evaluation ( EPE ) in the College of Education at the University of Kentucky invites applications and nominations for a tenure-eligible Assistant Professor position, effective August 15, 2027. The individual will be responsible for carrying out research, teaching, and service within the department. We welcome applicants with methodological expertise in qualitative research design and methods that aligns with the topical areas of focus within EPE . Main duties and responsibilities include the following: Teach courses in EPE Have an active research agenda including the active pursuit of extramural funding Maintain a professional service agenda appropriate for rank and career stage Assist with the recruitment and advising of graduate students and serve on doctoral program committees Support the strategic goals and priorities of the Department, College, and University Required qualifications include: An earned doctorate in qualitative research design and methods or related area, or an earned doctorate in disciplinary areas such as education policy, public policy, higher education, or a closely related field with extensive preparation in qualitative research design and methods Experience in conducting qualitative research Demonstrated or evidenced potential to teach qualitative methods and methodologies at the graduate level Evidence of scholarly productivity Experience working with student populations Excellent oral and written communication skills Preferred qualifications include: Successful post-secondary teaching and advising of graduate students Online teaching experience Research and methodological interests in emerging areas such as artificial intelligence and large language models, community engaged inquiry, and participatory research methods To apply for the position, please upload the following: Curriculum vita Cover letter – Address your qualifications, area(s) of specialization, and desired courses to teach Two representative publications or writing samples Unofficial Academic Transcripts – Official transcripts required upon hire Statement on Teaching, Advising, and Service – (One page, upload under Specific Request 1) Statement on Research and Scholarly Activity – (One page, upload under Specific Request 2) Names and contact information of three people from whom references may be solicited The review of applications begins September 11, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Kayla Johnson, Search Committee Chair, at kayla.johnson@uky.edu Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred qualifications include: Successful post-secondary teaching and advising of graduate students; Online teaching experience Research and methodological interests in emerging areas such as artificial intelligence and large language models, community-engaged inquiry, and participatory research methods. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status or whether the person is a smoker or nonsmoker, as long as the person complies with University regulation concerning smoking. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Writing Sample Academic Transcript Specific Request 1 Specific Request 2 Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
