    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/635701": {
      "title": "Student Worker-Football",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Worker-Football Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Worker-Football Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Worker-Football Requisition Number DU13002 Department Name 12B00:Mens Sports Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00 per hour Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education High School + Some College Required Related Experience None Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements To be able to lift up to 10 lbs. Shift Days, Evenings, Weekends Job Summary This position will be assisting the football office with clerical and general office duties. Duties include but not limited to: data entry, recruit mailings and assisting with recruit check-in process. Applicants must be willing to perform diverse tasks requiring good organizational and communication skills. Must be able to comply with all SEC , University and NCAA rules and regulations. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Exceptional communication, organizational, and writing skills, computer skills (Word/Excel), knowledge of the game of basketball, ability to multi-task. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * As part of the Southeastern Conference, candidates considered for staff or coaching positions within UK Athletics are required to disclose any unethical conduct. Please answer the below questions regarding your personal NCAA record. Have you ever been charged with a violation of NCAA 10.1 Unethical Conduct by the NCAA or any NCAA member institution? Yes No * Have you ever been charged with a NCAA Level I, II or III, secondary or major violation? Yes No * Are you currently involved in any pending NCAA investigation, charges and/or violations of NCAA legislation? Yes No * Has the NCAA Committee on Infractions ever issued you show-cause penalty? Yes No * If you answered yes, to either of the previous two questions, please list all violations in which you’ve been charged or were involved. If you answered no to both of the previous questions please type: N/A (Open Ended Question) * I agree to and understand that failure to disclose any NCAA violation or false information regarding my NCAA compliance history will result in removal of my application for consideration. Yes No * Please list any football teams that you have been associated with in the past four years (e.g. high school, prep school, AAU, 2-year college). (OPEN ENDED) (Open Ended Question) * Please list any current prospective student-athletes you are associated with (e.g. personal trainer, coach, family member, mentor, etc.). (Open Ended Question) * I certify that I am not associated with any prospective student-athlete(s) UK is currently recruiting. (YES/NO) Yes No * I certify that I am not associated with any prospective student-athlete(s) that UK is currently recruiting. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
