    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/634977": {
      "title": "College of Public Health Instructional Aide",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | College of Public Health Instructional Aide Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support College of Public Health Instructional Aide Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title College of Public Health Instructional Aide Requisition Number DU14758 Department Name 7P700:Public Health Academic Excellence Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15 - $20 based on experience Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Bachelor’s degree and must currently be enrolled as a graduate student at the university. Required Related Experience None Required License/Registration/Certification None Physical Requirements May require lifting up to 10 pounds, sitting for extended periods of time, repetitive motion. Shift Flexible schedule; Based on course needs. Job Summary An Instructional Aide is an academically qualified graduate student that assists instructors in preparing and managing course materials. Students who currently have a graduate assistantship (TA, RA, GRA ) are not eligible. Applicants must have a bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline and be currently enrolled as a graduate student at the university. This position does not include tuition or student health plan assistance. Instructional Aides do not perform teaching duties. Duties May Include: Grade homework, quizzes and exams for assigned course Maintain written records of grades earned in close consultation with course instructor Proctor tests including mid-term and final exams Provide support for lecture set up and demonstrations as needed Provide support for learning management system ( CANVAS ) Assist with the development of visual aids, answer keys, supplementary notes, etc. Assist with clerical and administrative tasks related to the assigned course(copies, etc.) Attend meetings as requested by instructor Other duties as assigned Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Proficient in the use of technology and educational software. Commitment to compliance to confidentiality and data protection standards. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently. Must be dependable and deadline conscious. Able to manage multiple tasks and prioritize. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience None Deadline to Apply 05/31/2027 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Which program is your completed bachelor’s degree from? If you are currently finishing your degree this term, please indicate that. (Open Ended Question) * What graduate program are you currently enrolled in or will be enrolled in during the next term? (Open Ended Question) * What is your UK Student ID number? (Open Ended Question) * Will you be receiving a graduate assistantship during the next term? Please note that students who have an assistantship are not eligible. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Academic Transcript Optional Documents Curriculum Vita 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
