    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/633401": {
      "title": "Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Chandler Central Operations",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Chandler Central Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Chandler Central Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacist Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Chandler Central Operations Requisition Number DU11260 Department Name H3330:Pharmacy Services Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $50.34-$64.08 Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education B.S. Pharmacy or PharmD Required Related Experience none Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed pharmacist or license eligible in Kentucky Physical Requirements May require standing or sitting for greater than 5 hours at a time. Shift Varies Job Summary In this position the candidate will provide pharmaceutical care to patients admitted to the University of Kentucky Healthcare Albert B. Chandler Medical Center. Responsibilities include: reviewing and perfecting medication orders, reviewing drug profiles to ensure appropriateness of therapy and contacting and conferring with physicians and other practitioners to optimize medication therapy. Actively participating in all aspects of the medication reconciliation process and promotion of economically conscientious use of medication. Daily activities may include active participation on patient care rounds, review of patient profiles, and provision of pharmacokinetic evaluation of therapeutic regimens. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities knowledge of inpatient pharmacy practice, strong clinical skills, ability to prioritize Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Hospital experience preferred Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky (or another state) and are eligible for licensure in KY? Yes No How many years of experience do you have as a pharmacist? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/633399": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Sr Tech I/OnCall/UKHC - Good Samaritan Inpatient",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Sr Tech I/OnCall/UKHC - Good Samaritan Inpatient Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Sr Tech I/OnCall/UKHC - Good Samaritan Inpatient Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Sr Tech I/OnCall/UKHC - Good Samaritan Inpatient Requisition Number DU11825 Department Name H6290:Pharmacy Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $18.50 - $27.31 Type of Position Staff Position Time Status On Call Required Education HS diploma Required Related Experience 2 yrs Pharmacy Experience Required License/Registration/Certification National Pharmacy Technician Certification and Registration with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy. Physical Requirements May include standing and/or walking for greater than 5 hours at a time as well as lifting up to 30 pounds. Walking could be of significant distance throughout the medical center campus. May require the ability to reach items above the shoulder level. Shift Varies – Covers days off for full-time employees; shifts include 7a – 530p; 7a – 7p; 12n – 10p; 7p – 7a; 8:30p – 7a; among others; opportunities 7 days a week. Job Summary The Pharmacy Senior Technician assists pharmacists in providing medications to patients in an inpatient hospital setting by compounding complex sterile and non-sterile products and participating in the deliver of comprehensive pharmaceutical care. Areas of service include Good Sam Inpatient Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability, excellent customer service and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Must be self-motivated and be able to stay on task. Must be reliable and punctual. This position requires teamwork, good communication skills and interpersonal skills to be applied with both patients and other medical professionals. Must be proficient in speaking/hearing English and must be able to be understood in English. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience 2yrs of Retail and/or Hospital pharmacy technician experience required. Hired candidate must maintain licensure as CPhT from PTCB /ExCPT during employment in this position. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a National Pharm Tech Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacy Technician? Yes No Please select the response that best represents your full years paid, full-time, employment experience in pharmacy or pharmacy related. *If you have part-time work experience that you want to include, please refer to the following to determine your credit of full years of related employment experience: 35+ hours worked per week = full credit for time worked 28-34 hours worked per week = 75% credit for time worked 18-27 hours worked per week = 50% credit for time worked 9-17 hours worked per week = 25% credit for time worked < 9 hours worked per week = no credit given for time worked None Some, but less than one full year of employment listed above. At least 1 full year but less than 2 years of employment listed above At least 2 full years but less than 3 years of employment listed above At least 3 full years but less than 4 years of employment listed above At least 4 full years but less than 5 years of employment listed above At least 5 full years but less than 6 years of employment listed above. At least 6 full years but less than 7 years of employment listed above. At least 7 full years or more of employment listed above. Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
