    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/628115": {
      "title": "Summer, Fall, and Spring 2026-2027 Assistant Teacher / Student Worker - Early Childhood Laboratory",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Summer, Fall, and Spring 2026-2027 Assistant Teacher / Student Worker - Early Childhood Laboratory Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Summer, Fall, and Spring 2026-2027 Assistant Teacher / Student Worker - Early Childhood Laboratory Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Describe your experience working with young children - birth - 5 years of age. Preference is given to IECE, Elementary ED and Special ED majors. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Summer, Fall, and Spring 2026-2027 Assistant Teacher / Student Worker - Early Childhood Laboratory Requisition Number DU11868 Department Name 8G070:Early Childhood, Spec Ed & Counselor Ed Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range varies Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education Interdisciplinary Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, Special Education or Psychology are preferred fields of study. Other fields may be considered if applicant has a strong background in early childhood. Required Related Experience Applicant should have experience working with young children, preferably in school or child care settings. We are looking for students who love working with children during the Summer of 2026, Fall of 2026, and/or Spring of 2027 at the UK Early Childhood Lab. Required License/Registration/Certification Applicant must have a current negative TB test (within the last 2 years) or be willing to get one. CPR and 1st aid certification is required within 3 months of employment. All employees must have a finger print background check. This will be done when applicants are offered the job. Physical Requirements Must be able to pick up children weighing up to 40 pounds, push strollers and be able to get up and down from the floor several times a day. The children also go outside at least 2 times each day. Teachers go outside with children. Shift The ECL opens at 7:00a.m. and closes at 5:30.p.m. Job Summary Job duties of a student worker at the ECL include playing with and supervising young children, helping classroom teachers with cleaning and organizing, assisting with daily routines, reading to children, and going to the playground and walks around campus. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities We are hoping to employ students who are professional, and understand the importance of coming to work during their planned schedules. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Have cared for children in child care or at home. Deadline to Apply 12/31/9999 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Optional Documents Resume 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
