    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/620145": {
      "title": "Student Summer Intern - Plant and Soil Sciences",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Student Summer Intern - Plant and Soil Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Student Summer Intern - Plant and Soil Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Student Summer Intern - Plant and Soil Sciences Requisition Number DU11761 Department Name 81060:PLANT AND SOIL SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range Varies Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education As required by supervisor. Required Related Experience As required by supervisor. Required License/Registration/Certification As required by supervisor. Physical Requirements As required by supervisor. Shift During the Summer: Monday – Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm (40 hrs/wk). During the crop growing season different hours, either earlier start times or later end times, may be necessary to complete research activities. Job Summary This program will be responsible for the development and execution of agricultural field research, including managing corn, soybean, wheat rotations and protection systems, conducting field sampling of crop productivity, pest, disease, weed, and weather logger monitoring. Field work will require long hours in the hot humid summer conditions Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This is a temporary position with Plant and Soil Sciences. The position will be under the supervision of a department faculty or staff member to perform lab or field research as directed by supervisor or Graduate Research Assistant. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our s