    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/614881": {
      "title": "Physician - Obstetrician / Urogynecologist (OB/GYN)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Obstetrician / Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Obstetrician / Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Obstetrician / Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Requisition Number FE04794 Working Title Urogynecologist Department Name 7H513:OB-GYN/UROGYNECOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN Required License/Registration/Certification Eligibility for or current medical license in the state of Kentucky. Board certified or eligibility in OB/ GYN . Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine is seeking a Division Director of Gynecologic Subspecialty Surgery who is a Board Certified, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery ( URPS ) fellowship–trained urogynecologist for a full-time faculty position. The Division Director will provide strategic, clinical, and academic leadership for the division while advancing excellence in patient care, education, and research. The successful candidate is expected to be appointed at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor , commensurate with experience and qualifications. The successful candidate will have completed a residency in Obstetrics and Gynecology and a fellowship in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery. This role includes an active clinical practice, mentorship and education of residents and medical students, and opportunities to develop and lead scholarly and quality initiatives within the division. Prior leadership experience is preferred. A competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package are offered. The University of Kentucky is committed to fostering a collaborative and welcoming academic environment. Please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience in teaching and supervising medical students preferred. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you first see this position advertised? InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com AAMC.org Indeed.com LinkedIn.com UK Physician Recruiter Current Resident or Fellow A Colleague, Friend and/or Family Member (Please specify below.) Recruiter or Search Firm (Please specify below.) Other (Please specify below.) * Please provide additional details about how you first heard about this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/614829": {
      "title": "Physician - Urogynecologist (OB/GYN)",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Urogynecologist (OB/GYN) Requisition Number FE04629 Working Title Urogynecologist Department Name 7H513:OB-GYN/UROGYNECOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN Required License/Registration/Certification Eligibility for or current medical license in the state of Kentucky. Board certified or eligibility in OB/ GYN . Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky, is seeking a Board Certified/Board Eligible URPS fellowship trained Physician (Urogynecology) to join the Division of Gynecologic Subspecialty Surgery for a full-time faculty position. The successful candidate will have completed a residency in OBGYN and completed or be completing a fellowship in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery. Recent graduates are encouraged to apply. Enjoy an active role caring for patients and performing research while educating residents and medical students. A competitive salary and benefits package is being offered. Please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Preferred experience in teaching and supervising medical students preferred. Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
