    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/613752": {
      "title": "AFS Student Worker - Equine",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | AFS Student Worker - Equine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support AFS Student Worker - Equine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title AFS Student Worker - Equine Requisition Number DU11815 Department Name 81070:ANIMAL AND FOOD SCIENCES Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $12.00 Type of Position Student Position Time Status Part-Time Required Education HS Required Related Experience To be discussed with hiring supervisor. Attention to detail, good work ethic, punctuality, good communication skills. Required License/Registration/Certification May require a driver’s license Physical Requirements Positions may require, but not limited to, lifting, bending, squatting, repetitive motion, working outside, heat/cold temps (weather), working with animals. Shift Shifts vary – supervisor will work with individual schedules. Job Summary This is typically a pre-hire position. Join the Equine Unit team at Maine Chance Farm. Responsibilities encompass a diverse range of tasks such as daily care of horses (including mares, foals, and yearlings), feeding, grooming, groundwork, preparing yearlings for sales, aiding in veterinary and blacksmith duties, maintaining cleanliness in stalls, barns, and facilities, as well as operating equipment. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Good work ethic, punctuality, good communication skills and attention to detail. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Farm and animal experience. Computer knowledge. Deadline to Apply Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
