    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/612062": {
      "title": "Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacist Intern Senior/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Requisition Number DU12331 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $18.50- $27.35 per hour Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education High School plus Admitted to a College of Pharmacy Required Related Experience n/a Required License/Registration/Certification Registered with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacist Intern Physical Requirements May include standing for greater than 5 years at a time and possibly walking several miles per day. May require the ability to reach items above shoulder level. Shift Varies- Monday- Friday 7:30am- 5pm; no weekend availability Job Summary This position is designed to expose student interns to all facets of specialty pharmacy practice. Interns will rotate through specialty operations, multiple disease state specific call centers, clinics, and the infusion center. Additionally, there will be opportunities to participate in clinical research projects and develop policies and procedures. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Attention to detail, knowledge of ambulatory retail pharmacy operations, and ability to prioritize. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Retail Ambulatory experience preferred Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently registered with the Kentucky Board of Pharmacy as a Pharmacist Intern? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
