    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/605838": {
      "title": "Hematology Clinical Physician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Hematology Clinical Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Hematology Clinical Physician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Hematology Clinical Physician Requisition Number FE04415 Working Title Department Name 7H368:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - HEM/BMT Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, MD/PhD , DO degree or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency, as well as fellowship training in Hematology/Oncology Required License/Registration/Certification License to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Board-Certified/Board Eligible Hematologist or Hematologist/Oncologist Job Summary The Division of Hematology and Blood & Marrow Transplantation at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine Markey Cancer Center is currently seeking an academically focused clinician to join as an Assistant Associate or Professor for clinical services. In our Division of Hematology & BMT , our mission is to reduce cancer deaths through innovative research, dedicated patient care, and education. We provide access to highly specialized, comprehensive and personalized care, state of the art research and clinical trials. The University of Kentucky offers excellent and comprehensive compensation based on rank and experiences plus outstanding benefits packages. The University of Kentucky Medical Center is a premier research institution in the Commonwealth serving a wide geographic area, treating patients from throughout Kentucky, Tennessee, West Virginia, and beyond, providing the opportunity for large practice growth with the Markey Cancer Center being the only NCI -designated Cancer Center in Kentucky. The UK Markey Cancer Center for a seventh straight year earned a national ranking from the U.S. News & World Report Best Hospitals. For the eighth year in a row, UK HealthCare was ranked the No. 1 hospital in Kentucky Applicants should include a current CV. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
