    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/602430": {
      "title": "Physician - Medical Director of UK Sleep Center/Clinic",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Physician - Medical Director of UK Sleep Center/Clinic Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Physician - Medical Director of UK Sleep Center/Clinic Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Physician - Medical Director of UK Sleep Center/Clinic Requisition Number FE04676 Working Title Department Name 7H363:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - PULMONAR Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, DO or Equivalent Degree Required Related Experience Completion of Sleep Medicine Fellowship Sleep Medicine physician experience Required License/Registration/Certification Ky Medical License with 30 days of employment Board certified in Internal Medicine and Board Eligible in Sleep Medicine Job Summary The Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine at the University of Kentucky is seeking a Sleep Physician to serve as the Medical Director of the Sleep Center at the University of Kentucky. The ideal candidate will have a strong interest in and experience in sleep medicine, evidence of educational and/or research accomplishments within the field of sleep medicine, be board certified in Sleep Medicine and qualify at the Associate Professor level or above. Candidates will have protected time to serve as the medical director of the sleep center and will be expected to play a leadership role in the growth and development of the sleep center/program at the University of Kentucky as well as participate in the care of outpatients in the sleep clinic. Candidates will have the opportunity and are encouraged to be involved in the teaching of University of Kentucky medical students, residents, and fellows. There are also opportunities to participate in patient-oriented research in the areas of sleep disorders. Salaries and academic rank are commensurate with experience The University of Kentucky College of Medicine and UK HealthCare are located in the beautiful Bluegrass Region of Lexington, an ideal location to experience the work-life balance we strive to provide for all of our employees. The College of Medicine seeks qualified applicants who value its mission and share its commitment to creating an environment in which all members feel welcomed and valued. As an Equal Opportunity Action Employer, we strive to foster a community in which individuals of all backgrounds, identities, and perspectives can feel secure and welcome. Questions or inquiries may be directed to Phillip.McCann@uky.edu . Please include your CV and letter of interest at time of email. Please address your letter to Eric Bensadoun, MD, MPH , Chief, Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep Medicine, 740 S. Limestone, K528, Lexington, KY 40536-0284. All inquiries will remain confidential. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
