    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/597698": {
      "title": "Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clin Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clin Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clin Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Amb/Retail Pharmacist Clin Staff/OnCall/UKHC - Specialty Pharmacy Requisition Number DU03762 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $50.34hr - 64.08/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education BS Pharmacy or Pharm D Required Related Experience 0 yrs. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed Pharmacist in Kentucky Physical Requirements May include sitting or standing for greater than 5 hours at a time. May require the ability to reach items above shoulder level and be able to lift up to 30 pounds. Shift Current operating hours of UK Specialty Pharmacy services are Monday thru Friday 730am-5pm. Hours and days of the week subject to change based on the growth and needs of the department. Shifts to be scheduled to not be more than 40 hours per week and number of hours available may vary. Job Summary This position will provide a variety of specialty pharmacy services aimed at improving the care for patients enrolled within the UK HealthCare Specialty Pharmacy service. This position will provide oversight of a variety of areas, including appropriateness of prescription processing, workflow improvement, mail order support, patient counseling, and coordination of prescription with clinic-based and call-center based specialty pharmacists. This position will provide a high patient-touch service while obtaining affordable access to these medications, both cornerstones of a high functioning Specialty Pharmacy. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Requires attention to detail and the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be reliable and punctual. This position also requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and strong interpersonal skills. Must be able to communicate effectively in English within a diverse population. Creates and maintains cultures where all staff delivers friendly, patient centered care . Must know State and Federal regulatory dispensing requirements, have attention to detail, must maintain knowledge of drug specific storage and shipping requirements, knowledge of current laws, procedures, and pharmaceutical knowledge. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Ambulatory/Retail Pharmacy Experience preferred. Deadline to Apply 12/31/2026 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you licensed or eligible to be licensed as a Pharmacist in the state of Kentucky? Yes No Please indicate your years of experience performing 340B audits. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Please describe your experience in working with physicians, nurses, and pharmacists to secure Prior Authorizations. (Open Ended Question) Please describe your retail pharmacy and/or medicare billing experience. (Open Ended Question) Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/597572": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Spec/On-Call/UKHC- Specialty Pharmacy",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Spec/On-Call/UKHC- Specialty Pharmacy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Spec/On-Call/UKHC- Specialty Pharmacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pharmacy Sr Tech I/Spec/On-Call/UKHC- Specialty Pharmacy Requisition Number DU03761 Department Name H5000: CHANDLER - RETAIL PHARMACY Work Location Lexington, KY Salary Range $15.26/hr - $23.89/hr Type of Position Temporary Position Time Status On Call Required Education High School Required Related Experience 2 yrs Required License/Registration/Certification National Pharmacy Technician Certification thru either PTCB or ExCPT with CPhT designation and Registration with Kentucky Board of Pharmacy. Physical Requirements May include standing and/or walking for greater than 5 hours at a time. Walking could be of significant distance throughout the medical center campus for medication delivery to clinic patients. May require the ability to reach items above the shoulder level and to carry items up to 25 pounds. Shift Current operating hours are Monday thru Friday 730am-5pm. Hours and days of week subject to change based on the needs and growth of the department. May require call center duties which could expand to later hours and may require occasional holiday and weekend rotation based on growth of department. Shifts assigned based on scheduling needs not to exceed 40 hours/week. Number of hours scheduled per week may vary. Job Summary This position will provide a variety of specialty pharmacy services including obtaining prior authorizations, enrolling patients’ in financial support programs, mail order tracking and drug inventory management, and coordinating first time dispenses and refills for specialty medications prescribed within UK HealthCare. You will work closely with nurses, physicians, and UK Specialty Pharmacy staff to improve access to medications for a variety of sub specialty disease states. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities This position requires dependability, excellent customer service and the ability to prioritize. The successful candidate must be reliable and demonstrate excellent attention to detail. Must be self-motivated and be able to stay on task. Must be reliable and punctual. This position requires teamwork, excellent communication skills and strong interpersonal skills to be applied with both patients and other medical professionals. Creates and maintains cultures where all staff delivers friendly, patient centered care. Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Retail and/or Hospital pharmacy technician experience preferred but not required. Hired candidate must maintain licensure as CPhT from PTCB /ExCPT during employment in this position. Salary range based on experience and certification Deadline to Apply 12/31/2025 Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you currently hold a National Pharmacy Technician Certification from either PTCB or ExCPT? Yes No The University of Kentucky HealthCare recognizes a set of values that guide us in our daily interactions. By applying for a position within UK Healthcare, you are indicating your commitment and expressing your agreement to our five values. These values are diversity, innovation, respect, compassion, and teamwork. Please choose one of the UK Healthcare values and give a specific example when you exhibited this quality in your professional experience. (Open Ended Question) Please select the answer that best describes your years of paid, full-time employment experience in a pharmacy. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 2 years More than 2 years, up through 3 years More than 3 years Please provide a specific example from your past experience that highlights your ability to provide great customer service. (Open Ended Question) Please describe your experience in working with physicians, nurses, and pharmacists to secure Prior Authorizations. (Open Ended Question) Please describe your retail pharmacy and/or medicare billing experience. (Open Ended Question) Please indicate your years of experience performing 340B audits. None More than 0, up through 1 year More than 1 year, up through 3 years More than 3 years, up through 5 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vita Cover Letter Academic Transcript 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
