    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/597314": {
      "title": "Pediatric Surgeon",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Pediatric Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Pediatric Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Pediatric Surgeon Requisition Number FE04564 Working Title Department Name 7H857:SURGERY/PEDIATRICS Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D. or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency training in General Surgery, as well as fellowship in Pediatric Surgery Required License/Registration/Certification Board Eligible/Board Certified in General Surgery and Pediatric Surgery Eligibility for license to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Job Summary The Division of Pediatric Surgery at the University of Kentucky, College of Medicine seeks a board-certified pediatric surgeon to join our expanding clinical and academic program as an Assistant, Associate, or Professor of Pediatric Surgery. This position offers the opportunity to work alongside seven pediatric general surgeons supported by advance practice professionals and trainees in a mission-driven and supportive environment. Key Responsibilities: · Lead the UK Pediatric Surgery Quality Program by setting the vision and strategy. Develop, monitor, and improve patient-centered quality and safety metrics using evidence-based practices and innovative solutions. Foster a culture of quality and performance improvement. · Provide exceptional clinical care to pediatric patients. · Educate and mentor residents and medical students. · Engage in innovative research and scholarly activities to advance the field of pediatric surgery. About Us: Kentucky Children’s Hospital is a Level 1 Pediatric Trauma Center with an 88-bed Level IV NICU , a 16-bed PICU , and an ELSO Center of Excellence co-located with the UK Hospital System. Serving a catchment area of over 1.6 million people, we offer a comprehensive range of pediatric and surgical care. We are pursuing ACS Pediatric Surgery Level 1 Verification and ACS Quality Verification currently. Why Join Us: · Work at the No. 1 Hospital in Kentucky, as ranked by U.S. News & World Report for nine consecutive years, and ranked in two Pediatric Specialties · Be part of a team at Kentucky Children’s Hospital dedicated to evidence based, high quality care across the full spectrum of pediatric surgery, including minimally invasive surgery, ECMO , fetal care, and trauma. Access to robotic surgery is available. · Benefit from mentorship and support in developing your academic career path with opportunities to lead and innovate · Enjoy living in Lexington, KY, a city known for its rich culture, outdoor activities, and top-rated schools. · Competitive salary and exceptional benefits/retirement package. Applicants should apply via the UK Jobs site and include an up-to-date Curriculum Vitae. This posting will remain open until the appropriate individual is recruited. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
