    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/597165": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics Requisition Number FE04353 Working Title Department Name 7H666:PEDIATRICS - PULMONOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, DO or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of Residency and Fellowship for Pediatric Pulmonology Required License/Registration/Certification Unrestricted KY Medical license Job Summary The Clinical Title Series position is needed in the Department of Pediatrics, Division of Pulmonology in order to meet the academic and clinical needs of the division and the Department in education, training and service consistent with the mission of the University Of Kentucky College Of Medicine. The Division of Pediatrics Pulmonology provides extensive clinical services to infants, children and adolescents with a variety of pulmonary disorders and diseases at the Kentucky Children’s Hospital and the Kentucky Clinics. The educational program encompasses medical students throughout their curriculum. The division is charged with care of a large population of patients and the development of clinical research. The primary responsibilities of this position are to provide quality cost-effective care to children with pulmonary disorders and diseases at the Kentucky Children’s Hospital and the Kentucky Clinic. In addition, the faculty member will participate in the education of our students, residents and extended medical community. The faculty member recruited to this clinical title series position will develop clinical investigations/ projects in a selected area of clinical Pulmonology. To apply, please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
