    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/597126": {
      "title": "Cardiology Clinician Scientist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Cardiology Clinician Scientist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Cardiology Clinician Scientist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Cardiology Clinician Scientist Requisition Number FE04317 Working Title Department Name 7H354:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - CARDIOLO Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD Degree or Equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency training in Internal Medicine and Cardiology Medicine; Completion of cardiovascular training or similar establishment of competence Required License/Registration/Certification KY Medical License Board certified in Internal Medicine Board eligible or board certified in subspecialty of Cardiovascular Diseases Board eligible or board certified in subspecialty of Interventional Cardiology Job Summary The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of Kentucky College of Medicine is seeking a clinician scientist to actively contribute to the basic and translational research mission in Cardiology. The successful candidate will be expected to bring and maintain a vigorous, independent, extramurally funded research program. Clinical work will include regular assignments in the faculty rotations to cover inpatient services ( CCU , consult, floor) and other procedures including outpatient cardiology clinics. Most all of these activities will include clinical care teaching activities with medical students, residents, and fellows. Professional development activities such as attending continuing education meetings, workshops, lectures, and other activities will be necessary to participate in the various missions of the Department, the College, and the University. Please include an updated CV when applying for position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
