    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596931": {
      "title": "Breast Radiologist",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Breast Radiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Breast Radiologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Breast Radiologist Requisition Number FE04015 Working Title Department Name 7H300:RADIOLOGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD degree or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of residency and fellowship as appropriate. Required License/Registration/Certification Board certified/board eligible by the American Board of Radiology. Must obtain Kentucky medical licensure upon appointment and maintain throughout the term of the appointment. Must be appropriately credentialed and accepted as a member of the active staff at the University Chandler and Good Samaritan Hospitals, Kentucky Clinic and other sites deemed necessary by the Chair of Radiology. Job Summary The University of Kentucky Division of Breast Radiology is expanding and seeks an exceptional radiologist for a traditional full-time faculty position. Practice locations include the academic medical center in Lexington and several community practices. We have a non ACGME -accredited breast radiology fellowship; our diagnostic radiology residency has 32 trainees. Academic rank will depend on qualifications. All full-time faculty are expected to work exclusively for the University of Kentucky. Along with the application, applicants should submit a Curriculum Vitae. Applications will be reviewed as received. This position will remain open until filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
