      "title": "Allergy/Immunology Clinical Physician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Allergy/Immunology Clinical Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Allergy/Immunology Clinical Physician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Allergy/Immunology Clinical Physician Requisition Number FE03998 Working Title Department Name 7H351:INTERNAL MEDICINE & DIVISIONS - ALLERGY Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD Degree or Equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of ACGME accredited Allergy fellowship Required License/Registration/Certification Board certified in Internal Medicine and board eligible for Allergy boards. KY Medical License at time of appointment Job Summary The University of Kentucky, Department of Internal Medicine is seeking an physician for an opportunity in an academically oriented ambulatory position in the Division of Allergy and Immunology in the University faculty practices. This position will have a full clinical faculty appointment, competitive compensation and benefits. Qualified applicants must be board eligible or board certified in internal medicine allergy. UK HealthCare is located in the beautiful Bluegrass Region of Lexington and is an ideal location to experience the work-life balance we strive to provide for all our employees. Lexington, Kentucky is consistently ranked nationally in the top sectors for Business and Careers (Forbes), Young Professionals (Kiplinger), and Education (Parenting). Please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
