    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596889": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in OB/GYN",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor in OB/GYN Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor in OB/GYN Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor in OB/GYN Requisition Number FE03920 Working Title Department Name 7H505:OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY - ONCOLOGY Work Location Bowling Green, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D or D.O Required Related Experience Completion of residency in OB/ GYN Required License/Registration/Certification Eligible for, or currently licensed, to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky Board Certified/Board Eligible in OB/ GYN Board eligible in Gynecologic Oncology Job Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of Kentucky, College of Medicine, Lexington, Kentucky is seeking a Board Certified/Board Eligible physician to join the Division of Gynecologic Oncology at our Bowling Green, KY location for a full-time faculty position. Responsibilities include: 1. Serve as a full-time clinician within the Medical Center at Bowling Green system, including outpatient clinics, inpatient care, and consults in the hospital and Emergency Department. 2. Serve as a faculty member in the Division of Gynecologic Oncology in the College of Medicine ( COM ) at the University of Kentucky. 3. Provide Outreach Services (telehealth or in-person) as needed. 4. Contribute to the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows in the Department, the UK COM , and at The Medical Center at Bowling Green. 5. Engage in scholarly activity pertinent to clinical care, education, quality and safety or health services. 6. Engage as a citizen of the Department, the Division, and The Medical Center at Bowling Green by attending departmental and divisional faculty meetings, Grand Rounds, patient care conferences, tumor board, and other important functions by teleconferencing. Applicants should have a strong interest in clinical care, education, and clinical research. Experience in teaching and supervising medical students and resident physicians is desirable. A competitive salary and benefits package is being offered. Please include an updated CV when applying for the position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite