    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596852": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics in Rheumatology",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics in Rheumatology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics in Rheumatology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor of Pediatrics in Rheumatology Requisition Number FE03756 Working Title Department Name 7H671:PEDIATRICS-RHEUMATOLOGY/MUSCULOSKELETAL Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, DO or equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of Pediatric Residency and Fellowship for Pediatric Rheumatology Required License/Registration/Certification Unrestricted KY Medical license Job Summary The University of Kentucky College of Medicine invites applications and seeks nominations for the position of Assistant Professor of Pediatrics. The successful candidate will also serve as a faculty member within the Division of Rheumatology. The primary responsibilities of this position are to provide quality cost-effective care to children at the Kentucky Children’s Hospital and the Kentucky Clinic as well as outreach locations located primarily in Eastern Kentucky. In addition, the faculty member will participate in the education of our students, residents and extended medical community. The faculty member will be involved in medical student and resident programs. Excellent opportunities for research are available. To apply, please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596849": {
      "title": "Clinical Title Series Assistant Professor-Emergency Medicine Physician",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Clinical Title Series Assistant Professor-Emergency Medicine Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Clinical Title Series Assistant Professor-Emergency Medicine Physician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinical Title Series Assistant Professor-Emergency Medicine Physician Requisition Number FE03734 Working Title Department Name 7H140:EMERGENCY MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD/DO Required Related Experience N/A Required License/Registration/Certification License to practice medicine in the state of Kentucky, Board Eligible or Board Certified Job Summary The Department of Emergency Medicine at University of Kentucky is recruiting a full-time physician. The desired individual must be BP/BC in emergency medicine. This position will function as a full-time attending physician in the Emergency Department. To be considered an applicant, qualified applicants must submit an application via the UK Jobs website. Please include a current Curriculum Vitae when applying for this position. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience MD/DO Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
