    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596840": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor in Adolescent Medicine",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant, Associate or Professor in Adolescent Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant, Associate or Professor in Adolescent Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant, Associate or Professor in Adolescent Medicine Requisition Number FE03648 Working Title Department Name 7H668:PEDIATRICS - ADOLESCENT MEDICINE Work Location Lexington, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education MD, DO or PhD Required Related Experience Previous experience providing adolescent services as a Licensed physician to children and adolescents. Required License/Registration/Certification Licensed by Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure Job Summary The University of Kentucky is currently seeking a faculty member in the Department of Adolescent Medicine, to provide clinical services at the University of Kentucky Medical Center and the Kentucky Children’s Hospital. The responsibilities of this position will be to provide exemplary, state-of-the-art, compassionate care to patients in the department. This position will also participate in the Department’s courses and medical learner education, supervise house staff assigned to the service during these rotations, and medical students providing services in the outpatient clinics. The faculty member will have an active role in the College of Medicine, and is expected to lecture and participate in small group and individual student instruction. In addition, this position is expected to engage in professional development. Please include a CV along with application. Rank will be determined based on qualifications for the position. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
