    "https://ukjobs.uky.edu/postings/596788": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Neonatal Pediatrics",
      "description": "University of Kentucky Applicant Site | Assistant Professor in Neonatal Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Sign Up For Job Alerts! Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Support Assistant Professor in Neonatal Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Assistant Professor in Neonatal Pediatrics Requisition Number FE03204 Working Title Department Name 7H665:PEDIATRICS - NEONATOLOGY Work Location Pikeville, KY Type of Position Faculty Position Time Status Full-Time Tenure Track Status Non-Tenure Track Required Education M.D., DO or the foreign equivalent Required Related Experience Completion of Residency in Pediatrics and Fellowship in Neonatology Required License/Registration/Certification Board certified or board eligible in Pediatrics, board certified or board eligible in Neonatology, and eligible for a state-required medical license. Job Summary The University of Kentucky seeks a clinical faculty member in Corbin, KY to provide inpatient care services in the Pediatric Neonatology Intensive Unit. This position will be hired at the Assistant Professor rank, and will be working as coverage at the Baptist Health facility. This position requires an MD or DO, or the foreign equivalent, as well as completion of Residency in Pediatrics and Fellowship in Neonatology. Qualified applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Pediatrics, board certified or board eligible in neonatology, and eligible for a state-required medical license. Please include a CV along with application. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. Skills / Knowledge / Abilities Does this position have supervisory responsibilities? No Preferred Education/Experience Deadline to Apply Open Until Filled Yes Our University Community We value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus. The University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status. Any candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Cover Letter 805 Las Cimas Parkway Suite 400 Austin, Texas, 78746 © University of Kentucky Lexington, Kentucky 40506 An Equal Opportunity University Accreditation Directory Email Privacy Policy Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
